const e={C0001:["TCS Control Channel A Valve 1","C0001 concerns the first traction control valve of hydraulic channel A, usually one of the two brake circuits in the ABS/ESC modulator. To brake a spinning drive wheel without driver input, a TCS-capable modulator carries an extra isolation valve and priming valve per circuit: the normally open isolation valve closes off the master cylinder, while the normally closed priming valve opens so the pump can draw fluid…",["Solenoid coil open or shorted","Corroded or chafed wiring to the modulator","Internal hydraulic modulator fault"],["ABS warning lamp on","Traction and stability control disabled","Normal braking retained without ABS"],4,2,["C0002","C0003","C0004"],""],C0002:["TCS Control Channel A Valve 2","C0002 points to the second traction control valve of channel A. Together with valve 1 it forms the valve pair a TCS modulator adds to each brake circuit: an isolation valve that cuts the circuit off from the master cylinder and a priming valve that opens the path from the master cylinder to the return pump, so pressure can rise at a driven wheel while the pedal is released.",["Solenoid coil open or shorted","Corroded or chafed wiring to the modulator","Internal hydraulic modulator fault"],["ABS warning lamp on","Traction and stability control disabled","Normal braking retained without ABS"],4,2,["C0001","C0003","C0004"],""],C0003:["TCS Control Channel B Valve 1","C0003 is the counterpart of C0001 in channel B, the second brake circuit of the modulator. A pump patent for such units shows the layout plainly: two normally open isolation valves and two normally closed priming valves, one of each per circuit, operated by the control unit alongside the apply and release valves when traction control intervenes.",["Solenoid coil open or shorted","Corroded or chafed wiring to the modulator","Internal hydraulic modulator fault"],["ABS warning lamp on","Traction and stability control disabled","Normal braking retained without ABS"],4,2,["C0001","C0002","C0004"],""],C0004:["TCS Control Channel B Valve 2","C0004 completes the set with the second traction control valve of channel B. During an intervention the module closes the isolation valve and opens the priming valve of the circuit concerned so the pump can supply pressure to a wheel that is spinning; afterwards both return to rest so the driver's pedal again acts through the master cylinder.",["Solenoid coil open or shorted","Corroded or chafed wiring to the modulator","Internal hydraulic modulator fault"],["ABS warning lamp on","Traction and stability control disabled","Normal braking retained without ABS"],4,2,["C0001","C0002","C0003"],""],C0010:["Left Front Inlet Control","Covers the left front inlet (apply) solenoid valve of the ABS hydraulic modulator. During ABS, traction or stability control the module closes this valve to isolate the left front brake circuit from the master cylinder and hold wheel pressure, then opens it to let pressure back in. The module checks the coil for opens, shorts and out-of-range resistance and monitors valve response.",["Inlet valve coil open or shorted","Brake control module fault or false setting","Harness or connector corrosion"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS and stability control disabled","Normal braking retained"],4,2,["C0011","C0012","C0014"],"בקרת כניסה קדמית שמאלית"],C0011:["Left Front Outlet Control","Covers the left front outlet (release) solenoid valve of the ABS hydraulic modulator. This valve opens to dump brake fluid from the left front caliper into the low-pressure accumulator so the module can reduce wheel pressure during an ABS or stability event, then closes to allow reapply. The control module monitors the coil for opens, shorts to power or ground and resistance outside the normal range.",["Outlet valve coil open or shorted","Harness or connector corrosion","Internal hydraulic modulator fault"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS and stability control disabled","Normal braking retained"],4,2,["C0010","C0012","C0015"],"בקרת יציאה קדמית שמאלית"],C0012:["Left Front Hydraulic Release Too Long","Set when the ABS modulator cannot release pressure at the left front wheel within the expected time during a control cycle. Rather than a pure electrical fault it is a performance or plausibility code: after the module commands the left front outlet valve to dump pressure, it expects wheel speed to recover and pressure to fall;",["Outlet valve sticking or slow","Restricted hydraulic path or contaminated fluid","Pump or accumulator cannot accept fluid"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS and stability control disabled","Extended or firm pedal during hard braking"],4,2,["C0010","C0011","C0016"],""],C0014:["Right Front Inlet Control","Covers the right front inlet (apply) solenoid valve of the ABS hydraulic modulator, the mirror of C0010 on the right front corner. The module closes this valve to isolate the right front brake circuit and hold wheel pressure during ABS, traction or stability control, then opens it to reapply pressure from the master cylinder or pump.",["Inlet valve coil open or shorted","Harness or connector corrosion","Internal hydraulic modulator fault"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS and stability control disabled","Normal braking retained"],4,2,["C0010","C0015","C0016"],"בקרת כניסה קדמית ימנית"],C0015:["Right Front Outlet Control","Covers the right front outlet (release) solenoid valve of the ABS hydraulic modulator, the release counterpart to inlet valve C0014. It opens to dump brake fluid from the right front caliper into the low-pressure accumulator so wheel pressure can fall during an ABS or stability cycle, then closes for reapply.",["Outlet valve coil open or shorted","Harness or connector corrosion","Internal hydraulic modulator fault"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS and stability control disabled","Normal braking retained"],4,2,["C0014","C0016","C0011"],"בקרת יציאה קדמית ימנית"],C0016:["Right Front Hydraulic Release Too Long","Set when the ABS modulator cannot release pressure at the right front wheel within the expected time during a control cycle, the right front equivalent of C0012. After commanding the right front outlet valve to dump pressure the module expects wheel speed to recover and line pressure to fall;",["Outlet valve sticking or slow","Restricted hydraulic path or contaminated fluid","Pump or accumulator cannot accept fluid"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS and stability control disabled","Extended or firm pedal during hard braking"],4,2,["C0014","C0015","C0012"],""],C0018:["Left Rear Inlet Control","Covers the left rear inlet (apply) solenoid valve of the ABS hydraulic modulator, the rear-axle counterpart of C0010. The module closes this valve to isolate the left rear brake circuit and hold wheel pressure during ABS, traction or stability control, then opens it to reapply pressure. On many vehicles the rear channel also carries electronic brake-force distribution.",["Inlet valve coil open or shorted","Harness or connector corrosion","Internal hydraulic modulator fault"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS and stability control disabled","Normal braking retained"],4,2,["C0019","C001A","C001C"],"בקרת כניסה אחורית שמאלית"],C0019:["Left Rear Outlet Control","Covers the left rear outlet (release) solenoid valve of the ABS hydraulic modulator, the release counterpart to inlet valve C0018. It opens to dump brake fluid from the left rear caliper or wheel cylinder into the low-pressure accumulator so pressure can fall during an ABS or stability cycle, then closes for reapply.",["Outlet valve coil open or shorted","Harness or connector corrosion","Internal hydraulic modulator fault"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS and stability control disabled","Normal braking retained"],4,2,["C0018","C001A","C001D"],"בקרת יציאה אחורית שמאלית"],C001A:["Left Rear Hydraulic Release Too Long","Set when the ABS modulator cannot release pressure at the left rear wheel within the expected time during a control cycle, the left rear equivalent of C0012 and C0016. After the module commands the left rear outlet valve to dump pressure it expects wheel speed to recover and line pressure to fall;",["Outlet valve sticking or slow","Restricted hydraulic path or contaminated fluid","Pump or accumulator cannot accept fluid"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS and stability control disabled","Extended or firm pedal during hard braking"],4,2,["C0018","C0019","C001E"],""],C001C:["Right Rear Inlet Control","Covers the right rear inlet (apply) solenoid valve of the ABS hydraulic modulator, the right rear counterpart of C0010 and C0018. The module closes this valve to isolate the right rear brake circuit and hold wheel pressure during ABS, traction or stability control, then opens it to reapply pressure; on the rear axle the same channel often supports electronic brake-force distribution.",["Inlet valve coil open or shorted","Harness or connector corrosion","Internal hydraulic modulator fault"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS and stability control disabled","Normal braking retained"],4,2,["C001D","C001E","C0018"],"בקרת כניסה אחורית ימנית"],C001D:["Right Rear Outlet Control","Covers the right rear outlet (release) solenoid valve of the ABS hydraulic modulator, the release counterpart to inlet valve C001C. It opens to dump brake fluid from the right rear caliper or wheel cylinder into the low-pressure accumulator so pressure can fall during an ABS or stability cycle, then closes for reapply.",["Outlet valve coil open or shorted","Harness or connector corrosion","Internal hydraulic modulator fault"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS and stability control disabled","Normal braking retained"],4,2,["C001C","C001E","C0019"],"בקרת יציאה אחורית ימנית"],C001E:["Right Rear Hydraulic Release Too Long","Set when the ABS modulator cannot release pressure at the right rear wheel within the expected time during a control cycle, completing the per-wheel set with C0012, C0016 and C001A. After commanding the right rear outlet valve to dump pressure the module expects wheel speed to recover and line pressure to fall;",["Outlet valve sticking or slow","Restricted hydraulic path or contaminated fluid","Pump or accumulator cannot accept fluid"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS and stability control disabled","Extended or firm pedal during hard braking"],4,2,["C001C","C001D","C001A"],""],C0020:["ABS Pump Motor Circuit","Covers the electric pump (return) motor of the ABS hydraulic unit and its control circuit. The motor drives the piston pump that returns brake fluid from the low-pressure accumulators and builds pressure for ABS, traction and stability interventions. The control module commands the motor and monitors the drive circuit and motor-run feedback;",["Pump motor seized or windings failed","Open or shorted motor supply or ground","Brake control module driver fault"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS, traction and stability control disabled","No pump noise during self-test"],4,2,["C0021","C0010","C0014"],"מנוע משאבת ABS — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0021:["Brake Booster Performance","A performance code for the power brake booster, set when the booster does not deliver the expected level of assist or does not respond to the control module as commanded. On vehicles with an electronic or vacuum booster the module compares driver pedal demand, measured boost and the resulting brake pressure, and stores the code when assist is weak, slow or inconsistent.",["Booster worn or not holding vacuum/pressure","Low battery voltage during module programming","Faulty boost or pressure sensor input"],["Hard brake pedal and reduced assist","Service brake or reduced power message","ABS or brake warning lamp on"],4,2,["C0022","C0047","C0048"],"מגבר בלם — ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0022:["Brake Booster Solenoid","C0022 covers the solenoid valve of an electronically controllable brake booster. Patent literature shows a vacuum booster that works in two ways: by the driver's pedal in normal braking, and through a solenoid valve that changes the pressure in an auxiliary chamber so the booster applies the brakes without the pedal.",["Solenoid coil open or shorted","Corroded connector or chafed wiring","Internal booster assembly fault"],["Changed brake pedal effort or feel","Noise from the brake system","ABS or brake warning lamp on"],4,2,["C0021","C0047","C0048"],"סולנואיד מגבר בלם"],C0023:["Stop Lamp Control","Covers the stop lamp (brake light) control circuit as driven or monitored by the brake or stability control module. Modern ABS/ESC systems can command the stop lamps during autonomous braking events such as traction control, stability control and automatic emergency braking, independent of the driver pressing the pedal, and they monitor the circuit for opens, shorts and lamp-output disagreement.",["Open or shorted stop lamp wiring","Failed lamp or output driver","Faulty brake switch signal"],["Stop lamps stay on or do not light","Stability or driver-assist functions disabled","ABS or stability warning lamp on"],2,2,["C0040","C0041","C0042"],"בקרת נורת עצירה"],C0024:["Brake Pedal Feedback Pressure Solenoid Circuit","Covers the solenoid that generates brake pedal feedback pressure in an electronic or brake-by-wire braking system. Because the driver is hydraulically decoupled during controlled braking, a pedal-feel simulator uses this solenoid to build a controlled counter-pressure so the pedal feels natural.",["Feedback solenoid open or shorted","Harness or connector fault","Internal brake actuation unit fault"],["Changed or abnormal pedal feel","Loss of brake assist, driver messages","ABS or brake warning lamp on"],4,2,["C0025","C0021","C0047"],"סולנואיד לחץ משוב דוושת בלם — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0025:["Brake Pedal Feedback Pressure Sensor Circuit","C0025 covers the pressure sensor on the pedal feedback side of a decoupled or brake-by-wire system, the measuring partner of the feedback valve C0024. In such systems the pedal pushes fluid into a pedal feel simulator via a simulator valve the module can open or close, while separate sensors read pressure in the simulator circuit and in the wheel circuit.",["Feedback pressure sensor out of range","Harness or connector fault","Internal brake actuation unit fault"],["Changed or abnormal pedal feel","Loss of brake assist, driver messages","ABS or brake warning lamp on"],4,2,["C0024","C0021","C0047"],"חיישן לחץ משוב דוושת בלם — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0030:["Left Front Tone Wheel","Covers the left front tone wheel (reluctor or encoder ring) that the wheel speed sensor reads to measure rotation. This is a signal-plausibility code rather than a sensor circuit fault: the module sees an erratic, noisy or intermittent speed signal consistent with a damaged, contaminated or loose tone ring rather than a sensor electrical failure.",["Damaged or contaminated tone ring","Loose or displaced hub bearing","Excessive sensor-to-ring air gap"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS and stability control disabled","Grinding noise from wheel hub"],2,2,["C0031","C0033","C0036"],""],C0031:["Left Front Wheel Speed Sensor","Covers the left front wheel speed sensor and its circuit. The sensor, usually an active Hall-effect type, reports wheel rotation to the ABS/ESC module for anti-lock, traction and stability control and for speed-dependent functions. The module monitors the circuit for opens, shorts to power or ground, a signal outside the valid range and a missing signal while the vehicle is moving.",["Wheel speed sensor failed","Open, shorted or chafed sensor wiring","Corroded sensor connector"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS and stability control disabled","Speedometer may read erratically"],2,2,["C0030","C0032","C0034"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל קדמי שמאלי"],C0032:["Left Front Wheel Speed Sensor Supply","Covers the supply circuit that powers the left front active wheel speed sensor. Active sensors need a regulated voltage from the ABS/ESC module; this code is set when that supply is open, shorted to ground or to another voltage, or is outside the regulated range so the sensor cannot report a valid signal.",["Open or shorted sensor supply wire","Corroded connector on the supply side","Module sensor supply output fault"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS and stability control disabled","No wheel speed signal from this corner"],2,2,["C0031","C0030","C0038"],"אספקת חיישן מהירות גלגל קדמי שמאלי"],C0033:["Right Front Tone Wheel","Covers the right front tone wheel (reluctor or encoder ring) read by the right front wheel speed sensor, the mirror of C0030. It is a signal-plausibility code: the module sees an erratic, noisy or intermittent speed signal consistent with a damaged, contaminated or loose tone ring rather than a sensor electrical failure.",["Damaged or contaminated tone ring","Loose or displaced hub bearing","Excessive sensor-to-ring air gap"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS and stability control disabled","Grinding noise from wheel hub"],2,2,["C0034","C0030","C0039"],""],C0034:["Right Front Wheel Speed Sensor","Covers the right front wheel speed sensor and its circuit, the mirror of C0031. The active sensor reports wheel rotation to the ABS/ESC module for anti-lock, traction and stability control and speed-dependent functions. The module monitors the circuit for opens, shorts to power or ground, a signal outside the valid range and a missing signal while the vehicle is moving.",["Wheel speed sensor failed","Open, shorted or chafed sensor wiring","Corroded sensor connector"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS and stability control disabled","Speedometer may read erratically"],2,2,["C0033","C0031","C003A"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל קדמי ימני"],C0035:["Right Front Wheel Speed Sensor Supply","C0035 reports a fault in the feed that powers the right front active wheel speed sensor, the right-hand partner of C0032. The ABS/ESC module supplies the sensor with a regulated voltage; an open feed, a short to ground or to another voltage, or a supply outside its window leaves the sensor unable to send a speed signal. NHTSA's EPS safety report lists C0035 with this meaning in its table of J2012 wheel speed codes.",["Open or shorted supply wire to the right front sensor","Corroded or loose sensor connector","Sensor shorted internally and pulling the supply down","Sensor supply output of the ABS module faulty"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS, traction and stability control disabled","No speed signal from the right front wheel"],2,2,["C0032","C0034","C0033","C0038","C003B"],"אספקת חיישן מהירות גלגל קדמי ימני"],C0036:["Left Rear Tone Wheel","Covers the left rear tone wheel (reluctor or encoder ring) read by the left rear wheel speed sensor, the rear-axle counterpart of C0030 and C0033. It is a signal-plausibility code set when the module sees an erratic, noisy or intermittent rear speed signal consistent with a damaged, contaminated or loose tone ring rather than a sensor circuit failure.",["Damaged or contaminated tone ring","Loose or displaced hub bearing","Excessive sensor-to-ring air gap"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS and stability control disabled","Grinding noise from wheel hub"],2,2,["C0037","C0030","C0039"],""],C0037:["Left Rear Wheel Speed Sensor","Covers the left rear wheel speed sensor and its circuit, the rear-axle counterpart of C0031 and C0034. The active sensor reports rear wheel rotation to the ABS/ESC module for anti-lock, traction and stability control and electronic brake-force distribution. The module monitors the circuit for opens, shorts to power or ground, a signal outside the valid range and a missing signal while moving.",["Wheel speed sensor bent or failed","Open, shorted or chafed sensor wiring","Corroded sensor connector"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS and stability control disabled","Speedometer may read erratically"],2,2,["C0036","C0038","C003A"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי שמאלי"],C0038:["Left Rear Wheel Speed Sensor Supply","Covers the supply circuit that powers the left rear active wheel speed sensor, the rear-axle counterpart of C0032. Active sensors need a regulated voltage from the ABS/ESC module; this code is set when that supply is open, shorted to ground or to another voltage, or outside the regulated range so the sensor cannot produce a valid signal.",["Open or shorted sensor supply wire","Corroded connector on the supply side","Module sensor supply output fault"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS and stability control disabled","No wheel speed signal from this corner"],2,2,["C0037","C0032","C003B"],"אספקת חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי שמאלי"],C0039:["Right Rear Tone Wheel","Covers the right rear tone wheel (reluctor or encoder ring) read by the right rear wheel speed sensor, completing the four-corner tone-wheel set with C0030, C0033 and C0036. It is a signal-plausibility code set when the module sees an erratic, noisy or intermittent rear speed signal consistent with a damaged, contaminated or loose tone ring rather than a sensor circuit failure.",["Damaged or contaminated tone ring","Loose or displaced hub bearing","Excessive sensor-to-ring air gap"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS and stability control disabled","Grinding noise from wheel hub"],2,2,["C003A","C0036","C0033"],""],C003A:["Right Rear Wheel Speed Sensor","Covers the right rear wheel speed sensor and its circuit, completing the four-corner sensor set with C0031, C0034 and C0037. The active sensor reports rear wheel rotation to the ABS/ESC module for anti-lock, traction and stability control and electronic brake-force distribution. The module monitors the circuit for opens, shorts to power or ground, a signal outside the valid range and a missing signal while moving.",["Wheel speed sensor bent or failed","Open, shorted or chafed sensor wiring","Corroded sensor connector"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS and stability control disabled","Speedometer may read erratically"],2,2,["C0039","C0037","C0034"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי ימני"],C003B:["Right Rear Wheel Speed Sensor Supply","Covers the supply circuit that powers the right rear active wheel speed sensor, completing the supply set with C0032 and C0038. Active sensors need a regulated voltage from the ABS/ESC module; this code is set when that supply is open, shorted to ground or to another voltage, or outside the regulated range so the sensor cannot produce a valid signal.",["Open or shorted sensor supply wire","Corroded connector on the supply side","Module sensor supply output fault"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS and stability control disabled","No wheel speed signal from this corner"],2,2,["C003A","C0038","C0032"],"אספקת חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי ימני"],C003C:["Rear Tone Wheel","Covers a single rear tone wheel (reluctor or encoder ring) on vehicles that use one combined rear wheel speed signal, for example from a differential or rear axle sensor, rather than separate left and right rear rings.",["Damaged or contaminated tone ring","Loose or displaced bearing or axle ring","Excessive sensor-to-ring air gap"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS and stability control disabled","Intermittent rear speed signal"],2,2,["C003D","C003E","C0036"],""],C003D:["Rear Wheel Speed Sensor","Covers a single rear wheel speed sensor on vehicles that use one combined rear speed signal, for example a rear axle or differential-mounted sensor, instead of separate left and right rear sensors. It reports rear rotation to the ABS/ESC module for anti-lock, traction and stability control and electronic brake-force distribution.",["Rear wheel speed sensor failed","Open, shorted or chafed sensor wiring","Corroded sensor connector"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS and stability control disabled","Speedometer may read erratically"],2,2,["C003C","C003E","C0037"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי"],C003E:["Rear Wheel Speed Sensor Supply","Covers the supply circuit that powers a single rear active wheel speed sensor on vehicles with one combined rear speed signal. Active sensors need a regulated voltage from the ABS/ESC module; this code is set when that supply is open, shorted to ground or another voltage, or outside the regulated range so the sensor cannot produce a valid signal.",["Open or shorted sensor supply wire","Corroded connector on the supply side","Module sensor supply output fault"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS and stability control disabled","No rear wheel speed signal"],2,2,["C003D","C003C","C003B"],"אספקת חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי"],C003F:["Wheel Speed Sensors Rotation Direction Correlation","A correlation code set when the directional information from the wheel speed sensors does not agree across wheels or with other motion inputs. Directional (bidirectional) wheel speed sensors tell the ABS/ESC module whether a wheel turns forward or backward, which the module uses for hill-hold, rollback detection and stability functions.",["Faulty directional wheel speed sensor","Damaged tone ring giving false direction","Sensor wiring fault or miswire"],["ABS warning lamp on","Hill-hold or stability functions disabled","Incorrect rollback or direction detection"],2,2,["C0031","C0034","C0037"],""],C0040:["Brake Pedal Switch A","C0040 reports a fault on brake pedal switch A, the first of two switch signals that tell the brake, engine and transmission modules the pedal is pressed. Mazda defines C0040:24 as a circuit malfunction of brake switch signal no. 1; on the 2024 CX-90 it appears with P0504 and a push button start warning, and service alert SA-062-23 cures it by moving the switch one adjustment notch.",["Brake switch out of adjustment (Mazda SA-062-23)","Water or corrosion in the battery junction box (Ford TSB 22-2044)","Damaged switch or shift-interlock wiring","Brake switch failed internally"],["Stop lamps stay on or do not light","Vehicle will not shift out of park","Push button start malfunction warning (Mazda)"],1,2,["C0041","C0042","C0043"],"מתג דוושת בלם‏ A"],C0041:["Brake Pedal Switch B","Covers brake pedal switch B, the redundant second brake switch used to cross-check brake pedal switch A. The two switches change state in a defined pattern as the pedal is applied; the module compares them and sets this code when switch B is stuck, open, shorted or disagrees with switch A. The redundant signal supports driver-assist features that must reliably know whether the driver is braking.",["Brake switch failed or misadjusted","Open or shorted switch wiring","Corroded or loose connector"],["Driver-assist features disabled or false triggers","Cruise or adaptive cruise will not set","Warning lamp or driver message"],1,2,["C0040","C0042","C0043"],"מתג דוושת בלם‏ B"],C0042:["Brake Pedal Position Sensor Circuit A","Covers circuit A of the brake pedal position sensor, which reports how far the pedal is pressed rather than just on/off like a switch. The brake or stability module uses this analog signal for brake-by-wire assist, regenerative braking blending and precise stop-lamp and cruise control.",["Pedal position sensor out of range","Pedal home position not learned","Harness or connector fault"],["Brake lights stay on","Cruise control will not set","ABS or brake warning lamp on"],2,2,["C0043","C0040","C0041"],"מעגל חיישן מצב דוושת בלם‏ A"],C0043:["Brake Pedal Position Sensor Circuit B","Covers circuit B of the brake pedal position sensor, the redundant second channel that the module cross-checks against channel A (C0042). Dual-channel pedal position sensors provide two independent voltage signals, often with opposite slopes, so the module can detect a single-channel fault by correlation. This code is set when channel B is out of range, open, shorted or does not track channel A within tolerance.",["Pedal position sensor channel B out of range","Channel A/B signals do not correlate","Harness or connector fault"],["Brake lights stay on or behave oddly","Cruise control will not set","ABS or brake warning lamp on"],2,2,["C0042","C0040","C0041"],"מעגל חיישן מצב דוושת בלם‏ B"],C0044:["Brake Pressure Sensor A","Covers brake pressure sensor A (sensor 1) in the ABS/ESC hydraulic unit, which measures master-cylinder or circuit brake pressure. The stability and brake modules use this reading to know how hard the driver is braking and to control traction, stability, brake assist and hill-hold.",["Pressure sensor failed or out of range","Fault internal to the integrated brake unit","Harness or connector fault"],["ABS or brake warning lamp on","Stability and assist functions disabled","Changed brake assist behaviour"],4,2,["C0045","C0046","C0024"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ A"],C0045:["Brake Pressure Sensor B","C0045 covers brake pressure sensor B, the second pressure transducer in the ABS/ESC hydraulic unit next to sensor A (C0044). Two sensors let the module watch both brake circuits or check one reading against the other for stability control, brake assist and brake-by-wire functions. The code sets for a signal out of range, an open or short, or a value that disagrees with sensor A or the pedal demand.",["Pressure sensor failed or out of range","Fault internal to the integrated brake unit","Signal does not correlate with sensor A"],["ABS or brake warning lamp on","Stability and assist functions disabled","Changed brake assist behaviour"],4,2,["C0044","C0046","C0024"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ B"],C0046:["Brake Pressure Sensor A/B","A correlation code for the pair of brake pressure sensors A and B, set when their readings do not agree within the expected tolerance. Where C0044 and C0045 flag a single-sensor electrical fault, this code is a plausibility fault: at the same instant both sensors should report consistent pressure (allowing for their known relationship), and a persistent mismatch indicates one sensor has drifted, a hydraulic fault…",["One pressure sensor drifted or biased","Hydraulic fault separating the circuits","Signal corruption or wiring fault"],["ABS or brake warning lamp on","Stability and assist functions disabled","Changed brake assist behaviour"],4,2,["C0044","C0045","C0024"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ A/B"],C0047:["Brake Booster Pressure Sensor","Covers the pressure sensor in the power brake booster or brake actuation unit, which measures boost or assist pressure so the module can regulate assist and detect loss of boost. The module monitors the sensor for a signal outside the valid range, an open or short and values that disagree with pedal demand or master-cylinder pressure.",["Booster pressure sensor out of range","Module calibration or software issue","Harness or connector fault"],["Lack of power brake assist","Soft or extended pedal at start-up","ABS or brake warning lamp on"],4,2,["C0048","C0021","C0022"],"חיישן לחץ מגבר בלם"],C0048:["Brake Booster Travel Sensor","Covers the travel (position) sensor of the power brake booster or brake actuation unit, which reports how far the booster input rod or piston has moved so the module can match assist to driver demand. The module monitors the sensor for a signal outside the valid range, an open or short and a position that is implausible against pedal position or boost pressure.",["Travel sensor out of range or failed","Binding or worn booster mechanism","Harness or connector fault"],["Changed brake pedal feel","Reduced or inconsistent brake assist","ABS or brake warning lamp on"],4,2,["C0047","C0021","C0022"],""],C0049:["Brake Fluid Level","Covers the brake fluid level input to the brake or stability module, used to warn the driver and to disable functions that must not run with low fluid. A float switch or sensor in the master-cylinder reservoir signals when fluid drops below a safe level; the module sets this code and lights the red brake warning indicator.",["Low fluid from worn pads or a leak","Faulty reservoir level sensor or float","Reservoir fault causing false reading"],["Red brake warning indicator on","Low brake fluid message","ABS and stability control may be disabled"],1,2,["C004B","C004A","C0044"],"מפלס נוזל בלם"],C004A:["Brake Lining Wear Sensor","Covers the brake lining (pad) wear sensor circuit, which warns the driver when friction material is worn to its limit. Electronic wear sensors use a loop embedded in the pad that the disc contacts and opens, or a wear-indicator circuit, as the lining wears down; the module reports pad wear and may store this code for an open, shorted or implausible sensor circuit as well as for a genuine worn-pad signal.",["Brake pads worn to the sensor limit","Open or shorted wear sensor circuit","Sensor not renewed after pad change"],["Brake pad wear warning message","Warning lamp on","Possible squeal from a mechanical indicator"],1,0,["C0049","C004B","C0047"],""],C004B:["Brake Fluid Level Sensor/Switch Circuit/Open","Covers an electrical fault, specifically an open or out-of-range circuit, in the brake fluid level sensor or switch, as opposed to C0049 which reports an actual low-level condition. The float switch or level sensor in the reservoir provides a defined signal to the brake or stability module;",["Open or chafed sensor wiring","Failed level switch or float","Corroded or loose connector"],["Red brake warning indicator on","Brake fluid level reads as unknown","Intermittent low-fluid warnings"],1,2,["C0049","C004A","C0044"],"חיישן/מתג מפלס נוזל בלם — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C004C:["Brake Booster Motor A Position Sensor Exceeded Learning Limit","Set in an electric or electro-hydraulic brake booster when the position sensor of booster motor A reports a learned reference value outside the allowed adaptation range. The brake control unit learns the rest and travel positions of the motor-driven actuator so it can meter assist precisely;",["Position sensor worn or shifted","Mechanical wear in the booster actuator","Learning routine ran under wrong conditions"],["Reduced or inconsistent brake assist","Changed brake pedal feel","ABS or brake warning lamp on"],4,2,["C004D","C004E","C0024"],""],C004D:["Brake System Pressure Slow Response","A performance code set when the brake system builds or changes hydraulic pressure more slowly than the control unit commands during an assisted or automated braking event. In electronically controlled brake systems the module commands a target pressure and watches the pressure sensor;",["Air in the hydraulic system or low fluid","Weak pump or motor performance","Sticking valve or hydraulic restriction"],["Longer pedal travel or delayed assist","Automated braking functions limited","ABS or brake warning lamp on"],4,2,["C004E","C004C","C0044"],"לחץ מערכת בלם — תגובה איטית"],C004E:["Brake System Pressure Control Valve Actuator Stuck","Set when the actuator of a brake system pressure control valve does not move as commanded and appears mechanically stuck. In electronically controlled brake and stability systems a pressure control valve regulates how much hydraulic pressure reaches the wheel circuits; the module commands the valve and checks the resulting pressure against the demand.",["Valve actuator stuck by contamination or wear","Corrosion or debris in the valve bore","Valve driver or wiring fault"],["ABS, traction and stability control disabled","Abnormal brake behaviour on one circuit","ABS or brake warning lamp on"],4,2,["C004D","C004C","C0044"],"מפעיל שסתום בקרת לחץ מערכת בלם — תקוע"],C004F:["ABS Control Module Over Temperature","Set when the ABS/ESC control module or its integrated pump motor reaches a temperature above the safe operating limit. Repeated or prolonged pressure modulation, for example during long downhill ABS use, frequent stability interventions or an electrical fault that keeps the pump running, heats the hydraulic unit and its motor;",["Stuck valve causing continuous pump run","Pump motor seizing or high friction","Prolonged heavy ABS/ESC use"],["ABS and stability control temporarily disabled","Function returns after cooling","ABS warning lamp on during the event"],4,2,["C0020","C004D","C004E"],"מודול בקרת ABS — חום יתר"],C0050:["Right Rear Wheel Speed Sensor Circuit Malfunction","A general circuit-malfunction code for the right rear wheel speed sensor, covering an electrical fault not resolved to a more specific sub-type: open circuit, short to power or ground, or a signal that drops out or becomes implausible while driving. The active sensor reports rear wheel rotation to the ABS/ESC module for anti-lock, traction and stability control and electronic brake-force distribution;",["Broken or chafed sensor harness wiring","Wheel speed sensor failed","Corroded sensor connector"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS and stability control disabled","Speedometer may read erratically"],2,2,["C0060","C0066","C0056"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי ימני — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0051:["Steering Wheel Position Sensor","Covers the steering wheel position (steering angle) sensor and its circuit. The sensor reports absolute steering-wheel angle and rate to the ESC module, which combines it with yaw rate, lateral acceleration and wheel speeds to decide when the car is understeering or oversteering.",["Neutral position not learned after service","Steering angle sensor failed","Harness or connector fault"],["Stability control disabled","ABS/ESC warning lamp on","Sets after battery disconnect"],2,2,["C0052","C0053","C0054"],"חיישן מצב גלגל הגה"],C0052:["Steering Wheel Position Sensor Signal A","Covers signal A of the steering wheel position sensor. Multi-track steering-angle sensors output several phase-shifted signals (A, B, C, D) so the ESC module can reconstruct absolute angle and detect a single bad channel by cross-checking. This code is set when channel A is out of range, open, shorted or does not agree with the other channels.",["Signal A open or unconnected","Steering angle sensor channel A failed","Harness or connector fault"],["Stability control disabled","ABS/ESC warning lamp on","Implausible steering angle reading"],2,2,["C0053","C0054","C0055"],"אות חיישן מצב גלגל הגה‏ A"],C0053:["Steering Wheel Position Sensor Signal B","Covers signal B of the steering wheel position sensor, the second of the multi-track channels the ESC module cross-checks against signals A, C and D to reconstruct absolute steering angle. This code is set when channel B is out of range, open, shorted or inconsistent with the other channels.",["Signal B open or unconnected","Steering angle sensor channel B failed","Harness or connector fault"],["Stability control disabled","ABS/ESC warning lamp on","Implausible steering angle reading"],2,2,["C0052","C0054","C0055"],"אות חיישן מצב גלגל הגה‏ B"],C0054:["Steering Wheel Position Sensor Signal C","Covers signal C of the steering wheel position sensor, the third multi-track channel the ESC module uses with signals A, B and D to reconstruct absolute steering angle and detect a bad channel by cross-checking. This code is set when channel C is out of range, open, shorted or inconsistent with the others.",["Signal C open or unconnected","Steering angle sensor channel C failed","Harness or connector fault"],["Stability control disabled","ABS/ESC warning lamp on","Implausible steering angle reading"],2,2,["C0052","C0053","C0055"],"אות חיישן מצב גלגל הגה‏ C"],C0055:["Steering Wheel Position Sensor Signal D","Covers signal D of the steering wheel position sensor, the fourth multi-track channel that completes the set with signals A, B and C. The ESC module reconstructs absolute steering angle from all channels and uses their agreement to detect a single faulty track; this code is set when channel D is out of range, open, shorted or inconsistent with the others.",["Signal D open or unconnected","Steering angle sensor channel D failed","Harness or connector fault"],["Stability control disabled","ABS/ESC warning lamp on","Implausible steering angle reading"],2,2,["C0052","C0053","C0054"],"אות חיישן מצב גלגל הגה‏ D"],C0056:["Left Rear Wheel Speed Sensor Circuit Intermittent","Covers an intermittent fault in the left rear wheel speed sensor circuit, where the signal is lost or corrupted only part of the time rather than permanently. The ABS/ESC module expects a clean pulse train proportional to wheel speed; a chafed wire that opens over bumps, a loose or corroded connector, a cracked sensor or a contaminated encoder ring can make the signal drop out briefly.",["Chafed wire or loose connector","Cracked sensor or contaminated encoder","Excessive or varying air gap"],["Intermittent ABS warning lamp","ABS/ESC drops out briefly","Speedometer flickers"],2,2,["C0060","C0066","C0050"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי שמאלי — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],C0060:["Right Rear Wheel Speed Sensor Circuit","Covers a general fault in the right rear wheel speed sensor circuit. The active sensor feeds rear wheel rotation to the ABS/ESC module for anti-lock, traction and stability control and electronic brake-force distribution; the module monitors the two-wire circuit for opens, shorts to power or ground, out-of-range current and a missing signal while the vehicle moves.",["Broken or chafed sensor harness wiring","Wheel speed sensor failed","Corroded sensor connector"],["ABS warning lamp on","ABS and stability control disabled","Speedometer may read erratically"],2,2,["C0050","C0066","C0056"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי ימני — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0061:["Lateral Acceleration Sensor","C0061 flags the lateral acceleration signal, which the stability module compares with the value expected from steering angle, yaw rate and speed. The code sets when the signal is out of range, frozen, noisy or implausible against the other inertial channels. FCA uses it on the 2022 Jeep Compass as C0061-29, signal invalid, together with C0062-29 and C0063-29;",["ABS module software fault (FCA bulletin 08-007-23)","Headlight leveling sensor position not learned after transport (Mazda)","Lateral accelerometer failed or out of range","Sensor cluster loose or shifted on its mount"],["Stability control disabled, ESC warning lamp on","MIL on together with ESC and parking brake warnings (FCA)","Headlight leveling warning flashes (Mazda)"],2,3,["C0062","C0063","C006A"],"חיישן תאוצה צידית"],C0062:["Longitudinal Acceleration Sensor","C0062 flags the longitudinal acceleration signal, the fore-aft reading used for hill hold, grade detection, all-wheel-drive torque split and brake distribution. The module checks it against the change in wheel speed, braking and throttle and against the other inertial channels, and stores the code for a value out of range, frozen, noisy or implausible.",["ABS or PCM software fault (FCA 08-007-23, 18-058-20)","Longitudinal accelerometer failed","Sensor cluster loose or shifted on its mount","Harness or connector fault"],["Stability and hill-hold functions disabled","ABS/ESC warning lamp on","AWD behaviour may change"],2,3,["C0061","C0063","C006A"],"חיישן תאוצה אורכית"],C0063:["Yaw Rate Sensor","C0063 flags the yaw rate signal, the rotation about the vertical axis that stability control compares with a reference built from steering angle, lateral acceleration and speed. A lasting gap means understeer or oversteer, so a corrupt signal would trigger wrong interventions; the module therefore stores the code and stops ESC when the value is out of range, frozen, noisy or implausible.",["ABS or driver assistance module software (FCA 08-007-23, 08-128-24)","Yaw rate gyro failed or out of range","Sensor cluster loose or shifted on its mount"],["Stability control disabled","ABS/ESC warning lamp on","Unexpected or absent stability intervention"],2,3,["C0061","C0062","C0064"],"חיישן קצב סבסוב"],C0064:["Roll Rate Sensor","C0064 covers the roll rate sensor, a gyroscope that measures rotation about the vehicle's longitudinal axis. NHTSA's brake safety study names roll rate among the vehicle dynamics inputs of the ABS/ESC module, and roll stability control uses it, mainly on tall vehicles, to spot the onset of a rollover and counter it with braking and torque reduction.",["Roll rate gyro failed or out of range","Loose or shifted sensor cluster mounting","Harness or connector fault"],["Roll stability control disabled","ABS/ESC warning lamp on","Rollover mitigation unavailable"],2,2,["C0063","C0065","C006A"],""],C0065:["Vertical Acceleration Sensor","C0065 covers the vertical acceleration sensor, which measures up-and-down acceleration of the body. Bosch's inertial measurement unit shows where it lives today: one housing measures the rates of yaw, pitch and roll plus vertical, longitudinal and lateral acceleration and serves several control systems at once.",["Vertical accelerometer failed","Loose or shifted sensor cluster mounting","Harness or connector fault"],["Stability or suspension functions disabled","ABS/ESC or suspension warning lamp on","Degraded rough-road handling control"],2,2,["C0064","C0063","C006A"],"חיישן תאוצה אנכית"],C0066:["Pitch Rate Sensor","Public SAE J2012 code lists still mark C0066 as ISO/SAE reserved, and no manufacturer documents the code in a retrievable bulletin or service text. One current code table assigns it to the pitch rate sensor, which fits its place between roll rate (C0064), vertical acceleration (C0065) and the yaw/longitudinal pair (C0069); the title follows that use.",["Pitch rate gyro failed, drifting or out of range","Sensor cluster loose or tilted on its mount","Harness or connector fault at the sensor cluster"],["ESC or stability warning lamp on","Rollover and stability functions reduced"],2,2,["C0064","C0065","C0063","C006A"],""],C0069:["Yaw Rate/Longitude Sensors","C0069 is a plausibility code for the yaw rate and longitudinal acceleration sensors taken together. When the vehicle brakes in a bend, yaw, longitudinal and lateral motion must stay in a physical relationship; if the two signals keep contradicting each other or the rest of the inertial set, one channel has drifted, both share a fault, or the cluster has shifted on its mount.",["One inertial channel drifted or biased","Sensor cluster shifted on its mount","Shared harness or connector fault"],["Stability control disabled","ABS/ESC warning lamp on","Inertial signals implausible together"],2,2,["C0063","C0062","C006A"],""],C006A:["Multi-axis Acceleration Sensor","C006A covers a combined multi-axis sensor that delivers several motion axes from one device, the integrated form of the separate lateral, longitudinal, vertical, yaw and roll sensors; NHTSA's brake study and Bosch's six-axis IMU describe such units. The module treats the device as a whole and sets C006A for an internal fault, a failed self-test, lost communication or values that disagree across the axes.",["ABS module software fault (FCA bulletin 08-061-20)","Internal sensor fault or failed self-test","Harness or connector fault"],["Stability and roll control disabled","ABS/ESC warning lamp on","Multiple inertial faults at once"],2,3,["C0061","C0063","C0069"],""],C006B:["Stability System Active Too Long","Set when the stability or traction control system has been intervening continuously for longer than the calibrated maximum. ESC and traction control are meant to act in short bursts; if the controller keeps modulating brakes or reducing torque beyond a time limit it concludes something is wrong, for example a persistently spinning wheel on ice, a dragging brake, a mismatched tyre or a sensor feeding a wrong signal,…",["Wheel spinning or slipping for a long time","Dragging brake or mismatched tyre","Wrong sensor input driving the intervention"],["Stability/traction control cuts out","ABS/ESC warning lamp on","Prolonged intervention before fault"],2,2,["C006C","C0084","C0073"],""],C006C:["Stability System","A general stability-system fault code covering the electronic stability control function as a whole rather than one named sensor or actuator. The ESC module sets it when an internal self-check fails, when the stability function cannot run because required inputs are missing or inconsistent, or when a system-level plausibility check is violated and no more specific code applies.",["Underlying sensor or actuator fault","Missing or inconsistent input data","Internal control module fault"],["Stability control disabled","ABS/ESC warning lamp on","Appears with companion DTCs"],2,2,["C006B","C0063","C0051"],"מערכת יציבות"],C0070:["Vehicle Speed Sensor Circuit","Covers the vehicle speed sensor circuit, the source of the overall road-speed signal used by the ABS/ESC module and shared with the speedometer, transmission and other systems. On many vehicles road speed is derived from the wheel speed sensors or a transmission output sensor; this code is set when that speed signal is open, shorted, out of range or implausible against the individual wheel speeds.",["Open or shorted speed signal wiring","Failed wheel or output speed sensor","Corroded or loose connector"],["Speedometer inaccurate or dead","Stability and speed functions disabled","Erratic transmission shifting"],2,2,["C0050","C0060","C0035"],"חיישן מהירות הרכב — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0071:["2/4 Wheel Drive Status Input","Covers the input that tells the ABS/ESC module whether the vehicle is in two- or four-wheel-drive mode. Because four-wheel drive links the axles and changes how wheel speeds relate, the stability and ABS strategy must know the current drive mode; this signal comes from the transfer-case switch, the drive-mode selector or a message from the drivetrain controller.",["Transfer-case or mode switch fault","Missing drive-mode message on the bus","Harness or connector fault"],["Stability or ABS strategy limited","ABS/ESC warning lamp on","Drive-mode display incorrect"],2,2,["C0090","C0095","C006C"],""],C0072:["Brake Temperature Too High","Set when the brake or stability module estimates that brake temperature has risen above a safe threshold. Few vehicles measure rotor temperature directly; most run a thermal model that integrates braking force, speed and time to estimate how hot the brakes are, and warn or adapt control when overheating is likely, for example on a long descent.",["Brakes overheated on a long descent","Dragging brake or stuck caliper","Implausible input to the thermal model"],["Brake temperature warning to driver","Reduced regenerative braking blend","Brake fade on long descents"],2,0,["C004F","C0021","C0082"],"טמפרטורת בלם — ערך גבוה מדי"],C0073:["Delivered Driving Torque","Covers the delivered-driving-torque signal that the engine or powertrain controller reports to the ABS/ESC module during traction and stability control. To limit wheel spin the stability controller asks the powertrain to reduce torque; it then needs confirmation of how much torque was actually delivered to close the loop.",["Lost or implausible torque message","Powertrain controller fault","Mismatched controller calibration"],["Traction and stability control limited","ABS/ESC warning lamp on","Appears with powertrain DTCs"],2,2,["C0074","C0076","C006B"],""],C0074:["Requested Driving Torque","Covers the requested-driving-torque signal that the ABS/ESC module sends to the powertrain controller during traction and stability control, the counterpart to the delivered-torque signal C0073. When a driven wheel spins the stability controller computes a torque-reduction request and transmits it;",["Fault on the torque request path","Stability or powertrain module fault","Mismatched controller calibration"],["Traction and stability control limited","ABS/ESC warning lamp on","Appears with powertrain DTCs"],2,2,["C0073","C0076","C006B"],""],C0075:["Brake Pedal Position Performance","A performance code for the brake pedal position input, set when the signal is present but behaves implausibly, for example it does not change as expected, lags, or disagrees with brake pressure and the switch. The stability and brake modules use pedal position to blend regenerative and friction braking and to arm or cancel driver-assist functions.",["Pedal/pressure sensor signal implausible","Pedal or switch out of adjustment","Harness or connector fault"],["Degraded regenerative braking blend","Driver-assist functions limited","ABS/ESC warning lamp on"],2,2,["C0042","C0024","C0082"],"מצב דוושת בלם — ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0076:["PWM for Traction Control","Covers the pulse-width-modulated signal used within the traction control interface, for example a PWM torque-request or status line exchanged between the stability and powertrain controllers or driving a traction-related actuator. The module monitors the PWM signal's duty cycle, frequency and presence and sets this code when it is missing, out of range or implausible.",["PWM signal missing or out of range","Open or shorted signal line","Sending or receiving module fault"],["Traction control limited","ABS/ESC warning lamp on","Appears with torque request DTCs"],2,2,["C0073","C0074","C0084"],""],C0077:["Low Tire Pressure","Covers a low-tire-pressure indication reaching the ABS/ESC or body module, typically from an indirect tyre-pressure monitoring system that infers pressure from wheel behaviour rather than from in-tyre sensors. An under-inflated tyre has a smaller rolling radius and turns faster, and its vibration spectrum shifts; the system detects this from the ABS wheel speed signals and raises a low-pressure warning.",["One or more tyres under-inflated","System not reset after inflation","TPMS threshold/software issue"],["Low tire pressure indicator on","Warning despite correct pressure","Requires reset after inflation"],1,0,["C0078","C0083","C0080"],""],C0078:["Tire Diameter","Covers a tyre-diameter fault or mismatch detected by the ABS/ESC or indirect-TPMS logic. The system learns the rolling diameter of each tyre from wheel speeds at known vehicle speed; a tyre that is a different size, badly worn, or a mismatched spare makes one wheel turn at a different rate, which the module flags as a diameter problem.",["Mismatched or wrong-size tyre fitted","Badly worn tyre changing rolling radius","Diameter not relearned after tyre change"],["TPMS or stability warning lamp on","Inaccurate speed or TPMS readings","Learn routine will not complete"],1,0,["C0077","C0080","C0083"],""],C0079:["Variable Effort Steering","Covers the variable-effort (speed-sensitive) power steering function, where steering assist is high at low speed for easy parking and reduced at high speed for stability. The ABS/ESC or steering module uses vehicle speed to command the assist level through a solenoid-controlled hydraulic valve or an electric power-steering actuator.",["Variable-effort valve or actuator fault","Missing or wrong vehicle speed input","Harness or connector fault"],["Steering effort fixed or abnormal","Steering warning lamp or message","Heavy steering at low speed"],2,0,["C0070","C0051","C0052"],"היגוי מאמץ משתנה"],C0080:["Wheel Speed Mismatch (Front Axle)","Set when the two front wheel speed signals disagree by more than the allowed amount under conditions where they should match, pointing to a wheel-speed or tyre problem rather than a single open circuit. The ABS/ESC module continuously compares left and right front speeds; a persistent mismatch on a straight road can mean a failing sensor, a damaged tone ring, a mismatched or badly worn tyre or uneven inflation.",["Mismatched, worn or unevenly inflated tyres","Failing sensor or damaged tone ring","Intermittent sensor wiring"],["ABS warning lamp on","Traction or stability control limited","Possible false low-pressure warning"],2,2,["C0081","C0078","C0077"],""],C0081:["ABS Malfunction Indicator","Covers the ABS malfunction indicator (warning lamp) itself as driven or monitored by the ABS/ESC module. The module commands the ABS lamp on for a fault and off when healthy, and monitors the output circuit; this code is set when the lamp circuit is open or shorted, the lamp does not respond, or the commanded and observed states disagree, for example a bulb-check failure or a bus message not reaching the cluster.",["Open or shorted indicator circuit","Lamp request not reaching the cluster","Failed indicator bulb or driver"],["ABS warning lamp stuck on or off","Failed lamp self-check","Driver loses ABS warning"],2,0,["C0082","C0086","C0050"],""],C0082:["Brake System Malfunction Indicator","Covers the brake system malfunction indicator (red brake warning lamp) as driven or monitored by the brake/stability module. The module commands this lamp for serious brake faults such as low fluid, pressure problems or a control fault, and monitors the output; this code is set when the lamp circuit is open or shorted, the lamp does not respond, or commanded and observed states disagree.",["Open or shorted indicator circuit","Lamp request not reaching the cluster","Failed indicator bulb or driver"],["Red brake lamp stuck on or off","Failed lamp self-check","Driver loses brake warning"],2,0,["C0081","C0049","C0072"],""],C0083:["Tire Pressure Monitor Malfunction Indicator","Covers the tyre-pressure-monitor indicator (TPMS lamp) as driven or monitored by the responsible module. Regulations distinguish a steady low-pressure warning from a flashing TPMS-malfunction indication; this code concerns the indicator path, set when the TPMS lamp circuit is open or shorted, the lamp does not respond, or the commanded and observed states disagree.",["Open or shorted indicator circuit","TPMS cannot monitor, requests fault lamp","Failed indicator bulb or driver"],["TPMS indicator stuck on or flashing","Failed lamp self-check","Loss of tyre pressure warning"],2,0,["C0077","C0078","C0082"],""],C0084:["Traction Active Indicator","Covers the traction-active indicator, the lamp that flashes to tell the driver traction control is currently intervening, as driven or monitored by the ABS/ESC module. The module flashes this lamp during a traction event and monitors the output circuit; this code is set when the indicator circuit is open or shorted, the lamp does not respond, or commanded and observed states disagree.",["Open or shorted indicator circuit","Lamp request not reaching the cluster","Failed indicator bulb or driver"],["Traction indicator stuck on or off","No feedback during traction events","Failed lamp self-check"],2,0,["C0085","C0089","C008A"],"חיווי פעיל אחיזה"],C0085:["Traction Disable Indicator","Covers the traction-disable indicator, the lamp that shows traction control has been switched off by the driver or by the system, as driven or monitored by the ABS/ESC module. The module lights this lamp when traction control is disabled and monitors the output; this code is set when the indicator circuit is open or shorted, the lamp does not respond, or commanded and observed states disagree.",["Open or shorted indicator circuit","Lamp request not reaching the cluster","Failed indicator bulb or driver"],["Traction-off indicator stuck on or off","No feedback when toggling traction control","Failed lamp self-check"],2,0,["C0084","C0089","C008A"],""],C0086:["Vehicle Dynamics Indicator","Covers the vehicle-dynamics indicator, the lamp that signals the status of the electronic stability / vehicle-dynamics control to the driver, as driven or monitored by the ESC module. The module lights or flashes this lamp for stability status and faults and monitors the output; this code is set when the indicator circuit is open or shorted, the lamp does not respond, or commanded and observed states disagree.",["Open or shorted indicator circuit","Lamp request not reaching the cluster","Failed indicator bulb or driver"],["Dynamics indicator stuck on or off","Loss of stability status feedback","Failed lamp self-check"],2,0,["C0081","C0082","C006C"],""],C0089:["TCS Disable Switch","Covers the driver switch that turns traction (or stability) control off, and its circuit to the ABS/ESC module. Pressing the switch tells the module to disable intervention and light the traction-off indicator; this code is set when the switch signal is stuck, implausible, or the circuit is open or shorted, for example a switch that reads permanently pressed or a broken wire.",["Switch stuck or reads permanently pressed","Open or shorted switch circuit","Corroded or loose connector"],["Traction control cannot be toggled","Traction-off indicator wrong","ABS/ESC warning lamp on"],1,0,["C008A","C0085","C0084"],""],C008A:["TCS Mode Control","Covers the traction-control mode selector and its input to the ABS/ESC module, used where the driver can choose among traction/terrain modes such as snow, sand, mud or sport that change the slip targets and intervention strategy. This code is set when the mode signal is stuck, implausible, out of range or the circuit is faulty, so the module cannot tell which mode is selected.",["Mode selector signal stuck or implausible","Open or shorted selector circuit","Corroded or loose connector"],["Terrain/traction mode cannot be selected","System defaults to a safe mode","ABS/ESC warning lamp on"],1,0,["C0089","C0071","C0084"],""],C0090:["4WD/AWD Power Transfer Unit Actuator","Covers the actuator that engages or modulates the power transfer unit (transfer case / front coupling) in a four- or all-wheel-drive system. On demand the controller drives this actuator, typically an electric motor or an electromagnetic/electro-hydraulic clutch operator, to send torque to the secondary axle.",["PTU actuator motor or coil failed","Open or shorted actuator circuit","Binding or worn transfer mechanism"],["AWD/4WD warning lamp on","Stuck in one drive mode or 2WD default","Reduced traction on loose surfaces"],4,2,["C0091","C0092","C0093"],""],C0091:["4WD/AWD Power Transfer Unit Position Sensor A","Covers position sensor A of the power transfer unit actuator, which reports how far the transfer-case or coupling actuator has moved so the controller can close the loop on torque split or mode. The controller commands the actuator and reads this sensor to confirm the achieved position; this code is set when the sensor signal is out of range, open, shorted or implausible against the commanded or expected position.",["Position sensor A failed or out of range","Harness or connector fault","Actuator not reaching expected position"],["AWD/4WD warning lamp on","Default torque split or 2WD mode","Inconsistent AWD engagement"],4,2,["C0090","C0092","C0093"],""],C0092:["4WD/AWD Power Transfer Unit Position Sensor B","Covers position sensor B of the power transfer unit actuator, the redundant or second-channel position feedback the controller cross-checks against sensor A (C0091). Dual position sensors let the controller detect a single faulty channel and keep metering the AWD coupling safely. This code is set when sensor B is out of range, open, shorted or does not track sensor A within tolerance.",["Position sensor B failed or out of range","Sensor A/B signals do not correlate","Harness or connector fault"],["AWD/4WD warning lamp on","Default torque split or 2WD mode","Inconsistent AWD engagement"],4,2,["C0091","C0090","C0093"],""],C0093:["4WD/AWD Power Transfer Unit Temperature Sensor","Covers the temperature sensor of the power transfer unit, which lets the controller protect the AWD clutch from overheating. Sustained torque transfer, for example prolonged slip or towing, heats the clutch pack and its fluid; the controller reads this sensor and reduces or opens the coupling when temperature climbs too high. This code is set when the sensor signal is out of range, open, shorted or implausible.",["Temperature sensor out of range or failed","Harness or connector fault","Genuine clutch overheating event"],["AWD/4WD warning lamp on","Reduced AWD engagement for protection","No thermal protection of the coupling"],4,2,["C0090","C0094","C0091"],""],C0094:["4WD/AWD Rear Differential Unit Temperature Sensor","Covers the temperature sensor of the rear differential unit in an all-wheel-drive system, used to protect the rear drive module and its electronically controlled coupling from overheating. Prolonged torque transfer to the rear axle heats the clutch and fluid; the controller reads this sensor and limits engagement when it gets too hot.",["Temperature sensor out of range or failed","Harness or connector fault","Genuine rear unit overheating event"],["AWD/4WD warning lamp on","Reduced rear-axle engagement for protection","No thermal protection of the rear unit"],4,2,["C0093","C0095","C0096"],"חיישן טמפרטורת יחידת דיפרנציאל אחורי הנעה כפולה"],C0095:["4WD/AWD Rear Differential Unit Actuator A","Covers actuator A of the rear differential unit, which engages or modulates the electronically controlled rear coupling or locking differential in an all-wheel-drive system. The controller drives this actuator, typically a motor-operated clutch operator or an electromagnetic coil, to send or lock torque at the rear axle on demand.",["Rear coupling actuator A failed","Open or shorted actuator circuit","Binding or worn rear coupling"],["AWD/4WD warning lamp on","Rear axle stuck engaged or open","Reduced traction on loose surfaces"],4,2,["C0096","C0097","C0094"],"מפעיל יחידת דיפרנציאל אחורי הנעה כפולה‏ A"],C0096:["4WD/AWD Rear Differential Unit Actuator A Data","Covers the data or feedback associated with rear differential actuator A (C0095), as opposed to a plain circuit fault. Where C0095 flags the drive circuit, this code is set when the actuator's reported data, its position, current or status feedback, is missing, out of range or implausible against the command, so the controller cannot confirm what the actuator is doing.",["Actuator feedback data missing or implausible","Communication fault with the rear module","Actuator not responding as reported"],["AWD/4WD warning lamp on","Rear engagement unconfirmed","Default safe AWD state"],4,2,["C0095","C0097","C0098"],"נתוני מפעיל יחידת דיפרנציאל אחורי הנעה כפולה‏ A"],C0097:["4WD/AWD Rear Differential Unit Actuator B","Covers actuator B of the rear differential unit, the second actuator used on rear drive modules that control two functions, for example torque transfer and a limited-slip or locking element, or that use two coils for redundancy. The controller drives this actuator to engage or modulate the rear coupling; this code is set when the actuator B circuit is open, shorted, out of range or the actuator does not respond.",["Rear coupling actuator B failed","Open or shorted actuator circuit","Binding or worn rear coupling"],["AWD/4WD warning lamp on","Limited-slip or lock function lost","Reduced traction or torque vectoring"],4,2,["C0098","C0095","C0096"],"מפעיל יחידת דיפרנציאל אחורי הנעה כפולה‏ B"],C0098:["4WD/AWD Rear Differential Unit Actuator B Data","Covers the data or feedback associated with rear differential actuator B (C0097), as opposed to a plain circuit fault. Where C0097 flags the drive circuit, this code is set when actuator B's reported data, its position, current or status feedback, is missing, out of range or implausible against the command, so the controller cannot confirm what the actuator is doing.",["Actuator feedback data missing or implausible","Communication fault with the rear module","Actuator not responding as reported"],["AWD/4WD warning lamp on","Rear function engagement unconfirmed","Default safe AWD state"],4,2,["C0097","C0095","C0096"],"נתוני מפעיל יחידת דיפרנציאל אחורי הנעה כפולה‏ B"],C0099:["4WD/AWD Rear Differential Unit Actuator A Position Sensor A","The title gives actuator A of the rear differential unit three position channels, A to C. That layout matches the way brushless actuator motors track their rotor: three Hall elements on the stator read a magnet on the rotor, and their combined states step the motor through six commutation phases. C0099 concerns channel A alone.",["Open or grounded signal wire of channel A between actuator and module","Corroded or loose connector at the rear drive unit","Failed Hall element A inside the actuator motor","Missing sensor supply or ground from the module"],["AWD/4WD warning lamp or message in the cluster","Rear axle no longer driven, front-wheel drive only","Reduced traction on slippery surfaces"],3,2,["C009A","C009B","C009C","C0095","C009D"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל יחידת דיפרנציאל אחורי הנעה כפולה‏ A A"],C009A:["4WD/AWD Rear Differential Unit Actuator A Position Sensor B","Channel B is the second of the three position signals that actuator A of the rear differential unit reports to its control module. This code points at that one line or element, while channels A and C still deliver plausible edges.",["Damaged or chafed signal wire of channel B","Loose or spread terminal for channel B in the actuator connector","Hall element B in the actuator motor defective"],["AWD warning with the vehicle driving on the front axle only","Fault may come and go with temperature or vibration"],3,2,["C0099","C009B","C009C","C009E"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל יחידת דיפרנציאל אחורי הנעה כפולה‏ A B"],C009B:["4WD/AWD Rear Differential Unit Actuator A Position Sensor C","C009B covers the third position channel, C, of actuator A in the rear differential unit. With A and B intact the module can still see motion, so a fault on C is caught by comparing edges: a Woodward patent identifies the failed sensor as the one whose output stays constant between two invalid state combinations, roughly one electrical revolution apart, and then keeps the motor running on two sensors with a…",["Open circuit or short on the channel C signal line","Hall element C inside the actuator motor failed","Moisture in the actuator connector at the rear axle"],["AWD/4WD fault message","All-wheel drive switched off for the rest of the trip"],3,2,["C0099","C009A","C009C","C009F"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל יחידת דיפרנציאל אחורי הנעה כפולה‏ A C"],C009C:["4WD/AWD Rear Differential Unit Actuator A Position Sensor Correlation","Each of the three position channels of actuator A may look electrically fine, yet together they make no sense: a combination that cannot occur, a sequence that skips states or runs against the commanded direction. With 120-degree spacing the patterns 000 and 111 are invalid, as a Woodward patent notes.",["Rear drive unit connector not fully seated or loose pins (Ford C413)","Poor shared sensor ground or supply corrupting all three channels","Internal sensor or magnet fault in the rear drive unit motor"],["4WD Malfunction message and AWD switched off","Service AdvanceTrac, hill start assist or pre-collision assist unavailable (Ford)","Reduced Power message"],2,2,["C0099","C009A","C009B","C00A0","C0095"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל יחידת דיפרנציאל אחורי הנעה כפולה‏ A — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],C009D:["4WD/AWD Rear Differential Unit Actuator B Position Sensor A","Actuator B exists only on rear units with a second controlled element, for instance twin-clutch modules that apply torque to each rear wheel on its own, or a rear axle with an extra disconnect. GKN describes a separate actuator controller managing such twin-clutch actuation, adapting to clutch temperature and wear.",["Wiring fault on channel A of actuator B","Poor contact in the actuator B connector","Hall element A in actuator B failed"],["AWD warning, torque vectoring or locking function unavailable","Vehicle may push wide in corners where it normally rotates"],3,2,["C009E","C009F","C00A0","C0097","C0099"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל יחידת דיפרנציאל אחורי הנעה כפולה‏ B A"],C009E:["4WD/AWD Rear Differential Unit Actuator B Position Sensor B","Middle channel B of the second rear-unit actuator is reported here. It belongs to designs with two independently controlled elements; GKN's Twinster, used on the Focus RS rear drive module, can send torque to either rear wheel separately through two wet clutches. A fault in channel B of actuator B is typically an interrupted, grounded or frozen signal while channels A and C still switch.",["Channel B signal of actuator B interrupted or grounded","Harness chafed near the rear axle or exhaust heat shield","Internal sensor failure in actuator B"],["AWD fault message, one rear wheel no longer driven actively","Drift or sport drive modes unavailable"],3,2,["C009D","C009F","C00A0","C009A"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל יחידת דיפרנציאל אחורי הנעה כפולה‏ B B"],C009F:["4WD/AWD Rear Differential Unit Actuator B Position Sensor C","Third position channel C of actuator B in the rear differential unit is the subject of this code. Its absence is noticed because the remaining channels A and B still produce transitions that C should follow. Woodward's patent shows the method: after an invalid combination the controller waits for the next one, and the sensor whose output did not move in between is the failed one;",["Open or high-resistance channel C line of actuator B","Hall element C of actuator B defective","Fault in electronics integrated in the actuator motor"],["AWD warning lamp","Rear torque split or locking function deactivated"],3,2,["C009D","C009E","C00A0","C009B"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל יחידת דיפרנציאל אחורי הנעה כפולה‏ B C"],C00A0:["4WD/AWD Rear Differential Unit Actuator B Position Sensor Correlation","C00A0 is the plausibility check across all three position channels of actuator B. Each line may be intact, but the pattern they form is impossible, out of sequence or contradicts the commanded movement, so the controller can no longer trust where the second actuator stands. Woodward lists 000 and 111 as illegal states for 120-degree spacing and 101 or 010 for 60-degree spacing.",["Shared sensor ground or supply of actuator B faulty","Actuator B connector not fully latched","Rotor magnet or sensor carrier shifted inside actuator B"],["AWD fault message with rear torque control switched off","Possible loss of related assist functions shown in the cluster"],3,2,["C009D","C009E","C009F","C009C","C0097"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל יחידת דיפרנציאל אחורי הנעה כפולה‏ B — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],C00A1:["Driveline Control Module","This umbrella code concerns the driveline control module itself, often called AWD or 4WD module, not one of its outputs or sensors. It covers internal faults such as memory or processor errors, a missing or poor supply and ground, or software and configuration problems that stop the module from controlling clutches, transfer case or disconnects.",["Loose or corroded module ground (Ford G239 on 2023 Super Duty)","Low battery voltage or poor supply to the module","Module software or configuration fault, update or reprogramming needed","Internal failure of the driveline control module"],["Four-wheel drive inoperative","4WD/AWD warning or service message","Further driveline codes or lost communication with the module"],2,2,["C00A2","C00A3","C00A4","C00A5","U041E"],""],C00A2:["Driveline Control Module Power Transfer Unit Control Circuit Driver","The power transfer unit sits at the front transaxle of a front-based AWD car and, on disconnecting systems, can uncouple the propshaft. AAM's EcoTrac, introduced on the 2014 Jeep Cherokee, separates the driveline at both the PTU and the rear module under command of its own control unit.",["Short to ground or battery on the PTU actuator circuit","PTU actuator coil or motor open or internally shorted","Damaged output stage inside the driveline module"],["AWD unavailable, vehicle stays in front-wheel drive","AWD warning lamp or message"],3,2,["C00A1","C00A3","C00A5","C0631"],""],C00A3:["Driveline Control Module Rear Differential Unit A Control Circuit Driver","C00A3 points to the driver stage inside the driveline module that powers actuator A of the rear differential unit, not to the actuator itself. The module's own transistor monitoring reports something wrong at that output.",["Short to ground or battery in the actuator A supply lines","Actuator A motor or coil drawing excessive current (binding, winding short)","Output stage in the module overheated or defective"],["Rear clutch released, AWD inactive","AWD warning in the instrument cluster"],3,2,["C00A1","C00A4","C0095","C0096"],""],C00A4:["Driveline Control Module Rear Differential Unit B Control Circuit Driver","Where a rear unit carries a second actuator, for example the second clutch of a twin-clutch module that can drive each rear wheel on its own, the driveline module needs a second output stage, and C00A4 reports a fault in that one.",["Phase or supply line of actuator B shorted to ground or battery","Winding fault or blocked rotor in actuator B causing overcurrent","Failed output stage B in the module"],["AWD or torque vectoring warning","One rear clutch or locking function inactive"],3,2,["C00A1","C00A3","C0097","C0098"],""],C00A5:["Driveline Control Module Transfer Case Unit Control Circuit Driver","C00A5 concerns the output stage in the driveline module that powers the transfer case actuator, typically a DC gearmotor that shifts range and mode or presses a multi-plate clutch. Bosch describes such a transfer case clutch driven by a DC motor with worm gear through an H-bridge, with motor speed, worm wheel position and motor current measured;",["Shorted transfer case motor wiring or connector","Binding or worn transfer case motor causing overcurrent","Defective H-bridge in the driveline module"],["4WD/AWD cannot be engaged or range shift refused","4WD service warning in the cluster"],3,2,["C00A1","C00A6","C00A7","C00A8"],""],C00A6:["4WD/AWD Transfer Case Unit Actuator","C00A6 is the general code for the transfer case actuator, the motor unit that presses the transfer case clutch or moves its shift mechanism. Ford uses it with many failure-type suffixes. SSM 49669 covers 2020–2021 Explorer and Aviator AWD with C00A6:07, :18, :19, :4B, :66, :71, :74 or :99 and an AWD lamp, noting that the clutch actuator is not always at fault and that revised pinpoint tests should be followed.",["Harness to the actuator motor chafed on the underbody heat shield","Front axle disconnect actuator/intermediate shaft fault (Ford Explorer/Aviator)","Transfer case clutch actuator motor worn or seized","Actuator overheated from heavy use"],["Wrench (powertrain malfunction) indicator or AWD lamp (Ford)","4WD Fault Service Required message","AWD function lost"],3,2,["C00A5","C00A7","C00A8","C0631","C0633"],"מפעיל יחידת תיבת העברה הנעה כפולה"],C00A7:["4WD/AWD Transfer Case Unit Actuator Position Sensor A","Position sensor A reports where the transfer case actuator, and thus the range or mode mechanism, currently stands. Magna patents a linear Hall sensor bolted from outside into the case, reading a stepped sector plate (four positions over about 60 degrees) or a plate on the range fork, with a duty-cycle output.",["Transfer case shift motor connector not fully seated (Stellantis 2023)","Harness chafed where it routes to the actuator motor (Ford)","Position sensor A in the actuator failed"],["MIL on (Stellantis) or wrench indicator (Ford)","4WD Service light or 4WD Fault Service Required message","4WD modes cannot be selected"],2,3,["C00A8","C00A6","C00A5","U0403"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל יחידת תיבת העברה הנעה כפולה‏ A"],C00A8:["4WD/AWD Transfer Case Unit Actuator Position Sensor B","C00A8 is the second position signal of the transfer case actuator. Whether B is a redundant copy of A or tracks a different part, the motor or the cam, is not published by any maker; BorgWarner, for example, puts a contact probe on the shift drum cam instead of the motor because a torsion spring sits in between, and reads five plateaus from 2WD high to 4WD low.",["Shift motor connector not latched (Stellantis 2023)","Harness damage at the heat shield near the transfer case (Ford)","Position sensor B defective"],["MIL illuminated (Stellantis), wrench indicator (Ford)","4WD Service light, four-wheel drive not available"],2,3,["C00A7","C00A6","C00A5","U0403"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל יחידת תיבת העברה הנעה כפולה‏ B"],C0110:["ABS Pump Motor Circuit Malfunction","C0110 does not appear in the accessible J2012 code tables; it is documented by General Motors, whose brake modules use it for the electric motor of the ABS return pump. In the Saab 9-5 (2010–2011) and 9-4X service data the motor sits in the brake pressure modulator valve while its relay is inside the EBCM;",["Open or high-resistance pump motor supply or ground (fuse, connector, ground point)","Seized or worn pump motor in the modulator valve assembly","Faulty pump motor relay inside the brake control module"],["ABS and red brake warning lamps on","Traction and stability control indicator on, systems disabled","No ABS intervention on slippery surfaces"],3,2,["C0267","C052C","C0121","C0265"],"מנוע משאבת ABS — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0111:["ABS Activation Excessively Long","No accessible J2012 table, manufacturer index or NHTSA bulletin lists C0111, so the code cannot be traced to any published application. The title describes a plausibility monitor rather than a wiring fault: the controller notices that an anti-lock intervention, or one of its pressure-release phases, lasts longer than makes physical sense. Bosch patented such a guard in 1988.",["Spare wheel, mixed tyre sizes or very uneven tyre pressures","Weak or disturbed wheel speed signal (air gap, dirty sensor ring)","Sluggish valve in the hydraulic unit prolonging a control phase"],["ABS warning lamp on, anti-lock function switched off","Pedal pulsing or long release phases during gentle braking"],2,2,["C0112","C0080","C0110"],""],C0112:["ABS Activation Frequency Too High","C0112 is not found in any accessible J2012 table or in the NHTSA bulletin index, and no manufacturer documents it publicly. Read literally, the title flags anti-lock control that starts again and again although the wheel situation does not justify it, as opposed to one overlong event (C0111). Nissan and Unisia patented a counter that sums pressure-release time across successive control cycles;",["Tyre or wheel of the wrong rolling circumference","Cracked, loose or contaminated sensor ring","Interference or intermittent contact on a wheel speed sensor circuit"],["ABS kicks in at low speed or on dry road without reason","ABS warning lamp on after repeated interventions"],2,2,["C0111","C0080","C0060"],""],C0121:["Valve Relay Circuit Malfunction","C0121 is absent from the accessible J2012 lists. GM includes it in the chassis code keyword list of bulletin PIP5094 (2013), and AA1Car's ABS code table, which follows GM numbering, names it Valve Relay Circuit Malfunction. This relay passes battery voltage to all solenoid valves of the hydraulic unit, while the controller grounds each valve on its own.",["Blown fuse or poor battery feed to the valve relay","Corroded or loose ground of the brake control module","Valve relay contact sticking or burnt (relay often inside the module)"],["ABS warning lamp on, often together with traction or stability lamp","No anti-lock action, wheels can lock under hard braking"],3,2,["C0225","C0220","C053B","C0110"],"ממסר שסתום — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0128:["Low Brake Fluid Indicated","C0128 is not part of the accessible J2012 tables. GM lists it among its chassis codes in bulletin PIP5094, and the GM-based ABS table published by AA1Car words it Low Brake Fluid Circuit Low. The input comes from the level switch in the master cylinder reservoir: a float carrying a magnet closes a reed contact once the fluid drops, as patents from ITT and from Nabco/Nissan show.",["Fluid level genuinely low from pad wear or a leak","Stuck float or shorted reed switch in the reservoir","Chafed switch wiring shorted to ground"],["Red brake warning lamp or low fluid message","Possibly longer pedal travel if fluid is really missing"],1,0,["C0201"],""],C0131:["Master Cylinder Pressure Sensor Range/Performance","C0131 is not in the accessible J2012 lists; GM and Saab use it for the brake pressure sensor that measures master cylinder pressure inside the modulator. In the Saab 9-5 up to 2010 a signal above 4.75 V or under 0.25 V lasting 0.1 s, or a supply outside 4.4–5.6 V, sets it and ABS, TCS and ESP go out of service.",["Brake pressure sensor in the modulator faulty or out of calibration","Shipping material left on the sensor after modulator replacement (GM)","Fault on the 5 V reference or signal circuit of the sensor","Incorrect brake pedal signal used for the plausibility check"],["Traction/stability control warning on, systems switched off","On some models ABS lamp on as well"],2,2,["C0044","C053D","C0540","C0161"],"חיישן לחץ משאבת בלם ראשית — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0136:["Stop Lamp Switch Circuit","No public J2012 list, NHTSA bulletin or manufacturer table carries C0136, so it cannot be matched to a vehicle. Its title is word for word that of C0205, and at GM the brake switch input of ABS/TCS modules is C0161; which number a given car uses can only come from its own service data. The function itself is well described.",["Brake light switch misadjusted, worn or sticking","Open or short in the switch circuit or connector","Blown stop lamp fuse"],["Stop lamps stay on or do not work","Cruise control will not engage or cancels","ABS or stability warning lamp may come on"],1,0,["C0205","C0161","C0040"],"מתג נורת עצירה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0141:["Left Front ABS Inlet Solenoid Circuit","C0141 is not listed in the accessible J2012 tables. Saab documents it for the Bosch 5.3 TC/ABS of the 9-3 and 9-5 from 1998 and for the later 9-5 ESP as the left pressure-increase valve, kept apart from the wheel valve group code C2450; GM's chassis keyword list (PIP5094) includes it, and AA1Car's GM-based table calls it Left TCS Solenoid #1.",["Open or shorted coil of the left pressure-increase valve","Poor contact between control unit and valve block","Failed valve driver in the control module"],["ABS, brake and central warning lamps on","TCS/ESP off indicator lit, no ABS, TCS or ESP function"],3,2,["C0146","C0151","C0200"],"סולנואיד כניסת ABS קדמי שמאלי — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0146:["Left Front ABS Outlet Solenoid Circuit","Like its neighbours, C0146 is missing from the accessible J2012 tables and is documented only in Saab and GM material. Saab's 9-3/9-5 data for the Bosch 5.3 TC/ABS name it the left pressure-reduction valve, the ESP version of the 9-5 calls it the left pressure relief valve; the GM keyword list PIP5094 includes the number and AA1Car's GM-based table labels it Left TCS Solenoid #2.",["Open or shorted coil of the left pressure-reduction valve","Control module fault (Saab replaces the control module after checks)","Weak supply or ground to the brake control unit"],["Several brake-related warning lamps on together","ABS, traction and stability control unavailable"],3,2,["C0141","C0156","C0200"],"סולנואיד יציאת ABS קדמי שמאלי — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0148:["Right Front ABS Outlet Solenoid B Circuit Malfunction","C0148 is listed neither in the publicly available J2012 tables nor in maker indexes or NHTSA bulletins, so what the letter B stands for cannot be verified. The title suggests a second release solenoid for the right front wheel, as some hydraulic units pair two valves per channel. In any ABS unit the outlet side lets fluid escape from the caliper so the wheel can spin up again.",["Solenoid coil open, shorted or out of resistance range","Corroded contact between coil and control module","Failed output stage in the ABS module"],["ABS warning lamp on immediately after key-on","Anti-lock and related functions switched off"],3,2,["C0156","C0153","C0203"],"סולנואיד יציאת ABS קדמי ימני‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0151:["Right Front ABS Inlet Solenoid Circuit","C0151 mirrors C0141 on the right side and, like it, is not in the accessible J2012 tables. Saab's 9-3 and 9-5 workshop pages for the Bosch 5.3 TC/ABS and for the 9-5 ESP define it as the right pressure-increase valve, separate from the right front wheel valve code C2455; GM's PIP5094 keyword list carries it, and AA1Car's GM-based table reads Right TCS Solenoid #1.",["Defective coil of the right pressure-increase valve","Contact fault at the module-to-valve-block interface","Valve driver fault in the brake control module"],["Brake, ABS and central warning lamps on","No traction control when a front wheel spins"],3,2,["C0156","C0141","C0203"],"סולנואיד כניסת ABS קדמי ימני — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0153:["Right Front ABS Inlet Solenoid B Circuit Malfunction","C0153 cannot be found in any accessible J2012 list, NHTSA bulletin or manufacturer table; neither the code nor its B suffix is publicly documented. By title it concerns a second inlet solenoid for the right front wheel. Inlet valves are open at rest and close to hold caliper pressure while the module decides whether to release or rebuild it.",["Defective inlet solenoid coil","Poor plug contact between coil and module","Internal fault in the ABS control module"],["ABS lamp on, anti-lock unavailable","Stability control may also be switched off"],3,2,["C0151","C0148","C0203"],"סולנואיד כניסת ABS קדמי ימני‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0156:["Right Front ABS Outlet Solenoid Circuit","C0156 completes the Saab/GM group of four and is likewise absent from the accessible J2012 tables. Saab lists it as the right pressure-reduction valve for the 9-3/9-5 with Bosch 5.3 traction control and as the right pressure relief valve in the 9-5 ESP; GM's PIP5094 keyword list names the code, and AA1Car's GM-based table gives Right TCS Solenoid #2.",["Open or shorted coil of the right pressure-reduction valve","Fault inside the control unit carrying the valve coils","Moisture or corrosion at the control unit connector"],["ABS, brake and TCS/ESP OFF lamps on","Wheels may lock under emergency braking"],3,2,["C0151","C0146","C0203"],"סולנואיד יציאת ABS קדמי ימני — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0158:["Left Rear ABS Inlet Solenoid Circuit Malfunction","C0158 is publicly undocumented: it appears in no accessible J2012 table, NHTSA bulletin or manufacturer index. Saab, for example, reports the rear left valve group under C2415 instead. The title points to the electrical circuit of the inlet solenoid for the left rear brake. That valve stays open during normal braking and closes when the rear wheel starts to lock, trapping pressure in the caliper.",["Rear left inlet coil open, shorted or with wrong resistance","Corrosion at the hydraulic unit connector","Failed output stage in the control module"],["ABS warning lamp on, anti-lock switched off","Rear wheels can lock under hard braking"],3,2,["C0163","C0206"],"סולנואיד כניסת ABS אחורי שמאלי — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0161:["ABS/TCS Brake Switch Circuit","C0161 is outside the accessible J2012 tables but well documented at GM. Service data for the later Saab 9-5 and the 9-4X define it as an implausible ABS brake switch signal: the EBCM receives the pedal-applied message from the body module and compares it with brake pressure and vehicle motion.",["Brake pedal position sensor or switch out of adjustment","Loose or backed-out terminal in the pedal sensor wiring (GM X205)","Brake applied while accelerating (left-foot braking)","Brake pressure sensor reading that contradicts the pedal signal"],["Service stability or traction message","Cruise control or brake lights may misbehave","Hill start assist unavailable"],1,0,["C0136","C0205","C0131"],""],C0163:["Left Rear ABS Outlet Solenoid Circuit Malfunction","None of the reachable J2012 lists, maker indexes or NHTSA bulletins mention C0163, so its use cannot be shown for any vehicle. The title names the outlet solenoid of the left rear brake, the valve that opens during anti-lock control to dump caliper pressure toward the return pump and lets the wheel recover. If it cannot open, the rear wheel may lock;",["Rear left outlet coil open or shorted","Poor contact at the hydraulic unit connector","Outlet valve mechanically stuck by contaminated fluid"],["ABS warning lamp on","Unstable rear axle under hard braking without ABS"],3,2,["C0158","C0206"],"סולנואיד יציאת ABS אחורי שמאלי — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0168:["Right Rear ABS Inlet Solenoid Circuit Malfunction","C0168 has no public trace: it is missing from the accessible J2012 tables, from the NHTSA bulletin index and from the manufacturer pages checked, where Saab for instance uses C2485 for the rear right valves. Taken at face value it covers the inlet solenoid of the right rear brake, which isolates that caliper from master cylinder pressure while the module regulates the wheel.",["Open winding in the rear right inlet coil","Short between coil and housing","Corroded plug at the valve block"],["ABS lamp on, often directly at key-on","No anti-lock control on any wheel"],3,2,["C0173","C0209"],"סולנואיד כניסת ABS אחורי ימני — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0173:["Right Rear ABS Outlet Solenoid Circuit Malfunction","No accessible J2012 list, maker index or NHTSA bulletin contains C0173, so the code cannot be tied to any vehicle; Saab, for instance, reports a fault in either valve of the right rear wheel as C2485. By its title it covers the release valve of the right rear brake.",["Open or shorted coil of the right rear outlet valve","Corroded or loose contact between valve block and control module","Faulty valve driver stage inside the control module"],["ABS and brake warning lamps on, ABS/TCS/ESC switched off","Right rear wheel may lock under hard braking"],3,2,["C0168","C0209","C0163"],"סולנואיד יציאת ABS אחורי ימני — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0185:["Lateral Acceleration Sensor Range/Performance","C0185 is missing from the accessible J2012 lists and from the NHTSA bulletin index, and no maker documents it, so it is not publicly verifiable; its title is shared with C0499. It describes a lateral acceleration signal that is electrically intact but does not fit the motion of the car.",["Sensor offset drifted or calibration not learned after replacement","Sensor or module loose or mounted at the wrong angle","Implausible comparison signal (steering angle, wheel speeds)"],["Stability control warning lamp on, ESC switched off","Unwanted stability interventions when cornering"],2,2,["C0186","C0499","C0196"],"חיישן תאוצה צידית — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0186:["Lateral Acceleration Sensor Circuit","C0186 lies outside the publicly available J2012 tables but is firmly established at GM and Saab for the lateral accelerometer. On Saab 9-5 models through 2010 the ESP module sets it when the 0–5 V signal leaves the 0.25–4.75 V band for over 0.1 s or makes no sense; at standstill the reading should be close to 0 m/s².",["Faulty yaw/lateral (multi-axis) sensor module","Corroded connector or terminals in the sensor or bus wiring","Outdated software in the module that hosts the sensor (e.g. airbag module)"],["Service StabiliTrak / ESP OFF message or lamp","Traction and stability control unavailable","Further chassis codes (C0196, C0287, U-codes) stored"],2,2,["C0185","C0498","C0196"],"חיישן תאוצה צידית — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0196:["Yaw Rate Sensor Circuit","C0196 is absent from the accessible J2012 lists, yet it is the yaw rate code of GM and Saab and is also used by Karma. The Saab 9-5 sets it when the sensor output leaves 0.25–4.75 V for longer than 0.1 s or its 2.1–2.9 V reference strays for 0.2 s; GM's multi-axis sensor reports 00 for a faulty signal and 5A when offset or plausibility against lateral acceleration, steering angle and speed fail.",["Code set during transport or flat towing while modules were awake","Faulty or unlearned yaw rate / multi-axis sensor","Signal spikes from body vibration, stone impacts or loose mounting","Corroded connector or CAN wiring fault"],["Service StabiliTrak message, traction/ABS or ESP OFF lamp","Stability control and hill start assist disabled","Red brake lamp on in some vehicles"],2,2,["C0186","C0496","C0497","C0288"],"חיישן קצב סבסוב — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0200:["ABS Solenoid Valve Front Left Circuit","Neither the reachable J2012 tables nor NHTSA's bulletin index nor the manufacturer indexes checked contain C0200, so no published vehicle is known to use it. Its title, a circuit fault of the front left ABS solenoid valves, matches what Saab records as C2450 on 9-5 cars equipped with Bosch 5.3 TC/ABS.",["Open or shorted coil of a front left valve","Poor contact between valve coils and control module (solder joint, contact strip)","Faulty valve driver in the control module"],["ABS warning lamp on from key-on, ABS inactive","Traction and stability control also switched off"],3,2,["C0203","C0141","C0146"],"שמאלי קדמי שסתום סולנואיד ABS — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0201:["Brake Fluid Level Switch Circuit","Searches of J2012 tables, NHTSA bulletins and maker indexes found no trace of C0201, so no vehicle use can be shown; GM files its low-fluid input under C0128. The title concerns the wiring of the float switch fitted to the master cylinder reservoir.",["Corroded or loose connector at the reservoir cap or switch","Level switch shorted or open internally, float stuck","Chafed wiring between switch and module","Actually low fluid from worn pads or a leak"],["Red brake warning lamp on or flickering","Low-fluid message although the reservoir is full"],1,0,["C0128","C0049","C004B"],"מתג מפלס נוזל בלם — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0202:["Brake Pedal Position Sensor","No accessible J2012 list, NHTSA bulletin or maker index mentions C0202; the code is publicly unverifiable, and C0230 carries an almost identical title. A brake pedal position sensor reports how far the pedal moves instead of a mere on/off state. GM patented a resistive design with two outputs: one goes to the engine module for diagnosis, the other to the brake module, which uses it to release the shift interlock.",["Worn, misadjusted or not relearned pedal position sensor","Loose or corroded connector at the pedal","Pedal bracket or return spring binding"],["Brake or stability warning lamp on","Shift lever cannot be moved out of park, cruise control inactive"],2,0,["C0230","C0042","C0075"],"חיישן מצב דוושת בלם"],C0203:["ABS Solenoid Valve Front Right Circuit","C0203 has no public trace: neither the accessible J2012 lists nor the NHTSA bulletins or maker indexes include it. Read literally it is the front right counterpart of C0200; Saab's 9-5 fitted with the Bosch 5.3 traction/ABS unit reports this case as C2455.",["Open or shorted coil of a front right valve","Poor contact between control module and valve block","Faulty valve driver in the control module"],["ABS lamp on, anti-lock function off","Front right wheel can lock under hard braking"],3,2,["C0200","C0151","C0156"],"ימני קדמי שסתום סולנואיד ABS — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0205:["Stop Lamp Switch Circuit","C0205 cannot be found in the accessible J2012 lists, in NHTSA bulletins or in maker indexes; its title is identical to that of C0136, and GM-designed brake modules such as that of the Saab 9-4X use C0161 for the brake switch input. The switch itself is a closing contact that passes battery voltage to the brake module and the stop lamps when the pedal is pressed, as Saab's 9-3 ESP data show.",["Stop lamp switch misadjusted, worn or broken","Blown stop lamp bulbs or fuse interrupting the monitoring path","Broken wire or corroded connector at the pedal"],["Stop lamps stay off or stay on","Cruise control will not engage or does not switch off when braking","ABS/ESC warning lamp on"],1,0,["C0136","C0161","C0040"],"מתג נורת עצירה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0206:["ABS Solenoid Valve Rear Left Circuit","C0206 is not documented publicly; the publicly available J2012 lists, the NHTSA bulletin index and maker indexes do not contain it. The title describes an electrical fault of the left rear ABS valves, which Saab's 9-5 TC/ABS data file as C2415 and watch for opens and shorts at all times, with the active valve check above 6 km/h.",["Open or shorted coil of a rear left valve","Cracked solder joint or contact strip, often worse when cold","Faulty valve driver in the control module"],["ABS and red brake warning lamps on","No ABS or electronic brake-force distribution, rear may lock early"],3,2,["C0209","C0158","C0163"],"שמאלי אחורי שסתום סולנואיד ABS — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0209:["ABS Solenoid Valve Rear Right Circuit","C0209 appears in none of the accessible J2012 tables, NHTSA bulletins or manufacturer indexes and is therefore not publicly verifiable. Its title, a circuit fault of the rear right ABS solenoid valves, corresponds to Saab's C2485 on the 9-5 with Bosch TC/ABS. In the Saab ESP unit twelve valves share one block: an inlet and an outlet valve for each wheel plus two pairs used only for traction control.",["Open or shorted coil of a rear right valve","Poor contact between control module and valve block","Internal failure of the hydraulic unit"],["ABS, brake and ESP OFF lamps on","No anti-lock, traction or stability intervention"],3,2,["C0206","C0168","C0173"],"ימני אחורי שסתום סולנואיד ABS — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0220:["ABS Valve Block Supply Voltage","C0220 has not turned up in any accessible J2012 table, NHTSA bulletin or maker index; there is no public evidence of its use. The title refers to the voltage that feeds the solenoid valves of the hydraulic unit. In GM-designed systems such as the TRW EBC450 of the 2011 Saab 9-5, the brake control module itself feeds both the valve coils and the pump motor.",["Low system voltage from a weak battery or charging fault","Blown fuse or high resistance in the module supply line","Poor ground connection of the brake control module","Faulty valve supply relay or driver inside the module"],["ABS, brake and stability lamps on, often intermittently","ABS and traction control unavailable"],2,2,["C0225","C0121","C0110"],""],C0225:["ABS Valve Relay Circuit","C0225 is missing from the accessible J2012 lists. GM does use the number: its terminal-test bulletin PIP5094 for 2014 and older cars and light trucks lists it among the chassis codes, and AA1Car's table of GM ABS codes gives it as Left Front Wheel Speed Sensor Circuit Open, not as a valve relay fault. No maker on record documents a valve relay meaning.",["On GM vehicles open left front wheel speed sensor or its wiring","Burnt or sticking valve relay contact","Blown fuse or poor ground in the relay circuit"],["ABS warning lamp on, ABS disabled","Traction control or speedometer function affected on some vehicles"],2,2,["C0121","C0220","C0035"],"ממסר שסתום ABS — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0230:["Brake Pedal Position Sensor Circuit","C0230 is in none of the accessible J2012 tables and in no NHTSA bulletin or manufacturer index, so it cannot be traced to a vehicle. The title points to the electrical side of a brake pedal position sensor: a supply, signal or ground line that is open or shorted, so the reading falls outside the band the module accepts.",["Open or shorted supply, signal or ground wire of the sensor","Corroded or loose connector at the pedal sensor","Internal sensor fault (worn track, failed Hall element)"],["Brake or stability warning lamp on","Stop lamps or cruise control behave incorrectly"],2,0,["C0202","C0042","C0043","C0562"],"חיישן מצב דוושת בלם — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0234:["Wheel Speed Sensor Frequency Error","C0234 is publicly unverifiable: the publicly available J2012 tables, NHTSA's bulletins and maker indexes all lack it; in AA1Car's list of GM ABS codes the same wording belongs to C0245. The title describes a speed signal whose frequency is implausible.",["Damaged, cracked or wrong tone ring (missing teeth, wrong tooth count)","Tyre or wheel size differs from the other wheels","Excessive air gap or metal debris on the sensor"],["ABS and traction lamps on, sometimes only above a certain speed","Unwanted ABS or traction intervention"],2,2,["C0245","C0235","C0080"],"שגיאת תדר חיישן מהירות גלגל"],C0235:["Wheel Speed Sensor Signal Erratic","C0235 does not show up in the publicly available J2012 lists. GM's bulletin PIP5094 names the number among chassis codes for cars and light trucks up to 2014, and AA1Car's GM-based ABS table renders it as Rear Wheel Speed Signal Circuit Open; an erratic-signal meaning is not documented by any maker. Taken by its title, the code concerns a speed signal that jumps or briefly drops out while the wheel turns steadily.",["Intermittent wire break or loose connector, often at moving harness sections","Dirt, rust or metal debris on the sensor, enlarged air gap","Wheel bearing play letting the encoder wobble"],["ABS lamp comes and goes","Pulsing pedal or ABS intervention at low speed without reason"],2,2,["C0234","C0237","C0245"],""],C0237:["Loss of Speed Sensor Signal Front Left","The publicly available J2012 tables skip C0237. GM lists the number in PIP5094, and AA1Car's GM-based code table reads it as Rear Wheel Speed Signal Erratic, so GM's use concerns the rear axle, not the front left wheel of the title.",["Broken sensor cable or damaged connector at the front left wheel","Sensor failed or pushed out of position after suspension work","Tone ring damaged or missing after drive shaft or hub replacement"],["ABS, traction and stability lamps on","No ABS; speedometer may misread if it uses this wheel"],2,2,["C0035","C0235","C0500"],""],C0238:["Speed Wheel-to-Wheel Mismatch","C0238 does not appear in the publicly available J2012 code lists. GM uses it: the terminal-check bulletin PIP5094 for 2014 and older GM cars and light trucks names it as a chassis keyword, and AA1Car's table of GM ABS codes calls it Wheel Speed Mismatch, which fits the title. GM does not publish its setting rule for this number.",["One tyre with different size, wear or pressure, or a space-saver spare fitted","Cracked, corroded or wrong tone ring on one wheel","Wheel speed sensor loose or with excessive air gap, or worn wheel bearing"],["ABS and traction control warning lamps on","ABS and traction control disabled for the rest of the trip"],2,2,["C0245","C0234","C0035","C0040"],""],C0240:["Brake Pressure Sensor","C0240 cannot be verified publicly: it is missing from the accessible J2012 lists, from the NHTSA bulletin index, from GM's PIP5094 keyword list and from the Saab and Mitsubishi indexes. Only the part in the title can be described. In a modern brake control unit a pressure sensor reports how hard the driver presses; on the TRW EBC450 of the 2011 Saab 9-5 it is built into the valve block.",["Open or shorted 5 V supply or signal wire to the pressure sensor","Faulty pressure sensor inside the hydraulic unit","Sensor offset not calibrated after module or valve block replacement"],["ABS, traction and stability warning lamps on","Brake assist and stability control unavailable"],3,2,["C0131","C0161","C0110"],"חיישן לחץ בלם"],C0241:["ABS Warning Lamp Control Circuit","None of the reachable J2012 tables contain C0241, and a warning lamp meaning is documented nowhere. GM's PIP5094 keyword list includes the number; AA1Car's table of GM ABS codes names it EBCM Control Valve Circuit.",["On Saab 9-5 (1998) open or shorted torque limitation line or throttle fault in the Trionic engine module","On GM vehicles fault in a control valve circuit driven by the brake module","Brake module programmed for the wrong engine variant"],["TCS OFF or ABS warning lamp on","Traction control not working","Check engine lamp on at the same time when the engine module is the source (Saab)"],2,2,["C0244","C0242","P0856"],"נורת התרעת ABS — תקלה במעגל הבקרה"],C0242:["PCM Indicated Traction Control Malfunction","C0242 is a GM brake module code that the accessible J2012 lists do not contain. The Saab 9-5 and 9-4X of 2011 describe it as Powertrain Control Module Indicated Traction Control Malfunction, and the GM bulletin PIC4740C for the 2007 Cadillac STS calls it ECM Indicated TCS Malfunction. During traction control the brake module asks the engine module over the data bus for less torque.",["Stored fault in the engine control module that blocks torque reduction","Loose or poorly seated terminals at the transmission connector (GM PIC4740C)","Faulty engine control module, rarely the brake module"],["Traction or stability control lamp on, systems disabled","Check engine lamp or reduced engine power from the engine side fault"],2,2,["P0856","C061B","C0561"],""],C0244:["PWM Brake Pressure Modulation Circuit","No public J2012 table carries C0244, and no maker documents a meaning matching the title. The only public use is Saab's, and it concerns the engine torque signal. On the 1998 9-5 with TC/ABS 5.3 the Trionic engine module reports actual torque to the brake module as a pulse-width signal; C0244 is stored when that line is open or shorted.",["Open or shorted torque signal line between engine and brake module (Saab 9-5 1998)","Fault in the engine control module that invalidates the torque value","Data bus problem between engine and brake module"],["TCS OFF or ESP OFF lamp on","No traction or stability control, ABS still active"],2,2,["C0241","C0242","P0856"],""],C0245:["Wheel Speed Sensor Frequency Mismatch","C0245 is missing from the reachable J2012 lists but is a documented GM code: PIP5094 lists it, AA1Car's GM table names it Wheel Speed Sensor Frequency Error, and the 2010 and 2011 Saab 9-5 manuals call it Wheel Speed Sensor Frequency Malfunction. The active sensors there get 12 V from the brake module and return a square wave whose frequency gives the wheel speed.",["Tyre with wrong size or pressure on one wheel","Damaged or contaminated tone ring or magnetic encoder","Sensor not seated correctly or excessive wheel bearing play"],["ABS, traction/stability and brake warning lamps on together","ABS, stability control and hill start assist disabled"],2,2,["C0238","C0234","C0035","C0050"],""],C0246:["ABS/TCS Control Module Internal Performance","The accessible J2012 tables lack C0246, and an internal brake module fault is not what any maker uses it for. Two makers use it differently. In the 2011 Saab 9-5 (GM) it is set by other modules on the fast CAN network when the periodic wheel speed message from the brake module stops arriving: Invalid Data Received From Electronic Brake Control Module.",["On GM vehicles wheel speed message from the brake module missing on the CAN bus","On Toyota 4Runner unstable ECU ground caused by aftermarket LED or HID headlight bulbs","Damaged brake module connector or ground wires"],["ABS warning lamp on","Functions that use wheel speed run degraded in other modules (GM)"],2,2,["C0035","C0045","U0121","C0110"],""],C0250:["Power Steering Pump Pressure","C0250 is publicly unverifiable: neither the reachable J2012 lists, nor NHTSA's bulletin index, nor GM's PIP5094 keywords, nor the Saab manuals contain it. What can be described is the part named in the title. On hydraulic power steering a pressure switch or sensor at the pump outlet tells the engine control when steering adds load.",["Faulty or stuck power steering pressure sensor or switch","Damaged wiring or connector at the pressure sensor","Low fluid level or worn pump giving abnormal pressure"],["Idle speed dips or stalls when steering at standstill","Warning lamp or stored code without noticeable steering change"],2,0,["P0550","P0551","P0552"],"לחץ משאבת הגה כוח"],C0252:["Pump Motor Ground Circuit Open","C0252 has no entry in the publicly available J2012 tables, nor does any maker tie it to a pump motor ground. Saab and GM use it for stability control plausibility. The 2002 to 2010 Saab 9-5 with Bosch ESP sets it after a rare event while ABS or ESP is regulating, such as the car sliding sideways with locked wheels, or after a brief voltage drop at the steering angle or yaw rate sensor.",["Steering angle sensor not calibrated, misaligned or disturbed by column play","Loose or wrongly mounted yaw rate / multi-axis acceleration sensor","Incorrect wheel alignment after suspension work","Rare driving situation during regulation (sliding with stationary wheels)"],["ESP OFF or stability control lamp on","Unwanted stability control intervention when turning","Stability control and hill start assist disabled"],2,2,["C0196","C0186","C0710","C0460","C0287"],"הארקת מנוע משאבה — מעגל פתוח (נתק)"],C0258:["Brake Booster Vacuum Sensor Circuit","No public record of C0258 exists: the publicly available J2012 lists, the NHTSA bulletin index and the GM and Saab indexes all lack it. Only the sensor named in the title can be described. A booster vacuum sensor tells the control unit whether enough vacuum is stored for power-assisted braking; GM needs it on cylinder-deactivation engines, which return to all cylinders when vacuum gets low.",["Open or shorted sensor supply, ground or signal wire","Faulty or drifting vacuum sensor","Leaking vacuum hose, check valve or booster diaphragm"],["Warning lamp or message about brake assistance","Cylinder deactivation or engine stop-start inhibited on affected vehicles"],2,0,["P0556","P0557","P0558","C0269","C0273"],"חיישן ואקום מגבר בלם — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0265:["EBCM Relay Circuit","C0265 does not appear in the published J2012 lists; it belongs to GM's numbering. PIP5094, GM's terminal-check bulletin for 2014 and older vehicles, includes it, and in AA1Car's listing of GM ABS faults it is EBCM Relay Circuit, matching the title. GM does not publish the setting rule for this number.",["Blown fuse or poor battery feed to the relay","Burnt or sticking relay contacts (internal relay in later modules)","Poor ground at the brake control module"],["ABS warning lamp on, ABS disabled","Traction control unavailable on equipped vehicles"],2,2,["C0266","C0121","C0225"],""],C0266:["Active Brake Booster","Active brake booster faults are filed under C0266 by no maker, and the reachable J2012 lists omit the code. The number is a GM one: it shows up among PIP5094's keywords, and AA1Car words it exactly like C0265, EBCM Relay Circuit, so on GM vehicles it points to the relay that powers the ABS valves and pump rather than to a booster.",["On GM vehicles fault in the brake module relay supply (fuse, contact, ground)","Faulty actuator or motor of an active booster","Damaged wiring or connector to the booster or relay"],["ABS or brake warning lamp on","Assistance functions such as automatic braking unavailable"],3,2,["C0265","C0273","C0595"],"מגבר בלם פעיל"],C0267:["Brake Pump Motor Circuit","C0267 is missing from the accessible J2012 lists; GM has used it with two meanings. AA1Car's table of older GM ABS codes names it Pump Motor Circuit Open/Shorted, matching the title, and PIP5094 confirms the number.",["On newer GM vehicles brake fluid below MIN (check pad wear and leaks)","Loose ground (GM G203) or corroded brake module connector","On older GM ABS open or shorted pump motor circuit or worn pump motor"],["Red brake warning lamp or low brake fluid message","Traction and stability control disabled, ABS lamp on with older systems"],2,2,["C0268","C0110","C0128","C0201"],"מנוע משאבת בלם — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0268:["Brake Pump Run Time Exceeded","C0268 appears in no public J2012 table. It is a GM number named in PIP5094, and AA1Car repeats for it the wording of C0267, Pump Motor Circuit Open/Shorted. A run-time limit as in the title is documented by no maker for this code. Why pump run time matters is shown by a Kelsey-Hayes patent for GM-type ABS: one DC motor drives the return pumps that empty the low-pressure accumulators after the dump valves open;",["Worn or sluggish ABS pump motor","Low supply voltage or poor ground at the pump motor circuit","Open or shorted pump motor wiring or connector (GM wording)"],["ABS warning lamp on, ABS and traction control disabled","Pump runs audibly long during self-test or ABS events"],3,2,["C0267","C0110","C0269"],""],C0269:["Brake Vacuum Sensor","C0269 lacks a J2012 entry in the sources available, and a vacuum sensor meaning appears nowhere. On GM vehicles, where PIP5094 names the code, AA1Car translates it as Excessive Dump/Isolation Time: the brake module has held wheel pressure isolated or released for longer than its software allows.",["Erratic or weak wheel speed signal making a wheel appear locked","Sticking isolation or dump valve in the hydraulic unit","Weak return pump or full low-pressure accumulator"],["ABS warning lamp on, ABS disabled","Long or soft brake pedal feel during an ABS stop"],3,2,["C0268","C0110","C0035","C0258"],"חיישן ואקום בלם"],C0273:["Brake Booster Pressure Sensor Circuit Malfunction","Neither the reachable J2012 lists nor any maker describe C0273 as a booster pressure sensor code. GM's PIP5094 does include the number, and AA1Car translates it, like C0271 and C0272, as EBCM Malfunction, meaning an internal fault of the brake module. In that case the module is normally replaced after supply, ground and connector have been checked.",["On GM vehicles internal fault of the brake control module","Low supply voltage, poor ground or corroded module connector","Faulty booster pressure sensor or its wiring"],["ABS and traction warning lamps on","ABS and stability functions disabled"],3,2,["C0258","C0279","P0556","C0266"],"חיישן לחץ מגבר בלם — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0277:["Brake Pedal Position Sensor Circuit","The publicly available J2012 tables omit C0277; GM assigns it to the brake pedal position sensor, not for a booster vacuum sensor. In the 2011 Saab 9-4X the body module watches the sensor with 9 to 16 V supply and the brake applied: failure type 06 means the signal or 5 V reference line is grounded or interrupted, 07 that a line touches battery voltage or the low reference is open, 09 a signal changing too fast, 4B…",["Loose, backed-out or bent terminals in the sensor connector or GM connector X205","Short or open in signal, 5 V reference or low reference wire","Brake module software (GM 19-NA-202) or rest position not learned"],["Rear stop lamps inoperative","Service Stabilitrak message, traction control lamp on","Cruise control cannot be set or drops out"],2,2,["C0161","C05C0","C0230","C0595"],"חיישן מצב דוושת בלם — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0279:["Brake Booster Boost Sensor Circuit Malfunction","C0279 is absent from every publicly available J2012 list, and no maker describes it as a booster sensor code. GM does use the number: its bulletin PIP5094 names it among the chassis keywords for 2014 and older cars and light trucks, and the GM brake code chart published by AA1Car renders it as Powertrain Configuration Not Valid, meaning the brake module received engine or driveline data it was not set up for.",["Open or shorted 5 V supply, signal or ground wire of the booster sensor","Booster pressure sensor failed or its grommet leaking","Brake module not configured for the fitted engine or driveline (GM meaning of the number)"],["Brake or ABS warning lamp on","Electric vacuum pump runs constantly or not at all","Start/stop or brake assist unavailable"],2,0,["C0273","C0277","C0267"],"חיישן לחץ גדישה מגבר בלם — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0287:["Longitudinal Acceleration Sensor Circuit","The publicly available J2012 lists do not contain C0287, and no maker uses it for an ESP Performance fault. In later GM brake systems the number belongs to the longitudinal acceleration sensor: the Saab 9-5 of 2010 and 2011 and the 2011 Saab 9-4X file it under the multi-axis sensor that also delivers lateral acceleration and yaw rate over CAN.",["Multi-axis sensor replaced or disturbed without setup and yaw sensor learn","Corroded or loose connector in the sensor supply or CAN lines","Faulty multi-axis sensor or outdated software in the module hosting it"],["Hill start assist not available","Stability control or airbag warning lamp on when stored together with C0186 or C0196"],2,0,["C0186","C0196","C0288"],"חיישן תאוצה אורכית — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0288:["Yaw Rate Sensor Range","No reachable J2012 list carries C0288, and no known maker files a yaw rate range fault under it. GM's PIP5094 contains the number, and AA1Car's GM brake table gives it a quite different meaning: Brake Warning Lamp Circuit Shorted to B+. The title describes a yaw rate signal that leaves its permitted span.",["Sensor bracket loose, bent or sensor mounted crooked after body repair","Yaw rate sensor drifting internally","Unstable supply or ground at the sensor"],["Stability and traction control warning lamp on","Stability control disabled for the rest of the trip"],2,2,["C0196","C0186","C0287"],"טווח חיישן קצב סבסוב"],C0290:["Brake Pedal Stroke Sensor Circuit Malfunction","C0290 does not show up in the publicly available J2012 lists, and no maker ties it to a pedal stroke sensor. GM lists the number in PIP5094; AA1Car's GM brake table translates it as Lost Communications With PCM, a data bus fault between brake and engine module. A pedal stroke sensor measures how far the driver pushes the pedal or brake rod.",["Damaged wiring or connector at the pedal travel sensor","Pedal travel sensor failed or its magnet displaced","Data bus fault between brake and engine module (GM meaning of the number)"],["Brake warning lamp on","Higher pedal effort or changed pedal feel","Regenerative braking reduced on hybrid or electric cars"],2,2,["C0291","C0277"],"חיישן מהלך דוושת בלם — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0291:["Brake Pedal Apply Sensor Circuit Malfunction","C0291 is in no publicly available J2012 table, and no maker uses it for a brake apply sensor. GM names the number in its PIP5094 keyword list, and AA1Car's table of GM brake codes reads it as Lost Communications With BCM, a lost data link to the body module. An apply sensor tells the control units whether, and how firmly, the pedal is pressed.",["Chafed wire or loose connector at the pedal sensor","Pedal sensor replaced or pedal adjusted without relearning the rest position","Data link to the body module interrupted (GM meaning of the number)"],["Stop lamps stay on or do not light","Cruise control or shift lock release not working","ABS or stability control warning lamp on"],2,2,["C0290","C0277"],""],C0295:["Steering Sensor Indicates Bias","Public evidence for C0295 is lacking. The code appears neither in the publicly available J2012 tables nor in GM's PIP5094 keywords, the AA1Car chart, the Saab manuals or the NHTSA bulletin index. What remains is the fault the title names, a steering angle sensor whose zero point no longer matches straight-ahead driving. GM stores this case as C0710 5A on the 2011 Saab 9-5, comparing steering angle with yaw rate;",["Wheel alignment or steering parts changed without recentring the sensor","Calibration lost after battery disconnection or a voltage dip","Steering angle sensor or clock spring assembly faulty"],["Stability control warning lamp on","Steering wheel off centre when driving straight","Unexpected stability control interventions"],2,2,["C0710","C0460","C0455"],""],C0300:["Inlet Valve Front Left Performance","C0300 appears in none of the published J2012 lists, and no maker documents it as an ABS valve code. GM uses the number: it is among the chassis keywords of PIP5094, and AA1Car's GM table calls it Rear Speed Sensor Malfunction, listed in the same block as the transfer case motor codes C0306 to C0315. The title describes the front left inlet valve of the ABS valve block.",["Inlet valve sticking from contaminated or aged brake fluid","Valve coil or driver in the brake module faulty","On GM 4WD trucks, rear speed sensor fault in the transfer case system (GM meaning of the number)"],["ABS and stability control warning lamps on","Car pulls during hard braking"],3,2,["C0302","C0303","C0305"],"שמאלי קדמי שסתום כניסה — ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0301:["Air Suspension Compressor Relay","No reachable J2012 table, no GM keyword list such as PIP5094, no AA1Car chart and no NHTSA bulletin carries C0301. Makers that document this fault use their own numbers. Mercedes-Benz stores open-circuit compressor actuation on AIRMATIC cars as C1562 and, after moisture froze in the compressor and the start current blew the 40 A fuse, replaces compressor, fuse and relay together.",["Relay contacts burnt or welded by excessive compressor current","Worn, seized or water-damaged compressor drawing too much current","Blown compressor fuse or corroded relay socket and wiring"],["Air suspension warning message, compressor silent","Vehicle sinks or leans after standing","Compressor runs continuously when the relay sticks"],2,2,["C0317","C0312"],"ממסר מדחס מתלי אוויר"],C0302:["Outlet Valve Front Left Performance","C0302 has no public footprint: the publicly available J2012 tables, GM's PIP5094, the AA1Car chart and the NHTSA bulletin index all lack it. This text therefore covers only the front left outlet valve named in the title. Unlike the inlet valve it stays closed at rest and opens only when the brake module wants to drop pressure at a locking wheel;",["Outlet valve seat leaking because of dirt or wear","Valve coil or its driver in the brake module faulty","Old or wrong brake fluid slowing the valve"],["ABS warning lamp on, ABS switched off","Front left wheel locks or pedal sinks slowly"],3,2,["C0300","C0304","C0309"],"שמאלי קדמי שסתום יציאה — ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0303:["Inlet Valve Front Right Performance","C0303 has no public evidence at all: the accessible J2012 lists, GM's PIP5094 keyword list, AA1Car's GM table and the NHTSA index all lack it. The title points to the front right inlet valve. A performance fault here means the brake module saw the valve respond wrongly, for example a coil current out of range during the self-test or a wheel that does not hold pressure as commanded.",["Inlet valve stuck from debris after brake work","Open or shorted valve coil inside the hydraulic unit","Low supply voltage to the valve circuit during self-test"],["ABS, traction and stability control lamps on","Car pulls to the left when braking"],3,2,["C0304","C0300","C0307"],"ימני קדמי שסתום כניסה — ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0304:["Outlet Valve Front Right Performance","No public source confirms C0304; searches of the J2012 tables at hand, of GM's keyword bulletin PIP5094, of AA1Car and of the NHTSA bulletin index came up empty. The title concerns the front right outlet valve, the part that bleeds pressure off that caliper when the wheel starts to lock.",["Outlet valve not resealing because of dirt in the seat","Valve coil or brake module output stage defective","Accumulator or return pump unable to take the released fluid"],["ABS and stability control warning lamps on","Long brake pedal or front right wheel locking"],3,2,["C0303","C0302","C0309"],"ימני קדמי שסתום יציאה — ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0305:["Inlet Valve Rear Left Performance","C0305 is missing from the published J2012 lists and is not described by any maker as an ABS valve code. GM does use it: PIP5094 lists the number, and AA1Car's GM table calls it Front Speed Sensor Malfunction, the partner of C0300 in the block before the transfer case motor codes. The title refers to the rear left inlet valve.",["Rear left inlet valve sticking from contaminated fluid","Valve coil or brake module driver defective","On GM 4WD trucks, front speed sensor fault in the transfer case system (GM meaning of the number)"],["ABS and brake warning lamps on","Rear wheel locking early or hill start assist unavailable"],3,2,["C0307","C0300"],"שמאלי אחורי שסתום כניסה — ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0306:["Transfer Case Motor A or B Circuit","C0306 is not in the publicly available J2012 lists, and nobody uses it for a ride height sensor. GM uses it in its transfer case module (TCCM) for the two circuits that drive the shift motor: AA1Car's GM table names it Motor A or B Circuit, and bulletins PIP5080 and PIP5080B for 2012–13 Silverado, Sierra, Tahoe, Suburban, Avalanche and Yukon point to terminals at X109 and to connector X3 of the module, which carries…",["Loose, corroded or poorly crimped terminals at the motor or module connector","Transfer case shift motor with internal short or open winding","Faulty motor driver in the transfer case control module"],["Service 4WD message in the driver information centre","Transfer case does not shift between 2WD, 4WD and low range"],2,2,["C0308","C0310","C0327","C0387"],""],C0307:["Inlet Valve Rear Right Performance","C0307 has no public trace: not in the accessible J2012 lists, not in GM's PIP5094 or AA1Car's GM table, and not in the NHTSA bulletin index. Described here is the rear right inlet valve of the title.",["Rear right inlet valve slowed by dirt or aged fluid","Coil of the valve or brake module output defective","Poor contact between brake module and valve block"],["ABS and stability control lamps on","Stability control unavailable"],3,2,["C0305","C0309","C0303"],"ימני אחורי שסתום כניסה — ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0308:["Transfer Case Motor A/B Circuit Low","None of the publicly available J2012 lists contains C0308, and no source links it to a ride height sensor. GM uses it for the transfer case shift motor: PIP5094 lists the number, AA1Car's GM chart labels it Motor A/B Circuit Low, and Dorman's guide for its replacement motor covers 1998–2005 S10 Blazer, Sonoma, Tahoe, Suburban, Yukon, Silverado, Sierra, Escalade, Avalanche and related trucks.",["Motor control wire A or B chafed against the frame and grounded","Shift motor internally shorted","Transfer case control module output stage faulty"],["Service 4WD lamp on","No shifting into or out of four-wheel drive"],2,2,["C0306","C0310","C0327"],"מנוע תיבת העברה‏ A/B — אות נמוך במעגל"],C0309:["Outlet Valve Rear Right Performance","C0309 is no part of any public J2012 table, and no manufacturer documents it as a valve code. GM does use it: it is among the keywords of PIP5094, and the GM code chart on AA1Car calls it Motor A/B Circuit High, a transfer case shift motor fault next to C0308 and C0310; that meaning rests on this single source. The title instead names the rear right outlet valve.",["Rear right outlet valve not closing fully","Valve coil or brake module driver faulty","On GM 4WD trucks, transfer case motor circuit shorted to voltage (GM meaning of the number)"],["ABS and stability control warning lamps on","Weak braking at the right rear wheel"],3,2,["C0307","C0304","C0302"],"ימני אחורי שסתום יציאה — ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0310:["Transfer Case Motor A/B Circuit Open","C0310 is not listed in any publicly available J2012 table; no maker uses it for a rear left ride height sensor. GM assigns the number to the transfer case shift motor: it is in PIP5094, AA1Car gives the GM wording Motor A/B Circuit Open, and Dorman describes it for GM trucks and SUVs of 1998 to 2005.",["Broken motor control wire or pigtail exposed under the vehicle","Corroded or unseated connector at the shift motor","Open winding or worn brushes in the shift motor"],["Service 4WD lamp on, 4WD switch lights flash","Transfer case stays in its last range"],2,2,["C0306","C0308","C0327"],"מנוע תיבת העברה‏ A/B — מעגל פתוח (נתק)"],C0312:["Ride Height Sensor Rear Right","Searches for C0312 in reachable J2012 lists, in GM sources and in the NHTSA bulletin index returned nothing, so only the component is described here. A ride height sensor at the right rear converts the swing of a lever arm linked to the suspension into an electrical signal, usually by inductive or Hall measurement, and feeds air suspension, damping or headlamp levelling.",["Bent, detached or wrongly clipped sensor lever or link rod","Corroded connector or broken wire at the rear right sensor","Sensor failed internally after water ingress"],["Air suspension or levelling warning message","Rear right corner sits too high or too low","Headlamp levelling incorrect"],2,2,["C0301","C0317"],""],C0317:["Compressor Relay Circuit","C0317 is publicly undocumented: it is missing from every publicly available J2012 list, from GM's keyword bulletin PIP5094 and from the whole NHTSA bulletin index. What follows describes only the part named in the title. On air or self-levelling suspension a relay carries the heavy compressor current and is energised by the suspension module.",["Relay contacts burnt or welded by a compressor drawing too much current","Open or shorted control line between suspension module and relay coil","Worn or seized compressor overloading the relay","Blown compressor fuse or corroded relay socket"],["Suspension warning or air suspension fault message","Vehicle sits low and does not rise","Compressor runs constantly or never starts"],2,2,["C0301","C0312"],"ממסר מדחס — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0327:["Encoder Motor","C0327 has no entry in the published J2012 tables, but GM documents it: the transfer case control module (TCCM) of 4WD trucks and SUVs uses it for the encoder that tells the module where the motor has turned the shift shaft. Dorman's instruction sheets for GM pickups and SUVs from 1998 to 2009, the Saab 9-7X included, describe it as a voltage outside the expected window on the encoder circuit;",["Loose or corroded ground terminal for the encoder channels (GM circuit 550)","Damaged encoder harness or water in the motor connector","Encoder in the shift motor assembly defective","Worn shift shaft lets the encoder read a false position"],["Service 4WD message or flashing 4WD switch lamps","Transfer case does not shift or shifts only intermittently","Fault appears mainly on the first drive after cold or damp standing"],2,2,["C0306","C0310","C0387"],"מנוע מקודד"],C0374:["4WD Drive Coupling","No publicly available J2012 list carries C0374; GM uses it in the transfer case control module of its 4WD trucks and SUVs, and PIP5094 names it among GM chassis codes. Dorman's sheets for the S10, Blazer, Astro and Safari, the Trailblazer, Envoy and Isuzu Ascender call it General 4WD Failure: in Auto 4WD the module notices rear wheel slip, commands torque to the front axle and still sees the front and rear…",["Encoder motor too weak or sticking, so the clutch is not applied","Front or rear propshaft speed sensor or its wiring giving false values","Worn transfer case clutch pack or wrong fluid","Tires of unequal size or pressure faking a speed difference"],["Service 4WD message until the next engine start","Auto 4WD does not engage, rear wheels spin on slippery ground"],3,2,["C0376","C0387","C0327"],""],C0376:["Front Axle Disconnect","C0376 is not in the published J2012 lists. The number exists at GM, whose bulletin PIP5094 lists it next to transfer case codes such as C0374 and C0387, but no reachable GM document states what it means. The title part decouples the front axle so the front driveline stands still in two-wheel drive.",["Water or corrosion in the axle actuator connector","Chafed actuator harness near the axle","Disconnect actuator or its position switch defective"],["Service 4WD message or flashing 4WD indicator","Front wheels not driven although 4WD is selected","Grinding or clicking from the front axle when shifting"],2,2,["C0374","C0387","C0306"],"ניתוק סרן קדמי"],C0387:["Transfer Case Unable to Complete Shift","C0387 is absent from the publicly available J2012 lists. GM uses it in its transfer case control module as Unable to Complete Shift; there is no evidence of a position sensor code. PIP5003C for 2010–13 Silverado, Sierra, Tahoe, Yukon, Avalanche, Escalade and hybrids explains that once a range change or a slip correction has been commanded, the module watches the shift shaft and sets the code when the motor has not…",["Encoder motor too slow to start moving the shift shaft","Poor terminal fit at the module connectors (GM X109, X3)","Low supply voltage or extreme temperatures during the shift","Mechanical binding inside the transfer case shift mechanism"],["Service 4WD message, often intermittent","Requested range or mode is not reached","Transfer case stays in a default 4HI or 4LO"],2,2,["C0306","C0327","C0374"],""],C0388:["Transfer Case High Range Switch Circuit Malfunction","No public source can be found for C0388; neither the reachable J2012 tables nor GM's PIP5094 or NHTSA's index of bulletins contain it. The text therefore covers only the title part. A transfer case reports its engaged range to the control module through a switch or position sensor; the high range is the normal road gear. Makers that document this file it under their own numbers.",["Open, shorted or corroded wire or terminal of the range switch","Range switch or position sensor on the transfer case defective","Transfer case module calibration needing an update"],["Service 4WD or 4x4 warning displayed","Range indicator does not match the selected gear","Shifts out of high range refused"],2,2,["C0389","C0399","C0387"],""],C0389:["Transfer Case Low Range Switch Circuit Malfunction","There is no evidence that any maker uses C0389. Neither the publicly available J2012 tables nor GM's chassis keyword bulletin PIP5094 nor NHTSA's index name it, so only the switch named in the title is described.",["Damaged or corroded wiring of the low range switch","Low range switch or range sensor defective","Transfer case stuck between ranges so no switch position is reached"],["4LO cannot be selected or left","4WD warning and low range indicator flashing","Stability control behaves unexpectedly after restart"],2,2,["C0388","C0399","C0387"],""],C0399:["4WD Mode Switch Circuit Malfunction","C0399 cannot be traced publicly. Publicly available J2012 tables do not list it, PIP5094 from GM omits it, and the only matches in NHTSA's index are Mack recall numbers. Only the switch itself is therefore described. With the 4WD mode switch on the dash the driver chooses 2WD, Auto, 4HI or 4LO, and the transfer case module turns that choice into shift commands.",["Switch variant not matching the transfer case (e.g. Auto position without Auto 4WD)","Worn switch contacts or resistor ladder giving invalid voltages","Open or shorted lead between switch and transfer case module"],["Service 4WD message","Mode changes ignored or 4WD indicators flash"],1,2,["C0388","C0389","C0387"],"מתג מצב הנעה כפולה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0400:["Traction Control Solenoid Valve Circuit","C0400 is publicly undocumented: none of the published J2012 lists contains it, neither does GM's PIP5094, and a search of NHTSA's bulletin index finds nothing. Only the part from the title is described here. For traction control the brake unit must build pressure without the driver pressing the pedal.",["Open or shorted coil of a traction control valve","Valve driver inside the brake control module failed","Poor supply or ground of the brake control module"],["ABS, traction control and stability warning lamps on","Wheels spin freely when pulling away on slippery ground"],4,2,["C0401","C0405","C0300"],"שסתום סולנואיד בקרת אחיזה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0401:["Traction Control Switch Circuit","There is no public evidence that any maker uses C0401. The code is missing from the publicly available J2012 lists and from GM's PIP5094; the only NHTSA index hit is a BMW program number. The description is limited to the switch itself. On the 2004 Saab 9-5 a spring-loaded dash button beside the steering wheel turns ESP and TCS off together;",["Button stuck pressed or contacts dirty","Open or grounded lead between button and brake module","Liquid spilled into the switch panel"],["Traction or stability control cannot be switched off or on","TCS OFF or ESP OFF lamp lit permanently"],1,0,["C0400","C0405"],"מתג בקרת אחיזה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0402:["Rear Drive Clutch Solenoid Valve","Publicly available J2012 tables skip C0402, yet GM assigns it in its rear differential clutch control module: the 2010–11 Saab 9-5 and the 2011 9-4X call it Transfer Case Solenoid Valve and describe the rear drive clutch solenoid, which the module drives by PWM to set the clutch pressure and so the torque sent rearward; the 2008–12 Saab 9-3 XWD calls it Differential Clutch Solenoid Valve.",["Open or shorted solenoid valve circuit at the rear drive unit","Valve calibration not stored after module replacement","Solenoid valve sticking because of contaminated or aged clutch fluid","Corroded connector on the rear axle module"],["Service Rear Axle or AWD warning displayed","Car drives on the front wheels only"],3,2,["C0374","C0400"],"שסתום סולנואיד מצמד הנעה אחורית"],C0405:["Traction Control Active Too Long","C0405 could not be found in any public source, including the public J2012 tables, GM's PIP5094 and NHTSA's bulletin index, and no maker publishes a time limit for a traction control intervention. So only the monitored function is outlined. Traction control brakes a spinning drive wheel and asks the engine for less torque; Bosch counts it among the functions of ESP.",["Erratic wheel speed signal faking continuous wheel spin","Spare wheel or tires of different size on one axle","Hydraulic control valve sticking in the brake unit"],["Traction control lamp flashes for a long time or stays on","Engine power reduced and a wheel braked without reason","Hot or smelling brake on one wheel"],2,2,["C0400","C0401"],""],C0410:["Adaptive Cruise Control Sensor Circuit Malfunction","C0410 has no public trace; searches of the publicly available J2012 tables, of GM's keyword bulletin PIP5094 and of NHTSA's bulletin index came up empty. The text is therefore restricted to the sensor named in the title. Adaptive cruise control relies mostly on a radar sensor behind the front fascia that watches the lane ahead;",["Loose or corroded connector of the front radar sensor","Sensor or bracket bent after a minor impact, alignment lost","Radar sensor internally defective"],["Adaptive cruise control unavailable with a warning message","Forward collision warning or emergency braking disabled"],4,0,["C0420"],"חיישן בקרת שיוט אדפטיבית — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0420:["Adaptive Cruise Control Module Internal Performance","No public document shows a maker using C0420. It does not appear in the openly accessible J2012 lists, in GM's PIP5094 or in the NHTSA bulletin index, so only the module from the title is covered. The ACC module evaluates the radar data and requests engine torque and braking to keep speed and gap, as Bosch outlines.",["ACC module software or calibration out of date","Low or unstable supply voltage during self-test","Internal hardware fault of the ACC module"],["Adaptive cruise control and related assists unavailable","Driver assist warning in the instrument cluster"],4,0,["C0410"],"פנימי מודול בקרת שיוט אדפטיבית — ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0440:["Steering Wheel Position Sensor Circuit","C0440 cannot be verified publicly; searches of the available J2012 tables, GM bulletin PIP5094 and the full NHTSA index found no hit. Its title is word for word that of C0455, which GM does use for the steering wheel position sensor read by the brake module; the description here sticks to the sensor. It sits on the steering column and gives stability control the driver's intended direction.",["Fretting corrosion or loose fit at the sensor connector","Zero position not calibrated after alignment or column work","Steering angle sensor internally defective"],["Stability control and traction control warning lamps on","Service StabiliTrak or ESP message"],2,2,["C0455","C0445","C0460"],"חיישן מצב גלגל הגה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0445:["Steering Wheel Position Sensor Calibration","No accessible J2012 list contains C0445, and no manufacturer bulletin or service page using it could be found, so its exact meaning cannot be proven publicly. The title points to a steering wheel position sensor whose zero point was never learned or has been lost. Saab explains for the 9-5 that the sensor only knows straight ahead after a calibration, which is due after front-end work or a sensor swap.",["Zero-point calibration skipped after alignment, steering work or sensor replacement","Stored calibration lost after battery disconnection or low voltage","Stability control module replaced or reprogrammed without relearning the angle"],["ESC or traction control warning lamp on","Stability control unavailable","Steering wheel reading not zero when driving straight (scan tool)"],2,2,["C0455","C0710","C0529"],"כיול חיישן מצב גלגל הגה"],C0450:["Rear Wheel Steering Position Sensor Circuit","C0450 does not occur in the accessible J2012 lists. Its only public manufacturer use is GM: bulletin PIC5321A for the 2010–2011 Cadillac DTS links C0450 with Service Power Steering and Service Brake System messages, a lit check-engine lamp and cycling door locks, caused by an engine harness chafed through on the transmission.",["Wiring harness chafed or pinched (GM DTS case at the transmission)","Faulty position sensor in the rear steering actuator","Corroded or loose connector on the actuator"],["Steering or brake system warning message in the cluster","Rear steering locked straight ahead, larger turning circle","Check-engine lamp on some GM models"],3,2,["C0455","C0460"],"חיישן מצב היגוי גלגל אחורי — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0455:["Steering Wheel Position Sensor Circuit","C0455 is absent from the accessible J2012 lists but well documented at GM, where the electronic brake control module (EBCM) stores it for the steering wheel position sensor circuit. Bulletin PI0639C, covering 2007–2016 full-size pickups, SUVs, vans and the Colorado/Canyon, blames rising resistance between sensor and EBCM caused by fretting corrosion and a connector with too much play;",["Fretting corrosion and play at the sensor connector (GM PI0639C)","Steering wheel not aligned with the shaft master spline","EBCM programmed for the wrong sensor design","Steering wheel position sensor defective"],["Service StabiliTrak message and stability lamp on","ABS lamp may come on first","Stability control unavailable"],2,2,["C0440","C0710","C0460","C0445"],"חיישן מצב גלגל הגה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0460:["Steering Position Signal Implausible","C0460 is not in the accessible J2012 lists; GM and Saab use it for the steering angle signal. On the 2016 Malibu the EBCM sets it after a brief low-voltage event, and turning lock to lock with ignition on resets the sensor (16-NA-151). On 2017–2018 XT5 and Acadia, C0460 symptom 5A in the power steering module came from a sensor trim error and is fixed by reprogramming (17-NA-284);",["Brief low voltage leaving the sensor uninitialised","Sensor trim error or control module software (GM 17-NA-284)","Angle offset after alignment or steering work","Steering angle sensor or column module defective"],["Traction or stability control lamp on","Reduced Steering Assist message, sometimes without actual loss of assist","Stability control switched off"],2,2,["C0455","C0710","C0545","C0528"],""],C0496:["Yaw Rate Sensor Circuit","C0496 appears in no accessible J2012 list, and neither the NHTSA bulletin index nor the manufacturer portals checked contain it, so the code is not publicly verifiable; the established code with this title is C0196. What the title covers: a micromechanical gyro, usually combined with the lateral accelerometer and mounted near the centre of gravity.",["Open circuit or short in the sensor wiring","Loose or corroded sensor connector","Yaw rate sensor internally defective"],["Stability and traction control unavailable","ESC warning lamp on, depending on the make"],2,2,["C0196","C0497","C0520","C0498"],"חיישן קצב סבסוב — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0497:["Yaw Rate Sensor Range/Performance","Neither the accessible J2012 lists nor any manufacturer bulletin or service text mention C0497, so its use cannot be confirmed publicly. The title describes a yaw rate signal that is electrically present but does not match how the car moves.",["Yaw rate sensor offset or drift","Sensor loose, twisted or mounted in the wrong orientation","Wrong comparison input (steering angle not calibrated, wheel speed fault)"],["ESC lamp on, stability control switched off","Unwanted brake interventions when cornering"],2,2,["C0196","C0496","C051C","C05B2"],"חיישן קצב סבסוב — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0498:["Lateral Acceleration Sensor Circuit","C0498 is in none of the accessible J2012 lists. GM does use the number: bulletin PIP5094, a terminal-test reminder for GM cars and light trucks of 2014 and earlier, names C0498 and C0499 among many chassis codes, but without any wording, so GM's meaning stays undocumented and a lateral accelerometer fault is not confirmed; the established code with this title is C0186.",["Open circuit or short in the signal, reference or ground wire","Loose or corroded connector at the sensor cluster","Lateral acceleration sensor defective"],["Stability control unavailable, ESC lamp depending on the make","Lateral acceleration reads a fixed value on the scan tool"],2,2,["C0186","C0499","C0520","C0496"],"חיישן תאוצה צידית — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0499:["Lateral Acceleration Sensor Range/Performance","C0499 is missing from the accessible J2012 lists. GM bulletin PIP5094 names C0499 next to C0498 without saying what it stands for, so no manufacturer confirms a lateral acceleration meaning; the established code with this title is C0185. The title describes a lateral acceleration reading that is wired correctly but implausible.",["Offset or drift of the lateral acceleration sensor","Sensor cluster loose or not mounted level","Steering angle reference not calibrated"],["ESC lamp on, stability control switched off until restart","Unexpected ESC interventions on banked roads"],2,2,["C0185","C0498","C051C","C0497"],"חיישן תאוצה צידית — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0500:["Left Front Wheel Speed Sensor A Circuit/Open","C0500 flags lost continuity in the left front wheel speed sensor circuit. An active sensor draws a steady current even with the car parked; Allegro gives 7 and 14 mA as the usual levels of a two-wire interface, so a reading near zero means a broken path.",["Sensor plug corroded or loose, or a wire broken along the wheel arch","Left front sensor open internally","ABS module supply, fuse or fusible link faulty (Mitsubishi lists these)"],["ABS, ESC and traction control warning lamps on, check-engine lamp on some makes","ABS, stability control and hill start assist unavailable","Scan tool shows no left front wheel speed while driving"],2,3,["C0501","C0502","C0503","C0504","C0505","C0506","C05A4","C0031"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל קדמי שמאלי‏ A — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C0501:["Left Front Wheel Speed Sensor A Range/Performance","C0501 means the left front speed signal is present but does not fit the situation. GM shows how differently this is judged: its 2016 hybrid tables flag the code when that wheel reads 0 mph while the other three exceed 7.45 mph at a vehicle speed above 11.8 mph (Type A), whereas the 2023 tables test the air gap and set it when magnetic flux stays below 2.2 mT for at least five wheel turns, as Type B with two trips.",["Sensor not fully seated or air gap to the tone ring too large","Tire on the left front differs in size from the specified one","Tone ring or magnetic encoder damaged or dirty","Control module software sets the code falsely (Stellantis reflash)"],["ABS and stability warning lamps on after driving, not at key-on","Unexpected ABS or traction control intervention at low speed","Code stored in the engine controller without MIL (Stellantis)"],2,3,["C0500","C0502","C0503","C0504","C0505","C0507","C053C","C0030"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל קדמי שמאלי‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0502:["Left Front Wheel Speed Sensor A Circuit Low","C0502 reports the left front sensor circuit below its valid level, mostly a grounded wire or a supply that has sagged. In GM's 2019 tables (19OBDG03D) the brake module's Polaris ASIC sets C0502 for three conditions: the low side shorted to ground, tested only at power-up or after clearing codes (100 ms); sensor undervoltage (20 ms);",["Sensor wire chafed through to ground or poorly crimped in the connector","Sensor supply voltage too low (battery, fuse or module output)","Internal short in the left front sensor"],["ABS and ESC lamps on right after starting","Parking brake warning or electric parking brake functions restricted on some models"],2,3,["C0500","C0501","C0503","C0504","C0508","C05A4","C0032"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל קדמי שמאלי‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],C0503:["Left Front Wheel Speed Sensor A Circuit High","With C0503 the left front circuit reads above its permitted level, which in practice means the signal wire is in contact with battery voltage. GM's 2016 hybrid tables set it when the signal line exceeds 12 V for 0.12 s; the 2023 tables look at current instead and react above 50 mA, many times what a healthy active sensor draws. Both rate it Type A, with a MIL on the first trip.",["Signal wire shorted to a battery-voltage feed","Internal short in the left front sensor","Sensor input stage in the ABS module defective"],["ABS and ESC warnings directly after switching on","Check-engine lamp on some makes (GM Type A, Mitsubishi)","Brake assist and hill descent control switched off"],2,3,["C0500","C0501","C0502","C0504","C0509","C05A4"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל קדמי שמאלי‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],C0504:["Left Front Wheel Speed Sensor A Intermittent/Erratic","C0504 points to a left front speed signal that jumps or produces far too many edges, not one that is missing. GM's 2016 hybrid brake module stores a time stamp for every sensor edge in a buffer and sets C0504 within 0.03 s when that buffer overflows; the 2023 tables apply the same idea to a DMA transfer unit receiving time stamps too often.",["Metal debris or dirt on the reluctor ring (GM PIT5707)","Loose contact in the sensor plug or a wire breaking under movement","Damaged tone ring or encoder"],["ABS lamp and service stability message on the driver display","Fault comes and goes with road surface or steering angle"],2,3,["C0500","C0501","C0502","C0503","C0505","C050A","C0030"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל קדמי שמאלי‏ A — אות לא יציב"],C0505:["Left Front Wheel Speed Sensor A Correlation","C0505 says the left front wheel speed is out of step with the other wheels although the circuit tests pass. GM's 2019 tables (19OBDG03D) group several comparisons under this code: a missing sensor, meaning this wheel shows under 1.5 km/h while another exceeds 6 km/h (3 to 120 s depending on speed); a dropout check paused after sudden accelerations; a start-up check that runs until 15 km/h;",["Tire of a different size or heavily worn tire on the left front","Sensor not seated correctly, air gap out of tolerance","Demagnetized or damaged magnetic encoder ring"],["ABS/ESC lamps after a drive, often following a tire change","Traction control intervenes although wheels are not slipping"],1,3,["C0500","C0501","C0504","C050B","C053C","C0555"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל קדמי שמאלי‏ A — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],C0506:["Right Front Wheel Speed Sensor A Circuit/Open","C0506 reports an open or grounded circuit at the right front wheel speed sensor. GM's 2023 tables describe it as a grounded or interrupted line, recognized from the signal-line current: below 3.8 mA for 0.12 s, Type A, and only evaluated after the start-up sensor test has finished without a supply undervoltage.",["Broken wire or open contact between ABS module and right front sensor","Right front sensor failed open","Old stored code after repair, vehicle not yet driven"],["ABS, ESC and traction control lamps on from start-up","Right front wheel speed reads zero in live data"],2,3,["C0507","C0508","C0509","C050A","C050B","C0500","C0034"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל קדמי ימני‏ A — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C0507:["Right Front Wheel Speed Sensor A Range/Performance","C0507 flags an implausible right front speed signal. In GM's 2019 tables the brake module's ASIC watches the sensor current itself: a level hanging in the grey zones between 7 and 14 mA or 14 and 28 mA for 750 ms points to a high-resistance harness or leakage to battery voltage. Those bands sit between the base, data and speed-pulse levels Allegro lists for AK-protocol sensors.",["Corroded contacts or damaged insulation causing resistance or leakage current","Damaged tone ring or wrong tire size on the right front","Engine controller software storing the code falsely (Stellantis)"],["ABS/ESC lamps after driving off","Code present only in the engine controller during a full vehicle scan"],2,3,["C0506","C0508","C0509","C050A","C050B","C0501","C0033"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל קדמי ימני‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0508:["Right Front Wheel Speed Sensor A Circuit Low","C0508 reports the right front sensor circuit below range. A 2024 Jeep Wrangler case from the Stellantis STAR center shows a typical picture: after an earlier repair the ABS lamp came on with C0508-00, ABS disabled and implausible-speed network codes; the sensor harness had been pinched and only needed rerouting.",["Sensor harness pinched or misrouted after suspension or brake work","Poorly crimped terminal in the sensor connector (Audi)","Right front sensor shorted internally"],["ABS lamp on, often right after a repair","Additional network codes about implausible wheel or vehicle speed","Parking brake warning on some models"],2,3,["C0506","C0507","C0509","C050A","C0502","C05A4"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל קדמי ימני‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],C0509:["Right Front Wheel Speed Sensor A Circuit High","C0509 means the right front sensor line carries more current or voltage than allowed. GM's 2019 tables (19OBDG03D) set it within 100 ms when the high-side current passes 40 mA, or when the Polaris ASIC reports either sensor line shorted to battery or an overcurrent on the low side; it is Type A.",["Sensor line chafed against a battery-voltage wire","Right front sensor drawing excess current due to an internal short","Sensor supply driver in the ABS module defective"],["ABS and ESC lamps on immediately, check-engine lamp on some makes","ABS, EBD and hill start assist suspended"],2,3,["C0506","C0507","C0508","C050A","C0503"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל קדמי ימני‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],C050A:["Right Front Wheel Speed Sensor A Intermittent/Erratic","C050A is the erratic-signal code for the right front sensor. GM's 2019 tables show how this is judged: an unfiltered wheel acceleration above 491 m/s² feeds a counter that latches the fault at 40 s and decays again on clean readings, so only persistently unrealistic jumps set it; a separate check trips when the edge count exceeds 55 (25 ms).",["Metal debris or heavy dirt on the right front reluctor ring","Missing tone-ring teeth or excessive wheel bearing play","Electromagnetic interference or intermittent contact in the harness"],["ABS lamp and stability system message that appear and disappear","Pulsing brake pedal or ABS action at low speed without wheel lock"],2,3,["C0506","C0507","C0508","C0509","C050B","C0504","C0033"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל קדמי ימני‏ A — אות לא יציב"],C050B:["Right Front Wheel Speed Sensor A Correlation","C050B is the correlation code for the right front wheel. GM's 2025 tables (25OBDG04A) rate it Type B, so the MIL waits for a second trip, and add a check not found under C0505 in the 2019 tables: the brake module compares the switching state it requests from the sensor supply driver with the state reported back, an internal module fault rather than a sensor problem.",["Right front tire of a different size or circumference","Sensor-to-ring gap out of tolerance or demagnetized encoder","Internal fault in the ABS module's sensor supply switch (GM)"],["ABS/ESC lamps after the second drive with the fault","Stability and traction control unavailable, normal braking retained"],1,3,["C0506","C0507","C050A","C0505","C053C","C0556"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל קדמי ימני‏ A — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],C050C:["Left Rear Wheel Speed Sensor A Circuit/Open","C050C is stored when the brake controller loses the current path to the left rear speed sensor. GM's 2023 OBD tables (23OBDG07) read 0.12 s at under 3.8 mA in the signal wire as a ground short or a break and rate the code Type A, so the MIL can come on in the first trip. Mitsubishi lists C1065-13 of the Outlander PHEV as C050C, detected within one second, with ABS, ASC and engine lamps lit.",["Sensor lead chafed or torn where it follows the rear suspension","Left rear sensor connector corroded or not latched","Left rear sensor open internally"],["ABS and stability warning lamps on right after key-on, check-engine lamp on some makes","ABS, stability control and on some models electric parking brake functions restricted","Live data shows no left rear wheel speed"],2,3,["C050D","C050E","C050F","C0510","C0511","C0512","C0037","C05A4"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי שמאלי‏ A — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C050D:["Left Rear Wheel Speed Sensor A Range/Performance","C050D says the left rear signal exists but is not trustworthy. In GM's 23OBDG07 tables several checks share this code: a weak magnetic flux under 2.2 mT across at least five wheel turns (detected after 8 s at 3.1 mph or 22 s at 1.24 mph), missing standstill pulses for 3.6 s, and an undervoltage on the sensor supply; all are Type B with two trips, and the tables list Bosch, Continental and DF11i sensor variants.",["Air gap to the rear encoder too large (sensor not seated, worn or loose hub bearing)","Contact resistance or leakage in the rear sensor wiring","Left rear tire differs in rolling circumference","Control module software sets the code falsely (Stellantis reflash)"],["ABS and stability lamps come on only after some driving","Stability or traction control intervenes without reason at low speed","Code may be stored without a lit MIL on some Stellantis models"],2,3,["C050C","C050E","C050F","C0510","C0511","C0513","C051A","C0557"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי שמאלי‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C050E:["Left Rear Wheel Speed Sensor A Circuit Low","C050E reports the left rear sensor circuit pulled below its expected level. GM's 2019 EBCM tables (19OBDG03D) let the Polaris ASIC set it for three separate findings: an open sensor bit, a grounded low side, looked for only at start-up or once codes have been cleared, and sensor undervoltage, which needs only 20 ms; all are Type A with the MIL.",["Sensor wire grounded against the subframe or body","Moisture or corrosion in the left rear connector","Left rear sensor shorted internally","Low supply voltage at the brake module (fuse, battery)"],["ABS, stability and electric parking brake warnings on (Mitsubishi)","ABS and stability control disabled for the rest of the trip"],2,3,["C050C","C050D","C050F","C0510","C0511","C0514","C0038"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי שמאלי‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],C050F:["Left Rear Wheel Speed Sensor A Circuit High","C050F covers the opposite electrical case: the left rear circuit sits too high, as when the signal wire touches a battery-fed conductor. For GM's 2016 hybrids, 12 V surpassed on the signal wire for 0.12 s, with more than 6.9 V system voltage, is the trigger; the 2023 tables instead look at current and flag a signal wire carrying over 50 mA, again within 0.12 s and as Type A.",["Signal wire shorted to a battery-fed circuit in the rear loom","Left rear sensor draws excessive current internally","Brake module input stage defective"],["ABS and stability lamps on immediately, MIL on some makes","No ABS regulation, rear brake force distribution in fallback mode"],2,3,["C050C","C050D","C050E","C0510","C0511","C0515"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי שמאלי‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],C0510:["Left Rear Wheel Speed Sensor A Intermittent/Erratic","C0510 flags a left rear speed signal that jumps instead of changing smoothly. GM's 19OBDG03D EBCM logic counts every moment in which the unfiltered wheel acceleration exceeds 491 m/s² at vehicle speeds beyond 3.58 m/s and sets the code once that tally reaches 40 s; a second path latches it within 25 ms when more than 55 edges arrive too quickly.",["Sensor loose in its bore or play in the rear wheel bearing","Missing or damaged teeth, rust flakes on the tone ring","Wire breaking up intermittently as the rear suspension moves","Heavy payload or trailer on rough roads (Ram 3500 case)"],["ABS or stability lamp on after bumps, railway crossings or rumble strips","Brief, unexpected ABS pulsing at the rear","Fault often gone after the next ignition cycle"],2,3,["C050C","C050D","C050E","C050F","C0511","C0516","C051A","C0037"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי שמאלי‏ A — אות לא יציב"],C0511:["Left Rear Wheel Speed Sensor A Correlation","C0511 means the left rear speed does not match what the other three wheels report. In GM's 19OBDG03D tables four monitors feed it: missing sensor (this wheel below 1.5 km/h while the rest exceed 6 km/h, 3 to 120 s), dropout (no edges for 150 ms after a valid reading above 30 km/h, with thresholds that depend on axle and brake pedal), fast missing (counted from key-on until 15 km/h is first reached) and too fast…",["Left rear tire of a different size or heavily worn compared with the others","Demagnetized encoder or damaged tone ring at the left rear","Wrong sensor fitted after a repair (GM PIT5950)"],["ABS and stability lamps on after setting off or at moderate speed","Speedometer and driver aids act up after a tire change"],1,3,["C050C","C050D","C050E","C050F","C0510","C0517","C051A"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי שמאלי‏ A — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],C0512:["Right Rear Wheel Speed Sensor A Circuit/Open","C0512 is the open-circuit code for the right rear wheel. GM's 2016 hybrid tables run the check only after the sensor self-test has finished and system voltage is above 6.9 V; then 0.12 s with less than 3.8 mA flowing in the signal wire is enough for a Type A entry. The XT4 section of GM's 2019 tables words the same test as a ground short or interruption and monitors the supply line separately.",["Broken lead or unplugged connector at the right rear","Right rear sensor open internally","Fuse or power feed of the brake module (Mitsubishi lists it)"],["ABS and stability lamps on at key-on, sometimes the MIL","Right rear wheel speed reads zero in live data","ABS and traction control unavailable"],2,3,["C0513","C0514","C0515","C0516","C0517","C050C","C003A"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי ימני‏ A — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C0513:["Right Rear Wheel Speed Sensor A Range/Performance","C0513 marks a right rear signal that is present but implausible. GM's 2016 hybrid tables catch two patterns: the wheel shows 0 mph while the other three turn and the car exceeds 11.8 mph, and a start-up check in which the right rear stays at zero while the others pass 7.45 mph; both mature at once as Type A, but not during ABS or traction control action.",["Excessive air gap or damaged encoder at the right rear","ABS harness rubbing on the rear drive unit (2024 Silverado EV)","Right rear tire of a different size","False setting by control module software (Stellantis)"],["ABS lamp with a service stability message","Lamps come on after driving off, not at key-on","Code stored without MIL on some Stellantis models"],2,3,["C0512","C0514","C0515","C0516","C0517","C050D","C051B","C0558"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי ימני‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0514:["Right Rear Wheel Speed Sensor A Circuit Low","C0514 reports the right rear sensor circuit below its valid range. GM's 2025 EBCM tables (25OBDG04A) show how broadly that is read: the Polaris ASIC raises an open-sensor bit when the high-side current drops under 3.5 mA, and a separate bit for a low side shorted to ground, both after 100 ms as Type A; the listed suspects run from sensor and harness to the printed circuit board and the ASIC.",["Harness worn through and grounded near the rear axle or drive unit","Right rear sensor defective","Brake module circuit board or ASIC faulty (GM lists it)"],["ABS lamp and service stability message","Electric parking brake warning on some models (Mitsubishi)","ABS and stability control switched off"],2,3,["C0512","C0513","C0515","C0516","C0517","C050E","C003B"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי ימני‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],C0515:["Right Rear Wheel Speed Sensor A Circuit High","C0515 says the right rear sensor circuit draws or sees too much. GM's 2025 tables bundle four ASIC flags under this code: high-side current above 40 mA, high side shorted to battery, low-side overcurrent and, perhaps unexpectedly, a low side shorted to ground; each sets it after 100 ms as Type A. The 2023 tables keep it simpler: 50 mA exceeded for 0.12 s in the signal wire.",["Insulation damage in the right rear harness causing a short","Right rear sensor shorted internally","Sensor supply stage in the brake module defective"],["ABS and stability lamps on as soon as the self-test ends","Stability and traction control unavailable"],2,3,["C0512","C0513","C0514","C0516","C0517","C050F","C05A3"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי ימני‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],C0516:["Right Rear Wheel Speed Sensor A Intermittent/Erratic","C0516 stands for a right rear signal that stutters or spikes. GM's 2025 tables use the 491 m/s² wheel acceleration limit at speeds beyond 3.58 m/s but let the fault mature in about 200 ms of near-continuous violation, sampled every 5 ms, and decay the counter when the signal calms; the 2016 hybrid tables instead set it after a 0.03 s overflow of the timer buffer that stores sensor edges.",["Damaged tone ring teeth or loosely mounted right rear sensor","Rear axle vibration disturbing the signal (GM program 18316)","Harness chafing intermittently (2024 Silverado EV)","Brake module calibration too sensitive, update available"],["ABS, stability and traction lamps after rough road sections","Functions return only after the next ignition cycle"],2,3,["C0512","C0513","C0514","C0515","C0517","C0510","C051B","C003A"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי ימני‏ A — אות לא יציב"],C0517:["Right Rear Wheel Speed Sensor A Correlation","C0517 reports that the right rear speed disagrees with the rest of the vehicle. GM's 2025 tables (25OBDG04A) run missing, dropout, fast-missing and too-fast checks for this wheel; the missing-sensor test, a wheel under 1.5 km/h while others exceed 6 km/h, is rated Type B there, i.e. MIL after two trips.",["Right rear tire not matching the others in size or wear","Weak encoder or excessive air gap at the right rear","Wrong sensor installed during an earlier repair","Sensor supply driver inside the brake module faulty (GM)"],["ABS and stability lamps after driving off or at moderate speed","Code returns after sensor replacement if the true cause is elsewhere"],2,3,["C0512","C0513","C0514","C0515","C0516","C0511","C051B"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי ימני‏ A — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],C0518:["Left Front Wheel Speed Sensor - Mechanical","C0518 points to a mechanical rather than electrical problem at the left front speed sensor: wrong part, wrong position, a damaged or soiled encoder, or play in the hub. No manufacturer documents this exact code publicly; GM's tables and Mitsubishi's index file such faults under range or correlation codes instead. The mechanics are well described elsewhere.",["Magnetic encoder or tone ring dirty, cracked or missing teeth","Sensor for the other side fitted or tip turned away from the encoder","Worn or loose left front hub bearing changing the air gap"],["ABS and stability lamps on, often recurring after a repair","Uneven or missing left front speed reading at low speed"],2,2,["C0519","C051A","C051B","C0501","C0505","C0555"],""],C0519:["Right Front Wheel Speed Sensor - Mechanical","C0519 is the mechanical-fault code for the right front sensor. It appears in code lists, but no manufacturer publishes a setting rule for it; the known diagnostics put such faults under range, erratic or correlation codes.",["Metal debris or rust buildup on the right front reluctor ring","Sensor not fully seated or bracket bent, air gap too large","Right front hub bearing worn"],["ABS lamp and stability service message","ABS may regulate unexpectedly at walking pace"],2,2,["C0518","C051A","C051B","C0507","C050A","C0556"],""],C051A:["Left Rear Wheel Speed Sensor - Mechanical","C051A names a mechanical fault at the left rear sensor. Like its siblings it is listed but not documented by any manufacturer, so the actual setting rule is unknown. At the rear axle the encoder sits in different places: inside the hub bearing seal on many cars, as HELLA describes for multipole rings, or on the axle shaft or hub of rigid axles.",["Metal particles or rust on the rear encoder or sensor tip","Rear tone ring bent or cracked, often after hub or brake work","Left rear hub bearing worn, encoder seal damaged"],["ABS lamp, sometimes only under load or on rough roads","Rear wheel speed drops out or jitters in live data"],2,2,["C051B","C0518","C0519","C050D","C0510","C0511","C0037"],""],C051B:["Right Rear Wheel Speed Sensor - Mechanical","C051B covers a mechanical defect at the right rear wheel. No public manufacturer document defines when it is set; the cases known from bulletins carry other codes. They still show what to inspect at a right rear wheel.",["Right rear tone ring deformed or corroded","Right rear hub bearing loose or worn","Axle vibration disturbing the signal on rough surfaces"],["ABS, stability and traction lamps after rough stretches","Driver aids unavailable until the next ignition cycle"],2,2,["C051A","C0518","C0519","C0513","C0516","C0517","C003A"],""],C051C:["Multi-axis Acceleration Sensor Module A Range/Performance","Module A delivers yaw rate and accelerations along several axes, but at least one channel sits outside what the vehicle's motion allows, for example a turn rate while parked or a lateral g that does not fit speed and steering. No manufacturer documents C051C publicly, so exact limits are unknown.",["Module A loose, tilted or mounted on a deformed bracket","Internal offset of the inertial sensor drifted beyond tolerance","Defective sensing element inside module A","Wrong module variant fitted or installed in the wrong orientation"],["ESC or traction control warning lamp on","Stability control unavailable or intervening without reason","Yaw rate or acceleration not zero at standstill (scan tool)"],2,2,["C051D","C051E","C051F","C0520","C0521","C006A"],""],C051D:["Multi-axis Acceleration Sensor Module A Missing Calibration","The module holds no valid zero point or mounting orientation, typically after it or the brake controller was replaced and the setup step was skipped. Corrections like these live in non-volatile memory: Kelsey-Hayes measures the offset of the whole assembly on a turning stand and adds the in-car tilt.",["Module A or brake control module replaced without configuration and yaw sensor learn","Learn procedure aborted, e.g. vehicle not level or voltage dropped","Stored calibration lost after software update or module fault"],["ESC warning lamp on right after a repair","Stability and traction control unavailable","Driver assistance such as adaptive cruise may be disabled"],2,2,["C051C","C051E","C051F","C0520","C0522"],""],C051E:["Multi-axis Acceleration Sensor Module A Intermittent/Erratic","Module A's data arrive, but values jump, freeze briefly or vanish for short moments instead of changing smoothly. Modern units digitise yaw rate and accelerations inside the module and pass them on over a serial link: Bosch's SMI810 uses SafeSPI with 16-bit data, and a Hyundai/Kia design checks each value against the sensor's measuring range before sending it over CAN to the stability controller.",["Loose or corroded connector at module A","Brief supply or ground dropouts, weak battery","Module not firmly fastened, picks up vibration","Sporadic internal fault of the sensor electronics"],["ESC warning lamp comes and goes","Stability control occasionally unavailable","Jumping yaw or acceleration values in live data"],2,2,["C051C","C051D","C051F","C0520","C0523"],""],C051F:["Multi-axis Acceleration Sensor Module A Correlation","The brake controller finds that module A's signals do not agree with a second source of the same motion. Audi uses this code on the e-tron: the ABS unit (address 0003) stores C051F00, and Audi's 2019 bulletin names the suspension control module as sensor module A. Waking the bus while the car falls asleep could set it, along with implausible lateral acceleration and yaw codes and a lost airbag-unit message;",["ABS or suspension control software fault (Audi e-tron update)","Bus woken while modules enter sleep mode (door, charger)","Module A misaligned so its axes no longer match the reference","Fault in the comparison source (second inertial sensor, steering angle, wheel speeds)"],["ESC warning lamp and several cluster messages","Yellow drive fault message (Audi e-tron)","Fault often gone after the next ignition cycle"],2,2,["C051C","C051E","C0520","C0524","C05B2"],""],C0520:["Multi-axis Acceleration Sensor Module A","General fault of module A without a narrower fault type. GM gives the most detail: in the 2023 and 2025 OBD tables of its Super Cruise controller (EOCM3), C0520 watches the high-performance IMU and sets when initialisation does not finish in time, the unit resets, its temperature status is invalid, offset or orientation learning is missing, or a swapped IMU is detected via its serial number.",["IMU fails to initialise in time or resets during operation","Module swapped, offset or orientation calibration not learned","Software fault in the module or the receiving controller","Internal electronic failure of module A"],["ESC warning lamp or service message for stability control","Adaptive cruise or hands-free driving assistance unavailable (GM)","No check-engine lamp"],3,2,["C051C","C051D","C051E","C051F","C0525","C006A"],""],C0521:["Multi-axis Acceleration Sensor Module B Range/Performance","Same fault type as C051C, but for a second inertial module B: its rates or accelerations lie outside what driving physics permits. No manufacturer explains C0521 publicly, and which unit is B on a given car is not documented either. A second unit is common on vehicles with automated driving, where Bosch offers IMUs up to two-fold ASIL-D and stresses redundancy.",["Module B loose, tilted or bracket bent after a repair or impact","Bias of the accelerometers or gyros drifted out of tolerance","Defective sensing element inside module B"],["Driver assistance or ESC warning message","Adaptive cruise or lane functions unavailable","Module B reading not zero at standstill (scan tool)"],2,2,["C051C","C0522","C0523","C0524","C0525"],""],C0522:["Multi-axis Acceleration Sensor Module B Missing Calibration","Module B lacks its stored zero point or installation data, so its readings cannot be trusted. No manufacturer publishes C0522, and which unit carries the letter B is not documented. A Hyundai/Kia design that moves the inertial sensor into the airbag control unit applies offset correction inside the sensor according to the vehicle set-up and keeps data in one-time-programmable memory;",["Module B or its host control unit replaced without configuration","Vehicle variant or mounting position coded incorrectly","Calibration data lost after software update"],["Warning message appears directly after a repair","Assistance or stability functions unavailable"],2,2,["C051D","C0521","C0523","C0524","C0525"],""],C0523:["Multi-axis Acceleration Sensor Module B Intermittent/Erratic","Module B sends values that jump or drop out now and then. No manufacturer publishes C0523, so limits and the identity of module B stay open. GM bulletins show that a separate multi-axis module is a networked unit of its own: on 2013 to 2014 Malibu, LaCrosse and Regal it logs U0121 in history at key-up because the brake module answers late, which GM calls normal, and on 2018 to 2020 Equinox and Terrain U0125 for a…",["Loose or corroded connector or ground at module B","Supply dips from a weak battery or poor connections","Sporadic internal fault in module B"],["Assistance or ESC warning comes and goes","Code stored in history without current fault","Jumping values from module B in live data"],2,2,["C051E","C0521","C0522","C0524","C0525","U0125"],""],C0524:["Multi-axis Acceleration Sensor Module B Correlation","Module B's readings disagree with another source for the same motion, most likely module A or values computed from steering angle and wheel speeds. No manufacturer publishes C0524; Audi documents only the A counterpart.",["Module A or B rotated on its mount after repair or impact","Drifting sensor in one of the two modules","Software or timing fault in the comparing controller"],["ESC or assistance warning message","Stability or assistance functions limited"],3,2,["C051F","C0521","C0522","C0523","C0525"],""],C0525:["Multi-axis Acceleration Sensor Module B","General fault of module B, without stating whether range, calibration, signal stability or correlation is at fault. No manufacturer publishes C0525, and the location of module B is not documented. According to Bosch, one inertial unit can feed stability control as well as the airbag electronics, and an integrated version exists;",["Software fault, fixed by an update of the host module","Internal electronic failure of module B","Supply or ground fault at module B"],["ESC, airbag-related or assistance warning depending on host module","Stability or assistance functions unavailable"],3,2,["C0520","C0521","C0522","C0523","C0524","C006A"],""],C0526:["Steering Angle Sensor Module","C0526 is the base code for the steering angle sensor module, used when a fault is reported without a more specific failure type. MINI documents it for the 2017 Countryman F60 plug-in hybrid: an on-board diagnosis error in the electric power steering software stored C0526, readable only with a generic OBD tool, and lit the check-engine lamp.",["Power steering software error (MINI F60 PHEV 2017)","Supply loss or battery disconnection without relearning","Internal fault in the steering angle sensor module"],["Check-engine lamp on (MINI F60 PHEV)","ESC warning lamp on, stability control limited"],2,3,["C0527","C0528","C0529","C052A","U0126"],"מודול חיישן זווית הגה"],C0527:["Steering Angle Sensor Module Mechanical","C0527 marks a mechanical rather than electrical fault of the steering angle sensor module. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. Many sensors are gear-driven: Bosch and Saab describe a hub gear on the steering shaft turning two measuring gears with different tooth counts (28 and 26 on the Saab 9-5), whose magnet positions encode the absolute angle.",["Worn or broken measuring gears inside the sensor","Sensor drive dog or mounting loose on the steering shaft","Sensor installed out of position after column or clock spring work"],["ESC warning lamp on","Angle on the scan tool jumps or stops changing while steering","Possible noise from the steering column"],2,2,["C0526","C0528","C0529","C052A"],"מכני מודול חיישן זווית הגה"],C0528:["Steering Angle Sensor Module Range/Performance","C0528 means the module delivers an angle that is out of range or behaves implausibly while it still communicates. Audi documents it on the 2015–2018 A3 e-tron as C052800, steering angle sender with implausible signal, sometimes stored together with P060700 after ESC had been switched off (TSB 2060682/1); the ESC lamp lights.",["Steering angle sensor module delivering implausible values","ABS/ESC module software issue (Audi A3 e-tron)","Offset after alignment or steering work without re-zeroing"],["ESC warning lamp on","Stability control unavailable or intervening at odd moments"],2,2,["C0526","C0527","C0529","C052A","C0608"],"מודול חיישן זווית הגה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0529:["Steering Angle Sensor Module Missing Calibration","C0529 is set when the steering angle sensor module has no valid zero point. Stellantis documents it as C0529-00 on the 2023 Dodge Hornet and the 2023–2024 Alfa Romeo Tonale: if the wheel was turned without assist between key-off and key-on, the calibration was lost and the MIL came on, going out again after a lock-to-lock turn; an EPS software update fixes it (TSB 08-148-23, 08-163-23).",["Calibration lost after battery disconnection or steering while switched off","Initialisation skipped after steering gear, sensor or alignment work","EPS software losing the calibration (Stellantis 2023–2024)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on (Stellantis)","ESC warning lamp on, stability control limited until calibrated","Lamp goes out after turning the wheel from lock to lock"],1,3,["C0526","C0527","C0528","C052A","C0445"],"מודול חיישן זווית הגה — חסר כיול"],C052A:["Steering Angle Sensor Module Correlation","The steering angle sensor module reports wheel angle and turn rate to the stability control unit, which cross-checks that value against an independent estimate. Correlation means the reading and the estimate disagree for longer than the calibrated window; the signal itself is present.",["Angle offset after wheel alignment or steering work without zero-point adjustment","Internal fault in the steering angle sensor module","Faulty comparison signal (yaw rate, wheel speed or steering angle from power steering)"],["ESC or traction control warning lamp on","Stability control switched off or intervening at the wrong moment","Steering wheel off-centre when driving straight"],2,2,["C0526","C0528","C0529","C05B2"],"מודול חיישן זווית הגה — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],C052B:["ABS Pump Motor Control Range/Performance","Range/performance fault of the ABS pump motor: the drive is commanded, but the motor or its relay does not behave as expected. On the 2023 Mitsubishi Outlander PHEV the brake unit maps C1051-04 (and C1051-49, added by bulletin TSB-23-35-002) to C052B; it is checked with normal supply voltage, set within 12 s; after a single trip the ASC, ABS and brake warnings plus the check-engine lamp come on.",["Pump motor worn (brushes) or pump seized in the hydraulic unit","Motor relay or switching stage in the ABS unit faulty","Marginal supply or ground connection under motor load"],["ABS, ESC and brake warning lamps on","ABS and stability control unavailable, normal braking remains","No pump noise during the self-test after starting off"],3,3,["C052C","C052D","C052E","C0020"],"בקרת מנוע משאבת ABS — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C052C:["ABS Pump Motor Control Circuit/Open","Open circuit in the ABS pump motor drive: the control unit finds no current path through motor or relay where one should exist. Mitsubishi lists C1051-13 as C052C on the 2023 Outlander PHEV within the same frame as C052B (normal supply, up to 12 s, ABS, ASC, brake and engine lamps after one trip, stability and regenerative braking functions off).",["Loose or corroded connector at the ABS unit","Worn brushes or open winding in the pump motor","Motor relay contact not closing"],["ABS and ESC warning lamps on","ABS, traction and stability control switched off","Code returns only after a short drive"],3,3,["C052B","C052D","C052E","C052F"],"מנוע משאבת ABS — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],C052D:["ABS Pump Motor Control Circuit High","The pump motor control circuit reads higher than the commanded state allows, which normally means the control line or motor terminal is shorted toward battery voltage or the switching stage is stuck on. No manufacturer publishes this code; Mitsubishi, for example, reports its pump motor faults under C052B and C052C.",["Motor relay or semiconductor switch in the ABS unit stuck closed","Motor lead or control line shorted to battery voltage","Moisture bridging pins in the ABS connector"],["ABS warning lamp on","Pump motor runs continuously or hums with ignition on","Battery discharged after standing"],3,2,["C052B","C052C","C052E"],"מנוע משאבת ABS — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],C052E:["ABS Pump Motor Control Circuit Low","Low counterpart of C052D: the pump motor control signal stays near ground when it should rise, pointing to a short to ground on the control side, a failed driver stage or a weak ground path of the hydraulic unit. No maker documents C052E publicly. In the Bosch patent US5329238 a terminal below the lower threshold is treated as a short to minus, and the drive is limited or switched off.",["Poor ground connection of the ABS unit or hydraulic block","Control line or motor lead shorted to ground","Driver stage in the ABS control unit failed"],["ABS and ESC warning lamps on","ABS and stability control unavailable"],3,2,["C052D","C052C","C0020"],"מנוע משאבת ABS — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],C052F:["ABS Pump Motor Supply Voltage Circuit/Open","The pump motor has its own battery feed, separate from the logic supply, and this code reports that feed as missing or open. Mitsubishi's 2023 Outlander PHEV manual shows the layout: motor and motor relay draw from a 60 A fusible link and must see 10–16 V at the unit connector, the valves from a separate 50 A link, the electronics from a 5 A fuse.",["Pump motor fuse or fusible link blown","Corroded or loose battery feed terminal at the ABS connector","Open or high-resistance ground of the ABS unit"],["ABS and ESC warning lamps on","Pump motor never runs, ABS and stability control off"],2,2,["C055A","C055B","C055C","C052C"],"מתח אספקה מנוע משאבת ABS — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C0530:["Motor Control A Range/Performance","Plausibility fault of motor control A: the circuit is electrically intact, but the motor does not answer its command as the module expects – it stalls, runs too slowly or keeps turning. SAE J2012 lists the code in the chassis block beside the ABS pump motor and valve codes without naming the motor, and no manufacturer was found that publicly assigns it, so which drive counts as A stays open.",["Motor or driven mechanism stiff or seized","Worn motor (brushes, bearings) delivering too little speed","Fault in the control unit's motor stage or feedback evaluation"],["Chassis or brake warning lamp on","The function driven by motor A is unavailable"],3,2,["C0531","C0535"],"בקרת מנוע חשמלי‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0531:["Motor Control A Circuit/Open","Motor control A sees an open circuit: with the stage switched off, the module cannot detect the expected current path through the motor. J2012 names no specific motor and no public manufacturer assignment was found, so the actuator behind A depends on the vehicle.",["Connector to motor A unplugged or corroded","Broken motor lead in the harness","Open winding or worn brush in motor A"],["Warning lamp of the affected system on","Motor A does not run at all"],2,2,["C0530","C0532","C0533","C0536"],"בקרת מנוע חשמלי‏ A — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C0532:["Motor Control A Circuit High","Motor control A reads high: a motor output sits near supply voltage although the driver commands it low or off. That points to a short to battery voltage in the motor leads or a high-side switch that no longer opens. J2012 leaves the motor unnamed and no manufacturer publication assigning C0532 was found.",["Motor lead chafed against a live wire","High-side switch in the control unit stuck on","Moisture bridging pins in the connector"],["Warning lamp of the affected system on","Motor A runs on or gets hot"],2,2,["C0531","C0533","C0537"],"בקרת מנוע חשמלי‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],C0533:["Motor Control A Circuit Low","Motor control A reads low: an output that should be driven up stays close to ground. Typical reasons are chafed motor wiring touching the body, water in a connector or a failed low-side stage; a stalled motor drawing excess current can look similar to the driver. The J2012 title gives no motor, and no maker was found that documents C0533, so the A assignment remains vehicle-specific.",["Motor lead chafed through to body ground","Water ingress in the motor connector","Low-side stage in the control unit failed"],["Warning lamp of the affected system on","Motor A does not start; a fuse may blow"],2,2,["C0531","C0532","C0538"],"בקרת מנוע חשמלי‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],C0534:["Motor Control A Supply Voltage Circuit/Open","The power feed of motor control A is missing or open, so the driver stage has nothing to switch even though the logic side of the module is alive. Chassis motors often get a dedicated battery feed: in the brake unit of the 2023 Mitsubishi Outlander PHEV, for example, the pump motor hangs on its own 60 A fusible link and needs 10–16 V at the connector. Driver ICs watch this rail as well;",["Fuse or fusible link of the motor feed blown","Open feed wire or loose supply terminal","Missing ground of the control unit's power stage"],["Warning lamp of the affected system on","Motor A never runs while other functions of the module work"],2,2,["C0531","C0539"],"מתח אספקה בקרת מנוע חשמלי‏ A — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C0535:["Motor Control B Range/Performance","Second motor channel B fails its plausibility check: wiring and supply test fine, yet the motor's reaction to commands is wrong, for example too little speed, a delayed start or no stop. Where a controller drives two motors or two channels, A and B separate them; J2012 does not say which motor B is, and no manufacturer publicly assigns C0535, so the meaning must come from the vehicle's own service data.",["Driven mechanism of motor B binding or blocked","Motor B worn and too slow","Faulty speed or position feedback in the control unit"],["Warning lamp of the affected system on","Function of motor B slow, incomplete or unavailable"],3,2,["C0536","C0530"],"בקרת מנוע חשמלי‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0536:["Motor Control B Circuit/Open","Motor control B finds its load missing. The module expects a closed path through the windings of channel B and sees an open circuit instead – a pulled connector, a cut lead, corroded pins or an internal break in the motor. Brake controllers have run dedicated open-circuit routines for pump motors for decades, as in a Kelsey-Hayes patent (now ZF) that checks the motor circuit while the pump is not requested;",["Connector to motor B pulled off or pins corroded","Motor lead cut or broken in the harness","Internal break in motor B (winding, brush)"],["Warning lamp of the affected system on","Motor B shows no reaction"],2,2,["C0535","C0537","C0538","C0531"],"בקרת מנוע חשמלי‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C0537:["Motor Control B Circuit High","Channel B of the motor control reads high, meaning a motor terminal is pulled toward battery voltage against the command. A pinched lead touching a live wire, moisture bridging pins in a shared connector, or a high-side switch stuck in the conducting state are the usual suspects.",["Pinched motor B lead contacting a live wire","Moisture between pins of a shared connector","High-side switch for channel B not opening"],["Warning lamp of the affected system on","Motor B runs on briefly or the function is switched off"],2,2,["C0536","C0538","C0532"],"בקרת מנוע חשמלי‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],C0538:["Motor Control B Circuit Low","Motor control B reads low: a channel-B output is held near ground. Besides a direct short of a motor lead to the body, the Bosch patent US5329238 also covers the case where both terminals deviate at once while driven, which it reads as a short across the motor itself or between its two lines.",["Motor B lead shorted to body near moving parts","Short across motor B or between its two lines","Water in the connector of motor B"],["Warning lamp of the affected system on","Motor B does not start"],2,2,["C0536","C0537","C0533"],"בקרת מנוע חשמלי‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],C0539:["Motor Control B Supply Voltage Circuit/Open","Motor control B has lost its power supply, or the supply circuit is open. In many brake and chassis controllers the motor stage is fed by its own fused battery line while the logic runs from ignition, so the module can still communicate and store this code.",["Fuse or fusible link of the channel B feed open","Loose or corroded supply connector","Weak 12 V battery pulling the motor supply below the limit"],["Warning lamp of the affected system on","Motor B never runs although the module communicates"],2,2,["C0536","C0534"],"מתח אספקה בקרת מנוע חשמלי‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C053A:["ABS Valves Missing Calibration","The brake control unit holds no valid calibration for its ABS valves. Analog-controlled inlet valves open at a current that depends on the pressure difference, manufacturing scatter and wear, so the controller needs a stored opening-current curve to meter pressure finely.",["ABS control unit or hydraulic unit replaced without valve calibration","Calibration run aborted (low voltage, air in the system, conditions not met)","Software update or memory fault erased the calibration data"],["ABS and ESC warning lamps on","ABS and stability control limited or switched off"],4,2,["C053B","C062D","C0529"],""],C053B:["ABS Valves Supply Voltage Circuit/Open","Supply fault on the ABS solenoid valves: the feed that powers the inlet and outlet valves, usually switched through a valve relay inside the brake unit, is missing or open. On the 2023 Mitsubishi Outlander PHEV the code is C1048-11 (valve relay), shown as C053B; it is checked with normal supply, set within 2 s, and lights ASC, ABS, brake and check-engine lamps after one trip.",["Valve relay inside the ABS unit faulty","Fusible link of the valve supply blown","Damaged or loose terminal in the ABS connector"],["ABS, ESC and brake warning lamps on","ABS, stability control and electric parking brake functions unavailable"],3,3,["C053A","C062D","C052F"],""],C053C:["Wheel Speed Sensor Generic Range/Performance","A wheel speed signal is implausible, but the fault is reported generically rather than for one named wheel. Mitsubishi uses C106A-64 as C053C on the 2023 Outlander PHEV and runs four detection paths, one per sensor, each with a delay of at most 1 s; listed causes include the sensor, its rotor and a wrong tire size, and the code needs two trips before ASC, ABS, brake, parking brake and check-engine lamps light.",["Mismatched tire sizes or a space-saver spare fitted","Damaged or dirty encoder ring (sensor rotor)","Wheel speed sensor faulty or not seated correctly"],["ABS, ESC and brake warning lamps on after two trips","ABS, traction control and stability control switched off","Speed-dependent assistance functions unavailable"],2,3,["C0500","C0506","C050C","C0512","C0555"],""],C053D:["Brake Pressure Sensor A Range/Performance","The brake pressure sensor A signal is electrically present, but its value does not fit the braking situation. GM stores C053D in the brake system control module, calling it a circuit performance fault: on 2019 Silverado/Sierra 1500 drivers got a hard pedal plus the Service Brake Assist warning (PIT5638), and bulletin 20-NA-073 lists it among faults that drop the brake-by-wire system into its mechanical Push-Thru…",["Brake or engine control software with an over-sensitive plausibility check (several bulletins)","Pressure and pedal sensors not initialized after module or hydraulic unit replacement","Air in the brake lines distorting the pressure build-up","Stop-light switch or pedal sensor delivering a mismatching reference","Drifting pressure sensor in the hydraulic unit"],["Brake assist or stability control warning shown","Brake pedal hard or travelling further than usual","Check-engine lamp on some models"],3,3,["C053E","C053F","C0540","C0541","C0044","C058E"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C053E:["Brake Pressure Sensor A Circuit Low","The voltage on the signal line of brake pressure sensor A has dropped under the lower limit the brake module accepts. Such ratiometric 5-V sensors normally stay within a window: an older Saab 9-5 brake unit faults its pressure sensor below 0.25 V held for 0.1 s. Usual triggers are a signal wire shorted to ground, a lost 5-V feed or a sensor failing internally.",["Signal wire chafed through and touching ground","Missing or weak 5-V reference to the sensor","Module software flagging the sensor during start-up warm-up (GM HD trucks 2024)","Pressure sensor failed internally"],["ABS or stability control warning lamp lit","Message in the driver display right after start-up","Stability, traction control or brake assist switched off"],2,3,["C053D","C053F","C0540","C0542"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],C053F:["Brake Pressure Sensor A Circuit High","Brake pressure sensor A reports a voltage above the upper limit of its valid band. Since the sensor is fed with 5 V, a short of the signal line to the reference or to battery voltage, a broken ground wire or an internal fault can push the reading up; a Saab 9-5 brake unit draws the line at 4.75 V lasting 0.1 s.",["Signal wire shorted to the 5-V reference or battery voltage","Open or corroded sensor ground","Pressure sensor in the hydraulic unit defective"],["ABS and stability control warning lamps on","Traction control, stability control and hill-start assist unavailable","Check-engine lamp on some hybrids"],2,3,["C053D","C053E","C0540","C0543"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],C0540:["Brake Pressure Sensor A Circuit/Open","General electrical fault in the circuit of brake pressure sensor A, typically an interrupted signal, reference or ground wire, or a connection with excessive resistance. No manufacturer documents this exact code publicly; Mitsubishi, for example, maps its sensor-A faults to C0044 and C053D to C053F instead.",["Loose, corroded or pushed-out pin at the sensor or brake module connector","Broken signal, reference or ground wire","Internal open circuit in the pressure sensor"],["ABS and ESC warning lamps on","Stability and traction control out of service","Brake assist or hill-start assist missing"],2,2,["C053D","C053E","C053F","C0544"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ A — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C0541:["Brake Pressure Sensor B Range/Performance","Brake pressure sensor B delivers a valid voltage, yet the value is implausible. Which sensor carries the letter B varies by maker. Bentley documents the code for the Continental GT/GTC (2018–2022) and Flying Spur (2020–2022): C054100 in the ESC unit J104 is labelled as a fault of the rear-left pressure sensor, adaptive cruise control becomes unavailable, and the repair is a new J104 because the sensor is built into…",["Pressure sensor inside the ESC hydraulic unit drifting or sluggish","Zero-point calibration not done after module or valve block replacement","Brake light switch or pedal sensor giving a contradictory reference"],["Adaptive cruise control unavailable","ESC or ABS warning in the cluster","Assistance functions such as brake assist reduced"],3,2,["C0542","C0543","C0544","C053D"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0542:["Brake Pressure Sensor B Circuit Low","Brake pressure sensor B pulls its signal below the lowest voltage the receiving module treats as valid. Two makers name the code in public bulletins. Bentley lists C054200 in the ESC unit J104 of the Continental GT/GTC and Flying Spur alongside C054100, with adaptive cruise switched off and the J104 replaced.",["Signal line shorted to ground","Sensor or the ESC unit with integrated sensor defective","Engine control software misjudging the signal (Jeep Cherokee 2019)","5-V sensor supply dragged down"],["Check-engine or ESC warning lamp on","Adaptive cruise control or stop-start unavailable"],2,3,["C0541","C0543","C0544","C053E"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],C0543:["Brake Pressure Sensor B Circuit High","Here the signal of brake pressure sensor B sits above the top of its permitted range, which points to a signal wire touching the 5-V reference or battery voltage, an open sensor ground, or a sensor that has failed high.",["Signal wire shorted to reference or battery voltage","Sensor ground open or high resistance","Engine control software fault (Jeep Cherokee 2019 bulletins)","Sensor failed with permanently high output"],["Check-engine lamp on","Stop-start or brake-related assistance not working"],2,3,["C0541","C0542","C0544","C053F"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],C0544:["Brake Pressure Sensor B Circuit/Open","The brake module sees a general electrical fault in the circuit of pressure sensor B, usually an interruption in signal, feed or ground. No maker publishes this exact meaning; note that GM bulletins use C0544 for a different, steering-related fault in its power steering module, so a GM scan result must be read with GM definitions.",["Connector at sensor or brake module loose or corroded","Interrupted signal, feed or ground wire","Open inside the sensor or the ESC unit carrying it"],["ABS, traction and stability warning lamps on","Driver assistance relying on brake pressure unavailable"],2,2,["C0541","C0542","C0543","C0540"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C0545:["VIN Not Programmed or Incompatible - BSCM","The brake system control module (BSCM) holds no vehicle identification number, or one that does not belong to the car it is fitted to. Modules store the VIN in non-volatile memory; GM patents describe a replacement module comparing its own stored VIN with the one held by another control unit and running a configuration routine when they differ, and point out that a swapped or tampered module shows up as a VIN…",["New brake module installed without VIN programming","Used module from another vehicle still carrying its old VIN","Programming session interrupted, for example by low battery voltage"],["ABS or ESC warning lamp on after a module replacement","Brake-related functions limited or disabled"],4,2,["C0546","P0630","P0631"],""],C0546:["VIN Not Programmed or Incompatible","Generic variant without a named module: a chassis control unit reports that its stored vehicle identification number is blank or does not match the car. Which unit sets it is left to the maker, so the scan tool entry shows the module concerned. The principle is documented in GM patents: each unit keeps the VIN in memory, possibly in write-once storage set at the factory;",["Replacement chassis module not programmed with the vehicle VIN","Second-hand module carrying a foreign VIN","Software level not matching the vehicle configuration"],["Warning lamp of the affected chassis system on","Function of the replaced module missing or limited"],4,2,["C0545","P0630","P0631"],""],C0547:["Vacuum Sensor Supply Voltage Circuit/Open","Fault in the feed circuit powering the vacuum sensor on the brake booster, usually an open or a short on the regulated supply. Such sensors need a stable 5 V: HELLA specifies 4.5 to 5.5 V for its three-pin vacuum sensor (output, ground, supply), whose analogue signal tells the brake control unit when to run the electric vacuum pump.",["Supply wire or connector pin interrupted","Supply line shorted to ground or another circuit","Vacuum sensor shorting the supply internally"],["Brake system or ESC warning shown","Stop-start inactive or electric vacuum pump running constantly"],2,2,["C0548","C0549","C054D","P0641"],"מתח אספקה חיישן ואקום — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C0548:["Vacuum Sensor Supply Voltage Low","The supply reaching the vacuum sensor is present but sags below its lower limit. With a ratiometric sensor every output voltage scales with the feed, so an under-supplied sensor reports a wrong vacuum even if it is healthy. HELLA rates its brake booster vacuum sensor for 4.5 to 5.5 V and maps 0 to −1000 hPa onto 0.5 to 4.5 V; a feed near the bottom of that window already shifts the reading.",["Another sensor on the same 5-V rail drawing it down","Corroded contact or damaged feed wire adding resistance","Weak sensor supply output in the control module"],["Brake or ESC warning lamp on","Vacuum reading implausible in live data","Further codes for sensors on the same supply"],2,2,["C0547","C054B","C054F"],"אספקת חיישן ואקום — מתח נמוך"],C0549:["Vacuum Sensor A Circuit/Open","General circuit fault of vacuum sensor A, usually a broken or disconnected signal, ground or feed line. The sensor measures the vacuum in the brake booster; Bosch notes that its value lets the system run the electric vacuum pump, permits engine stop-start and supports ESP functions.",["Sensor plug loose or not latched after work in the engine bay","Broken signal, ground or supply wire","Internal open in the vacuum sensor"],["Brake assist warning or ABS lamp on","Stop-start no longer switching off the engine"],1,2,["C054A","C054B","C054C","C054D","C0547"],"חיישן ואקום‏ A — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C054A:["Vacuum Sensor A Range/Performance","Vacuum sensor A delivers an in-range voltage that does not agree with what the booster should hold. Patents show the logic: GM compares booster vacuum with engine vacuum from the MAP sensor while the throttle is closed, because the two should track each other without braking, and flags a sensor biased high or low when the difference persists too long;",["Vacuum sensor drifted or contaminated (oil, moisture)","Real leak in hose, check valve or booster making the reading look wrong","Faulty comparison value, such as manifold pressure"],["Brake assist warning or reduced assist feel","Electric vacuum pump running more often than normal","Stop-start or cylinder deactivation inhibited"],2,2,["C0549","C054B","C054C","C054E","P0556"],"חיישן ואקום‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C054B:["Vacuum Sensor A Circuit Low","The signal of vacuum sensor A has fallen below the lowest voltage a working sensor can produce. In HELLA's design the output runs from 0.5 V at no vacuum to 4.5 V at −1000 hPa and is clamped to a 0.4–4.8 V band, so anything under that floor must be electrical: a grounded signal line, an absent 5-V feed or an internally failed sensor.",["Signal wire shorted to ground","5-V supply to the sensor missing","Sensor failed with output stuck low"],["Brake assist or brake system warning lit","Electric vacuum pump running continuously"],1,2,["C0549","C054A","C054C","C054F","C0548"],"חיישן ואקום‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],C054C:["Vacuum Sensor A Circuit High","Vacuum sensor A reports a voltage above its upper clamp. HELLA's booster sensor never exceeds 4.8 V when intact, even at full vacuum, so a higher reading indicates a signal shorted to the 5-V supply or to battery voltage, an open ground, or an internal defect. On a characteristic where more volts mean more vacuum, such a fault pretends a deep vacuum that may not exist;",["Signal line shorted to supply or battery voltage","Sensor ground interrupted","Sensor failed with output stuck high"],["Brake assist warning on","Harder brake pedal if the booster really runs short of vacuum"],1,2,["C0549","C054A","C054B","C0550"],"חיישן ואקום‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],C054D:["Vacuum Sensor B Circuit/Open","Circuit fault on a second vacuum sensor, labelled B, typically an open in its signal, ground or feed. Some systems carry more than one vacuum measurement, for example a booster sensor next to one on the pump or supply line, but which sensor is B is not published by any maker, and no manufacturer documents C054D.",["Connector of sensor B unplugged, loose or corroded","Interrupted wire in the sensor harness","Sensor B open internally"],["Brake system or brake assist warning","Vacuum pump control in fallback, pump running longer"],1,2,["C054E","C054F","C0550","C0549","C0547"],"חיישן ואקום‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C054E:["Vacuum Sensor B Range/Performance","Sensor B reports a plausible-looking voltage, but the vacuum it represents contradicts the expected value. With two vacuum sensors a module can also compare them with each other; publicly, the comparison methods come from patents on booster sensors: Ford treats booster pressure lying clearly above manifold pressure as sensor degradation, since a working check valve prevents that state, and checks whether booster…",["Sensor B drifting or fouled","Leak, faulty check valve or weak vacuum pump","Wrong sensor type fitted after repair"],["Brake assist or brake system warning","Pedal feels firmer after several brake applications"],2,2,["C054D","C054F","C0550","C054A","P0556"],"חיישן ואקום‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C054F:["Vacuum Sensor B Circuit Low","The voltage from vacuum sensor B is lower than any value its characteristic allows. Taking HELLA's booster sensor as the reference, the output should never drop below 0.4 V, while 0.5 V corresponds to no vacuum at all; a reading underneath that is electrical rather than physical.",["Signal wire of sensor B grounded","No 5-V feed at sensor B","Output stage of sensor B failed"],["Brake assist warning shown","Stop-start unavailable"],1,2,["C054D","C054E","C0550","C054B","C0548"],"חיישן ואקום‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],C0550:["Vacuum Sensor B Circuit High","Vacuum sensor B puts out more voltage than its design permits. HELLA caps the output of its booster sensor at 4.8 V, with 4.5 V already standing for −1000 hPa, so anything above is a wiring or sensor fault: signal touching the supply or battery voltage, a broken ground return or a failed sensor.",["Signal of sensor B shorted to supply or battery voltage","Ground return of sensor B broken","Sensor B stuck at high output"],["Brake assist or brake system warning on","Firm pedal possible if the pump is not switched on when needed"],1,2,["C054D","C054E","C054F","C054C"],"חיישן ואקום‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],C0551:["Longitudinal Acceleration Sensor Circuit/Open","C0551 reports an electrical break in the longitudinal acceleration sensor circuit: the brake or stability module no longer gets a usable fore-aft signal, usually because the signal or supply wire is open or a plug has lost contact. Earlier layouts mounted a separate g-sensor close to the centre of gravity and cabled it to the ABS unit;",["Broken signal or supply wire between sensor and brake module","Corroded, loose or pushed-back terminal at the sensor plug","Internal open in the sensor or, on integrated designs, in the ABS/ESC unit"],["ABS and/or ESC warning lamp on","Stability, traction or hill-start assistance unavailable","ABS on four-wheel-drive vehicles regulates less precisely"],2,2,["C0552","C0553","C0554","C0062"],"חיישן תאוצה אורכית — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C0552:["Longitudinal Acceleration Sensor Range/Performance","Here the fore-aft acceleration signal arrives but does not match how the car is actually moving. Mitsubishi's 2023 Outlander PHEV brake controller reports its built-in decel G sensor fault C1071-64 as C0552; the check needs a healthy supply and takes up to 2 s, and a second faulty drive turns on the ASC and ABS warnings as well as the check-engine lamp.",["Changed vehicle attitude, e.g. different tyre sizes front and rear or overload","ABS/ESC unit or sensor mounted at the wrong angle or loose","Sensor offset drifted or internal sensor defect","Faulty wheel speed data used as comparison value"],["ESC/ASC and ABS warning lamps on, MIL possible on some models","Stability control, traction control and hill start assist switched off","Fault returns after load or tyre changes"],2,3,["C0551","C0553","C0554","C0062","C0069"],"חיישן תאוצה אורכית — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0553:["Longitudinal Acceleration Sensor Circuit Low","C0553 is stored when the longitudinal acceleration signal sits below the lowest voltage the module accepts. Analog acceleration sensors idle at mid-scale; a Hyundai/Kia patent gives 2.5 V as the zero point of a G-sensor on a 5 V reference, so a level dragged toward 0 V cannot come from real braking but points to the wiring: signal shorted to ground, missing sensor supply, or a sensor whose output stage has failed.",["Signal wire chafed through and shorted to ground","Sensor reference supply missing or collapsed","Sensor output stage failed at the lower end"],["ESC and ABS warning lamps on from start-up","Stability control and hill-hold unavailable"],2,2,["C0551","C0552","C0554","C0062"],"חיישן תאוצה אורכית — אות נמוך במעגל"],C0554:["Longitudinal Acceleration Sensor Circuit High","C0554 is the upper counterpart of C0553: the fore-aft acceleration voltage stays above the highest value that a real sensor reading may take. With a mid-scale zero point, as in a Hyundai/Kia G-sensor patent (2.5 V on a 5 V supply), a value pinned near the reference voltage would mean an absurd, constant acceleration, so the module treats it as a circuit fault.",["Signal wire shorted to a supply voltage","Moisture or corrosion bridging pins in the sensor connector","Sensor output stage failed at the upper end"],["ESC and ABS warning lamps on","Traction and stability assistance switched off"],2,2,["C0551","C0552","C0553","C0062"],"חיישן תאוצה אורכית — אות גבוה במעגל"],C0555:["Left Front Wheel Speed Sensor A Incorrect Component Installed","The left front wheel speed signal is present, but the ABS module concludes that the part behind it is not the one it expects. Mitsubishi maps its code C1061-4A on the 2023 Outlander PHEV to C0555 and defines it as the front left sensor fitted in the wrong position;",["Wrong sensor variant fitted (other side, other axle or passive instead of active)","Sensors or their connectors swapped between wheel positions","ABS control unit misjudges a correct sensor"],["ABS and ESC/ASC warning lamps on after a sensor or hub repair","Check-engine lamp on some models","Electric parking brake and hill descent control unavailable"],1,3,["C0556","C0557","C0558","C0031","C0500","C0501"],""],C0556:["Right Front Wheel Speed Sensor A Incorrect Component Installed","Mirror of C0555 for the right front wheel: the sensor delivers pulses, yet the ABS module rejects it as the wrong component. Mitsubishi lists its code C1063-4A on the 2023 Outlander PHEV as C0556, with the same rule (fitted at the wrong position, at most 3 s, two trips to MIL plus ASC and ABS lamps).",["Replacement sensor of the wrong type (passive instead of active, other side)","Stored code left over because no test drive followed the repair","ABS control unit fault"],["ABS and stability warning lamps on, MIL on some models","No ABS or ESC intervention on slippery roads"],1,3,["C0555","C0557","C0558","C0034","C0506","C0507"],""],C0557:["Left Rear Wheel Speed Sensor A Incorrect Component Installed","C0557 concerns the speed sensor at the left rear wheel: its signal exists, but the ABS module judges the fitted part as not matching. Mitsubishi lists C1065-4A on the 2023 Outlander PHEV as C0557 (sensor in the wrong position, up to 3 s, MIL after two trips). Ford reports the same fault type with its base code plus failure byte, C0037:4A.",["Wrong or other-side sensor fitted at the left rear","ABS module software misjudges the sensor (fixed by reprogramming)","Rear sensor connectors swapped left and right"],["Several brake system warnings at start-up","ABS and stability control unavailable","Check-engine lamp on some models"],2,3,["C0555","C0556","C0558","C0037","C050C","C0510"],""],C0558:["Right Rear Wheel Speed Sensor A Incorrect Component Installed","For the right rear wheel, C0558 says the ABS module does not accept the installed speed sensor as the correct part. Mitsubishi maps C1067-4A on the 2023 Outlander PHEV to C0558 (wrong installation position, detection within 3 s, MIL after two trips).",["Wrong sensor variant fitted at the right rear","Sensor or harness damaged by brake heat","ABS module software fault"],["Yellow or red ABS warning indicator on","Stability and traction control switched off","Check-engine lamp on some models"],2,3,["C0555","C0556","C0557","C003A","C0512","C0516"],""],C0559:["Power Steering Control Module Range/Performance – Rear","C0559 covers the rear steering controller, the electronics of active rear-wheel steering, when it fails its own performance or plausibility checks. Systems such as ZF's AKC turn the rear wheels by up to 12° opposite to the front ones at low speed and in the same direction from about 60 km/h.",["Rear steering control module software fault (update available)","Disagreeing position or angle signals inside the rear steering actuator","Poor ground or supply of the rear steering unit","Damaged, contaminated or worn rear steering actuator"],["Steering or rear steering warning in the instrument cluster","Larger turning circle, rear wheels held straight","Driver assistance functions limited on some models"],4,2,["C059A","C0450","U0134","U0435"],""],C055A:["ABS Pump Motor Supply Voltage Circuit A High","Supply voltage A of the ABS pump motor is above its upper limit. The motor draws heavy current, so overvoltage stresses motor, relay or semiconductor switch; typical causes are a faulty alternator regulator, a jump-start or charger at too high a voltage, or a measuring fault in the module. No maker documents C055A publicly.",["Alternator regulator or DC/DC converter delivering too high a voltage","Jump-start or battery charger with excessive voltage","Voltage measurement fault in the ABS control unit"],["ABS and ESC warning lamps on","Other overvoltage warnings or flickering lights at the same time"],2,2,["C055B","C055C","C0565","C052F","C05A6"],"מעגל מתח אספקה מנוע משאבת ABS‏ A — ערך גבוה"],C055B:["ABS Pump Motor Supply Voltage Circuit A Low","Supply voltage A of the pump motor is below its lower limit. Under load the motor pulls the feed down, so a weak 12 V battery, a corroded terminal, a high-resistance fusible link or a poor ground can all set it, and the relay may chatter. No maker publishes C055B.",["Weak or discharged 12 V battery","Corroded terminal or high-resistance fusible link in the motor feed","Poor ground connection of the ABS unit"],["ABS and ESC warning lamps on, often after cold starts","Pump runs sluggishly or ABS functions drop out"],1,2,["C055A","C055C","C052F","C05A7"],"מעגל מתח אספקה מנוע משאבת ABS‏ A — ערך נמוך"],C055C:["ABS Pump Motor Supply Voltage Circuit A Range/Performance","The return pump motor of the ABS/ESC hydraulic unit has its own power feed, usually a fused line from the battery switched through a relay or a transistor stage in the module. C055C means this feed is present but its voltage does not behave as expected while the motor is off or running – sagging under load, slow to rise or drifting – as opposed to the hard open or short codes C052F, C055A and C055B.",["Corroded or loose pump motor fuse, feed terminal or ground at the hydraulic unit","Weak battery or charging fault letting the supply collapse under motor load","Worn or sticking pump motor drawing excessive current","Faulty motor relay or driver stage inside the ABS module"],["ABS and stability control warning lamps on","No pump buzz during the start-up self-test","Normal braking remains, but without ABS regulation"],2,2,["C052B","C052F","C055A","C055B","C0564"],"מעגל מתח אספקה מנוע משאבת ABS‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C055D:["Brake Hydraulic Circuit B Leak","Passenger-car brakes are split into two hydraulic circuits so that one can still stop the car if the other fails. Brake-by-wire units with a motor-driven plunger can estimate fluid loss directly: they compare the plunger travel with the measured pressure.",["Leaking brake line, hose, fitting or caliper in this circuit","Worn seal in the master cylinder or the brake-by-wire unit","Air left in the circuit after service, read as compliance or leakage","Overly sensitive leak calculation in the brake module software"],["Red brake warning and amber ABS or stability lamp","Soft or sinking brake pedal, longer stopping distance","Falling fluid level or wet spots at a wheel"],3,3,["C055E","C055F","C05B0","C05B1"],"דליפת מעגל הידראולי בלם‏ B"],C055E:["Brake Hydraulic Circuit A Leak","C055E reports a leak in hydraulic circuit A, the counterpart of C055D. Land Rover documents it on the Defender L663 from 2020 as C055E-7A, meaning lost fluid or a failed seal, with amber ABS and DSC lamps.",["Fluid escaping from a line, hose, union or caliper of circuit A","Internal seal failure in master cylinder or hydraulic unit","Repair done but the required self-check was not completed, so the code stays","Air trapped after bleeding or component replacement"],["Amber ABS and DSC/ESC lamps, possibly red brake warning","Longer pedal travel or spongy feel","Warning returns after clearing until the self-check passes"],3,3,["C055D","C055F","C05B0","C05B1"],"דליפת מעגל הידראולי בלם‏ A"],C055F:["BSCM/EBBC Hydraulic Unit Performance","The brake system control module (BSCM) or electronic brake boost controller (EBBC) has found that its hydraulic unit – master cylinder, pedal simulator, separation valves or boost plunger – does not perform as calculated. GM's 2019 tables test it during shutdown: a simulator leak sets C055F if secondary pressure drops under 15 bar; in 2025 a master cylinder leakage above 200 mm³/s also counts, Type A with MIL.",["Internal leak or failure of the master cylinder or pedal simulator","Low battery voltage, especially in severe cold, during the self-test","Brake module software flagging the unit too readily (update available)","Poor power or ground terminals at the brake module"],["Service Brake System message, ABS and stability lamps","Hard pedal or changed brake pedal effort","Check-engine lamp on some models"],4,3,["C055D","C055E","C0597","C053D","C0563"],""],C0560:["Brake Pressure Sensor A Missing Calibration","The brake module expects stored calibration data for pressure sensor A, normally the master cylinder pressure sensor: zero offset, sensor identity and a flag that the end-of-line or service calibration succeeded. C0560 means this data is absent or does not match the fitted sensor. GM's 2019 and 2025 tables check only the stored status, 500 ms after wake-up, Type A with MIL;",["Pressure sensor calibration skipped after replacing the brake module or hydraulic unit","Calibration interrupted, e.g. pedal touched or voltage dropped during the routine","Used or wrong hydraulic unit whose sensor data do not match the module","Non-volatile memory error in the brake module"],["ABS, traction or stability lamp on after brake repair","Brake assist or stability functions unavailable","Check-engine lamp on some GM models"],2,3,["C053D","C056B","C0541","C053A","C056A"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ A — חסר כיול"],C0561:["Vacuum Sensor A/B Correlation","Where two vacuum signals describe the brake booster supply, the module expects them to track each other; C0561 means sensor A and sensor B disagree beyond the allowed band. No maker documents this code number publicly. The principle is patented: Ford compares the booster vacuum sensor with a second reservoir sensor after the vacuum pump stops and flags a sensor mismatch;",["One vacuum sensor drifting or reading offset","Leaking or kinked vacuum hose or check valve between the two measuring points","Corroded connector or damaged wiring on one sensor","Unstable 5 V reference or ground shared by the sensors"],["Brake or stability warning lamp","Electric vacuum pump runs too often or not at all","Stop/start or brake assist unavailable on some cars"],2,2,["C0547","C0549","C054A","C054D","C054E","P0556"],"חיישן ואקום‏ A/B — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],C0562:["Brake Pedal Position Sensor Supply Voltage Circuit/Open","Hybrids, EVs and brake-by-wire cars measure how hard the driver wants to brake with a contactless pedal angle or travel sensor. Bosch builds these with a magnetic field sensor on a 5 V supply and two redundant outputs, often pulse-width modulated, so the module can cross-check them. C0562 reports that this 5 V feed is interrupted – the module sees no usable supply at all, unlike C056D (too low) and C056E (too high).",["Broken 5 V supply wire or pin pushed out at the pedal sensor","Sensor connector loose or left unplugged after pedal-area work","Internal open circuit in the pedal sensor","Brake module no longer providing the 5 V reference"],["Brake system or ABS warning lamp","Regenerative braking reduced or off, pedal feel changes","Brake lights or cruise control affected on some cars"],2,2,["C056D","C056E","P057B","P057E"],"מתח אספקה חיישן מצב דוושת בלם — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C0563:["ABS Control Module Performance","C0563 is a summary code: the ABS control module reports that it cannot carry out its own function correctly, without pinning the fault on one sensor or valve. Ford shows how it is used. In its 2015–2019 hybrids the ABS module stores internal faults as U3000 (control module) or U2200 (corrupt data), and the hybrid powertrain module mirrors both as C0563 so that regenerative braking faults appear in the OBD system.",["Air in the hydraulic system or brake service mode left active after work","Internal ABS module fault or corrupted memory","Outdated or incomplete module software or configuration","Unstable supply or ground at the ABS module"],["Check Brake System message and ABS lamp","ABS and stability control unavailable","Regenerative braking limited on hybrids"],4,2,["C0564","C0565","C055F","U0121"],"מודול בקרת ABS — ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0564:["ABS Control Module System Voltage Low","The ABS module needs a stable 12 V supply to switch its valves and pump. C0564 means its measured system voltage has dropped below the permitted minimum. Ford's hybrids accept 9.0 to 16.9 V and log anything outside as C0564 (low) or C0565 (high), suspending pump motor checks meanwhile.",["Weak or deeply discharged 12 V battery","High resistance in the module fuse, feed wire or ground","Alternator or DC/DC converter not supplying enough voltage","Parasitic drain or aftermarket equipment pulling the battery down"],["ABS, stability and brake warnings, often together with other modules' warnings","Electric parking brake or hill hold unavailable","Warnings disappear after recharging the battery"],1,2,["C0565","C055B","C0563","P0562"],"מערכת מודול בקרת ABS — מתח נמוך"],C0565:["ABS Control Module System Voltage High","C0565 is set when the ABS module measures a supply voltage above its permitted maximum; excess voltage can damage the valve and pump drivers, so the module stops regulating. Mitsubishi maps its C1056-17 to C0565 on the 2023 Outlander PHEV: 16 V or more on the ignition feed within 1 s, ASC, ABS, brake and parking brake lamps plus the MIL after two trips;",["Faulty alternator regulator or DC/DC converter overcharging the 12 V system","Jump-start or battery charger set to an excessive voltage","Poor ground making the module read voltage too high"],["ABS, stability, brake and parking brake warnings","Check-engine lamp on some models","Bulbs burning out or other modules reporting overvoltage"],2,3,["C0564","C055A","C0563","P0563"],"מערכת מודול בקרת ABS — מתח גבוה"],C0566:["Brake Booster Solenoid Circuit/Open","Some vacuum brake boosters carry an electrically operated valve that lets air into the working chamber without pedal input – for emergency brake assist or, on hybrids, to blend friction and regenerative braking. An Aisin patent shows the idea: when energised, the solenoid admits atmospheric pressure to an auxiliary chamber and raises boost. C0566 reports an open circuit in this solenoid's wiring or coil.",["Solenoid connector loose, unlatched or corroded at the booster","Broken wire between ABS module and booster solenoid","Open solenoid coil inside the booster"],["Brake system or stability warning","Brake assist or regenerative blending unavailable","Pedal feel changes on hybrids"],2,2,["C0567","C0568","C0569","C0022"],"סולנואיד מגבר בלם — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C0567:["Brake Booster Solenoid Circuit Low","C0567 flags the brake booster solenoid circuit as too low – typically a short to ground on the line between the module's high-side driver and the coil. Ford describes the check in its 2015–2019 hybrid summaries: with both high-side and low-side drivers switched off, the module measures the voltage on the solenoid supply;",["Chafed solenoid wire shorting to body ground","Moisture or corrosion bridging the connector pins","Shorted solenoid winding inside the booster"],["Brake system warning lamp","No automatic brake assist","Less regenerative braking on hybrids"],2,2,["C0566","C0568","C0569","C0022"],"סולנואיד מגבר בלם — אות נמוך במעגל"],C0568:["Brake Booster Solenoid Circuit High","C0568 is the high-side counterpart of C0567: the solenoid circuit carries voltage when it should be dead. In Ford's 2015–2019 hybrid logic both drivers are commanded off and the solenoid supply line must stay near zero; more than 3.0 V for 80 ms points to a short to battery voltage or a driver that will not switch off, and the hybrid powertrain module reports C0568 (ABS code C0022).",["Solenoid wire chafed against a powered circuit","High-side driver in the ABS module not switching off","Contamination bridging pins in the solenoid connector"],["Brake system warning lamp","Brake assist switched off","Unusual pedal feel on hybrids"],2,2,["C0566","C0567","C0569","C0022"],"סולנואיד מגבר בלם — אות גבוה במעגל"],C0569:["Brake Booster Solenoid Circuit Performance","C0569 covers booster solenoid faults that are neither a clear open nor a clean short: the circuit reacts, but not as the module expects. Ford's hybrids (2015–2019) run three checks during operation, each over 80 ms: more than 2 V over the low-side driver while the high side is off, less than 160 mA in the test pulse with the high side on, or under 3.0 V supply with the high side on.",["Corroded or loose terminals adding resistance in the solenoid circuit","Solenoid coil with out-of-range resistance","Degraded driver stage in the ABS module"],["Intermittent brake system warning","Brake assist occasionally unavailable","Code returns after clearing"],2,2,["C0566","C0567","C0568","C052B"],"סולנואיד מגבר בלם — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],C056A:["Brake Booster Pressure Sensor Power Supply Circuit","Pressure sensors in the brake system are ratiometric parts fed with 5 V from the control module; HELLA's booster vacuum sensor, for example, is specified for 4.5–5.5 V and answers with 0.5–4.5 V. If that supply is missing or out of range, every reading is wrong, so C056A is checked before the sensor signals are judged.",["Open or shorted 5 V supply wire to the sensor","Another sensor on the same reference pulling the supply down","Corroded sensor connector","Faulty 5 V regulator in the control module"],["Brake or stability warning, often with further sensor codes","Brake assist or electric vacuum pump control affected","Stop/start inactive on some cars"],2,2,["C0547","C0548","C0560","C056B","P0556"],"אספקת מתח חיישן לחץ מגבר בלם — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C056B:["Brake Pressure Sensor A Intermittent/Erratic","C056B means the signal from brake pressure sensor A drops out or jumps for short moments instead of being steadily wrong. Ford's hybrid summaries (2015–2019) name two triggers: a checksum error in the digital data coming from the sensor for 70 ms, or a commanded control signal that does not show up at the sensor within 70 ms; the check runs only with a healthy sensor supply (no C056A).",["Loose or corroded contact in the pressure sensor connector or harness","Disturbed digital sensor line, e.g. damaged shielding or poor ground","Sensor electronics failing intermittently, often in the hydraulic unit","Brief dips in the 5 V sensor supply"],["ABS and stability lamps that come and go","Stability control or hill start assist off until next start","Regenerative braking reduced on hybrids"],2,2,["C056C","C053D","C0560","C056A","C0044"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ A — אות לא יציב"],C056C:["Brake Pressure Sensor B Intermittent/Erratic","C056C is the intermittent fault of the second brake pressure sensor, B. Which pressure B measures depends on the system – in Ford's hybrid ABS modules the two sensors read different points of the hydraulic unit, and other makers fit sensor B in a separate circuit or in the boost chamber. No maker documents C056C publicly.",["Intermittent contact at the sensor B connector or harness","Sensor B electronics dropping out under heat or vibration","Poor ground or unstable reference voltage"],["Sporadic ABS or stability warning","Traction and stability control briefly unavailable","No noticeable change in normal braking"],2,2,["C056B","C0541","C0542","C0543","C0544"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ B — אות לא יציב"],C056D:["Brake Pedal Position Sensor Supply Voltage Circuit Low","The brake pedal angle sensor of a hybrid or brake-by-wire car is fed from a regulated 5 V line. C056D means this supply is present but sagging. Ford's 2015–2019 hybrid summaries set a joint window for C056D and C056E: if the supply leaves 4.87–5.13 V for 50 ms, the code for the low or high side is stored; in Ford's ABS module both appear as C100F and the hybrid powertrain module shows C056D for the low case.",["Pedal sensor loading the supply through an internal fault","Supply wire chafed to ground near the pedal box","Another sensor on the same 5 V rail pulling it down","Weak 5 V regulator in the brake module"],["Brake system warning and possibly stability lamp","Regenerative braking reduced, firmer friction braking","On GM models parking brake messages instead"],2,2,["C056E","C0562","P057B","P057E"],"חיישן מצב דוושת בלם — מתח נמוך במעגל מתח האספקה"],C056E:["Brake Pedal Position Sensor Supply Voltage Circuit High","C056E is stored when the 5 V feed of the brake pedal position sensor rises above its limit. In Ford's 2015–2019 hybrid logic that means more than 5.13 V for 50 ms; the ABS module records C100F and the hybrid powertrain module C056E. An elevated reference usually comes from a short between the supply and a battery-voltage wire, from a missing sensor ground that lets the line float up, or from a failing regulator.",["Supply wire shorted to a battery-voltage circuit","Open sensor ground letting the reference float high","Faulty 5 V regulator in the brake module"],["Brake system warning lamp","Regenerative braking limited","Pedal sensor plausibility codes may follow"],2,2,["C056D","C0562","P057B","P057E"],"חיישן מצב דוושת בלם — מתח גבוה במעגל מתח האספקה"],C056F:["Brake Booster Travel Sensor Circuit Low","The travel sensor tells the booster control how far its input side has moved. On older vacuum boosters it followed the movable wall; on Bosch's iBooster a differential travel sensor measures the offset between the pedal-driven input rod and the motor-driven booster body, and the controller works to bring that offset back to zero.",["Travel sensor signal wire chafed through and shorted to ground","Missing 5 V supply to the sensor, e.g. corroded connector pin at the booster","Internal fault of the travel sensor, usually built into the booster assembly","Defective sensor input stage in the booster control unit"],["Hard brake pedal with clearly higher pedal force","Brake system or stability warning lamp and a message to service the brakes","Brake assist, automatic emergency braking or regenerative braking unavailable"],3,2,["C0570","C0048","C056D","C056E","C05CC"],""],C0570:["Brake Booster Travel Sensor Circuit High","C0570 is the high-side counterpart of C056F: the booster travel signal reads above its plausible maximum. Typical triggers are a signal wire touching the 5 V reference line or battery positive, or a broken sensor ground that lets the input float upward.",["Signal wire shorted to the 5 V reference or to battery voltage","Open sensor ground letting the signal float to the upper limit","Travel sensor damaged internally, e.g. after water ingress at the booster","Wrong or not properly installed booster or sensor after a repair"],["Electric brake assist switched off, pedal much harder","Brake warning and stability control lamp on","Driver assistance braking functions disabled"],3,2,["C056F","C0048","C056E","C05CF"],""],C0571:["Brake Pressure Sensor C Circuit Low","Brake pressure sensor C is an additional hydraulic pressure sensor whose job depends on the brake system; each maker assigns the letter itself. GM uses C0571 in three variants. In the 2016–2019 hybrid brake control modules it is master cylinder pressure sensor 1, set when the signal line shows no voltage difference to ground for 0.1 s.",["Sensor signal line shorted to ground in the harness or connector","Sensor supply missing, so the output stays at its lowest value","Defective pressure sensor, often integrated in the hydraulic or brake module"],["Check engine light together with ABS or stability warning (GM)","Regenerative braking or brake assist reduced, pedal feel changed","Brake pressure reading on the scan tool stuck at its minimum"],3,3,["C0572","C0573","C0574","C059C","C053E"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל"],C0572:["Brake Pressure Sensor C Circuit High","C0572 marks the upper end of the same sensor C channel: the pressure signal is at or above its top limit. GM's 2016–2019 hybrid brake modules check the signal voltage against the supply voltage and set the code when the two are practically equal for 0.1 s. The 2019 EBCM uses more than 95.24 % of supply voltage and explicitly includes an open signal line, so GM has no separate open-circuit code for this sensor.",["Signal line shorted to the 5 V reference or another supply","Open signal line pulled high by the module input (GM counts this here)","Pressure sensor reporting full scale because of an internal fault"],["Check engine light plus ABS or stability lamp (GM)","Scan tool shows high brake pressure with the pedal released","Brake assist and regenerative braking restricted"],3,3,["C0571","C0573","C0574","C059C","C053F"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל"],C0573:["Brake Pressure Sensor C Circuit/Open","C0573 is reserved for an interrupted circuit of brake pressure sensor C – a broken signal, supply or ground wire, or a connector that has lost contact. No manufacturer documents it publicly; GM, which uses C0571 and C0572 for this sensor, books an open signal line under C0572.",["Loose, corroded or pushed-back pin at the sensor or module connector","Broken signal, supply or ground wire in the harness","Internal open circuit in the pressure sensor"],["ABS, stability or brake warning lamp on","Pressure value missing or fixed at a rail on the scan tool","Fault may come and go when the connector is moved"],2,2,["C0571","C0572","C0574","C0577","C0540"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ C — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C0574:["Brake Pressure Sensor C Circuit Range/Performance","Here the sensor C signal is electrically within limits but does not make sense. GM's 2016–2019 hybrid brake modules learn the zero point while the pedal is released and set C0574 if the offset exceeds ±1,500 kPa; to confirm a repair the car is driven at about 37 mph for 5 s without braking.",["Pressure sensor zero point drifted with age or temperature","Residual pressure while learning, e.g. dragging pedal or sticking valve","Poor sensor ground shifting the signal level","Sensor values not relearned after replacing the brake module"],["Check engine light and ABS or stability lamp (GM)","Uneven or changed braking feel when regeneration blends in","Code returns after clearing once the car has been driven"],3,3,["C0571","C0572","C0573","C059C","C053D"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],C0575:["Brake Pressure Sensor D Circuit Low","Brake pressure sensor D is a further hydraulic pressure sensor whose position is set by the manufacturer. In GM's hybrid brake control modules of 2016–2019 it measures brake pressure at the left rear wheel, and C0575 is stored when its signal stays under 0.3 V for 0.1 s while the ignition is on, rated Type A with MIL after one trip.",["Signal line of sensor D shorted to ground","Sensor supply interrupted, output drops to near 0 V","Defective pressure sensor"],["Check engine light with brake or stability warning (GM hybrids)","Regenerative braking reduced, more friction braking","Rear pressure reading near zero even when braking"],3,3,["C0576","C0577","C0578","C059D","C0571"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ D — אות נמוך במעגל"],C0576:["Brake Pressure Sensor D Circuit High","C0576 is set when the signal of brake pressure sensor D sits too high. GM's 2016–2019 hybrid brake tables, where D is the left rear wheel pressure sensor, compare the signal line against the supply: a level over 3.3 V lasting 0.1 s at ignition on stores the code, Type A with MIL after one trip. A short to the 5 V reference or to battery voltage and a broken sensor ground are the usual reasons;",["Signal line shorted to the 5 V reference or to battery voltage","Open sensor ground, signal floats high","Sensor internally damaged, reports maximum pressure"],["Check engine light and brake warnings (GM hybrids)","High rear pressure shown with the pedal released","Less regenerative braking, ABS/ESC restricted"],3,3,["C0575","C0577","C0578","C059D","C0572"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ D — אות גבוה במעגל"],C0577:["Brake Pressure Sensor D Circuit/Open","C0577 stands for an open circuit of brake pressure sensor D. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. GM, which assigns sensor D to the left rear wheel pressure sensor in its hybrid brake modules, uses only C0575, C0576 and C0578 there; C0577 also appears in GM's code list for 2014 and older vehicles (PIP5094), where it belongs to GM's earlier numbering.",["Connector of sensor D unplugged, corroded or with a spread terminal","Wire broken near the sensor, e.g. at a flex point toward the rear axle","Internal open circuit in sensor D"],["Brake, ABS or stability warning lamp","No valid value for sensor D on the scan tool","Regenerative braking or brake assist limited"],2,2,["C0575","C0576","C0578","C0573","C0544"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ D — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C0578:["Brake Pressure Sensor D Circuit Range/Performance","For sensor D the range/performance check targets a signal that is electrically fine but implausible. In GM's 2016–2019 hybrid brake modules, where D measures left rear brake pressure, the zero offset is learned while the car is being driven above about 4.5 mph with the brake released and the hydraulic pump idle; an offset beyond ±1,500 kPa sets C0578 at once, Type A with MIL.",["Zero point of sensor D drifted","Pressure trapped in the rear circuit, e.g. sticking caliper or valve","Ground offset between sensor and brake module"],["Check engine light and brake warnings (GM hybrids)","Rear brake pressure shown although no brake is applied","Code sets again after a short drive"],3,3,["C0575","C0576","C0577","C059D","C0574"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ D — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],C0579:["Brake Booster Temperature Sensor B Circuit Low","Electromechanical brake boosters watch the heat in their motor and power electronics so they can scale back assist before damage; a Hitachi Astemo patent, for example, describes one sensor on the motor and one in the drive circuit, with assist limited above set temperatures. GM reads two temperature channels from its booster: A under P25C6/P25C7, B under C0579/C057A.",["Temperature signal B shorted to ground inside the booster or its harness","Thermistor shorted, e.g. after overheating","Fault in the booster control electronics reading the channel"],["Check engine light after two trips (GM 2023/2025), brake warning","Brake assist may be reduced as a precaution","Booster temperature B shows an implausible value on the scan tool"],3,3,["C057A","C057B","C057C","C057D","P25C6"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מגבר בלם‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],C057A:["Brake Booster Temperature Sensor B Circuit High","C057A is the high counterpart: temperature channel B of the booster reads at its upper end, which GM interprets as the signal shorted to supply. GM's 2023 and 2025 EBCM tables set it above 3.14 V when five checks in a row fail within 0.6 s and rate it Type B, with MIL after two trips; the 2019 Cadillac XT4 version uses 3.34 V and is Type C without MIL.",["Temperature signal B shorted to the sensor supply or another voltage","Thermistor or its return line open, pulling the input to the rail","Moisture or corrosion inside the booster electronics"],["Check engine light after two trips (GM 2023/2025) and brake warning","Temperature B reading stuck at a limit","Reduced brake assist during long downhill braking"],3,3,["C0579","C057B","C057C","C057D","P25C7"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מגבר בלם‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],C057B:["Brake Booster Temperature Sensor B Circuit/Open","C057B is defined for an interrupted circuit of booster temperature sensor B. No manufacturer publishes it; GM maps the faults of this channel to C0579 and C057A only. Temperature sensors of this kind are normally NTC thermistors placed near the motor or on the power stage and read through a voltage divider.",["Open wire or loose pin between thermistor and booster electronics","Cracked thermistor body or broken lead after thermal or mechanical stress","Failed solder joint on the booster circuit board"],["Brake system warning and service message","Temperature B missing or at an extreme value on the scan tool","Assist possibly limited to protect the motor"],3,2,["C0579","C057A","C057C","C057D","P25C4"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מגבר בלם‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C057C:["Brake Booster Temperature Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","C057C covers a temperature B value that is electrically valid but behaves implausibly – it stays frozen, climbs too slowly after hard use, or departs from what the module's thermal estimate predicts. No manufacturer documents this code publicly.",["Thermistor resistance drifted through age, moisture or heat cycling","Sensor lost thermal contact with motor or power stage","Plausibility model in the booster software too strict"],["Brake warning, often after long or repeated braking","Temperature B frozen or lagging behind temperature A","Assist reduced earlier than usual"],3,2,["C0579","C057A","C057B","C057E","P25C5"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מגבר בלם‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],C057D:["Brake Booster Temperature Sensor Circuit B Intermittent/Erratic","C057D is meant for a temperature B signal that drops out or jumps for brief moments instead of failing for good – a loose connector pin, a cracked solder joint or a wire breaking under vibration are the classic reasons. No manufacturer publishes a threshold for it. GM's monitors for this channel require several consecutive out-of-range samples (two or five) before storing C0579 or C057A, which filters single spikes;",["Loose or fretting pin in the booster connector","Cracked solder joint of the thermistor on the circuit board","Moisture ingress causing leakage currents at the sensor"],["Brake warning that appears and disappears","Temperature B jumping on the scan tool","Code returns some time after clearing"],3,2,["C0579","C057A","C057B","C057C","P25C8"],"מעגל חיישן טמפרטורת מגבר בלם‏ B — אות לא יציב"],C057E:["Brake Booster Temperature Sensor A/B Correlation","With two temperature sensors in the booster the module can cross-check them: after a long rest both should be close to ambient, and under load they should move in a consistent pattern. C057E is set when sensors A and B disagree beyond a plausible margin. GM fits two such channels in its booster (A: P25C6/P25C7, B: C0579/C057A), but its public tables do not list C057E, and no other maker documents it either.",["One of the two thermistors drifted or lost thermal contact","Added resistance in one sensor circuit, e.g. corroded contact","Real local overheating of motor or power stage, e.g. after jammed mechanics"],["Brake system warning with service message","Temperatures A and B clearly apart on the scan tool after a cold start","Reduced brake assist"],3,2,["C057C","P25C5","C0579","C057A","C05B6"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מגבר בלם‏ A/B — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],C057F:["Brake Booster Motor A Phase U-V-W Circuit/Open","C057F covers an interrupted drive path in the three-phase motor of an electric brake booster: a winding, a phase lead or a power transistor that no longer carries current. GM documents it in several brake modules, always as Type A with MIL after one trip.",["Bridge transistor in the brake module no longer switching (drive stage defect)","Broken winding or failed internal phase connection in booster motor A","Corroded or loose phase contact between control unit and motor, raising coil resistance"],["Hard brake pedal, noticeably more pedal force needed","Brake system, ABS/traction and check engine lamps on","Message about reduced brake assist"],3,3,["C0580","C0581","C0582","C0583","C0590"],"פאזת מנוע מגבר בלם‏ A U-V-W — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C0580:["Brake Booster Motor A Phase U-V-W Circuit Low","C0580 flags a phase of booster motor A that is pulled too low, or a driver stage that cannot lift it properly. GM's 2016 and 2019 hybrid tables use it when the gate-drive supply of the bridge driver falls too far below the motor supply (7 V limit, 5 ms).",["Gate-driver or charge-pump supply in the brake module too low (internal defect or weak supply)","Phase lead of motor A chafed through and shorted to ground","Lower bridge transistor shorted or permanently driven"],["Electric brake assist off, pedal feels hard","Brake and stability warning lamps, on GM also the check engine lamp","Fault may appear right after switching the ignition on"],3,3,["C057F","C0581","C0582","C0584","C0591"],"פאזת מנוע מגבר בלם‏ A U-V-W — אות נמוך במעגל"],C0581:["Brake Booster Motor A Phase U-V-W Circuit High","C0581 is reserved for a phase of booster motor A whose voltage sits too high – typically a phase lead touching battery positive or an upper power transistor that stays conductive. No manufacturer publishes C0581: GM's brake tables list only C057F, C0580 and C0582 for the phase circuits of this motor, and its 2019 IBC unit books stuck-high phases under C057F.",["Upper bridge transistor in the brake module shorted or stuck on","Phase lead of motor A shorted to battery voltage","Moisture in the booster connector creating a leakage path to supply"],["Brake assist switched off, high pedal effort","Brake system warning lamp and service message"],3,2,["C057F","C0580","C0582","C0585"],"פאזת מנוע מגבר בלם‏ A U-V-W — אות גבוה במעגל"],C0582:["Brake Booster Motor A Phase U-V-W Circuit Range/Performance","C0582 is the plausibility check of the drive stage for booster motor A and the best documented code of this group. GM's 2016/2019 hybrid tables switch an upper and a lower transistor of different phases in all six pairings and trip above 150 A; the 2023/2025 EBCM tables expect an idle phase at 1.65 V during start-up and also file a temperature-sensor plausibility test here. Type A, MIL.",["Software fault in the brake system control module (GM 22-NA-100, fixed by reprogramming)","Defective bridge driver or shorted transistor pair in the drive stage","Internal fault of the eBooster unit, requiring booster and module replacement"],["Check engine, traction control and ABS lamps on together","Brake assist failure message, abnormal pedal feel","Reduced assist especially during hard or panic braking"],4,3,["C057F","C0580","C0581","C058A","C0586"],"פאזת מנוע מגבר בלם‏ A U-V-W — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],C0583:["Brake Booster Motor B Phase U-V-W Circuit/Open","C0583 refers to the second motor or second winding system, B, of an electric brake booster and reports an interrupted phase path there. Not every booster has a B side: GM's public tables diagnose motor A only, and no manufacturer documents C0583 in this meaning. GM's keyword list for 2014 and older vehicles (PIP5094) contains C0583 from an earlier numbering.",["Open winding or internal phase connection of motor/winding system B","Power module B with a transistor that no longer conducts","Loose or corroded phase contact on the B side"],["Brake warning lamp with a service message","Weaker or slower brake assist if only side A remains"],3,2,["C0584","C0585","C0586","C057F","C0592"],"פאזת מנוע מגבר בלם‏ B U-V-W — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C0584:["Brake Booster Motor B Phase U-V-W Circuit Low","C0584 means a phase of booster motor B is held too low – shorted to ground, a lower transistor that will not switch off, or a driver whose gate supply has collapsed. No manufacturer publishes the code in its booster meaning; it shows up only in GM's older keyword list (PIP5094), where the number belonged to another system.",["Phase lead of side B shorted to ground or housing","Lower transistor of power module B shorted","Gate-driver supply of channel B too low"],["Brake system warning and possibly reduced assist","Driver assistance braking functions may be limited"],3,2,["C0583","C0585","C0586","C0580","C0593"],"פאזת מנוע מגבר בלם‏ B U-V-W — אות נמוך במעגל"],C0585:["Brake Booster Motor B Phase U-V-W Circuit High","C0585 stands for a phase of booster motor B reading too high, for instance a lead shorted to battery positive or an upper transistor stuck on. The number had another use on older GM-platform cars: on the 2011 Saab 9-5 it identified the left rear damper actuator of the adaptive suspension. In its booster meaning no manufacturer publishes it.",["Phase lead of side B shorted to battery voltage","Upper transistor of power module B shorted or stuck on","Code read on an older GM-platform vehicle where C0585 belongs to a damper actuator"],["Brake system warning lamp","Reduced or switched-off electric assist"],3,2,["C0583","C0584","C0586","C0581"],"פאזת מנוע מגבר בלם‏ B U-V-W — אות גבוה במעגל"],C0586:["Brake Booster Motor B Phase U-V-W Circuit Range/Performance","C0586 is set when the B drive stage of the booster motor is electrically connected but behaves implausibly: phase currents that do not match the command, a transistor pair conducting at once, or a bridge driver that fails its start-up self-test. Nobody publishes limits for side B.",["Bridge driver of channel B failing its self-test","Current measurement of channel B drifting, currents no longer match the command","Control unit software issue, resolved by update where available"],["Brake warning or service message","Pedal response weaker or slower than usual"],4,2,["C0583","C0584","C0585","C0582"],"פאזת מנוע מגבר בלם‏ B U-V-W — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],C0587:["Brake Booster Motor A Position Sensor Circuit/Open","C0587 concerns the rotor position sensor of booster motor A – a resolver, a sine/cosine magnetic sensor or a set of Hall elements that tells the controller where the rotor stands so it can commutate the windings. The code reports an open sensor circuit.",["Broken signal or supply wire of the position sensor","Pushed-back or corroded pin at the sensor or module connector","Sensor element inside the booster failed, booster unit usually replaced"],["Electric brake assist reduced or off, hard pedal","Brake warning lamp and message"],3,2,["C0588","C0589","C058A","C058B"],"חיישן מצב מנוע מגבר בלם‏ A — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C0588:["Brake Booster Motor A Position Sensor Circuit Low","C0588 is set when the position signal of booster motor A sits below its valid band. GM documents it in its EBCM tables: the 2019 Cadillac XT4 unit trips when a raw sine or cosine value drops under 1,300 counts, or their sum under 3,876, for 10 ms; the 2023 and 2025 tables use a cosine value under 10 counts for 0.15 s, a sine line under 1.047 V or a vector length below 0.25.",["Sine or cosine line of the sensor shorted to ground","Missing sensor supply, signals collapse toward zero","Sensor element or target magnet damaged, amplitude too small"],["Check engine lamp together with brake/ABS warning (GM)","Electric assist switched off, high pedal effort"],3,3,["C0587","C0589","C058A","C058C"],"חיישן מצב מנוע מגבר בלם‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],C0589:["Brake Booster Motor A Position Sensor Circuit High","C0589 is the high counterpart: a sine or cosine line of motor A's position sensor reads above its permitted maximum. In GM's 2019 XT4 brake module a raw value above 2,795 counts, or a sum above 4,327, for 10 ms sets it; the 2023 and 2025 EBCM tables trip on a cosine reading above 4,075 counts lasting 0.15 s, a sine input above 2.252 V, or a calculated vector length above 1.14.",["Sensor signal line shorted to the sensor supply or battery voltage","Open sensor ground lifting the signals to the upper limit","Internal sensor fault in the booster unit"],["Brake assist warning with check engine lamp (GM)","Hard pedal, assist withdrawn"],3,3,["C0587","C0588","C058A","C058D"],"חיישן מצב מנוע מגבר בלם‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],C058A:["Brake Booster Motor A Position Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","C058A covers a position signal of booster motor A that is electrically valid but not believable. GM uses it widely: its 2016 and 2019 hybrid tables flag a rotor angle changing faster than 73° per ms, the 2019 IBC unit an invalid Hall pattern (all three high or all low) and a frozen signal, the XT4 module a vector length outside 0.6889–1.2996, and the 2023/2025 tables angle jumps beyond 711.2 rad/s – each Type A with…",["Position sensor delivering implausible angles (Hall element or sine/cosine sensor degraded)","Intermittent contact or interference on the sensor lines causing angle jumps","Booster unit internal fault or position data no longer matching the stored calibration"],["Brake assist failure message, abnormal pedal feel","Check engine and brake warning lamps (GM)","Fault may be hard to read out with a normal scan tool"],4,3,["C0587","C0588","C0589","C058E","C0582"],"חיישן מצב מנוע מגבר בלם‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],C058B:["Brake Booster Motor B Position Sensor Circuit/Open","C058B reports an open circuit at the position sensor of booster motor B. Such a second sensor exists where the booster has a second motor or winding system with its own commutation, or where the rotor angle is measured twice for safety. Stellantis shows that the eBooster of the Jeep Wagoneer has a motor B position channel, since its parts bulletin names C058E (range/performance) for it;",["Broken signal or supply wire of position sensor B","Loose or corroded contact in the sensor B connector","Failed sensor element B inside the booster"],["Brake system warning with service message","Possibly reduced assist or limited assistance functions"],3,2,["C058C","C058D","C058E","C0587"],"חיישן מצב מנוע מגבר בלם‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C058C:["Brake Booster Motor B Position Sensor Circuit Low","C058C applies when the motor B position signal sits below its lower limit – usually a sensor line shorted to ground, a missing sensor supply or a damaged sensor element. No manufacturer publishes this code; GM limits its documented position checks to motor A, where C0588 trips in the XT4 module below 1,300 counts.",["Signal line of sensor B shorted to ground","Supply of sensor B missing or too low","Sensor element B or its magnet degraded, signal amplitude too small"],["Brake warning lamp","Assist may continue on one channel with reduced dynamics"],3,2,["C058B","C058D","C058E","C0588"],"חיישן מצב מנוע מגבר בלם‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],C058D:["Brake Booster Motor B Position Sensor Circuit High","C058D is set when a signal of motor B's position sensor exceeds its upper limit, for example because a sensor line touches supply voltage or the sensor ground has opened. No manufacturer documents C058D publicly; the range/performance case of the same sensor is C058E, which Stellantis lists for the Jeep Wagoneer eBooster.",["Signal line of sensor B shorted to supply or battery voltage","Open ground of sensor B lifting the signal","Internal fault of sensor B in the booster"],["Brake system warning and message","Assist weaker or switched off depending on design"],3,2,["C058B","C058C","C058E","C0589"],"חיישן מצב מנוע מגבר בלם‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],C058E:["Brake Booster Motor B Position Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","C058E concerns a second rotor angle channel of the electric booster motor whose readings are electrically valid but not believable. In GM's 2019 integrated brake control unit this is MPS2, a SENT sensor checked against the faster SPI sensor MPS1 of the same motor: a gap above 2° plus a 3° speed allowance, opposite directions or a changed rest offset for 100 ms set it, Type A with MIL.",["Brake control module calibration causing false correlation faults (GM PIT5638)","Second rotor position sensor in the booster drifting or failing","Fault inside the brake control module or eBooster unit (replaced together)","Poor contact in the booster sensor connector"],["Service Brake Assist message in the instrument cluster","Hard brake pedal needing more effort, longer stopping distance","Check engine lamp via the brake module request (P25A2)"],4,3,["C058A","C058B","C058C","C058D","C05B0","P25A2"],"חיישן מצב מנוע מגבר בלם‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],C058F:["Regeneration Torque Performance","C058F covers the case where regenerative braking does not deliver the torque the brake system has planned with. In a blended brake the brake module asks the electric drive for generator torque, usually the smaller of the available capacity and the driver's demand, estimates what actually arrives and adds friction braking for the rest, as a GM/BMW/Daimler/Chrysler patent explains.",["Electric drive or inverter delivering less generator torque than requested","Traction battery unable to absorb charge (full, hot or cold)","Torque arbitration or estimation software in the brake or hybrid module","Missing or delayed torque messages between brake and drive modules"],["Regenerative braking reduced or disabled, friction brakes do more work","Uneven deceleration or changed pedal feel during light braking","Shorter electric range on plug-in hybrids and EVs","Brake or hybrid system warning message"],3,2,["C05AD","C0563","C05AB"],"מומנט התחדשות (רגנרציה) — ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0590:["Brake Booster Motor A Phase U-V-W Current High","C0590 means the current measured in the drive of booster motor A is too high, mostly checked while the bridge is idle and almost nothing should flow. GM uses it in several units, always Type A with MIL: its 2016/2019 hybrid booster trips on leakage current above 20 A for 5 ms, the XT4 module on an idle offset above 36.1 A or a phase current above 200 A, and the 2023/2025 EBCM tables on a shunt offset above 38 A for…",["Leaking or partly conducting MOSFET in the booster motor bridge","Shunt or measuring amplifier offset drifted upward","Winding short in booster motor A drawing excess current","Bridge driver chip failing its overcurrent self-test"],["Brake assist warning, much higher pedal effort","Check engine, ABS or brake warning lamps on","Regenerative braking and automatic brake functions unavailable"],4,3,["C0591","C0592","C0595","C0596","C057F"],"זרם פאזת מנוע מגבר בלם‏ A U-V-W — ערך גבוה"],C0591:["Brake Booster Motor A Phase U-V-W Current Low","C0591 is the low counterpart: the current value of booster motor A lies below what is plausible, in practice a negative reading when the motor is at rest. In GM's 2016/2019 hybrid booster a leakage reading under −20 A counts while a half bridge is idle; the 2023/2025 EBCM tables set it when the offset taken from the internal shunt falls below −38 A for 0.2 s.",["Current sense amplifier or ADC offset drifted below zero","Cracked solder joint or damaged shunt in the power stage","Unexpected reverse current through a faulty bridge transistor"],["Loss of electric brake assist, hard pedal","Check engine and brake warning lamps after one drive","Regenerative braking switched off"],4,3,["C0590","C0593","C0596","C0595"],"זרם פאזת מנוע מגבר בלם‏ A U-V-W — ערך נמוך"],C0592:["Brake Booster Motor B Phase U-V-W Current High","C0592 reports excessive current in the second motor or second winding system, B, of an electric brake booster. No manufacturer publishes it in this sense; the number appears only in GM's keyword list PIP5094 for 2014 and older vehicles, from an earlier numbering.",["Shorted or leaking transistor in power module B","Insulation fault in winding system B","Measuring offset of the side B current sensing"],["Brake assist warning, possibly weaker or slower assist","Brake or ABS warning lamp on"],4,2,["C0593","C0590","C05AF","C0583"],"זרם פאזת מנוע מגבר בלם‏ B U-V-W — ערך גבוה"],C0593:["Brake Booster Motor B Phase U-V-W Current Low","C0593 is meant for a current value on booster side B that is too low or negative where the controller expects about zero or a commanded positive current. It is not documented by any manufacturer; like C0592 it shows up only in GM's old keyword list PIP5094 with a different meaning. Unlike the high fault, a low value rarely reflects real current: more often the measuring chain has an offset.",["Zero point of the side B current measurement drifted","Defective power module B or its driver chip","High resistance in a side B phase connection"],["Brake assist warning message","Assist weaker under hard braking if only side A remains"],4,2,["C0592","C0591","C05AF","C0584"],"זרם פאזת מנוע מגבר בלם‏ B U-V-W — ערך נמוך"],C0594:["Brake Booster Motor A Performance","C0594 judges whether booster motor A moves as commanded, not its wiring. GM's 2016/2019 hybrid booster flags a motor turning against the commanded direction (under 15 rad/s while more than 25 rad/s is requested), more than seven direction reversals, oscillation with the brake applied, or unintended backward rotation above 40 rad/s.",["Binding gear, spindle or plunger inside the booster","Worn or damaged booster motor A","Air or leakage in the hydraulic circuit so pressure does not follow motor travel","Faulty rotor position feedback causing wrong direction or oscillation"],["Loss of brake assist with a heavy pedal","Check engine and brake warning lamps on","Booster noise or pedal vibration before the fault sets"],4,3,["C0590","C0591","C058A","C05C2","C0582"],"מנוע מגבר בלם‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0595:["Brake Booster Internal Power Driver Range/Performance","C0595 covers the power path inside the booster electronics: master switch, safety relay and the six-transistor bridge driver. GM's 2016/2019 hybrid booster switches its master switch on, off and on again at start-up and expects the voltage ratio behind it above 0.88.",["Brake module software (GM 20-NA-073, 19-NA-202)","Defective bridge driver chip or its SPI communication","Motor safety relay or master switch not switching correctly","Supply voltage dips or poor module ground"],["Loss of brake assist, longer and softer pedal with more force needed","Service StabiliTrak or brake messages, traction lamp on","Check engine lamp (requested by the brake module)"],4,3,["C0590","C0596","C0582","C05D2","P25A2"],"נהג כוח פנימי מגבר בלם — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0596:["Brake Booster Motor A Current Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","C0596 questions the current measurement of booster motor A itself rather than the motor. GM's 2016/2019 hybrid booster tests its overcurrent comparator at start-up by forcing minimum and maximum PWM and reading the comparator output back over a feedback line, while the voltage behind the master switch must sit near zero or near battery voltage;",["Faulty current sense amplifier or motor driver chip","Overcurrent comparator or its feedback line not responding","Supply voltage outside the test window during start-up"],["Brake assist warning right after switching on","Heavy brake pedal, check engine lamp on"],4,3,["C05AF","C0590","C0591","C0595"],"חיישן זרם מנוע מגבר בלם‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],C0597:["Brake System Control Module A Performance","C0597 is a summary code for the first brake system control module: it cannot carry out its function properly, and the failure type byte narrows the cause. Toyota uses C059746 (calibration or parameter memory) on 2020–22 Corolla, Corolla Cross and RAV4 with a parking brake warning, cured by reprogramming the skid control unit (T-SB-0078-21), and C059704 (internal failure) on the 2022–23 Tundra, covered by a software…",["Outdated or corrupted brake module software or calibration data","Low battery voltage or poor power and ground connections, especially in cold","Internal fault of the brake control unit or integrated master cylinder"],["Service Brake System or parking brake malfunction message","ABS, stability control and possibly check engine lamps on","Changed brake pedal effort"],4,3,["C0598","C055F","C0563","C0599"],"מודול בקרת מערכת בלם‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0598:["Brake System Control Module B Performance","C0598 is the same summary check for a second brake control module, B. Such a module is found where braking is split between two units: Bosch gives its integrated power brake a separate backup unit for automated driving, so the vehicle still stops if the main unit fails.",["Software or calibration fault in brake module B","Power supply or ground problem of module B","Internal hardware fault of module B","Fault on the link between the two brake modules"],["Brake system warning message","Driver assistance or automated driving functions unavailable","Reduced brake assist if the module handles boosting"],4,2,["C0597","C0563","C0599"],"מודול בקרת מערכת בלם‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0599:["Brake Booster Control Module Missing Calibration","C0599 means the control unit of an electric brake booster finds no valid calibration data. Stand-alone electromechanical boosters such as Bosch's iBooster carry their own controller, which converts the reading of a built-in differential travel sensor into motor commands; how the pedal feels is set by software parameters.",["Booster or its control module replaced without running the setup/calibration routine","Software update or programming of the booster module aborted or incomplete","Internal memory fault in the booster control module losing stored data"],["Brake warning or service brake assist message in the cluster","Hard brake pedal with reduced power assist","Driver assistance functions using the booster (e.g. emergency braking) unavailable"],4,2,["C0560","C05AE","C05D4","C058E","C0597"],"מודול בקרת מגבר בלם — חסר כיול"],C059A:["Power Steering Control Module - Rear Missing Calibration","C059A concerns active rear-axle steering: its control module lacks the calibration it needs to position the rear wheels. Systems like ZF's AKC turn the rear wheels by a few degrees with an electrically driven spindle, either through one central actuator or one per wheel.",["Rear steering module or actuator replaced without centre calibration","Programming or setup after a software update not completed","Suspension or alignment work requiring a new rear steering zero point","Low 12 V supply interrupting the calibration routine"],["Rear steering warning in the cluster and rear wheel steering inactive","Larger turning circle and changed handling at speed","Steering wheel slightly off centre on straight roads"],4,2,["C0599","C0051"],""],C059B:["Brake Pressure Sensor B Missing Calibration","The brake module cannot confirm that pressure sensor B has been calibrated and that its sensitivity is right. GM uses C059B in the brake controller of its 2016 and 2019 hybrid tables for the rear-left wheel pressure sensor: during a test pulse the sensor response must stay between 90 % and 110 %, checked only after at least one completed offset learn, with low master cylinder pressure and no ABS, traction or…",["Calibration or offset learn not completed after module or hydraulic unit replacement","Pressure sensor responding outside the allowed test-pulse window","Brake control module storing or evaluating calibration data incorrectly"],["ABS and stability control warning lamps on, MIL possible","Regenerative braking blending or ESC functions restricted"],4,3,["C0560","C059C","C059D","C059E","C0541","C0578"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ B — חסר כיול"],C059C:["Brake Pressure Sensor C Missing Calibration","For pressure sensor C the module finds no confirmed calibration record. Such a record usually holds the zero offset and a status flag written on the assembly line or by the scan tool. No maker documents C059C publicly.",["Sensor calibration not performed after replacing the brake module or modulator","Calibration aborted because the pedal was pressed or the vehicle moved","Stored data does not match the fitted sensor (checksum or ID)"],["ABS/ESC warning lamp on","Stability control or brake assist functions switched off"],4,2,["C059B","C059D","C059E","C0560","C0574"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ C — חסר כיול"],C059D:["Brake Pressure Sensor D Missing Calibration","C059D flags missing calibration data for a fourth hydraulic pressure sensor. No manufacturer publishes this code. Where the letter D appears elsewhere, GM's 2016 hybrid brake controller uses it for the rear-left wheel pressure sensor (C0575–C0578), yet reports that sensor's calibration fault as C059B; the letters of the calibration codes therefore follow each maker's own list.",["Calibration of the sensor not done after hydraulic unit or module replacement","Code stored from an earlier event, sensor already calibrated","Brake module losing calibration data in its memory"],["ABS and ESC warning lamps on","Brake pressure based functions such as hill hold or brake blending limited"],4,2,["C059B","C059C","C059E","C0578","C0560"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ D — חסר כיול"],C059E:["Brake Pressure Sensor E Missing Calibration","C059E reports that sensor E, one more pressure sensor in a multi-sensor brake unit, has never been calibrated successfully or that its record is lost. No maker documents C059E publicly; for sensor E only the circuit codes C059F–C05A2 exist.",["Calibration run while the vehicle moved or the brake pedal was pressed","Calibration skipped after replacing the brake module or hydraulic unit","Sensor offset too large or unstable so the calibration is rejected"],["ABS/ESC or brake system warning lamp on","Brake assist or stability functions disabled"],4,2,["C059F","C05A0","C05A1","C05A2","C059D","C05C4","C05D4"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ E — חסר כיול"],C059F:["Brake Pressure Sensor E Circuit Low","The signal of brake pressure sensor E sits below its valid window. Analogue brake pressure sensors run on 5 V and report roughly 0.5–4.5 V; a Bosch trainer notes such a sensor shows under 1 V with the brake released.",["Signal wire of the sensor shorted to ground","Open 5 V supply or signal wire pulled low by the module input","Pressure sensor failed internally (often part of the hydraulic unit)"],["ABS/ESC warning lamp on","Stability control and pressure-based brake functions switched off"],3,2,["C05A0","C05A1","C05A2","C059E","C05C6","C0575"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ E — אות נמוך במעגל"],C05A0:["Brake Pressure Sensor E Circuit High","C05A0 is set when sensor E reports a voltage above its usable range. In the Denso patent on vehicle pressure sensors the band from 4.7 to 5 V is reserved for faults, and a lost ground wire pushes the output into it through the divider formed by the sensor's internal resistance and the module's pull-down resistor.",["Signal shorted to the 5 V reference or to battery voltage","Open sensor ground lifting the output to the upper rail","Sensor signalling an internal fault at full scale"],["ABS/ESC warning lamp on","Stability control unavailable, brake lights may be requested falsely on some systems"],3,2,["C059F","C05A1","C05A2","C059E","C05C7","C0576"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ E — אות גבוה במעגל"],C05A1:["Brake Pressure Sensor E Circuit/Open","This code points to an interrupted circuit of sensor E: a broken signal, 5 V supply or ground wire, or a connector that has lost contact. No maker documents C05A1 publicly. Whether an open is recognised as such or as low or high depends on the input circuit, which is why many systems book it under C059F or C05A0 instead.",["Corroded or loose connector at the sensor or hydraulic unit","Broken signal, supply or ground wire","Internal open circuit in the sensor"],["ABS/ESC warning lamp on, possibly coming and going","Stability control and brake assist switched off"],2,2,["C059F","C05A0","C05A2","C05C8","C0577"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ E — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C05A2:["Brake Pressure Sensor E Range/Performance","Here sensor E delivers a voltage that is electrically valid but does not fit the braking situation: a drifting zero point, wrong gain or a value that disagrees with other pressure signals. No maker documents C05A2 publicly. The usual tests are known from related sensors. GM's hybrid brake controller learns each wheel sensor's zero while the pedal is released and flags an offset beyond ±1,500 kPa at once.",["Sensor zero point or gain drifted with age or temperature","Residual pressure trapped in the circuit during the zero learn","Ground offset between sensor and module distorting the reading"],["ABS and ESC warning lamps on","Stability or regenerative brake functions reduced"],3,2,["C059F","C05A0","C05A1","C059E","C05C5","C0578"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ E — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C05A3:["Wheel Speed Sensors Supply Circuit High","Active wheel speed sensors are fed by the ABS module and send their pulses back as a current on the same pair of wires, as HELLA explains. C05A3 reports that this common supply is too high or cannot be switched off. GM's 2016 and 2019 hybrid brake controllers look for reverse current on the supply line, the sign of a short to the battery feed, for over 3.5 s.",["Wheel speed sensor wire chafed and shorted to battery voltage","Supply switch or ASIC in the brake module stuck on","Water in a wheel speed sensor connector bridging to a powered circuit"],["ABS, traction and stability control warning lamps on at the same time","Several or all wheel speed signals lost, speedometer may drop out","MIL on (GM)"],2,3,["C05A4","C0500","C0503","C0565"],""],C05A4:["Wheel Speed Sensors Supply Circuit Low","The shared feed for the active wheel speed sensors is too low for them to work. In GM's hybrid tables of 2016 and 2019 the brake controller measures, via an internal comparator, the voltage between the sensor supply line and the signal line and sets C05A4 below 6.7 V for 0.06 s while system voltage is above 6.9 V, Type A with MIL; it also blocks the single-wheel codes such as C0500–C0504.",["Discharged or failing 12 V battery (FCA 08-106-21)","Wheel speed sensor wiring shorted to ground, pulling the shared supply down","Sensor supply stage inside the brake module failing"],["ABS, traction and stability control lamps on, MIL possible","Several wheel speed codes at once, often with low-voltage codes","Hard starting or no start when the 12 V battery is the cause"],2,3,["C05A3","C0500","C0502","C0564","P0562"],""],C05A5:["ABS Pump Motor Supply Voltage B Circuit/Open","Supply B is a second power feed for the pump motor of the brake unit; C05A5 reports it as missing or open. A second feed is found where the motor or its drive is built redundantly. Hyundai Mobis patents a brake motor with two windings, each with its own power module and own supply input from the battery; if one side fails it is shut off and the other carries the full current.",["Blown fuse or fusible link in the B supply","Open wire or loose terminal in the B feed to the brake unit","Internal fault in the second power stage of the brake module"],["ABS/ESC or brake system warning on","Reduced pressure build-up or loss of redundancy message"],2,2,["C05A6","C05A7","C05A8","C05A9","C052F"],"מתח אספקה מנוע משאבת ABS‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C05A6:["ABS Pump Motor Supply Voltage B Circuit High","C05A6 says the second pump motor feed, supply B, carries more voltage than allowed. Overvoltage strains the motor and above all the transistors that switch it; gate driver ICs for brake motors such as TI's DRV8305-Q1 therefore watch their supply and raise an overvoltage warning in the mid-30 V range.",["Alternator or DC/DC converter regulating too high","Jump start or battery charger with excessive voltage","Voltage measurement fault in the brake module"],["ABS/ESC warning lamp on, possibly with other overvoltage codes","Very bright lights or battery warning if charging is the cause"],2,2,["C05A5","C05A7","C05A8","C05A9","C055A","C0565"],"מתח אספקה מנוע משאבת ABS‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],C05A7:["ABS Pump Motor Supply Voltage B Circuit Low","Supply B of the pump motor reads below its lower limit. The pump motor draws high current, so a weak 12 V battery, corroded terminals, a fuse holder with high resistance or a poor ground show up first under load. No maker documents C05A7 publicly.",["Weak or discharged 12 V battery","Corroded terminal, fuse holder or ground in the B feed","Charging system not keeping up (alternator or DC/DC converter)"],["ABS/ESC lamp on, often after cold starts or long standstill","Pump motor running audibly slower during self-test"],1,2,["C05A5","C05A6","C05A8","C05A9","C055B","C0564"],"מתח אספקה מנוע משאבת ABS‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],C05A8:["ABS Pump Motor Supply Voltage B Circuit Range/Performance","C05A8 means supply B is present but behaves implausibly: it sags too far once the pump starts, recovers too slowly, or does not match the state the module has commanded. That is different from a hard open (C05A5) or a steady high or low reading (C05A6, C05A7). No maker publishes a threshold for C05A8.",["Excessive voltage drop in the B feed when the pump starts","Relay or semiconductor switch in the B path responding slowly or partly","Aged 12 V battery with high internal resistance"],["Intermittent ABS/ESC warning, mostly during pump activity","Message about reduced braking redundancy on brake-by-wire vehicles"],2,2,["C05A5","C05A6","C05A7","C05A9","C055C","C052B"],"מתח אספקה מנוע משאבת ABS‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],C05A9:["ABS Pump Motor Supply Voltage Circuit A/B Correlation","With two feeds for the pump motor, the module can compare them: both come from the same vehicle supply and should read almost alike. C05A9 is set when the two drift apart beyond the allowed margin, even though each may still lie in its own window.",["Corroded terminal, fuse or connector in only one of the two feeds","Voltage measurement channel in the brake module drifting","Poor ground affecting only one supply path"],["ABS/ESC or brake system warning lamp on","Pump operation or brake redundancy restricted"],2,2,["C05A5","C05A8","C052F","C055C"],"מעגל מתח אספקה מנוע משאבת ABS‏ A/B — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],C05AA:["ABS Pump Motor Temperature Too High","C05AA signals that the ABS return or high-pressure pump motor, or its switching stage, has become too hot. Few units have a sensor on the motor, so the temperature is usually modelled. A Kelsey-Hayes (now ZF) patent estimates the heat of the transistor that drives the pump from separate heating and cooling curves, starting from the module's ambient sensor;",["Long ABS, traction or stability interventions, e.g. on rough or slippery roads","Stiff pump or worn motor brushes raising current and heat","High under-hood or ambient temperature","Module ambient sensor or temperature model giving false values"],["ABS or stability control temporarily unavailable","ABS or brake warning lamp on, often clearing after cooling down"],3,2,["C052B","C052D","C05AE","C055B"],"טמפרטורת מנוע משאבת ABS — ערך גבוה מדי"],C05AB:["Brake Blending Separation Valve Performance","C05AB concerns the separation valve that decouples the driver's master cylinder from the wheel circuits while the brakes work by wire, so that pedal pressure does not cut into regenerative braking. It is usually open without current, so the pedal acts on the wheels if power fails, as in Continental's brake-by-wire layout. A performance fault means it does not seal or switch as expected.",["Dirt or debris on the valve seat causing leakage","Valve coil or its driver in the module not switching properly","Old or wrong brake fluid making the valve sluggish","Pressure sensor errors making the valve look faulty"],["Pedal kickback or vibration during braking","Regenerative braking reduced, brake warning message","Brakes switch to direct pedal operation with higher effort"],4,2,["C05AC","C05AD","C058F","C0024"],""],C05AC:["Brake Blending Separation Valve Stuck Closed","C05AC names one specific failure: the separation valve of the blended brake stays closed when it should open. Toyota's patent for a hybrid brake defines this closure failure and shows how it is pinned down: the control pressure sensor lags its target by more than a set amount for too long, the sensor passes its self-test and the upstream linear valve demonstrably delivers fluid, so the blockage must be the…",["Valve armature stuck by contamination or corrosion","Open coil or wiring so a normally closed valve cannot open","Valve driver stage in the brake module defective"],["Brake warning, assist and regeneration off","Higher pedal effort, longer stopping distance in backup mode","Uneven braking between axles possible"],4,2,["C05AB","C05AD","C0024"],""],C05AD:["Brake Blending System Performance","C05AD is the overall check of a blended brake: does the hydraulic pressure built by wire match what the controller asked for? GM's 2016 and 2019 hybrid tables (brake module BSC1) compare actual and target boost-piston pressure, for the by-wire side as well as the master cylinder side: more than 4,000 kPa too high points to a false high sensor value, more than 1,500 kPa too low to a low sensor value, an empty…",["Brake pressure sensor reading too high or too low","Low accumulator pressure or weak hydraulic pump","Air in the hydraulic circuit after service","External or internal leak in the brake hydraulics"],["Brake warning and check engine lamps","Soft or inconsistent pedal, braking stronger or weaker than expected","Regenerative braking reduced"],4,3,["C05AB","C05AC","C058F","C0571","C05B0"],""],C05AE:["ABS Pump Motor Calibration Not Learned","C05AE means the brake module lacks a valid zero calibration for the measuring channels of its pump motor. In GM's 2016 and 2019 hybrid brake module (BSC1) the motor voltages are read through a sigma-delta modulator that needs a 0 V calibration;",["Stored zero calibration missing or invalid after module replacement or programming","Low or unstable supply voltage during the calibration","Pump motor relay or shunt in the module out of tolerance"],["ABS and brake warning lamps plus check engine lamp","ABS or stability functions limited until the calibration succeeds"],3,3,["C052B","C052D","C052F","C055B","C05AA"],"כיול מנוע משאבת ABS — לא בוצע לימוד"],C05AF:["Brake Booster Motor B Current Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","C05AF is the plausibility check of the current measurement on booster side B, the second motor or winding system. No manufacturer publishes it. A separate sensing chain for B is needed wherever each power module controls its own winding, as in the Hyundai Mobis dual-winding booster motor, since every module must know its phase currents to regulate torque and to judge its own health.",["Faulty current sense amplifier of side B","Zero offset of side B outside its allowed band","Damaged shunt or solder joint in power module B"],["Brake assist or brake system warning","Possibly weaker assist under hard braking"],4,2,["C0596","C0592","C0593"],"חיישן זרם מנוע מגבר בלם‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],C05B0:["Brake Hydraulic Circuit C Leak","C05B0 reports lost fluid or volume in a hydraulic circuit the maker designates C; at GM its meaning has changed over time. GM's 2016–2019 hybrid brake controllers used it for the front axle circuit: wheel behaviour not matching vehicle deceleration during ABS or EBD for 1 s, or master cylinder pressure above rear axle pressure at constant pedal.",["Caliper pistons pushed back during pad work and not reseated before driving (GM 22-NA-247)","Air in the plunger or brake circuit after service or bleeding","Real fluid leak at a line, hose, caliper or valve","Brake module software calibration causing false detection (GM PIT5638)"],["Service brake assist or brake system message, brake warning lamp","Longer or softer pedal travel","MIL on (GM)"],3,3,["C05B1","C055D","C055E","C055F","C058E","C0049"],"דליפת מעגל הידראולי בלם‏ C"],C05B1:["Brake Hydraulic Circuit D Leak","C05B1 is the leak code for hydraulic circuit D. The only public maker use is GM's hybrid brake controller of 2016–2019, where it covers the rear axle circuit. Two checks feed it: during pressure hold phases with the pump off and the car at rest, a calculated rear leakage above 0.3 ml/s, judged over more than 300 s of cumulative braking;",["Fluid leak at a rear brake line, hose or caliper","Internal leakage of an inlet or outlet valve in the hydraulic unit","Air in the rear circuit after service"],["Brake and ABS warning lamps on, MIL possible","Longer pedal travel and weaker rear braking"],3,3,["C05B0","C055D","C055E","C0049"],"דליפת מעגל הידראולי בלם‏ D"],C05B2:["Steering Wheel Angle Sensor Signal - Yaw Rate Sensor Signal Correlation","C05B2 flags a mismatch between how far the driver has turned the wheel and how quickly the car actually rotates about its vertical axis. The stability controller turns steering wheel angle and road speed into an expected yaw rate through a single-track vehicle model; a Siemens patent applies that model only up to about 4 m/s² of lateral acceleration.",["Steering angle sensor not recalibrated after wheel alignment, steering or column work","Yaw rate sensor or sensor cluster loose, rotated or wrongly installed","Offset drift or internal fault in the yaw rate or steering angle sensor","Mismatched tyres or bent steering parts making the vehicle model invalid"],["ESC and often traction control warning lamp on","Stability control interventions unavailable","Steering wheel off-centre when driving straight, if alignment is the cause"],2,2,["C0497","C0608","C052A","C0830"],""],C05B3:["Brake Booster Temperature Sensor C Circuit Low","C05B3 means the third temperature channel of an electromechanical brake booster has dropped below its usable band. Mitsubishi documents the code for the Outlander PHEV: the DTC index pairs it with the brake unit's own code C18FC-18, EBA temperature sensor 1, and lights the brake system warning lamp plus the MIL after two trips. The value comes from the control electronics inside the electric intelligent brake unit.",["Fault in the temperature detection inside the electric brake unit's control module","Corroded or loose brake unit connector or damaged harness","Supply disturbance during start-up distorting the reading"],["Brake system warning lamp on","Check engine lamp on after two trips (Mitsubishi)","Braking assist usually unchanged"],3,1,["C05B4","C05B5","C05B6","C05B7","C0579"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מגבר בלם‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל"],C05B4:["Brake Booster Temperature Sensor C Circuit High","C05B4 is the upper-limit counterpart: temperature channel C of the electric booster reports a value above its permitted maximum. In Mitsubishi's Outlander PHEV index it stands next to C18FC-19, again EBA temperature sensor 1, with the same lamp logic – brake system warning lamp and MIL after the second trip.",["Temperature circuit on the brake unit's control board defective","Poor contact at the brake unit connector or chafed wiring","Genuinely excessive electronics temperature after heavy booster use"],["Brake system warning lamp on","MIL on after the second trip (Mitsubishi)","Code returns immediately after clearing if the unit is defective"],3,1,["C05B3","C05B5","C05B6","C05B7","C057A"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מגבר בלם‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל"],C05B5:["Brake Booster Temperature Sensor C Circuit/Open","C05B5 is reserved for an interrupted circuit of booster temperature sensor C. No manufacturer documents it publicly; Mitsubishi, the one maker naming sensor C codes, reports problems with this channel only as C05B3 or C05B4. Boosters typically carry several NTC thermistors: Hitachi Astemo places one on the motor and one in the controller near the motor drive stage and caps motor current when either runs hot.",["Cracked thermistor body or broken lead inside the booster","Fractured solder joint on the control board from vibration or heat cycles","Open wire or pin where the sensor is wired externally"],["Brake or brake system warning lamp on","Booster may restrict assist as a precaution, depending on design"],3,0,["C05B3","C05B4","C05B6","C05B7","C057B"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מגבר בלם‏ C — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C05B6:["Brake Booster Temperature Sensor C Circuit Range/Performance","C05B6 targets a sensor C reading that is electrically inside its band yet does not behave like a real temperature: it stays flat during long assist phases, lags far behind the other channels, or contradicts the thermal estimate of the module. No manufacturer publishes this code.",["Thermistor resistance drifted through ageing, moisture or micro-cracks","Sensor lost thermal contact with the part it should measure","Thermal model or calibration in the booster control unit not matching the hardware"],["Brake system warning lamp on","Assist reduced earlier than usual during long descents or repeated braking"],3,2,["C05B3","C05B4","C05B5","C05B7","C057C"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מגבר בלם‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],C05B7:["Brake Booster Temperature Sensor C Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","C05B7 is meant for a temperature C signal that jumps or briefly drops out rather than failing permanently. No manufacturer documents it publicly. In Mitsubishi's Outlander PHEV the sensor C channel is judged against fixed limits with a detection time of up to one second, so short spikes there end up as C05B3 or C05B4 instead of a separate erratic code.",["Cracked solder joint or lead at the thermistor","Loose pin or fretting corrosion at the booster connector","Moisture reaching the sensing element through a damaged coating"],["Brake system warning lamp flickers or appears only at times","Code returns after clearing, often after rough roads or temperature changes"],3,0,["C05B3","C05B4","C05B5","C05B6","C057D"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מגבר בלם‏ C — אות לא יציב במעגל"],C05B8:["Brake Booster Motor A Position Sensor Supply Circuit/Open","The rotor position sensor of booster motor A – Hall, magnetoresistive or a digital SENT angle sensor – is fed from a regulated 5 V output of the brake control unit. C05B8 reports that this feed is interrupted. No manufacturer documents the code publicly; GM's 2019 integrated brake control lists supply faults of its two motor position sensors under C05D1 and C05BB only.",["Broken supply wire or pin between control unit and motor position sensor","Sensor supply output in the brake control unit failed","Internal open in the position sensor's supply path"],["Brake warning lamp and message such as service brake assist","Noticeably harder brake pedal","Regenerative or electronic brake functions unavailable"],3,2,["C05B9","C05BA","C05BB","C05BC","C0587"],"אספקת חיישן מצב מנוע מגבר בלם‏ A — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C05B9:["Brake Booster Motor A Position Sensor Supply Circuit Low","C05B9 is set when the feed voltage for motor A's position sensor sags below its lower limit. No manufacturer publishes C05B9; as a reference point, GM's 2019 brake module calls its 5 V sensor supplies low below 4.85 V lasting 100 ms, but books that under C05D1 or C05BB. A low supply usually means the line is shorted to ground or a sensor is drawing too much current.",["Supply line chafed through and shorted to ground","Defective position sensor or another sensor on the same rail loading the supply","Weak sensor supply regulator in the control unit"],["Brake warning lamp, often with several sensor codes at once","Brake pedal feels hard, assist reduced"],3,2,["C05B8","C05BA","C05BB","C05BD","C05D1"],"אספקת חיישן מצב מנוע מגבר בלם‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],C05BA:["Brake Booster Motor A Position Sensor Supply Circuit High","C05BA covers the opposite case: the 5 V feed of motor A's position sensor rises above its upper limit. The usual culprit is a supply line touching a battery-voltage wire, less often a regulator that has lost control. No manufacturer publishes C05BA; GM's 2019 brake module treats its sensor supplies as high above 5.15 V for 100 ms, filing them under C05D1 or C05BB.",["Supply line shorted to a battery-voltage circuit in the harness","Sensor supply regulator in the control unit no longer regulating","Poor control unit ground shifting the measured supply voltage"],["Brake warning lamp and assist warning message","Hard brake pedal, longer stopping effort"],3,2,["C05B8","C05B9","C05BB","C05BE","C05D1"],"אספקת חיישן מצב מנוע מגבר בלם‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],C05BB:["Brake Booster Motor A Position Sensor Supply Circuit Range/Performance","GM uses C05BB in the integrated brake control of 2019 models. There the processor generates two 5 V sensor supplies; each feeds one pedal travel channel plus one motor position channel. C05BB belongs to the second supply (PTS2 and MPS2), C05D1 to the first.",["Defective motor position sensor loading the shared supply","Defective pedal travel sensor on the same supply","Fault on the brake control unit's circuit board","Intermittent contact in the sensor supply wiring"],["Check engine lamp and brake warning on the first trip (GM)","Service brake assist message, hard pedal","Fault remains until the ignition is switched off"],4,3,["C05B8","C05B9","C05BA","C05BF","C05D1","C058E"],"אספקת חיישן מצב מנוע מגבר בלם‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],C05BC:["Brake Booster Motor B Position Sensor Supply Circuit/Open","C05BC reports an interrupted supply for the position sensor of booster motor B. A B channel exists where the actuator carries a second motor or winding set, or measures its rotor angle twice for redundancy. No manufacturer documents C05BC publicly. Hyundai Mobis describes a brake actuator with a dual-winding motor whose two power modules are fed separately;",["Broken wire or pushed-back pin in the motor B sensor supply","Second sensor supply output in the control unit failed","Open inside the motor B position sensor"],["Brake warning lamp, assist may remain partly available","Reduced maximum assist or slower pressure build-up"],3,2,["C05BD","C05BE","C05BF","C05B8","C058B"],"אספקת חיישן מצב מנוע מגבר בלם‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C05BD:["Brake Booster Motor B Position Sensor Supply Circuit Low","C05BD means the supply of motor B's position sensor reads below its permitted minimum – a ground short, a sensor pulling excess current or a weak regulator. No manufacturer publishes this code. Hitachi Astemo explains why two supplies need cross-checking: both share one ground, so without comparison the controller could not say which supply sagged.",["Motor B sensor supply line shorted to ground","Damaged motor B position sensor drawing too much current","Second sensor regulator in the control unit weak"],["Brake warning lamp on","Assist fades gradually or is limited at high demand"],3,2,["C05BC","C05BE","C05BF","C05B9","C058C"],"אספקת חיישן מצב מנוע מגבר בלם‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],C05BE:["Brake Booster Motor B Position Sensor Supply Circuit High","C05BE is stored when the 5 V feed of motor B's position sensor exceeds its upper limit. No manufacturer documents it publicly. Two mechanisms are typical: the supply line has contacted a wire carrying battery voltage, or the reference ground of the sensor side has lifted, which makes every voltage measured against it look too high.",["Motor B sensor supply shorted to a battery-voltage wire","Open or high-resistance sensor ground raising the measured voltage","Second sensor supply regulator out of regulation"],["Brake warning lamp and assist warning","Possibly further sensor codes if a shared ground is affected"],3,2,["C05BC","C05BD","C05BF","C05BA","C058D"],"אספקת חיישן מצב מנוע מגבר בלם‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],C05BF:["Brake Booster Motor B Position Sensor Supply Circuit Range/Performance","C05BF concerns a motor B sensor supply that stays inside its hard limits but behaves implausibly – it fluctuates, disagrees with the independent monitor, or does not match the first supply. No manufacturer documents C05BF publicly.",["Intermittent contact or corrosion in the motor B sensor supply wiring","Unstable sensor supply regulator or failing filter capacitor in the control unit","Fault in the supply monitoring circuit itself"],["Brake warning lamp appearing at times","Assist occasionally reduced, code returns after clearing"],3,2,["C05BC","C05BD","C05BE","C05BB","C058E"],"אספקת חיישן מצב מנוע מגבר בלם‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],C05C0:["Brake Pedal Position Sensor A Not Learned","The control unit has no valid learned rest position for channel A of the brake pedal position sensor, so it cannot turn the raw signal into a reliable pedal travel. No manufacturer documents C05C0 publicly. The closest GM analogue is C0277 with failure type 4B: the body module reports that the home position of the pedal sensor was never learned and asks for a recalibration.",["Learn procedure not run after sensor or module replacement","Learn routine aborted because the pedal was touched or the vehicle moved","Sensor channel A faulty or mounted out of position","Learned values lost in the control module memory"],["Brake or ABS warning lamp and message in the cluster","Brake lights or cruise control cancel react late or not at all","Regenerative braking or brake assist functions restricted"],2,2,["C05C1","C0619","C0277","C05D4"],"חיישן מצב דוושת בלם‏ A — לא בוצע לימוד"],C05C1:["Brake Pedal Position Sensor B Not Learned","Set when the second, redundant channel B of the brake pedal position sensor lacks a stored zero point. Many electric and hybrid brake pedals read travel twice so that one channel can cross-check the other; Bosch builds such pedal travel sensors with a magnetic field sensor and two redundant outputs. Without a learned rest value for B, that cross-check is lost even when channel A is fine.",["Channel B not learned after a repair or software update","Learn conditions not met (pedal pressed, vehicle rolling)","Channel B of the pedal sensor faulty or out of tolerance"],["Brake warning lamp or service message","Reduced redundancy, some assist or regeneration functions disabled"],2,2,["C05C0","C061A","C0277","C05D4"],"חיישן מצב דוושת בלם‏ B — לא בוצע לימוד"],C05C2:["Brake Booster Motor A Over Temperature","The electric booster or integrated brake unit has found its drive motor A, or the power stage feeding it, too hot. GM uses the code in several EBCM tables, all Type A with MIL: one design trips above 154 °C estimated motor temperature or on a bridge driver over-temperature shutdown, the Cadillac XT4 unit above 120 °C and 142 °C rotor/ECU temperature, 23OBDG07 and 25OBDG03B also when torque limiting stops the plunger…",["Long downhill braking or repeated hard stops overheating the motor","Hydraulic fault making the motor run longer than normal","Power stage or bridge driver reporting false or real over-temperature","Low supply voltage forcing current limitation"],["Malfunction indicator lamp and brake warning on GM models","Reduced brake assist, pedal feels harder","Regenerative braking temporarily disabled"],3,3,["C0594","C0590","C05B3","C05C3"],"מנוע מגבר בלם‏ A — חום יתר"],C05C3:["Brake Booster Motor A Supply Circuit","Points to the power feed of booster motor A: fuse, supply cable, ground or the module input that carries battery current to the motor stage, rather than the motor windings themselves. No manufacturer documents C05C3 publicly. Bosch specifies its iBooster for supply voltages above 9.8 V with up to 450 W of motor power, so a weak feed shows up quickly under load.",["Blown fuse or corroded high-current feed to the booster","Loose or corroded ground of the brake unit","Weak 12 V battery or charging fault causing voltage dips","Internal supply path of the brake module damaged"],["Brake warning lamp, loss or reduction of brake assist","Hard brake pedal, especially at low battery voltage","Further faults for regeneration or driver assistance braking"],2,2,["C05C2","C0590","C0591","C0595"],"אספקת מנוע מגבר בלם‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C05C4:["Brake Pressure Sensor F Missing Calibration","The brake controller finds no stored calibration (offset or zero point) for pressure sensor F, the sixth hydraulic pressure sensor in its numbering. Which physical sensor carries the letter F is up to the maker, and none publishes C05C4.",["Calibration skipped after module or hydraulic unit replacement","Calibration interrupted by brake application or low voltage","Calibration data lost in the module memory"],["ABS, ESC or brake warning lamp on","Stability control or brake assist functions disabled"],2,2,["C05C5","C0560","C059B","C059E"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ F — חסר כיול"],C05C5:["Brake Pressure Sensor F Circuit Range/Performance","Pressure sensor F delivers a voltage inside the electrical window, yet the value does not fit the braking situation: wrong offset at rest, a reading that disagrees with deceleration or the brake switch, or a pressure that does not match pedal travel. No manufacturer documents C05C5 for sensor F.",["Pressure sensor F drifting or with offset out of tolerance","Calibration not matching after component replacement","Air in the system or hydraulic fault falsifying pressure","Increased contact resistance at the sensor connector"],["ABS/ESC warning lamp, stability control off","Unusual pedal feel or uneven braking assistance"],2,2,["C05C4","C05C6","C05C7","C053D"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ F — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],C05C6:["Brake Pressure Sensor F Circuit Low","The signal of pressure sensor F sits below its valid band. Ratiometric 5 V pressure sensors normally output roughly 0.5 to 4.5 V; Denso describes treating 0 to 0.3 V as a fault zone, and with a pull-down resistor at the input a broken supply or signal wire also drags the reading toward zero.",["Signal wire shorted to ground","5 V reference interrupted or shorted to ground","Internal fault of pressure sensor F"],["ABS, ESC and traction control warning lamps on","Stability and traction control unavailable"],2,2,["C05C7","C05C8","C05C9","C059F"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ F — אות נמוך במעגל"],C05C7:["Brake Pressure Sensor F Circuit High","Here the voltage of pressure sensor F rises above the top of its measuring range. With the common pull-down input, Denso explains that a lost sensor ground lifts the output past 4.7 V, which lies in the upper fault band; a short of the signal to a voltage source has the same effect.",["Open or high-resistance sensor ground","Signal wire shorted to a voltage source","Sensor F reporting an internal fault at the upper rail"],["ABS/ESC lamp on, stability functions switched off","Live data shows implausibly high brake pressure with pedal released"],2,2,["C05C6","C05C8","C05C9","C05A0"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ F — אות גבוה במעגל"],C05C8:["Brake Pressure Sensor F Circuit/Open","General circuit fault of pressure sensor F, most often a break in one of its three wires (supply, signal, ground) or a connector that has lost contact. Where the reading ends up depends on the input circuit: Honeywell notes that after a power or ground loss the output goes high with a pull-up and low with a pull-down resistor, so an open line can look like C05C6 or C05C7 unless the module tells them apart.",["Connector unplugged, corroded or with pushed-back pins","Broken wire in the sensor harness","Internal open circuit in sensor F"],["ABS and ESC warning lamps on","Stability control and brake assist functions not available"],2,2,["C05C6","C05C7","C05C9","C05A1"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ F — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C05C9:["Brake Pressure Sensor Supply Circuit","Refers to the reference voltage the brake module provides to its hydraulic pressure sensors, not to one sensor's signal. If this feed collapses or rises, every sensor on it reads wrong at once, which is why the module checks the supply separately. Saab/GM monitors the 5 V reference of the brake pressure sensor and reacts within 0.1 s when that line touches ground or a voltage source.",["Reference line shorted to ground or to battery voltage","One pressure sensor internally shorted, pulling down the shared feed","Sensor supply regulator inside the brake module defective"],["Several brake pressure codes at the same time","ABS, ESC and brake assist warnings, functions off"],2,2,["C05C6","C05C7","C05C8","C05D1","C056A"],"אספקת חיישן לחץ בלם — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C05CA:["Brake Master Cylinder Piston Position Sensor A Circuit Voltage High","Channel A of the travel sensor at the master cylinder input rod reports a signal beyond its upper limit. In GM's booster-type brake modules this channel is a linear position sensor (LiPS) that talks to the EBCM digitally over SENT, so the high error is a message from the sensor itself: the Cadillac XT4 table in 19OBDG03D reacts within 0.033 s on the fast channel, 23OBDG07 and 25OBDG03B after 0.96 s on the slow…",["Position sensor A reporting out-of-range high internally","Supply voltage of the sensor out of tolerance","Sensor magnet or input rod out of position"],["Malfunction indicator lamp plus brake warning on GM models","Reduced brake assist or changed pedal feel"],3,3,["C05CB","C05CC","C05CD","C05D1"],"מעגל חיישן מצב בוכנת משאבת בלם ראשית בלם‏ A — מתח גבוה"],C05CB:["Brake Master Cylinder Piston Position Sensor A Circuit Voltage Low","Mirror image of C05CA: channel A of the master cylinder piston travel sensor reports that its value fell below the permitted range. GM documents it for its booster-type EBCMs, where the linear position sensor encodes travel digitally and flags its own low limit violation: the XT4 module acts after 0.033 s on the SENT fast channel, while the 2023 and 2025 tables wait 0.96 s for the slow-channel status, Type A, one…",["Position sensor A reporting out-of-range low","Sagging sensor supply voltage","Magnet carrier loose or damaged"],["Malfunction indicator lamp and brake system message","Brake assist reduced, regeneration possibly off"],3,3,["C05CA","C05CC","C05CE","C05D1"],"מעגל חיישן מצב בוכנת משאבת בלם ראשית בלם‏ A — מתח נמוך"],C05CC:["Brake Master Cylinder Piston Position Sensor A Circuit Range/Performance","Channel A (GM calls it PTS1) delivers a travel value that is electrically valid but physically wrong. GM's integrated controller with pedal simulator, the vacuum-free design ZF supplies, checks three things: travel above 38 mm (normal input piston travel is about 25 mm, about 36 mm without boost), a change faster than 700 mm/s, and a learned offset beyond 2.5 mm, each 100 ms, Type A.",["Sensor A offset drifted beyond the learn limit","Damaged travel sensor rod or mounting","Intermittent signal line producing jumps","Pedal not fully returning (floor mat, return spring)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp and brake warning","Changed pedal feel or reduced assist","Brake lights may react inconsistently"],3,3,["C05CA","C05CB","C05CF","C05D0"],"חיישן מצב בוכנת משאבת בלם ראשית בלם‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],C05CD:["Brake Master Cylinder Piston Position Sensor B Circuit Voltage High","Channel B of the master cylinder piston travel sensor is stuck at a permanent high level. In GM's booster-type EBCMs the second channel is not sent over SENT like channel A but as a PWM signal around 1 kHz, which is why high and low here mean a line that no longer toggles: the module sets C05CD when it sees a steady high state for 0.2 s, read as a short of the PWM line to supply (19OBDG03D XT4 section, 23OBDG07,…",["PWM signal line shorted to supply voltage","Output stage of sensor channel B failed high","Moisture or corrosion bridging pins in the connector"],["Malfunction indicator lamp and brake warning on GM models","Booster runs on channel A only or reduces assist"],3,3,["C05CE","C05CF","C05CA"],"מעגל חיישן מצב בוכנת משאבת בלם ראשית בלם‏ B — מתח גבוה"],C05CE:["Brake Master Cylinder Piston Position Sensor B Circuit Voltage Low","Here the second, PWM-coded output (channel B) of the piston travel sensor stays permanently low. GM's XT4 brake module and the later 23OBDG07 and 25OBDG03B tables interpret a constant low level for 0.2 s as the signal line shorted to ground, Type A, one trip, MIL.",["PWM signal line shorted to ground","Sensor channel B without supply or ground","Output stage of channel B failed low"],["Malfunction indicator lamp, brake system warning","Possibly reduced assist or regeneration off"],3,3,["C05CD","C05CF","C05CB"],"מעגל חיישן מצב בוכנת משאבת בלם ראשית בלם‏ B — מתח נמוך"],C05CF:["Brake Master Cylinder Piston Position Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","Plausibility fault on channel B (GM: PTS2) while its signal is electrically in range. GM's integrated controller with pedal simulator runs the same checks on B as on A: more than 38 mm of travel, a step faster than 700 mm/s that disagrees with channel A and the simulator pressure model, or an offset beyond 2.5 mm, all with 100 ms and Type A.",["Offset of sensor B outside the allowed range","Loose contact causing implausible jumps on channel B","Sensor rod or mounting worn or bent"],["Malfunction indicator lamp and brake warning","Pedal feels different, assist may be reduced"],3,3,["C05CD","C05CE","C05CC","C05D0"],"חיישן מצב בוכנת משאבת בלם ראשית בלם‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],C05D0:["Brake Master Cylinder Piston Position Sensor A/B Correlation","Both travel channels are individually plausible, but they disagree with each other. GM's integrated controller votes two out of three: PTS1, PTS2 and a third travel estimate (BAS); if PTS1 and PTS2 differ by more than 2 mm and one of them also deviates from the third value by over 2 mm, that channel is declared failed after 100 ms.",["One sensor channel drifting away from the other","Mechanical play at the sensor or input rod","Contact resistance on one channel only"],["Malfunction indicator lamp and brake warning","Brake system switches to reduced mode, regeneration may be off"],3,3,["C05CC","C05CF","C05D1"],"חיישן מצב בוכנת משאבת בלם ראשית בלם‏ A/B — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],C05D1:["Brake Master Cylinder Piston Position Sensor Supply Circuit","Fault on the reference supply of the master cylinder piston (pedal travel) sensor. GM's integrated brake controller provides two 5 V supplies, each feeding one pedal travel channel and one motor position channel; C05D1 covers the first (PTS1/MPS1), C05BB the second. The supply fails below 4.85 V or above 5.15 V for 100 ms;",["Supply line shorted to ground or to another voltage","Pedal travel or motor position sensor loading the supply","Supply circuit on the control module board defective"],["Malfunction indicator lamp, brake warning and loss of assist","Further codes for pedal travel and motor position sensors"],3,3,["C05CA","C05CB","C05BB","C05D0"],"אספקת חיישן מצב בוכנת משאבת בלם ראשית בלם — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C05D2:["Master Cylinder Piston Position Higher Than Expected","The piston has travelled further than the measured pressure justifies, a sign that fluid escapes or a sensor misreads. GM's integrated controller models the simulator pressure from pedal travel and sets C05D2 when the model exceeds the measured value by more than 20 bar (250 ms in 19OBDG03D, 500 ms in 25OBDG04B), naming master cylinder or simulator seal leakage and an in-range pressure sensor fault.",["Brake module software issue (GM 20-NA-073, reprogramming)","Internal leakage at master cylinder or simulator seals","Simulator pressure sensor reading too low within range","Air in the hydraulic system after service"],["Longer, softer brake pedal with higher pedal force","Loss of brake assist and messages in the driver information centre","Malfunction indicator lamp on GM models"],3,3,["C05D3","C05D5","C053D"],""],C05D3:["Driver Applied Pressure Higher Than Expected","The pressure the driver generates is higher than the measured pedal travel would predict, a hard pedal pattern. GM's integrated controller sets C05D3 when the measured simulator pressure is more than 20 bar above its travel-based model, outside fast applications, naming a closed or blocked simulator valve, a seized simulator and an in-range sensor fault.",["Weak or discharged 12 V battery (GM PIT6012)","Pedal simulator valve closed or blocked","Pedal simulator piston seized","Pressure or travel sensor misreading within range"],["Check engine lamp on together with brake system message","Brake pedal feels spongy, hard or unusual"],3,3,["C05D2","C05D5","C053D"],""],C05D4:["Brake Master Cylinder Piston Position Sensor Calibration Not Learned","No valid zero calibration exists for the master cylinder piston travel sensors. GM's integrated controller stores the end-of-line zeroing of its pedal travel sensors in non-volatile memory and reloads it each drive; C05D4 sets within 10 ms after start if the stored status shows the learn failed.",["Zeroing not done after replacement of the brake unit","Calibration disturbed by vehicle movement or pedal input","Sensor offset too large, too small or unsteady","Memory error in the brake control module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp and brake warning after start","Brake system in reduced mode until calibrated"],2,3,["C05CC","C05CF","C05C0","C05C1"],"כיול חיישן מצב בוכנת משאבת בלם ראשית בלם — לא בוצע לימוד"],C05D5:["Brake Master Cylinder Cut Off Valve","Electrical fault of the solenoid valve that separates the master cylinder from the wheel circuits in by-wire operation, so pressure comes from the motor and the pedal works against a simulator. In GM's booster-type EBCMs (XT4, 23OBDG07, 25OBDG03B) the valve driver reports over-current of about 4 to 6.5 A, an output stage above 195-220 °C, a lost power ground or lost freewheeling within 0.03 s.",["Valve coil shorted or open inside the hydraulic unit","Valve driver stage or ASIC in the module defective","Poor power ground of the brake module","Valve overheated by excessive activation time"],["Malfunction indicator lamp and brake warning","Loss of brake assist, pedal works on the master cylinder directly","ESC and traction control limited"],4,3,["C05D2","C05D3","C0595"],""],C05D6:["Power Steering Control Module Processor Performance","The electric power steering controller has found that its own processor, or the cross-check between its processors, is not working as expected. Toyota documents the code as C05D604 in the ECU of the EPS steering gear: 2019–2020 RAV4 and RAV4 Hybrid light the EPS warning in red or yellow at start-up or while driving (T-SB-0061-20), and the 2022 Tundra and Lexus LX 600 log it at start-up, often together with C15D704.",["EPS controller software flags a false processor fault, update available","Supply voltage dip during engine start disturbs the self-test","Internal hardware fault in the steering control module"],["Red or yellow power steering warning lamp","Steering suddenly heavier or assist reduced","Fault appears mainly right after starting the vehicle"],2,2,["U0131","C05D5"],"מעבד מודול בקרת הגה כוח — ביצועים לא תקינים"],C05D7:["Brake Transmission Shift Interlock (BTSI) Control Circuit","Covers the output that drives the brake transmission shift interlock, the solenoid that keeps the selector in park until the brake pedal is pressed. In the US, FMVSS 114 has required this lock since 1 September 2010 on vehicles up to 4,536 kg fitted with an automatic gearbox and a park position.",["Interlock solenoid coil open or shorted","Damaged wiring or corroded connector at the shifter","Driver stage in the shifter or body module faulty","Brake light switch signal missing, so the lock is never released"],["Selector cannot be moved out of park despite pressing the brake","Selector leaves park without the brake applied","No clicking of the interlock when the brake is pressed"],2,0,["P081F","P0928","P0929","P0930","P0931"],""],C05D8:["4WD/AWD Clutch A Actuator Control Circuit/Open","The AWD controller sees no plausible current path in the output that drives the actuator of clutch A, typically an open coil, motor winding or wire. Depending on the design, the actuator is an electromagnetic coil (JTEKT ITCC: coil current sets the transmitted torque) or an electric motor that turns a ball ramp through a worm gear, as in a Magna disconnect coupling.",["Actuator coil or motor winding open","Rear drive unit motor with misaligned magnet ring (Ford Bronco Sport 2.0L)","Broken wire or loose connector at the rear axle","Output stage in the AWD control module faulty"],["AWD warning lamp or message, vehicle drives on one axle only","Wheel spin on slippery surfaces when pulling away"],2,2,["C05D9","C05DA","C05DB","C05E7","C0095"],"מפעיל מצמד הנעה כפולה‏ A — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],C05D9:["4WD/AWD Clutch A Actuator Control Circuit Performance","The actuator circuit of clutch A is electrically intact, but the actuator does not respond as commanded, for example the measured current, motor speed or achieved torque differs from the target. Ford uses this code widely in its AWD module. Bronco 2021–2022: C05D9:19 or :99 with the wrench lamp and AWD off, caused by a discharged battery; check the battery and reprogram the module (TSB 22-2136, 22-2447).",["Low battery state of charge or weak supply voltage","AWD module software needs updating","Actuator motor worn or misassembled (magnet ring)","Ball ramp or gear train of the actuator binding"],["AWD fault message, AWD inoperative for the rest of the trip","Powertrain malfunction (wrench) lamp on","Function returns after restarting the vehicle"],2,2,["C05D8","C05DA","C05DB","C05E8","C0095","C05F9"],"מפעיל מצמד הנעה כפולה‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],C05DA:["4WD/AWD Clutch A Actuator Control Circuit Low","The voltage measured on the clutch A actuator line stays below the expected level, which usually means a short to ground somewhere between the control module and the coil or motor. Mitsubishi Electric describes a method for an electromagnetic driveline clutch: a high-side PWM transistor and a low-side switch feed the coil, the terminal voltages are compared with their normal values, and on a ground fault both…",["Actuator wire chafed through and shorted to ground","Water or corrosion in the connector at the axle","Coil or motor winding shorted to the housing"],["AWD switched off with warning lamp","Fault returns immediately after clearing"],2,2,["C05D8","C05DB","C05D9","C05E9"],"מפעיל מצמד הנעה כפולה‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],C05DB:["4WD/AWD Clutch A Actuator Control Circuit High","Set when the clutch A actuator line reads too high, typically because it touches battery voltage or because the low-side switch cannot pull it down. For an electromagnetic clutch, Mitsubishi Electric checks for this short with the selector in P or N by comparing the terminal voltages against normal values, then releases the clutch by turning off both drivers.",["Actuator wire shorted to a supply line in the harness","Output transistor in the AWD module stuck on","Corrosion bridging pins in the actuator connector"],["AWD warning, all-wheel drive disabled","Possible binding or tyre scrub in tight turns if the clutch drags"],2,2,["C05D8","C05DA","C05D9","C05EA"],"מפעיל מצמד הנעה כפולה‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],C05DC:["4WD/AWD Clutch A Temperature Too High","The calculated or measured temperature of clutch A has passed the protection limit, usually after long slipping in sand, snow or while towing. Audi stores C05DC00 in the AWD control unit of quattro ultra models: in TSB 2075681/1 the technician drives circles at full lock below 10 km/h for up to 15 minutes until the yellow four-wheel drive overheating lamp comes on, then erases the entry.",["Long periods of wheel slip in deep snow, sand or mud","Towing or steep climbs with heavy load","Different tyre sizes or wear front to rear force constant slip","Aged or wrong clutch fluid"],["Yellow AWD overheating warning","Less drive to the secondary axle until the clutch has cooled","Engine power briefly reduced during wheel spin"],1,2,["C05DD","C05DE","C05EB","C0093","C05F9"],"טמפרטורת מצמד הנעה כפולה‏ A — ערך גבוה מדי"],C05DD:["4WD/AWD Clutch A Performance/Stuck Disengaged","The AWD controller has commanded clutch A to close, but the speed difference across it or the actuator feedback shows that it is not transmitting the expected torque or has stayed open. Typical reasons are worn plates, a sticking actuator or a ball ramp that cannot travel far enough.",["Clutch plates worn, slipping under load","Actuator or ball ramp sticking short of full travel","Wrong, aged or low clutch fluid","Damaged shift fork or dog teeth in the decoupling unit"],["AWD malfunction message, vehicle behaves like two-wheel drive","Wheel spin and traction control interventions on slippery roads"],3,2,["C05DE","C05DF","C05DC","C05EC","C05E6"],""],C05DE:["4WD/AWD Clutch A Stuck Engaged","Clutch A keeps transmitting torque or stays connected although the controller has ordered it to open. Front and rear axles are then forced to turn together, which shows up as binding, tyre scrub or droning in tight, slow turns. Audi documents the twin code C05ED00 (clutch B stuck engaged) in its quattro ultra AWD module J492; TSB 2051558 traces it to a worn shift fork in the rear differential.",["Clutch plates welded or swollen after overheating","Actuator or ball ramp seized in the applied position","Aged clutch fluid causing drag and stick-slip","Worn shift fork keeps a dog clutch engaged"],["Binding, hopping or tyre scrub when parking or in tight turns","Droning or vibration from the rear axle","AWD malfunction message"],3,2,["C05DD","C05DC","C05ED","C05DF"],"מצמד הנעה כפולה‏ A — תקוע במצב משולב"],C05DF:["4WD/AWD Clutch A Engagement Fault","The engagement sequence of clutch A did not finish correctly: the actuator ran, but synchronisation, connection feedback or the timing check failed. This matters most for disconnecting systems that must reconnect a stationary driveline on the move. Audi states that quattro ultra synchronises the disconnected parts and closes the rear decoupling clutch in about 200 ms;",["Speeds not matched in time before the clutch closes","Actuator too slow because of low voltage or wear","Engagement feedback sensor reports wrong state","Damaged dog teeth block engagement"],["AWD unavailable message, sometimes only for one trip","Clunk from the driveline when AWD tries to engage"],3,2,["C05DD","C05DE","C05E6","C05EE"],""],C05E0:["4WD/AWD Clutch A Position Sensor Circuit","General electrical fault in the sensor that reports where the clutch A actuator stands, without the controller narrowing it down to low, high or intermittent. Electromechanical AWD clutches need this signal because the motor angle maps to plate travel and clamping force.",["Sensor wiring or connector damaged","Position sensor in the actuator faulty","Sensor supply or ground from the AWD module missing"],["AWD warning, all-wheel drive switched off","Traction loss when pulling away on low grip"],2,2,["C05E1","C05E2","C05E3","C05E4","C05E5"],"חיישן מצב מצמד הנעה כפולה‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C05E1:["4WD/AWD Clutch A Position Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","The clutch A position signal is electrically within limits but does not fit what the actuator should be doing, for instance it barely changes while the motor runs or jumps further than the gearing allows. Bosch's transfer-case clutch provides the data for such a cross-check: worm wheel position, motor speed and motor current are all measured, so a position that drifts away from the counted motor rotation stands out.",["Sensor magnet or target loose or misaligned","Position sensor drifting or degraded","Slipping or damaged actuator gearing"],["AWD warning, torque transfer to the secondary axle stopped","Fault often sets only after some driving"],2,2,["C05E0","C05E2","C05E3","C05E4","C05E6"],"חיישן מצב מצמד הנעה כפולה‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],C05E2:["4WD/AWD Clutch A Position Sensor Circuit Low","The position signal from the clutch A actuator has dropped below its valid band. On a sensor powered by a reference supply this normally means the signal line is shorted to ground, the supply is missing, or the sensor output is dead.",["Signal wire shorted to ground","Sensor supply open or shorted","Sensor output failed low"],["AWD warning lamp on","Vehicle drives with one axle only"],2,2,["C05E0","C05E1","C05E3","C05E4"],"חיישן מצב מצמד הנעה כפולה‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],C05E3:["4WD/AWD Clutch A Position Sensor Circuit High","Here the clutch A position signal sits above the highest value a working sensor can deliver. Usual explanations are a signal line touching the supply or battery voltage, a lost sensor ground that lets the output float up, or an internal sensor fault.",["Signal wire shorted to supply or battery voltage","Sensor ground open","Sensor output failed high"],["AWD warning lamp on","All-wheel drive disabled until the fault is repaired"],2,2,["C05E0","C05E1","C05E2","C05E4"],"חיישן מצב מצמד הנעה כפולה‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],C05E4:["4WD/AWD Clutch A Position Sensor Circuit Intermittent","The clutch A position signal drops out or jumps for short moments and then recovers, so the controller sees implausible steps between consecutive samples. The pattern points to a loose pin, a chafed wire that touches only on bumps, or moisture in the connector near the axle, rather than a dead sensor.",["Loose or corroded pin in the sensor connector","Harness chafing at the axle or subframe","Sensor with internal intermittent fault"],["AWD warning that comes and goes","Short losses of drive to the secondary axle"],2,2,["C05E0","C05E1","C05E2","C05E3"],"חיישן מצב מצמד הנעה כפולה‏ A — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],C05E5:["4WD/AWD Clutch A Position Not Learned","The controller has no valid stored reference for clutch A, typically the touch or kiss point where the plates begin to carry torque. Bosch finds this point on a transfer-case clutch by running the motor at constant speed and intersecting two regression lines from the free-travel and loaded ranges; the run is repeated at engine start or at standstill because wear shifts the curve.",["Learn not run after replacing actuator, clutch or module","Learn routine aborted, for example by low voltage or vehicle movement","Stored values lost after battery disconnection or module fault"],["AWD warning directly after a repair","All-wheel drive disabled or harsh engagement"],2,2,["C05E6","C05E0","C05E1","C05FF"],"מצב מצמד הנעה כפולה‏ A — לא בוצע לימוד"],C05E6:["4WD/AWD Clutch A Position Control Error","The closed-loop control that drives clutch A to a target position cannot hold or reach it: the deviation between commanded and measured position stays too large for too long. Magna describes an ECU that controls the angular position of the ball ramp actuator ring; Bosch drives its transfer-case clutch motor with a cascaded current and speed controller through an H-bridge;",["Actuator gear train or ball ramp binding","Weak actuator motor or low supply voltage","Incorrectly learned reference position","Control software calibration issue"],["AWD malfunction message, AWD disabled","Uneven or delayed torque transfer before the fault sets"],3,2,["C05E5","C05E1","C05DD","C05DF","C05EF"],"שגיאת בקרת מצב מצמד הנעה כפולה‏ A"],C05E7:["4WD/AWD Clutch B Actuator Control Circuit/Open","The AWD module finds no usable current path in its driver output for the clutch B actuator, most often an open coil, motor winding, connector or wire. A second clutch exists either in a twin-clutch rear drive unit with one clutch per rear wheel, or as a disconnect stage in the rear axle.",["Open coil or motor winding in the clutch B actuator","Misaligned magnet ring in the rear drive unit motor (Ford Bronco Sport 2.0L)","Broken wire or corroded connector between AWD module and rear drive unit","Faulty driver stage in the AWD module"],["AWD warning lamp or message, rear axle no longer driven","Rear locking or torque vectoring function unavailable on twin-clutch units","Fault is present again immediately after clearing"],2,2,["C05E8","C05E9","C05EA","C05D8"],"מפעיל מצמד הנעה כפולה‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],C05E8:["4WD/AWD Clutch B Actuator Control Circuit Performance","The clutch B actuator circuit is electrically intact, yet its response does not match the command: current, motor movement or the torque built up stays outside the expected band. Ford stores C05E8:71 in the AWD module of 2021–2022 Bronco Sport 2.0L vehicles (SSM 51117), together with C05D9:71 for clutch A;",["Misaligned magnet ring in the rear drive unit motor (Ford Bronco Sport 2.0L)","Worn or sluggish actuator motor or hydraulic control for clutch B","Low battery voltage limiting actuator current","Binding in the actuator mechanism or clutch pack"],["AWD fault message, all-wheel drive off for the rest of the trip","Reduced traction off-road because one rear wheel is no longer controlled"],2,2,["C05E7","C05E9","C05EA","C05D9"],"מפעיל מצמד הנעה כפולה‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],C05E9:["4WD/AWD Clutch B Actuator Control Circuit Low","The voltage on the clutch B actuator line reads below the expected value, which points to a short to ground between AWD module and coil or motor, or to a driver stage that pulls the line down.",["Chafed actuator wire shorting to ground near the rear axle","Water or corrosion in the rear drive unit connector","Internal short in the clutch B coil or motor"],["AWD warning, all-wheel drive disabled","Fault returns at once after clearing, often after driving through water"],2,2,["C05E7","C05EA","C05E8","C05DA"],"מפעיל מצמד הנעה כפולה‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],C05EA:["4WD/AWD Clutch B Actuator Control Circuit High","The clutch B actuator line reads too high, usually from contact with a battery feed or because the low-side switch no longer pulls it down. With coil-type clutches the danger is current flowing although the module wants the clutch open: in JTEKT's ITCC the coil current sets the transmitted torque, so a partly energised coil lets the clutch drag.",["Actuator wire shorted to a supply line","Low-side switch in the AWD module defective","Corrosion bridging pins in the actuator connector"],["AWD warning, all-wheel drive disabled","Possible binding or tyre scrub when manoeuvring"],2,2,["C05E7","C05E9","C05E8","C05DB"],"מפעיל מצמד הנעה כפולה‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],C05EB:["4WD/AWD Clutch B Temperature Too High","The AWD module has calculated or measured that clutch B has passed its permitted temperature, usually after long slipping in deep snow, sand or mud, or when towing. In a twin-clutch rear module the two wheel clutches heat up separately, so one side can reach its limit while the other is still cool, for instance when only one rear wheel spins.",["Long wheel spin on one rear wheel in snow, sand or mud","Towing or climbing with high, continuous torque transfer","Different tyre sizes or wear front to rear causing permanent slip","Aged or wrong fluid in the rear drive unit"],["AWD overheating or temporarily disabled message","Less drive to the rear until the clutch has cooled","Engine power briefly reduced during wheel spin"],1,2,["C05EC","C05ED","C05DC","C0093"],"טמפרטורת מצמד הנעה כפולה‏ B — ערך גבוה מדי"],C05EC:["4WD/AWD Clutch B Performance/Stuck Disengaged","Clutch B was commanded to connect, but speed signals or actuator feedback show that it carries no torque or has stayed open. In disconnecting systems the second clutch is often a positive shift element rather than a friction pack: Audi's quattro ultra releases both a gearbox-side multi-plate clutch and a decoupler in the rear differential, which autozine describes as an electromechanically operated dog clutch on the…",["Clutch B actuator sticking or too weak to shift the sleeve","Worn shift fork or damaged dog teeth in the rear differential","Worn friction plates on twin-clutch units","Low or wrong fluid in the rear drive unit"],["AWD malfunction message, vehicle drives on the front axle only","Wheel spin and traction control interventions on slippery roads"],3,2,["C05ED","C05EE","C05EB","C05EF","C05DD"],""],C05ED:["4WD/AWD Clutch B Stuck Engaged","Clutch B is still connected although the AWD module has ordered it to open. It is the one code of the clutch B group that a manufacturer documents in detail. Audi stores C05ED00 with symptom code 29725 in the AWD control unit J492 of quattro ultra models (A4, A5, A6, A7, Q5 and their S versions, mainly 2018–2020), and the instrument cluster sporadically reports a four-wheel drive malfunction.",["Worn shift fork in the rear differential (Audi quattro ultra)","Clutch B actuator seized in the engaged position","Welded or swollen plates on friction-type clutch B"],["Sporadic four-wheel drive malfunction message","Rear driveline keeps turning when it should be decoupled, possible noise"],3,2,["C05EC","C05EE","C05EB","C05DE"],"מצמד הנעה כפולה‏ B — תקוע במצב משולב"],C05EE:["4WD/AWD Clutch B Engagement Fault","The connection sequence of clutch B did not complete: the actuator moved, but speed matching, position feedback or the time window failed. This concerns above all positive dog clutches, which may only close once both halves turn at almost the same speed.",["Speed of the disconnected driveline not matched in time","Slow actuator, often from low voltage or cold, thick fluid","Faulty position or shaft speed feedback","Worn or chipped dog teeth blocking engagement"],["AWD unavailable message, sometimes only for one trip","Clunk or rattle from the rear when AWD tries to connect"],3,2,["C05EC","C05ED","C05EF","C05DF","C05F4"],""],C05EF:["4WD/AWD Clutch B Position Control Error","The position loop that moves clutch B to a target cannot reach or hold it: commanded and measured actuator position stay apart for too long. Such loops depend on a learned reference. Dana's patent finds the kiss point from motor current plotted against Hall or encoder shaft position; Bosch derives it from two regression lines while the motor pushes against the rising clutch load;",["Binding ball ramp, gear or shift mechanism","Weak actuator motor or low supply voltage","Learned reference no longer valid after wear or part replacement","Implausible actuator position signal"],["AWD malfunction message, AWD disabled","Delayed or uneven torque transfer before the fault sets"],3,2,["C05EC","C05EE","C05E8","C05E6"],"שגיאת בקרת מצב מצמד הנעה כפולה‏ B"],C05F0:["Rear Drive Shaft Speed Sensor Circuit Low","The signal of the rear drive shaft speed sensor stays below its valid range, typically due to an open circuit, a short to ground or a missing sensor supply. The AWD module needs this speed to match a disconnected rear driveline to the wheels before a clutch closes; American Axle's patent feeds a pinion shaft speed sensor into exactly that synchronisation check.",["Open sensor wire or loose connector","Signal or supply line shorted to ground","Failed Hall sensor IC"],["AWD warning, all-wheel drive not connected","Vehicle drives in front-wheel drive only"],2,2,["C05F1","C05F3","C05F4","C05F2","C05EE"],"חיישן מהירות ציר הנעה אחורית — אות נמוך במעגל"],C05F1:["Rear Drive Shaft Speed Sensor Circuit High","Here the rear drive shaft speed signal reads above its valid range, as caused by a short to supply voltage, a damaged sensor IC or a fault at the module input. With a two-wire Hall sensor the module watches the current between a low and a high level (Allegro A19420: about 7 and 14 mA); a current clearly above the upper band cannot be a speed pulse.",["Sensor signal line shorted to supply voltage","Damaged sensor IC drawing excessive current","Faulty sensor input in the AWD module"],["AWD warning, all-wheel drive not connected","Fault sets immediately at ignition on"],2,2,["C05F0","C05F3","C05F4","C05F2"],"חיישן מהירות ציר הנעה אחורית — אות גבוה במעגל"],C05F2:["Rear Drive Shaft Speed Sensor Circuit Intermittent","The speed signal from the rear drive shaft drops out or jumps for short moments and then recovers, so the AWD controller sees pulse gaps or sudden speed steps that no real shaft could make. Such sensors are often two-wire Hall ICs whose supply current toggles between two levels;",["Loose, corroded or water-affected connector at the sensor","Harness chafed or broken where it flexes near the axle or drive shaft","Sensor not seated firmly, air gap varies with vibration","Damaged or dirty target ring on the shaft"],["AWD or 4WD warning appears now and then and disappears again","All-wheel drive briefly unavailable, often on rough roads","Code stored as history without a current fault"],2,2,["C05F0","C05F1","C05F3","C05F4"],"חיישן מהירות ציר הנעה אחורית — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],C05F3:["Rear Drive Shaft Speed Sensor Circuit","Catch-all electrical fault for the rear drive shaft speed sensor circuit, stored when the controller detects a problem but does not narrow it to low, high or intermittent. Typical are an open supply or signal wire, a failed sensor IC or a fault in the module input. Two-wire Hall sensors such as the Allegro A19420 report speed as alternating current levels and can also signal an internal error;",["Open signal or supply wire between sensor and module","Failed speed sensor IC","Connector not latched or pins pushed back","Faulty input stage in the AWD control module"],["AWD or 4WD service message, all-wheel drive switched off","Vehicle drives on the primary axle only","No drive shaft speed shown in live data"],2,2,["C05F0","C05F1","C05F2","C05F4"],"חיישן מהירות ציר הנעה אחורית — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C05F4:["Rear Drive Shaft Speed Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","The rear drive shaft speed is electrically valid but does not fit the rest of the driveline. The controller can compare it with wheel speeds, the axle ratio and the clutch state: with AWD engaged the shaft must follow the rear wheels, and a reading that stays near zero, lags or runs too fast is implausible.",["Air gap too large, sensor not fully seated or wrong spacer","Target ring damaged, loose or covered with metal debris","Wrong sensor, target ring or axle ratio after repair","Slipping AWD clutch makes shaft speed deviate"],["AWD warning and all-wheel drive disabled","Rear axle no longer connects in a disconnecting AWD system","Live data shows shaft speed that does not match wheel speeds"],2,2,["C05F0","C05F1","C05F2","C05F3"],"חיישן מהירות ציר הנעה אחורית — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],C05F5:["4WD/AWD Range Actuator Control Circuit/Open","The range actuator is the electric gear motor that moves the transfer case between high range, neutral and low range. With this code the controller finds no usable current path in the motor drive circuit, usually an open winding, wire or connector. Automotive H-bridge drivers such as the TI DRV8873-Q1 run a dedicated open-load test besides short and overcurrent checks.",["Shift motor connector not fully seated or corroded","Broken wire between control module and motor","Open motor winding or worn brushes in the range actuator","Failed output stage in the control module"],["4WD service message, low range cannot be selected","Range indicator flashes or does not change","Transfer case stays in its last position"],2,2,["C05F6","C05F7","C05F8","C05FA"],"מפעיל טווח הנעה כפולה — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],C05F6:["4WD/AWD Range Actuator Control Circuit Performance","The drive circuit of the range actuator is electrically present, but the response does not match the command: motor current, run time or achieved travel fall outside the window the controller expects. Magna describes a range shift motor driven by pulse width modulation in phases, fast to neutral, slower through synchronisation at about 55 to 80 percent of travel, and under PID position control from about 90 percent.",["High resistance in ground or supply of the motor circuit","Weak battery or low system voltage during the shift","Worn shift motor drawing abnormal current","Degraded driver stage in the control module"],["Range shifts slow or incomplete","Intermittent 4WD service message, often when cold or at start-up","Shift attempt aborted, transfer case returns to previous range"],2,2,["C05F5","C05F7","C05F8","C05FA"],"מפעיל טווח הנעה כפולה — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],C05F7:["4WD/AWD Range Actuator Control Circuit Low","A range actuator drive line sits below its expected voltage, typically because a motor lead is shorted to ground or the driver pulls it down when it should not. In a reversing gear motor each terminal is alternately the high and the low side, so a ground short on either lead shows up depending on shift direction.",["Motor lead chafed through and shorted to the body or transfer case","Water or corrosion in the shift motor connector","Internal short in the shift motor","Faulty low-side driver in the control module"],["4WD service message, range change refused","Fault may appear only when shifting in one direction","Blown fuse for the transfer case motor possible"],2,2,["C05F5","C05F6","C05F8"],"מפעיל טווח הנעה כפולה — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],C05F8:["4WD/AWD Range Actuator Control Circuit High","A range actuator drive line carries more voltage than the controller expects, for example from a short to battery voltage or because a low-side switch no longer pulls the line down. The risk is a motor that runs or is braked when it should be idle, or a driver that cannot complete a commanded direction. The TI DRV8873-Q1 lists short to battery as its own protection case and disables the output that sees it.",["Motor lead shorted to a battery-fed wire","Low-side switch in the control module failed open","Corrosion bridging pins in the shift motor connector"],["4WD service message, range shift disabled","Shift motor may hum or run unexpectedly","Transfer case remains in the last selected range"],2,2,["C05F5","C05F6","C05F7"],"מפעיל טווח הנעה כפולה — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],C05F9:["4WD/AWD Range Actuator Temperature Too High","The controller has measured or estimated that the range actuator motor is too hot and blocks further shifts until it cools. Most designs model temperature from motor activity; a Denso patent for a similar shift actuator adds a fixed increment per motor start, lets the estimate decay over time and limits the motor above a protection value of 137 degrees C in its example.",["Many range shifts in a short time, motor protection active","Low battery charge prolongs motor run time and current","Stiff shift mechanism or blocked shift loads the motor","Worn shift motor drawing excess current"],["Message that 4WD is overheated or temporarily unavailable","Range shifts refused until the system cools","Wrench or 4WD service lamp on"],1,2,["C05FA","C05F6","C05DC"],"טמפרטורת מפעיל טווח הנעה כפולה — ערך גבוה מדי"],C05FA:["4WD/AWD Range Actuator Performance/Stuck","The range actuator received a valid command and its circuit looks fine, yet the transfer case did not reach the requested range in time or stays in one position. Range shifts use toothed sleeves that can meet tooth on tooth; BorgWarner places a torsion spring between motor and barrel cam so the motor can keep turning and the stored energy finishes the shift once the teeth align.",["Shift blocked tooth on tooth, often when not rolling or not in neutral","Binding range fork, cam or shift rail inside the transfer case","Worn or seized shift motor gear train","Low or wrong transfer case fluid"],["Low range does not engage or does not release","Range indicator keeps flashing","Grinding or clicking from the transfer case during the shift"],3,2,["C05F6","C05F9","C0600","C05FC"],""],C05FB:["4WD/AWD Range Actuator Position Sensor Circuit","General electrical fault in the circuit of the sensor that reports where the range actuator stands, without narrowing it to low, high or implausible. Designs vary: Magna mounts a programmable linear Hall IC on the transfer case housing that reads a stepped sector plate or the range fork and outputs a duty cycle; BorgWarner uses a single sensor whose probe rides five plateaus on the cam;",["Sensor or actuator connector not fully latched","Open supply, ground or signal wire of the position sensor","Failed position sensor, often integrated in the shift motor"],["4WD service message, range shifts disabled","Range indicator blank or flashing","Further transfer case codes stored at the same time"],2,2,["C05FC","C05FD","C05FE","C00A7","C00A8"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל טווח הנעה כפולה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C05FC:["4WD/AWD Range Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","The range actuator position signal is electrically valid but does not agree with what the actuator is doing: it does not change while the motor runs, lands between defined positions or contradicts a second position input. Magna's sensor resolves its four sector positions to about plus or minus 1.5 degrees, and BorgWarner's target has five plateaus, so a reading between steps is suspicious.",["Sensor target or magnet shifted, loose or worn","Moisture in the actuator, for example via a faulty breather","Sensor drifting with temperature or age","Actuator or module replaced without matching calibration"],["Flashing 4WD indicator, range display does not match actual range","Range shifts refused or repeated","4WD service message"],2,2,["C05FB","C05FD","C05FE","C05FF"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל טווח הנעה כפולה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],C05FD:["4WD/AWD Range Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Low","The range actuator position signal sits below the lowest value an intact sensor can deliver. With a sensor powered from a reference supply this usually means the signal line is shorted to ground, the supply is missing or the sensor output has failed low. Fixed diagnostic bands are common for such position inputs;",["Signal wire shorted to ground","Missing sensor reference supply","Sensor output failed low"],["4WD service message, range shifts disabled","Range indicator shows no valid position"],2,2,["C05FB","C05FC","C05FE"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל טווח הנעה כפולה — אות נמוך במעגל"],C05FE:["4WD/AWD Range Actuator Position Sensor Circuit High","The range actuator position signal lies above the highest value a working sensor produces. Usual explanations are a signal line touching supply voltage, a lost sensor ground that lets the output float up, or an internal sensor fault.",["Signal wire shorted to supply or battery voltage","Open sensor ground","Sensor output failed high"],["4WD service message, range shifts disabled","Range display flashes or shows a wrong range"],2,2,["C05FB","C05FC","C05FD"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל טווח הנעה כפולה — אות גבוה במעגל"],C05FF:["4WD/AWD Range Actuator Position Not Learned","The controller lacks valid reference positions for the range actuator, so it cannot translate sensor readings into high, neutral and low. GM full-size trucks run such a relearn at every start-up: per PIP5089A the transfer case module drives the encoder motor to locate its position, and if a sensor, motor or circuit problem prevents this it sets C0569 and runs no further checks.",["Actuator or control module replaced without running the learn routine","Learn routine aborted by a sensor, motor or wiring fault","Stored values lost after battery disconnection or low voltage"],["4WD service message right after a repair","Range shifts unavailable until the learn has run","Range indicator flashes at start-up"],2,2,["C05FC","C0600","C05FA"],"מצב מפעיל טווח הנעה כפולה — לא בוצע לימוד"],C0600:["4WD/AWD Range Actuator Position Control Error","The position loop that drives the range actuator to a target does not reach or hold it: commanded and measured position stay apart for too long, although sensor and drive circuit pass their own checks. Magna describes such a loop for a transfer case range shift, with speed profiles per shift phase and PID control over the last tenth of travel down to a stop at the target.",["Stiff range fork, cam or shift rail slows the actuator","Weak shift motor or low supply voltage","Learned end positions no longer match the hardware","Play between sensor target and shift mechanism"],["Range shift incomplete, indicator flashes","4WD service message and range shifts blocked","Noise from the transfer case while the motor hunts for position"],3,2,["C05FA","C05FC","C05FF","C05E6","C05EF"],"שגיאת בקרת מצב מפעיל טווח הנעה כפולה"],C0601:["Active Air Dam Control Circuit/Open","An active air dam is a panel below the front bumper that an electric drive lowers at speed to reduce drag and raises for slow driving, towing or rough ground. Ford's patent for this design moves the panel with two motor-driven screw jacks under command of the PCM or body module over LIN or CAN; a GM patent closes the loop with position, motor current and back-EMF feedback.",["Actuator connector loose, unplugged or corroded after water entry","Wire broken in the exposed harness behind the bumper, often after impact or road debris","Open motor winding or internal fault in the air dam actuator"],["Active Air Dam System Fault message in the cluster","Air dam no longer moves and stays raised or lowered","Slightly higher fuel use on the highway when stuck raised"],2,0,["C0602","C0603","C0604","C062E","C062F","C0630","U0645"],"סכר אוויר פעיל — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],C0602:["Active Air Dam Control Circuit Low","C0602 says the control line to the air dam actuator is held below its expected voltage, most often because a motor lead touches ground or because water has bridged pins in the connector. Smart H-bridge drivers such as the DRV8873-Q1 see a grounded output as overcurrent, trip within a few microseconds and turn that half-bridge off, so the motor never gets drive.",["Actuator wire chafed through and touching the body or frame","Water and corrosion in the actuator connector after a damaged seal","Shorted motor or electronics inside the actuator"],["Air dam warning message in the instrument cluster","Air dam stays in one position","Fault returns as soon as the system commands movement"],2,0,["C0601","C0603","C0604","C062E"],"סכר אוויר פעיל — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],C0603:["Active Air Dam Control Circuit High","With C0603 the air dam control circuit reads above its permitted level, which points to a lead shorted to battery voltage or to another powered wire in the front-end harness. Motor driver ICs like the DRV8873-Q1 list a short to battery as a separate protected fault and disable the affected output.",["Control wire shorted to a battery-fed wire in the front harness","Fault in the actuator electronics holding the line high","Wrong pin assignment or splice after a previous bumper or harness repair"],["Air dam system fault message","Air dam does not deploy at highway speed","Possible blown fuse for the air dam circuit"],2,0,["C0601","C0602","C0604","C062F"],"סכר אוויר פעיל — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],C0604:["Active Air Dam Control Circuit Performance","C0604 is the air dam code that makers really publish: the panel does not reach or hold its commanded position even though the circuit itself looks sound. Ford stores C0604:00 in the PCM of 2021–2023 F-150s, often with a cluster warning that the air dam system has failed;",["Actuator firmware or PCM software level with known false or real faults (Ford F-150)","Broken bolts between actuator and air dam, panel hangs","Air dam bent, cracked or jammed after ground contact or debris","Water or corrosion in the actuator connector","Air dam lip rubbing on the front fascia"],["Active Air Dam System Fault See Manual message","Air dam hangs down or does not retract","Clunk from the front end when driving at moderate speed or decelerating","Check engine lamp on some Ram trucks"],2,1,["C0601","C0602","C0603","C0630","U0645"],"סכר אוויר פעיל — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],C0605:["Steering Wheel Angle Sensor Circuit/Open","The steering wheel angle sensor tells the stability system how far and how quickly the driver turns. C0605 means its circuit is open or no usable signal arrives at all: a broken supply, ground or signal wire, an unplugged connector or a dead sensor. In a Bosch patent for a PWM-output sensor, the control unit treats the signal as missing when no high level appears within one PWM period;",["Connector at the steering column loose or not latched after airbag or column work","Broken supply, ground or signal wire in the column harness","Steering angle sensor electronics failed"],["ESC/stability control warning lamp on, system off","Traction control and lane or parking assistants may be unavailable","Steering angle reads zero or not available in scan data"],2,2,["C0606","C0607","C0608","C0526","U0126"],"חיישן זווית גלגל הגה — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C0606:["Steering Wheel Angle Sensor Circuit Low","C0606 flags a steering angle signal or sensor supply that reads too low, as caused by a short to ground, a sagging supply or an output stuck at the bottom of its range. In the Kelsey-Hayes design the two phase lines swing between roughly 0.6 V and 4.4 V on a 5 V feed, and anything below the lower band is a fault;",["Signal wire chafed against the steering column and shorted to ground","Low sensor supply from a weak battery or a damaged feed circuit","Sensor output stage failed low"],["ESC warning lamp on and stability control unavailable","Steering angle in scan data pinned at one end value","Driver assistance messages about limited function"],2,2,["C0605","C0607","C0608","C0526"],"חיישן זווית גלגל הגה — אות נמוך במעגל"],C0607:["Steering Wheel Angle Sensor Circuit High","C0607 is the mirror image of C0606: the steering angle signal sits above its allowed ceiling. Usual reasons are a signal wire shorted to the sensor supply or to battery voltage, an open ground at the sensor, after which the line drifts up, or an internal fault driving the output to its top end. In the Kelsey-Hayes quadrature sensor a valid high state is near 4.4 V and readings beyond the upper limit are faults;",["Signal wire shorted to the sensor supply or battery voltage","Open sensor ground, signal floats high","Sensor output stage failed high"],["ESC and traction control warning lamps on","Steering angle shown at an implausible maximum value","Lane keeping or park assist switched off"],2,2,["C0605","C0606","C0608","C0526"],"חיישן זווית גלגל הגה — אות גבוה במעגל"],C0608:["Steering Wheel Angle Sensor Circuit Performance","C0608 covers a steering angle signal that is electrically in range but cannot be trusted: it jumps, drifts, freezes or disagrees with what yaw rate, lateral acceleration and wheel speeds imply. The Kelsey-Hayes patent rejects a centre offset that moves by more than about 15° after a dropout, and Bosch builds plausibility checks of the individual measuring channels into its GMR sensor.",["Sensor not zeroed after wheel alignment, steering or column repair","Steering wheel fitted off centre or toe out of adjustment","Worn or faulty sensor giving jumping or frozen values","Brief signal dropouts from a loose connector"],["ESC lamp on, sometimes only after a few turns or straight driving","Unexpected ESC braking interventions","Steering angle not zero with the wheels pointing straight"],2,2,["C0605","C0606","C0607","C0528","C052A","C05B2","C0830"],"חיישן זווית גלגל הגה — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],C0609:["Park Brake Switch Circuit","The park brake switch is the driver's apply and release button for an electric parking brake; on some cars it also reports lever or button state to other modules. C0609 covers an electrical fault in its circuit, such as an open contact, a short to ground or supply, or an unplugged connector.",["Connector at the switch or in the dash not fully engaged","Poor ground or control unit software (Audi Q4 e-tron case)","Worn, contaminated or corroded switch contacts, e.g. after spilled drinks"],["Park brake or drive system warning in the cluster","Parking brake does not respond to the button","Gear selection refused in some electric models"],2,2,["C060A","P05E3","U0128"],"מתג בלם חניה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C060A:["Park Brake Switch Stuck","C060A means the park brake switch reports a state that does not change when it should, or that contradicts itself: a jammed or welded contact, a button held down mechanically, or paired contacts that disagree. EPB buttons carry duplicated contacts for safety;",["Button jammed by dirt, sticky residue or a broken housing","One contact of the redundant pair welded or worn","Object in the console pressing the button"],["Park brake warning lamp or message","Brake does not apply or release from the button","Code returns right after clearing while the button is untouched"],1,0,["C0609","P05E3","P05E7"],"מתג בלם חניה — תקוע"],C060B:["Left Park Brake Actuator Control Circuit/Open","On motor-on-caliper parking brakes, a small DC motor drives a gear stage and a spindle that pushes the rear piston; ZF quotes up to 19 kN clamping force with its early swash plate gearbox and up to 25 kN with a two-stage planetary set for heavy vehicles.",["Corroded or loose connector or extension harness at the left caliper","Wire broken where the harness flexes with the suspension","Open winding in the left actuator motor"],["Red park brake lamp flashing or Service Parking Brake message","Left rear brake does not apply when the switch is pulled","Auto-hold or hill-start assist unavailable"],2,2,["C060C","C060D","C060E","C060F","C0610","C0670"],"מפעיל בלם חניה שמאלית — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],C060C:["Left Park Brake Actuator Control Circuit Low","C060C indicates that a drive line of the left parking brake motor is pulled toward ground. Typical reasons are a motor lead chafed against the body or axle, water standing in the caliper connector, or a shorted motor. The motor is reversed through an H-bridge, and protected bridge drivers such as TI's DRV8873-Q1 treat a grounded output as overcurrent and cut that half-bridge within microseconds.",["Motor lead chafed and shorted to the body or axle","Water and corrosion in the left caliper connector","Internally shorted actuator motor"],["Park brake warning lamp and service message","Left rear brake does not apply or release","Fuse for the park brake motor may blow"],2,2,["C060B","C060D","C0611","C0670"],"מפעיל בלם חניה שמאלית — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],C060D:["Left Park Brake Actuator Control Circuit High","Here one of the two left motor leads reads high: it is shorted to battery voltage, or touches another live wire, so the low side of the bridge cannot pull it down. A bridge driver such as the DRV8873-Q1 detects an output shorted to the battery and disables the stage to protect itself.",["Motor lead shorted to a battery-fed wire","Moisture bridging pins in the caliper connector","Failed driver stage in the brake control module"],["Park brake warning lamp on","Left rear brake does not respond to the switch","Electronic pad change mode cannot be entered"],2,2,["C060B","C060C","C0612","C0670"],"מפעיל בלם חניה שמאלית — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],C060E:["Left Park Brake Actuator Performance/Stuck Off","C060E is set when the left actuator is driven but does not build or keep the clamping force it should, so the brake effectively stays off. Bosch's EPB patents derive clamping force from motor current: during apply it rises as pads meet the disc and then levels off at the target force. A current that never climbs points to a slipping belt, a stripped gear or a spindle that turns without pushing the piston.",["Worn gearbox, belt or spindle inside the left actuator","Pads or piston not set up correctly after brake service without maintenance mode","High resistance in the left motor circuit limits motor torque"],["Vehicle may creep on a slope with the parking brake applied","Park brake warning lamp or message","Motor noise without the usual clamping sound at the left rear"],3,2,["C060F","C060B","C0613","C0680"],"מפעיל בלם חניה שמאלית — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],C060F:["Left Park Brake Actuator Stuck On","C060F is the reverse of C060E: the left actuator does not release, or the module cannot confirm that it has. An Advics patent recognises release by watching motor current while the motor runs backwards: once the current stops changing after a minimum time of around 200 ms, the clamping force is taken as zero and the motor runs on briefly to set pad clearance.",["Seized caliper piston or corroded spindle nut","Pads frozen or rusted to the disc after standing","Broken gear stage in the actuator"],["Left rear brake drags, smells hot or the car pulls away sluggishly","Park brake lamp stays on after release","Release message or refusal to drive off"],3,2,["C060E","C060B","C0614","C0680"],"מפעיל בלם חניה שמאלית — תקוע במצב פעיל"],C0610:["Right Park Brake Actuator Control Circuit/Open","C0610 reports that the drive circuit of the right rear parking brake motor is open, so the controller switches its bridge but no motor current flows. Mitsubishi's 2023 Outlander PHEV shows how such a check works under its own code C10B0-01: during apply or release the ABS unit looks for an open motor circuit on the right side and reacts within about one second, then suspends the electric parking brake and hill start…",["Right caliper motor connector unplugged, corroded or with pushed-back pins","Broken wire in the harness that flexes with the right rear suspension","Open winding or worn brushes in the right actuator motor","Blown fuse or fusible link feeding the parking brake output stage"],["Parking brake warning lamp and service message","Right rear caliper neither applies nor releases electrically","Hill start assist or auto hold unavailable"],2,2,["C0611","C0612","C0613","C0614","C060B","C0680"],"מפעיל בלם חניה ימנית — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],C0611:["Right Park Brake Actuator Control Circuit Low","C0611 means one of the two leads to the right parking brake motor is dragged toward ground. The harness to the right rear caliper rides on the suspension and passes close to the brake disc, so chafing against the knuckle or water in the plug are the usual suspects, followed by a shorted motor.",["Motor lead chafed through at the right rear knuckle or bracket","Water and corrosion bridging pins in the right caliper connector","Internal short in the right actuator motor"],["Parking brake warning lamp on","Right side does not apply; vehicle may roll on a slope if not in Park or in gear","Fuse for the parking brake circuit may blow"],2,2,["C0610","C0612","C0613","C060C"],"מפעיל בלם חניה ימנית — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],C0612:["Right Park Brake Actuator Control Circuit High","With C0612 a lead of the right parking brake motor stays at or near battery voltage while the bridge tries to pull it low. Likely causes are a short to a live wire in the rear harness, a wrong splice after body or axle repair, or a defect in the output stage. Driver ICs such as the DRV8873-Q1 treat a short to the supply as its own protected fault and disable the output.",["Motor lead shorted to a battery-fed wire in the rear harness","Failed low-side switch in the control unit holding the lead high","Wrong pin or splice after an earlier harness or body repair"],["Service parking brake message and warning lamp","Right parking brake does not respond to the switch","Code may return as soon as an apply is commanded"],2,2,["C0610","C0611","C0613","C060D"],"מפעיל בלם חניה ימנית — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],C0613:["Right Park Brake Actuator Performance/Stuck Off","C0613 covers a right actuator that is powered but fails to clamp. The wiring is intact, yet the module never sees the motor turn or the current rise that marks pads pressed against the disc. Mitsubishi gives a concrete case with C10B0-09 on the 2023 Outlander PHEV: during apply the right motor does not rotate, and after ten seconds or more the ABS unit flags it and disables both the parking brake and hill start…",["Stripped gear, slipping belt or broken spindle inside the right actuator","Motor seized by corrosion after water entry","High resistance in the right circuit starving the motor of current","Pads or disc worn far beyond limit, or caliper not calibrated after a brake job"],["Parking brake warning lamp and message","Parked vehicle may creep on a slope","No motor noise from the right rear when the brake is applied"],3,2,["C0614","C0610","C060E","C0680"],"מפעיל בלם חניה ימנית — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],C0614:["Right Park Brake Actuator Stuck On","C0614 is set when the right parking brake will not let go, or when the module cannot confirm that it has. To release, the motor runs in reverse; Advics treats the force as released when, after a minimum run of roughly 200 ms, the current has settled, and then lets the motor run on briefly to restore pad clearance. If that pattern never appears, or the motor stalls, the right side counts as stuck on.",["Seized caliper piston or corroded spindle nut on the right side","Pads rusted to the disc after the car stood for a long time","Jammed gearbox or damaged motor in the right actuator"],["Right rear brake drags; car pulls or feels held back when driving off","Hot right rear wheel and burning smell","Parking brake warning and release request not completed"],3,2,["C0613","C0610","C060F","C0680"],"מפעיל בלם חניה ימנית — תקוע במצב פעיל"],C0615:["Park Brake Control Module Control Circuit/Open","C0615 points at the circuit that feeds or enables the parking brake control electronics, not at a single caliper: it reads as open. Today the parking brake logic often runs as a software block inside the ESC unit (VDA recommendation 305-100), while the host supplies the motor power stage; a few cars keep a separate module.",["Blown fuse or fusible link in the parking brake power feed","Loose or corroded terminal on the power or enable line at the module","Broken wire between fuse box and module","Internal fault in the module's supply stage"],["Electric parking brake inoperative on both sides","Parking brake warning lamp and service message","Auto hold and hill start assist unavailable"],2,2,["C0616","C0617","C0618","C0680"],"מודול בקרת בלם חניה — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],C0616:["Park Brake Control Module Control Circuit Performance","C0616 is the one code in this range that GM really uses. Its 2025 EBCM tables file over twenty parking brake self-tests under it, all Type C without MIL: the left and right H-bridge supplies may not differ by more than 12 % at 8–20 V, the current measuring path must read 10.5–17 A in its self-test, the motor voltage must stay between 7 and 18 V for 700 ms, plus watchdog, ASIC and rollaway checks.",["Software anomaly in the brake module (GM 2024 HD trucks, fixed by reprogramming)","Weak battery, poor ground or charging fault pushing motor voltage outside its window","Internal hardware fault in the parking brake ASIC, bridge or measuring path","Parking brake assembly check not completed after module replacement"],["Service Parking Brake message in the driver information center","Parking brake warning lamp; parking brake may be inhibited","Check engine lamp on some GM models"],2,3,["C0615","C0617","C0618","C0680","C0609"],"מודול בקרת בלם חניה — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],C0617:["Park Brake Control Module Control Circuit Low","C0617 says the supply or control line feeding the parking brake electronics reads too low. Because both caliper motors draw several amps when they clamp, a weak battery, a poor ground or a corroded feed shows up here first. Mitsubishi's ABS unit on the 2023 Outlander PHEV sets C10B7-16 when the ignition feed drops to 10 V or less for about a second and then suspends the parking brake and hill start assist.",["Discharged or failing 12 V battery","High resistance in the module ground or power feed","Control or enable line shorted to ground"],["Parking brake warning lamp, often together with other low-voltage messages","Parking brake applies slowly or not at all","Hill start assist unavailable"],1,2,["C0615","C0616","C0618","C0680"],"מודול בקרת בלם חניה — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],C0618:["Park Brake Control Module Control Circuit High","C0618 is the overvoltage counterpart of C0617: the feed or control line of the parking brake electronics reads above its window. A regulator fault in the alternator or DC/DC converter, jump starting with a booster set to 24 V, or a short between the enable line and a live wire are the usual reasons.",["Faulty voltage regulator in the alternator or DC/DC converter","Overvoltage from a jump starter or charger on a 24 V setting","Enable or control line shorted to a battery-fed wire"],["Parking brake warning lamp, possibly with a battery or charging warning","Parking brake does not respond to the switch","Other modules may log overvoltage codes at the same time"],2,2,["C0615","C0616","C0617","C0565"],"מודול בקרת בלם חניה — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],C0619:["Brake Pedal Position Sensor A Offset Exceeded Learning Limit","Pedal position sensors are taught their rest value, and C0619 says the offset found for channel A lies outside the band the controller will accept. A Hitachi patent on electric boosters learns the stroke sensor zero only with the pedal released and no brake request, and treats a zero beyond a prescribed range as a sensor fault.",["Intermittent connection in the sensor circuit that skewed the learned value","Pedal not returning fully (floor mat, stiff pivot, wrong adjustment)","Sensor drifted or fitted out of position after replacement","Learn procedure skipped or disturbed after sensor or module service"],["Brake or brake system warning lamp; check engine lamp on some vehicles","Brake lights, cruise control or shifting behave as if the pedal were pressed","Reduced brake assist or regenerative braking on electrified models"],2,3,["C061A","C05C0","C0042","C0277"],""],C061A:["Brake Pedal Position Sensor B Offset Exceeded Learning Limit","C061A is the same learn-limit check for the second channel, B. Many pedal sensors hold two independent elements; on GM trucks since 2012 one potentiometer feeds the ECM and the other the BCM, each with its own 5 V reference, ground and signal.",["Dropout or fretting corrosion on the channel B reference, ground or signal pin","Learn done in only one module, or the pedal moved during the learn","Pedal rest position changed by a mat, bracket damage or adjustment","Drifting second element inside the pedal sensor"],["Brake system warning or message","Mismatch between modules about pedal state, e.g. brake lights versus cruise control","Shift interlock or start function may act up"],2,0,["C0619","C05C1","C0277"],""],C061B:["ECM Request - Forced Traction Control Disable","C061B is not a brake fault at all. It records that the engine control module told the brake module to switch traction control off, usually because the engine can no longer cut torque on demand. A Hyundai patent spells out the logic: the TCS asks for a torque cut over CAN, the engine reports the torque it delivers, and if the gap stays outside ±10 % too often, TCS is turned off and a warning lamp lit.",["Engine misfire or other engine fault that blocks torque reduction","Electronic throttle or torque model fault stored in the ECM","Corrupt or missing torque messages between engine and brake module","ECM software issue setting the disable request without a real fault"],["Traction control off lamp or Service Traction Control message","Stability control may also be unavailable","Engine codes stored, sometimes with the check engine lamp"],2,2,["P0856","P0857","P0300"],""],C061C:["Variable Effort Steering Actuator Control Circuit/Open","Variable effort steering changes how hard a hydraulic system steers with road speed. In GM's Magnasteer a coil and permanent magnets on the rotary valve add or subtract from the torsion bar's stiffness; the GM and Steering Solutions patent EP2028081B1 describes this actuator, and ±3 A coil current is cited in a later patent. Ford's older variable-assist systems used a stepper-driven or solenoid orifice instead.",["Connector at the steering gear loose, corroded or soaked with fluid","Open actuator coil inside the steering gear","Broken wire between control module and steering gear"],["Steering effort no longer changes with speed","Heavier steering when parking or lighter, nervous steering on the highway","Steering or stability warning on some vehicles"],3,2,["C061D","C061E","C061F","C0620","C0624"],"מפעיל היגוי מאמץ משתנה — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],C061D:["Variable Effort Steering Actuator Control Circuit Low","C061D flags an actuator line held too low, most often a coil lead shorted to the steering gear housing or to the vehicle body. The Magnasteer coil sits in the cast valve housing, which forms part of its magnetic circuit, so insulation damage there grounds the winding; checking each coil terminal against the housing is a standard test.",["Actuator coil insulation broken down to the steering gear housing","Actuator wire chafed against subframe or exhaust heat shield","Failed output stage in the controlling module"],["Speed-dependent steering feel lost","Steering feels the same at all speeds","Fuse for the steering actuator may blow"],3,2,["C061C","C061E","C061F","C0626"],"מפעיל היגוי מאמץ משתנה — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],C061E:["Variable Effort Steering Actuator Control Circuit High","C061E means an actuator line reads above what the controller expects, typically a lead shorted to battery voltage or a driver stage stuck on. Delphi describes Magnasteer as electronically modulating the magnetic torsional rate, with coil polarity deciding whether effort rises or falls; a line stuck high can therefore hold the actuator in one direction or stop the bridge from regulating.",["Actuator lead shorted to a battery-fed wire","Output transistor in the module stuck on","Wrong pinning after a steering gear swap"],["Unusually heavy or unusually light steering that does not change with speed","Steering warning message on some vehicles"],3,2,["C061C","C061D","C061F","C0627"],"מפעיל היגוי מאמץ משתנה — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],C061F:["Variable Effort Steering Actuator Control Circuit Performance","C061F covers an actuator circuit that is electrically intact but does not behave as commanded: the current does not follow the request, or the expected change in effort fails to show up. In Magnasteer the coil runs from about −3 A to +3 A, and the current reverses around mid speed, so tracking errors appear as wrong feel in town or on the highway.",["Magnetic null shifted from valve centre, damaged magnet ring","Sticking rotary valve from contaminated fluid","High resistance in connector or wiring limiting coil current","Wrong or missing vehicle speed input to the controlling module"],["Steering effort wrong for the speed or changing unexpectedly","Pull to one side with no alignment fault","Steering warning on some vehicles"],3,0,["C061C","C061D","C061E","C0625"],"מפעיל היגוי מאמץ משתנה — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],C0620:["Variable Effort Steering Lock/Safety Actuator Control Circuit/Open","Some steering systems that vary effort or ratio carry a second actuator whose only job is safety: a solenoid lock that blocks the motor or gear so the wheel turns the wheels directly. Delphi's patent combining Magnasteer with an active steering actuator uses a solenoid that is energised to unlock and drops into lock without power; JTEKT and Continental lock their superimposed steering the same fail-safe way.",["Connector to the lock solenoid unplugged or corroded","Open lock solenoid coil, for example after overheating","Broken wire between the steering module and the lock"],["Variable steering function disabled; steering works with a fixed characteristic","Steering system warning","Possible click or no click from the steering when switching on"],3,2,["C0621","C0622","C0623","C061C"],""],C0621:["Variable Effort Steering Lock/Safety Actuator Control Circuit Low","C0621 reports the lock or safety actuator line held too low. In JTEKT's variable-ratio design a PNP transistor switches the lock coil, and the ECU holds the line low on purpose when it wants to lock, for instance after a motor or sensor fault or a broken cable. An unintended short to ground therefore looks like a permanent lock request: the solenoid cannot lift the arm, and the steering stays mechanically coupled.",["Lock solenoid wire shorted to ground in the column or gear harness","Shorted turns in the lock solenoid","Failed drive transistor in the steering module"],["Variable ratio or effort function off","Steering warning lamp or message"],3,2,["C0620","C0622","C0623","C061D"],""],C0622:["Variable Effort Steering Lock/Safety Actuator Control Circuit High","C0622 is the critical direction for a fail-safe lock: the actuator line reads high even when the controller wants it off. Since the lock in these designs releases when powered, a line shorted to battery voltage would keep it open when it should engage, so the safety path no longer works.",["Lock solenoid wire shorted to a battery-fed circuit","Drive transistor in the module stuck on","Charging system overvoltage"],["Steering system warning; variable function switched off","No noticeable change in normal steering"],3,2,["C0620","C0621","C0623","C061E"],""],C0623:["Variable Effort Steering Lock/Safety Actuator Control Circuit Performance","C0623 covers a lock or safety actuator whose circuit is sound but whose action does not match the command: it does not release when energised, does not engage in time, or its current is implausible. JTEKT's lock coil first gets full duty for about one second to pull the arm free, then 60 % below 13 V or 40 % above 14 V to hold it, which keeps the coil at or below 100 °C instead of near 200 °C.",["Sticking lock arm or pin, worn lock teeth","Solenoid weakened by heat, pull-in force too low","Low supply voltage during release","Weak or broken return spring, lock engages late"],["Steering warning and variable function off","Clicking or knocking from the steering column at start or stop","Steering wheel slightly off-centre after the system locks"],3,2,["C0620","C0621","C0622","C061F"],""],C0624:["Variable Effort Steering Sensor Circuit","Variable effort steering tunes hydraulic assist to the situation, and besides road speed some systems also read a steering wheel sensor. Ford's variable-assist steering, first used on the 1988 Lincoln Continental, fed its module from an optical sensor tracking how the wheel turns;",["Loose or corroded connector at the steering column sensor","Wire broken where the harness flexes in the steering column","Failed sensor, for example a dead optical detector"],["Steering effort no longer reacts to quick wheel movements","Effort stays at one level or follows only road speed","Steering warning on some vehicles"],2,0,["C0625","C0626","C0627","C0628","C061C"],"חיישן היגוי מאמץ משתנה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0625:["Variable Effort Steering Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","Here the sensor signal is electrically present but its content does not add up. With an incremental steering wheel sensor the module derives rate or angle from pulse counts; a Ford patent computes steering rate from the counts in a fixed sampling window, so lost pulses give a wrong rate.",["Dirt or damage on the encoder disc causing lost pulses","Intermittent contact at the connector producing short dropouts","Sensor loose or misaligned after column or steering work","Implausible road speed input used for the cross-check"],["Steering effort changes unexpectedly while turning","Variable assist switched off with a fixed steering feel","Steering or stability warning on some vehicles"],2,0,["C0624","C0626","C0627","C0608"],"חיישן היגוי מאמץ משתנה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],C0626:["Variable Effort Steering Sensor Circuit Low","C0626 means the signal of the variable effort steering sensor reads below the lowest level the module accepts. A Kelsey-Hayes patent shows the typical window for such a steering wheel sensor: with a 5 V supply each channel switches between roughly 0.6 V and 4.4 V, and anything under the lower band counts as low.",["Signal wire chafed through and shorted to ground","5 V sensor feed missing or pulled down by another fault","Sensor output stage failed and stuck low"],["Variable assist disabled, steering effort fixed","Steering warning lamp or message"],2,0,["C0624","C0625","C0627"],"חיישן היגוי מאמץ משתנה — אות נמוך במעגל"],C0627:["Variable Effort Steering Sensor Circuit High","The high counterpart: the sensor signal sits above the top of the band the module treats as valid. In the Kelsey-Hayes design a healthy channel peaks near 4.4 V on a 5 V supply, so a reading close to the supply rail or beyond it points to a short to the reference or to battery voltage, or to a broken sensor ground that lets the input float high.",["Signal wire shorted to the 5 V reference or to battery voltage","Open sensor ground letting the signal float high","Sensor output stage failed and stuck high"],["Variable assist disabled, steering effort fixed","Steering warning lamp or message"],2,0,["C0624","C0625","C0626"],"חיישן היגוי מאמץ משתנה — אות גבוה במעגל"],C0628:["Variable Effort Steering Module Performance","C0628 says the unit that runs variable effort steering fails its own function checks. On GM's Magnasteer that unit was a separate module in 1996–97 and became part of the brake control module from 1998. A GM patent describes the logic: a microcomputer reads coil current from speed and lateral acceleration tables, limits the total and its rate of change and drives the coil by PWM;",["Internal fault in the controlling module or its coil driver stage","Low or unstable supply voltage so the commanded current cannot be reached","Corrupt calibration or software after a module replacement or flash"],["Steering effort no longer changes with speed","Heavy steering when parking or light steering at highway speed","Steering, ABS or stability warning where the brake module hosts the function"],3,2,["C0629","C062A","C062B","C061C","C061F"],"מודול היגוי מאמץ משתנה — ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0629:["Variable Effort Steering Control Module Incorrect Component Installed","C0629 flags a mismatch between what the variable effort steering module expects and what is fitted. Variable-effort gears exist in versions that cannot be swapped blindly: replacement racks come with or without the EVO solenoid, and GM's second Magnasteer generation dropped the permanent magnet and only raises effort with speed, whereas the first one reverses coil current around 45 mph.",["Replacement steering gear of the wrong variant, for example without actuator","Module from another vehicle or not configured for this equipment","Actuator connected with reversed polarity after a repair"],["Variable assist inactive after a steering or module repair","Steering effort behaves the wrong way round, heavy when slow","Steering warning on some vehicles"],3,2,["C0628","C061C","C0624"],""],C062A:["Variable Effort Steering Module Temperature Too High","The variable effort steering module, or its coil driver, reports a temperature above its permitted limit. Heat matters twice here: a GM patent on magnetic variable effort steering notes that fluid viscosity, magnet properties and coil current all drift with temperature and either fits a sensor in the fluid sump or infers temperature from the current error.",["Very high underhood or fluid temperature, for example after long parking manoeuvres in heat","Partly shorted coil drawing excess current and heating the driver","Faulty internal temperature measurement reporting heat that is not there"],["Variable effort reduced or switched off temporarily","Steering feel changes after hard use and returns after cooling"],2,2,["C062B","C0628","C061F"],"טמפרטורת מודול היגוי מאמץ משתנה — ערך גבוה מדי"],C062B:["Variable Effort Steering Module Temperature Too Low","C062B is set when the module or its coil driver reads a temperature below the range it is designed for. Automotive driver chips such as TI's DRV8873-Q1 are specified down to an ambient of −40 °C, so a lower reading means either an extreme cold soak or a measurement that has failed.",["Vehicle parked for a long time in severe frost","Open or failed temperature measurement inside the module or at the fluid sensor","Moisture or corrosion at the connector distorting the reading"],["Variable effort inactive after a cold start","Heavy or uneven steering until the system warms up"],2,2,["C062A","C0628","C061F"],"טמפרטורת מודול היגוי מאמץ משתנה — ערך נמוך מדי"],C062C:["Brake Booster Motor B Performance","C062C judges whether the second drive, B, of an electric brake booster moves as commanded; the circuit may be intact. Boosters like Bosch's iBooster turn motor torque through a three-stage gear into force on the master cylinder, and in redundant layouts such as a Hyundai Mobis design a dual-winding motor is fed by two power modules, each able to carry the whole current command alone if the other is declared failed.",["Worn or damaged motor B, for example bearing or winding damage","Fault in the power module or driver stage feeding side B","Binding in gear stage or booster mechanism","Booster control software needing an update"],["Brake system or brake assist warning","Harder pedal or reduced assist in some situations","Driver assistance functions with automatic braking restricted"],4,2,["C0594","C0592","C0593","C058E"],"מנוע מגבר בלם‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],C062D:["ABS Valves Range/Performance","C062D means the ABS valve group does not work as expected, although no single valve or plain supply fault explains it. Mitsubishi is the one maker that maps it publicly: in the 2023 Outlander PHEV brake unit, valve relay code C1048-92 shows as C062D, set within 2 s with normal supply and the system switched on, with ASC, ABS, brake lamp and MIL after one trip; bulletin 23-35-002 adds C1048-01 to the same number.",["Internal fault in the ABS control unit or its valve relay","Weak supply through fuse, fusible link, wiring or 12 V battery","Corroded or loose connector at the hydraulic unit"],["ABS, stability control and brake warning lamps on","Check engine lamp on (Mitsubishi)","ABS, traction control and electric parking brake unavailable"],3,3,["C053B","C0010","C0011"],""],C062E:["Active Air Dam Supply Voltage Circuit Low","The active air dam actuators run from the vehicle battery while the PCM or body module commands them over LIN or CAN, as Ford's patent lays out. C062E reports that the supply reaching the actuator or its module is too low to move the panel safely. Small LIN motor drivers made for flaps and grille shutters watch this themselves: Melexis' MLX81350 has an undervoltage threshold selectable between about 4 and 9 V.",["Loose or corroded ground point in the front harness","Water or washer fluid wicking into an inline connector","Weak battery or low charging voltage","High resistance in fuse or feed wire to the actuator"],["Air dam no longer moves and stays in its last position","Air dam fault message in the cluster","Low-voltage codes in other modules at the same time"],2,0,["C062F","C0601","C0604","U0645"],"סכר אוויר פעיל — מתח נמוך במעגל מתח האספקה"],C062F:["Active Air Dam Supply Voltage Circuit High","C062F is the overvoltage side: the supply at the air dam actuator or its module lies above the permitted window. Ford's patent powers the screw-jack actuators from the vehicle battery, so a regulator fault in the charging system, jump-starting with a higher voltage or a load dump spike can push the feed too high.",["Charging system overvoltage from a faulty regulator","Jump start or battery charger with excessive voltage","Faulty voltage measurement inside the actuator electronics"],["Air dam stops moving, often together with other overvoltage codes","Air dam fault message in the cluster","Flickering lights or charging warning if the regulator is at fault"],2,0,["C062E","C0601","C0603","U0645"],"סכר אוויר פעיל — מתח גבוה במעגל מתח האספקה"],C0630:["Active Air Dam Stuck","C0630 says the air dam panel itself does not move although the actuator is driven and reports sensible values. GM's patent defines exactly this case: if measured position and motor current agree with each other but both differ from the commanded position, or back-EMF shows unusual load, the panel is at fault rather than sensor or drive.",["Panel bent or jammed after ground contact, debris or a kerb","Broken bolts between actuator and panel","Ice, snow or packed mud blocking the guides","Worn or seized screw jack in the actuator"],["Air dam hangs down or does not deploy","Air dam fault message in the cluster","Scraping on ramps or slightly higher fuel use on the highway"],2,0,["C0604","C0601","C062E","C062F","U0645"],"סכר אוויר פעיל — תקוע"],C0631:["Front Axle Disconnect Actuator","A front axle disconnect separates the front shaft from the driveline when only the rear or primary wheels need to drive, cutting drag; a BorgWarner patent shows a shift fork sliding a splined sleeve, with a cone synchroniser matching speeds first.",["Failed disconnect actuator or intermediate shaft (Ford Explorer/Aviator 2020–2021)","Loose, corroded or damaged actuator connector","Shift sleeve or synchroniser binding, often from wear or fluid problems","Outdated AWD module software"],["Wrench or 4WD/AWD warning lamp on","All-wheel drive not available or front axle does not engage","Possible noise from the front axle area"],3,2,["C0632","C0633","C00A6"],"מפעיל ניתוק סרן קדמי"],C0632:["Front Axle Disconnect Control Circuit","C0632 concerns the electrical path that drives the front axle disconnect, not the shift itself. The actuator may be electromagnetic or electromechanical; BorgWarner's patent even reads its position from the coil's inductance, which changes between engaged and released. Ford's Explorer and Aviator actuator has a four-wire connector. No maker publishes C0632;",["Chafed or cut wires close to the actuator connector","Water or corrosion in the actuator or inline connector","Spread or pushed-out terminals in the connector","Open or shorted actuator winding"],["4WD/AWD service message or warning lamp","Front axle does not engage or disengage"],2,2,["C0631","C0633","C00A6"],"ניתוק סרן קדמי — תקלה במעגל הבקרה"],C0633:["Front Half Shaft Speed Sensor","On all-wheel-drive systems that can uncouple the front axle, a speed sensor on a front shaft tells the controller how fast the uncoupled part turns, so it can match speeds before re-engaging. A BorgWarner patent uses a Hall sensor on the shift sleeve to read both speed and position and engages once the gap to wheel speed is within about ±100–200 rpm;",["Sensor contaminated with axle oil (Ford Explorer/Aviator 2020)","Failed sensor or damaged wiring and connector","Wrong air gap or damaged sensor target on the shaft"],["AWD or 4WD warning messages in the cluster","All-wheel drive limited or not engaging","Possible oil seepage near the sensor"],2,2,["C0631","C0632","C00A6","C05F3"],""],C0634:["Brake Pressure Sensor A/B Correlation","Two brake pressure sensors that see the same hydraulic pressure should report nearly the same value; C0634 means sensors A and B disagree beyond the allowed margin, even if each signal is valid on its own. Which sensor bears which letter depends on the maker.",["One sensor drifting in offset or gain","Fault in the brake control unit with integrated sensors, often replaced as a unit","Air or a blocked passage making the sensors see different pressures","Brake module software or calibration needing an update"],["ABS, stability or brake system warning lamp on","Brake assist or driver assistance functions with automatic braking off"],4,2,["C053D","C0541","C0574","C056B"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ A/B — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],C0635:["Brake Pressure Sensor G Circuit/Open","C0635 flags a broken circuit at brake pressure sensor G: a supply, signal or ground wire without continuity, or a plug that has lost contact. No manufacturer publishes C0635 in this meaning, so it is unknown which part carries the letter G. A seventh sensor only exists in large units, for example the Lucas/ZF electro-hydraulic layout with four wheel sensors, one supply sensor and two front push-through sensors.",["Plug at the sensor or hydraulic unit loose, corroded or with pushed-back terminals","Broken supply, signal or ground wire in the sensor harness","Internal interruption inside sensor G"],["ABS and ESC warning lamps on","Stability control and pressure-based brake functions switched off"],2,2,["C0636","C0637","C0638","C0639","C05C8","C05C9"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ G — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C0636:["Brake Pressure Sensor G Circuit High","The voltage of sensor G sits above anything a valid pressure can produce. A Toyota patent shows how a brake gets seven pressure sensors: one for the accumulator, two for the master cylinder chambers and four for the wheel cylinders, all read by the brake ECU. If one of them stops delivering sensible values, that ECU de-energises every valve and motor, and the front wheels are then braked with boosted pedal pressure.",["Signal wire shorted to the 5 V reference or battery voltage","Open or high-resistance sensor ground lifting the output","Sensor G failed internally and driving its output to the top"],["ABS/ESC warning lamp on","Live data shows high pressure with the pedal released","Brake assist and stability functions unavailable"],2,2,["C0635","C0637","C0638","C063A","C05C7"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ G — אות גבוה במעגל"],C0637:["Brake Pressure Sensor G Circuit Low","C0637 reports that sensor G delivers less voltage than its lowest valid reading. Brake pressure sensors keep a live zero at rest, so a signal near 0 V means a fault rather than zero pressure: Saab's 9-5 ESP flags a pressure signal under 0.25 V lasting 0.1 s, and GM's 2016 hybrid brake module treats under 0.3 V for 0.1 s on its left rear wheel pressure sensor (sensor D there) as a short to ground, Type A.",["Signal wire chafed and shorted to ground","5 V sensor reference shorted to ground or interrupted","Sensor G defective, often only replaceable with the hydraulic unit"],["ABS and ESC warning lamps on","Live data shows no pressure even when the pedal is pressed"],3,2,["C0635","C0636","C0638","C063B","C05C6","C0575"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ G — אות נמוך במעגל"],C0638:["Brake Pressure Sensor G Range/Performance","Here sensor G produces a voltage inside its window, but the pressure it reports disagrees with what the system expects. Lucas/ZF describe the classic test for multi-sensor EHB units: after the driver brakes to a stop, the isolation valve stays closed and all wheel valves open, so three or more sensors share one pressure; the odd one out is the faulty sensor, with size and direction of its error.",["Zero point or gain of sensor G drifted","Pressure trapped in the circuit during the comparison or zero learn","Valve sticking so the sensor does not see the shared test pressure"],["ABS lamp and ESC telltale on","Stability control reduced or off, regenerative braking possibly limited"],3,2,["C0635","C0636","C0637","C063C","C05C5","C0634"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ G — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0639:["Brake Pressure Sensor H Circuit/Open","Brake pressure sensor H has lost its electrical connection: an interrupted 5 V feed, signal or ground line, or a loose plug at the hydraulic unit. No published service data ties C0639 to a real part.",["Sensor plug loose or terminals corroded","Supply, signal or ground conductor broken","Open measuring bridge or failed electronics inside the sensor"],["ABS and ESC lamps on, possibly flickering with vibration","ABS or stability control disabled"],2,2,["C063A","C063B","C063C","C0635","C063D"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ H — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C063A:["Brake Pressure Sensor H Circuit High","The output of pressure sensor H is too high to be real. C063A is not documented by any carmaker. Another Toyota patent shows seven pressure points in one brake: accumulator, two master cylinder passages and four control pressures standing for the wheel cylinders. Which of them a system might label H is not public. An excessive signal usually means the line touches a voltage source or the sensor ground is lost;",["Signal line touching a 5 V or battery feed","Sensor ground open or high resistance","Sensor reports an internal fault or overpressure at its upper rail"],["ABS/ESC warning lamp on, ESC unavailable","Implausibly high brake pressure in live data at rest"],2,2,["C0639","C063B","C063C","C0636","C063E"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ H — אות גבוה במעגל"],C063B:["Brake Pressure Sensor H Circuit Low","C063B says sensor H reads below its valid floor. Unlike C063C the problem is electrical, not a believable but wrong pressure. A Bosch workshop article on a Teves MK60 unit describes the integrated sensor: fed with 5 V, it stays below 1 V with the brakes off and climbs as pedal pressure builds, so the fault limit has to sit well under that rest level.",["Signal conductor shorted to ground","5 V reference collapsed by a short in another sensor on the same feed","Sensor H without output due to an internal defect"],["ABS and ESC lamps on","Brake assist and stability control not available"],3,2,["C0639","C063A","C063C","C0637","C063F"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ H — אות נמוך במעגל"],C063C:["Brake Pressure Sensor H Range/Performance","Sensor H gives an electrically valid yet implausible pressure. In Toyota's eight-sensor patent the check connects a pressure source to a brake cylinder: both readings should then nearly match, and a gap beyond a threshold means one of the two sensors, the passage or the cylinder is at fault; the switch-over is preferably made at standstill.",["Offset or gain of sensor H drifted out of tolerance","Restricted passage or faulty brake cylinder so pressures really differ","Air in the brake fluid distorting the pressure build-up"],["ESC malfunction telltale and ABS lamp on","Changed pedal feel or reduced brake assistance"],3,2,["C0639","C063A","C063B","C0638","C0640"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ H — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C063D:["Brake Pressure Sensor J Circuit/Open","A wire or contact of brake pressure sensor J is interrupted. No manufacturer ties C063D to a specific sensor. Continental's one-box brake patent names sensors for the master cylinder and for the pressure supply unit and mentions optional further ones for brake circuits or wheel brake circuits, so a J sensor could be among those.",["Spread or corroded terminal in the sensor connector","Conductor interrupted between sensor and control unit","Open circuit inside sensor J"],["Brake system or ESC warning lamp on","Pressure-controlled brake functions switched off"],2,2,["C063E","C063F","C0640","C0639","C0641"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ J — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C063E:["Brake Pressure Sensor J Circuit High","C063E: sensor J sends more voltage than its range allows. GM's 2016 hybrid brake controller shows the method on a wheel pressure sensor: if the signal line exceeds 3.3 V and so no longer differs from the supply, a short to supply is stored after 0.1 s with the ignition on, rated Type A.",["Signal line shorted to the sensor supply","Sensor ground interrupted, output lifted through the input divider","Sensor J electronics failed with output stuck high"],["Brake or ESC warning lamp on","Live data shows brake pressure although no one is braking"],2,2,["C063D","C063F","C0640","C063A","C0576"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ J — אות גבוה במעגל"],C063F:["Brake Pressure Sensor J Circuit Low","The signal of brake pressure sensor J is stuck below its lower limit. Ipgate's double-stroke-piston patent fits one pressure sensor to each brake circuit and checks the delivered fluid volume against the pressure-volume curve of that circuit; such a circuit sensor is one possible J position, though no manufacturer confirms the letter.",["Chafed signal wire touching ground","5 V reference shorted to ground","Broken feed or signal wire pulled to 0 V by the module input","Failed sensing element in sensor J"],["ABS, traction and stability warning lamps on","ABS and ESC inoperative until the next ignition cycle"],2,2,["C063D","C063E","C0640","C063B","C0643"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ J — אות נמוך במעגל"],C0640:["Brake Pressure Sensor J Range/Performance","C0640 marks sensor J as valid in voltage but wrong in content. In plunger-based brakes the pressure can be cross-checked against what the actuator did: Ipgate compares delivered piston volume with the pressure-volume curve and closes the inlet valves one by one to find a leaking circuit, while Continental's one-box layout carries separate sensors for master cylinder and pressure supply that can be set against each…",["Sensor J drifting so its zero correction exceeds the limit","Leak or air in the brake circuit so pressure and delivered volume disagree","Inlet or isolation valve seized"],["Brake warning and ESC lamps on","Longer pedal travel or reduced brake boost in fallback mode"],3,2,["C063D","C063E","C063F","C063C","C0644","C0578"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ J — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0641:["Brake Pressure Sensor K Circuit/Open","Brake pressure sensor K has an open circuit. Because the letter I is skipped in this series, K stands for a tenth pressure sensor, which is rare in cars; no carmaker publishes C0641 and the assignment is unknown.",["Poor contact between sensor and module or harness connector","Open conductor where an external harness is used","Internal open in sensor K"],["ESC or ABS warning lamp on","Stability control off, basic ABS may remain available"],2,2,["C0642","C0643","C0644","C063D","C0635"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ K — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C0642:["Brake Pressure Sensor K Circuit High","C0642 means the output of sensor K exceeds its upper limit. Electro-hydraulic brakes like Mercedes' Sensotronic Brake Control work with a high-pressure accumulator and a pedal value sensor with two Hall elements; during a pre-drive check the unit pressurises the calipers to test, among other things, its pressure sensors. A high fault on any such sensor would make the module believe the brakes are applied.",["Signal shorted to 5 V or battery voltage","Lost sensor ground","Internal fault of sensor K signalled at the upper rail"],["Brake system and ESC warning lamps on","Brake lights or hold functions may be requested wrongly on some systems"],2,2,["C0641","C0643","C0644","C063E","C0572"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ K — אות גבוה במעגל"],C0643:["Brake Pressure Sensor K Circuit Low","Sensor K reports less voltage than any valid pressure would give. Bendix's truck ESP treats brake demand and load sensors individually and, if one of them fails, disables only ESP while ABS and traction control carry on; this graded reaction shows why the code may leave basic ABS working. GM's 2016 hybrid module compares the wheel pressure signal with ground and sets its low code under 0.3 V within 0.1 s.",["Signal line shorted to ground","Broken sensor supply read as 0 V through the input pull-down","Sensor K without output"],["ESC lamp on, ESC switched off","ABS and traction control may keep working"],2,2,["C0641","C0642","C0644","C063F","C0575"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ K — אות נמוך במעגל"],C0644:["Brake Pressure Sensor K Range/Performance","The voltage from sensor K is in range, yet the pressure is not believable. Bendix's EC-80 stores a plausibility error when the primary and secondary brake demand sensors disagree and asks for a static calibration after an ECU swap. Mercedes' SBC repeats self-tests about every 16 brake applications, pressurising the calipers to check sensors, valves and leaks;",["Sensor K offset or gain drifted","Sensor values not re-learned after module replacement","Leak, air or a valve that does not seal distorting the pressure"],["ABS and ESC lamps on until a later successful check","Stability control reduced, pedal may feel different in fallback mode"],3,2,["C0641","C0642","C0643","C0640","C0634"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ K — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0645:["Brake Pressure Sensor L Circuit/Open","C0645 reports lost continuity in the circuit of brake pressure sensor L, the eleventh letter of the series because I is not used. That is far beyond a normal car: a Bosch patent names one, three or five sensors as the usual ESP layouts and calls five the current maximum. No carmaker publishes which sensor would carry the L.",["Spring contact between sensor and module board bent, dirty or corroded","Plug or harness of an externally mounted sensor without continuity","Internal interruption in sensor L"],["ESC and ABS warning lamps on","Pressure-based functions such as brake assist or hill hold unavailable"],3,2,["C0646","C0647","C0648","C0649","C064D","C0641"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ L — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C0646:["Brake Pressure Sensor L Circuit High","C0646 means the signal of brake pressure sensor L lies above the band a real pressure can produce. A Kelsey-Hayes patent spells out the logic for a bridge-type brake sensor: a healthy output stays between zero and the supply voltage, so a reading equal to supply points to an open circuit, not to maximum pressure. A high code can therefore hide a lost ground or a broken signal line as well as a short to 5 V.",["Sensor ground open, so the signal floats up to supply level","Signal line shorted to the 5 V reference or battery voltage","Sensor electronics driving the output to its upper limit"],["ABS/ESC warning lamp on","Stability control or electronic brake pressure control switched off"],2,2,["C0645","C0647","C0648","C064A","C064E","C0642"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ L — אות גבוה במעגל"],C0647:["Brake Pressure Sensor L Circuit Low","Sensor L reads below its lowest valid value. In the Kelsey-Hayes scheme a near-zero bridge output is read as a probable short, because the sensor never reaches 0 V with a working circuit. Where the fault lies depends on the architecture: in a Continental Teves design the sensor in the hydraulic unit is only a bare Wheatstone bridge, and amplifier, offset correction and digitising sit in an IC on the control module,…",["Signal path shorted to ground","Sensor supply missing or pulled down","Amplifier or input stage in the brake control module defective"],["ABS/ESC warning lamp on","Brake assist and stability control unavailable"],3,2,["C0645","C0646","C0648","C064B","C064F","C0643"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ L — אות נמוך במעגל"],C0648:["Brake Pressure Sensor L Range/Performance","Sensor L delivers an electrically valid signal whose pressure does not fit the situation. Commercial vehicle EBS shows how such a check works with many sensors: WABCO's tractor EBS has pressure sensors in the front axle relay valve, in each channel of the rear axle modulator and in the trailer control valve.",["Sensor offset or gain drifted","Sticking valve, leak or trapped pressure in the measured circuit","Calibration data not matching the fitted sensor after a repair"],["ABS/ESC warning lamp on, sometimes only after several brake applications","Uneven or reduced electronic brake force distribution"],3,2,["C0645","C0646","C0647","C064C","C0650","C0644"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ L — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0649:["Brake Pressure Sensor M Circuit/Open","The circuit of brake pressure sensor M, the twelfth in the series, has no continuity. Where so many pressure inputs exist, they are often not reachable from outside: WABCO notes that the two rear axle pressure sensors of its truck EBS are wired inside the axle modulator, so the cabling cannot be tested from outside and a fault means work on the modulator. Passenger-car units behave similarly;",["Loose or corroded plug at an external sensor or at the modulator","Open in the internal wiring of the modulator or hydraulic unit","Broken wire in the sensor harness"],["Brake or ABS warning lamp on","Electronic pressure control replaced by a fallback mode"],3,2,["C064A","C064B","C064C","C0645","C064D","C0641"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ M — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C064A:["Brake Pressure Sensor M Circuit High","C064A: the voltage from sensor M exceeds what any valid pressure would give. On WABCO's Trailer EBS D the brake pressure sensor of an extra EBS relay valve, for example on a drawbar trailer's front axle, draws its supply from the trailer modulator and returns its actual value as an analog signal; all active sensors share supply outputs that are protected against short circuits.",["Signal pin shorted to the sensor supply or battery voltage","Open sensor ground or signal line letting the input float high","Sensor output stuck at its upper limit"],["Brake or ABS warning lamp on","Load-dependent or electronic pressure control disabled"],2,2,["C0649","C064B","C064C","C0646","C064E","C0642"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ M — אות גבוה במעגל"],C064B:["Brake Pressure Sensor M Circuit Low","Sensor M sits below its lower signal limit. Because modules often supply several pressure sensors together, a single low code can be the visible part of a wider fault: WABCO's trailer modulator powers all active sensors jointly, so a short on one sensor supply can pull others down too, and codes for neighbouring letters may then appear at the same time.",["Shared sensor supply shorted, pulling several sensors low","Signal line or contact of sensor M shorted to ground","Sensor element failed"],["Warning lamp on, possibly with further pressure sensor codes","Electronic brake functions reduced to a fallback mode"],2,2,["C0649","C064A","C064C","C0647","C064F","C05C9"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ M — אות נמוך במעגל"],C064C:["Brake Pressure Sensor M Range/Performance","Sensor M stays inside its electrical window, but the pressure it reports is not believable. Trailer EBS shows an active test: when the control pressure exceeds 0.3 bar, WABCO's modulator switches its redundancy valve to reservoir pressure and starts EBS braking;",["Sensor reading drifted from the true pressure","Valve in the measured circuit not switching as commanded","Contamination or air at the sensor port"],["Warning lamp on after a brake application","Braking switched to a backup mode with less precise pressure control"],3,2,["C0649","C064A","C064B","C0648","C0650","C0644"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ M — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C064D:["Brake Pressure Sensor N Circuit/Open","C064D concerns an interrupted circuit at brake pressure sensor N, the thirteenth of the series. Larger sensor counts push makers towards digital links. A Bosch patent proposes PSI5 or DSI current interfaces on which up to four pressure sensors share two wires for power and data; an open in such a pair would silence every sensor on it at once.",["Open in a line or plug shared by several sensors","Poor contact at the sensor plug or spring contact","Internal interruption in sensor N"],["ABS/ESC warning lamp on, often with other pressure sensor codes","Stability control and brake assist unavailable"],3,2,["C064E","C064F","C0650","C0645","C0649","C0641"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ N — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C064E:["Brake Pressure Sensor N Circuit High","The signal of sensor N is above its permitted maximum. What the brake does next is described well for truck EBS: WABCO checks every analog pressure sensor signal against its authorised values; if one is lost, the module may keep producing electrical brake pressure by auxiliary means with limited accuracy, and if electronic control is impossible the axle falls back on purely pneumatic backup braking.",["Signal shorted to sensor supply or battery voltage","Open sensor ground","Sensor electronics reporting full scale or an internal fault"],["Brake or ESC warning lamp on","Less precise brake pressure control or pure backup braking"],2,2,["C064D","C064F","C0650","C0646","C064A","C0642"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ N — אות גבוה במעגל"],C064F:["Brake Pressure Sensor N Circuit Low","C064F: sensor N reports less than its smallest valid signal. In integrated units the sensor element and its evaluation are split: Continental Teves fits a bare measuring bridge into the hydraulic block and leaves amplification and offset to an IC in the module, while Actronics, which repairs such units, names the ATE MK60 with its internal pressure sensor as the system with the most pressure sensor problems and…",["Internal pressure sensor of the hydraulic unit failed","Signal contact or line shorted to ground","Evaluation IC in the control module defective"],["ABS/ESC warning lamp on","Stability control unavailable"],3,2,["C064D","C064E","C0650","C0647","C064B","C0575"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ N — אות נמוך במעגל"],C0650:["Brake Pressure Sensor N Range/Performance","Sensor N reports a pressure that is electrically valid but disagrees with the commanded or expected value. WABCO's truck EBS runs a matching test: with a defined magnetic flux in the proportional valve a minimum brake pressure must build up at the front axle brakes, or at the valve that controls the trailer, and when the vehicle brakes via pneumatic backup the rear axle must reach a set minimum once the front…",["Sensor N reading drifted","Valve or modulator not building the commanded pressure","Leak or air in the measured circuit"],["Warning lamp on after braking","Pressure control falls back to an emergency mode"],3,2,["C064D","C064E","C064F","C0648","C064C","C0644"],"חיישן לחץ בלם‏ N — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0651:["Left Front Wheel Speed Sensor B Circuit/Open","C0651 reports an open circuit at the second speed sensor of the left front wheel. Sensor B exists only where a wheel carries two independent speed signals, mainly in redundant brake systems for automated driving.",["Broken wire in the sensor B cable near the wheel","Plug of the second channel loose or corroded","Second sensing element inside the sensor failed open"],["Warning for brake or driver assistance system","Automated driving or redundant brake functions unavailable"],2,2,["C0652","C0653","C0654","C0655","C0500","C0658"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל קדמי שמאלי‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C0652:["Left Front Wheel Speed Sensor B Range/Performance","The second left front wheel speed signal is present but implausible. With two channels per wheel the module has a direct partner to compare: Volvo Truck's patent for a dual-element sensor merges both signals with an integrity index, averages them while they agree within a band, takes the higher value when both run but differ, and drops a channel that reads zero.",["Air gap too large from bearing play or a sensor not seated fully","Damaged or contaminated magnetic encoder","Sensor variant not matching the vehicle"],["Driver assistance or redundant braking warning","Automated functions withdrawn while ABS on sensor A continues"],2,2,["C0651","C0653","C0654","C0655","C0656","C0501"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל קדמי שמאלי‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0653:["Left Front Wheel Speed Sensor B Circuit Low","C0653 means the circuit of left front sensor B sits below its valid level. Active wheel speed sensors usually signal through current steps; Allegro gives 7 and 14 mA as typical levels and a safe state below about 3.9 mA that a sensor uses to report its own fault. A reading under the lower band can therefore come from a shorted or chafed line, a supply that has dropped, or the sensor itself flagging an error.",["Sensor B line chafed through and shorted to ground","Supply from the secondary control unit too low","Sensor in its fault (safe) state after an internal error"],["Warning for brake or driver assistance system","Redundant braking or automated driving not available"],2,2,["C0651","C0652","C0654","C0655","C0502","C065A"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל קדמי שמאלי‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],C0654:["Left Front Wheel Speed Sensor B Circuit High","Here the circuit of the second left front sensor reads above its permitted level, typically a short to the battery feed or to the supply of another channel. That risk follows from the packaging: Continental's dual-element sensor gives each element its own two-wire cable but allows both to share one outer sheath, so a crushed or heat-damaged cable can affect both channels.",["Sensor B line shorted to battery voltage","Short between the two channels in a shared cable sheath","Internal fault in the second sensing channel"],["Warning for brake or driver assistance system","Possibly both speed signals of the wheel affected"],2,2,["C0651","C0652","C0653","C0655","C0503","C065B"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל קדמי שמאלי‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],C0655:["Left Front Wheel Speed Sensor B Intermittent/Erratic","C0655 points to a second left front speed signal that drops out or jumps. Active sensors read the wheel through closely spaced sensing elements whose phase-shifted signals also give the rotation direction, as FenderBender explains, so small mechanical faults show up as irregular pulses.",["Loose contact or partly broken wire that moves with the steering and suspension","Dirt or damage on the magnetic encoder","Excessive wheel bearing play changing the air gap"],["Warning that comes and goes, often on rough roads or while steering","Automated or redundant brake functions intermittently withdrawn"],2,2,["C0651","C0652","C0653","C0654","C0504","C065C"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל קדמי שמאלי‏ B — אות לא יציב"],C0656:["Left Front Wheel Speed Sensor B Correlation","C0656 flags a mismatch between the B signal at the left front hub and the values it is checked against, typically sensor A on the same hub, while the circuit itself tests good. No carmaker publishes this code or its limits. Two patent designs show what such a comparison can catch. Continental Teves placed two magnetoresistive paths of different sensitivity in one housing;",["Sensor not seated correctly, air gap out of tolerance","Damaged, dirty or partly demagnetized encoder ring","Sensor of a different type or side fitted"],["Warning for brake or driver assistance system","Automated or redundant brake functions withdrawn, ABS usually still active"],2,2,["C0651","C0652","C0655","C0657","C0505","C065D"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל קדמי שמאלי‏ B — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],C0657:["Left Front Wheel Speed Sensor B Incorrect Component Installed","Here the module receives something on the second left front speed channel but decides that the fitted sensor is not the type it expects. No carmaker documents C0657, so the exact detection rule is unknown.",["Conventional single-channel sensor fitted instead of the dual-channel part","Sensor variant with other protocol or for the other side","Brake module not configured or coded for the fitted sensor"],["Warning appears soon after a sensor or hub replacement","Redundant braking or automated driving functions not available"],1,2,["C0651","C0656","C0555","C065E"],""],C0658:["Right Front Wheel Speed Sensor B Circuit/Open","C0658 reports an open in the wiring of right front sensor B, so the module sees no supply current on that channel. Sensor B is the redundant partner found mainly in brake systems built for automated driving; ABS normally keeps running on sensor A, where an open would show as C0506.",["Broken or torn sensor cable, often near the steering knuckle","Connector not latched, corroded or with spread terminals","Sensor B interrupted internally"],["Warning for brake or driver assistance system","Redundant braking or automated driving not available"],2,2,["C0659","C065A","C065B","C065C","C0506","C0651"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל קדמי ימני‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C0659:["Right Front Wheel Speed Sensor B Range/Performance","The second right front speed signal arrives, but its quality or value does not fit. For sensors using the VDA AK protocol, Infineon's TLE5046SiC shows what a module can read besides speed: a 3-bit air gap gauge and, in one variant, a reserve bit that is set once the magnetic signal drops below twice the value at the limit air gap. A weakening signal thus becomes visible before pulses are lost.",["Air gap too large from wheel bearing play or a loose sensor holder","Encoder ring dirty, cracked or weakened","Unsuitable replacement sensor"],["Warning for brake or driver assistance system, often only while driving","Automated functions withdrawn while ABS on sensor A continues"],2,2,["C0658","C065C","C065D","C0507","C0652"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל קדמי ימני‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C065A:["Right Front Wheel Speed Sensor B Circuit Low","C065A means the current in the circuit of right front sensor B stays below its lowest valid level. TI's TPIC7218-Q1, an interface chip that powers and reads four wheel speed sensors, rates a current under about 4.5 mA as undercurrent and labels it a possible short to ground.",["Signal line chafed through and touching ground","Supply at the sensor too low, e.g. from contact resistance","Sensor reports an internal fault with its error current"],["Warning for brake or driver assistance system right after switching on","Redundant braking or automated driving not available"],2,2,["C0658","C065B","C0508","C0653"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל קדמי ימני‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],C065B:["Right Front Wheel Speed Sensor B Circuit High","In C065B the line of sensor B at the right front shows a level above its allowed window, which mostly means a short to the supply. TI's TPIC7218-Q1 sets this limit by sensor type: for active two-level sensors any current over 20 mA counts as overcurrent, for three-level VDA sensors only above 40 mA, in both cases marked as a possible short to battery.",["Signal line shorted to battery voltage","Contact with the supply of another sensor channel in a shared cable","Sensor draws excessive current due to internal damage"],["Warning for brake or driver assistance system","Channel switched off by the module, redundant functions unavailable"],2,2,["C0658","C065A","C0509","C0654"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל קדמי ימני‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],C065C:["Right Front Wheel Speed Sensor B Intermittent/Erratic","C065C describes a second right front speed signal that vanishes now and then or carries irregular pulses. With AK protocol sensors, Pico's oscilloscope guide shows that the sensor keeps sending a data packet roughly every 147 ms even while the wheel stands still, so a break in that rhythm exposes a loose contact without the car moving.",["Loose contact in plug or cable, often where the cable flexes with steering","Encoder ring with dirt, metal chips or cracks","Interference from nearby high-current lines or damaged shielding"],["Warning that comes and goes, e.g. on rough roads or while steering","Automated or redundant brake functions intermittently withdrawn"],2,2,["C0658","C0659","C050A","C0655"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל קדמי ימני‏ B — אות לא יציב"],C065D:["Right Front Wheel Speed Sensor B Correlation","C065D says the second right front speed value disagrees with its comparison partners although no circuit fault is found. What it is compared with depends on the architecture. A Knorr-Bremse patent for commercial vehicles lets a separate redundancy system read part of the wheel speeds, for instance one wheel per axle, and exchanges all values over CAN, which makes a second sensor at every wheel unnecessary;",["Sensor B badly seated or air gap differing from sensor A","Encoder track damaged where only one element reads it","Disturbed data exchange between the brake control units"],["Warning for brake or driver assistance system after a drive","Automated driving functions refused, ABS usually unaffected"],2,2,["C0659","C065C","C065E","C050B","C0656"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל קדמי ימני‏ B — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],C065E:["Right Front Wheel Speed Sensor B Incorrect Component Installed","C065E means the module rejects the part fitted as the second speed sensor on the right front hub. Wheel speed sensors differ in their output scheme, and the receiving electronics are set up for one of them: TI's TPIC7218-Q1 is configured per sensor type, using two current thresholds for active sensors and four for VDA sensors that add 9 data bits.",["Replacement sensor with a different output protocol or variant","Single-channel sensor fitted where a dual-channel part belongs","Brake module not configured or coded for the fitted sensor"],["Warning appears soon after a sensor or hub replacement","Redundant braking or automated driving functions not available"],1,2,["C0658","C065D","C0556","C0657"],""],C065F:["Left Rear Wheel Speed Sensor B Circuit/Open","C065F reports that the second speed channel at the left rear wheel has no closed circuit. No carmaker publishes this code and no service bulletin mentions it, so the exact test is unknown. With active sensors an open is easy to recognise: NXP's KMI25 draws a constant base current of about 7 mA through the same two wires that carry its speed pulses, so a broken lead or a loose plug leaves the module with no current…",["Broken lead or loose, corroded plug between sensor and module","Sensor B open internally","Supply output for channel B in the brake module not switched on"],["Warning for brake or driver assistance system right after switching on","Functions relying on the second rear left signal not available"],2,2,["C0660","C0661","C0662","C0663","C050C","C0666"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי שמאלי‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C0660:["Left Rear Wheel Speed Sensor B Range/Performance","C0660 means the wiring of sensor B at the left rear tests good, yet its output fails to act like a wheel speed: it may vanish at speed, jump or show an odd pulse pattern. No published service data defines the check. Mounting is a common reason.",["Sensor seated off-centre or too far from its encoder","Encoder ring worn, dirty or weakly magnetised","Sensor B degraded internally"],["Warning only appears while driving, often above a certain speed","Assistance functions withdrawn while ABS on sensor A continues"],2,2,["C065F","C0663","C0664","C050D","C0667"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי שמאלי‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0661:["Left Rear Wheel Speed Sensor B Circuit Low","With C0661 the second left rear speed signal sits below the lowest level an intact sensor ever outputs, typically because the signal lead touches ground or the sensor feed has collapsed. No carmaker documents this code.",["Signal lead chafed through and touching ground","Sensor supply pulled down, e.g. by water in the plug","Sensor B shorted internally"],["Warning for brake or stability system shortly after start","Emergency braking support of the electric parking brake may be restricted"],2,2,["C065F","C0662","C050E","C0668"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי שמאלי‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],C0662:["Left Rear Wheel Speed Sensor B Circuit High","C0662 is stored when the second left rear speed channel reads above anything the sensor itself can deliver. NXP's KMI25 uses three current steps: about 7 mA at rest, 14 mA for a logic one of its data protocol and 28 mA for each speed pulse. A higher value can only come from outside the sensor, such as contact with battery voltage, a chafed wire touching another feed or moisture bridging the plug.",["Signal lead shorted to battery voltage or to the sensor feed","Moisture or corrosion bridging pins in the connector","Sensor B drawing excessive current internally"],["Warning lamp for ABS or stability control","Module switches channel B off, redundant functions unavailable"],2,2,["C065F","C0661","C050F","C0669"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי שמאלי‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],C0663:["Left Rear Wheel Speed Sensor B Intermittent/Erratic","Here the second left rear speed signal drops out for moments or jumps, without a lasting circuit fault. No public service data describes the code, so diagnosis has to follow the sensor principle.",["Loose contact in plug or harness that opens on bumps","Encoder ring partly demagnetised or damaged","Interference from nearby motors or high-current cables"],["Warning comes and goes, often on rough roads","Brief, unexpected stability or ABS interventions"],2,2,["C065F","C0660","C0510","C066A"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי שמאלי‏ B — אות לא יציב"],C0664:["Left Rear Wheel Speed Sensor B Correlation","C0664 flags that the second left rear speed value disagrees with its reference speeds, although its circuit is sound. No carmaker publishes the comparison. Two patents show how a rear wheel can be cross-checked.",["Damaged or wrong encoder ring giving a false pulse count","Tyre of different size or heavily worn on the left rear","Sensor B losing pulses at high speed"],["Warning set after a longer drive, not at start","Automated or redundant brake functions refused"],2,2,["C0660","C0663","C0665","C0511","C066B"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי שמאלי‏ B — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],C0665:["Left Rear Wheel Speed Sensor B Incorrect Component Installed","C0665 says the part on the second left rear speed channel is not the one the module expects. No carmaker documents the code or how it identifies the part. Typical mix-ups arise at the wheel bearing.",["Wheel bearing fitted with the encoder facing away from the sensor","Sensor made for a different encoder type or vehicle","Replacement hub without encoder ring fitted"],["Warning appears right after a bearing, hub or sensor replacement","Redundant brake functions not available"],2,2,["C065F","C0664","C0557","C066C"],""],C0666:["Right Rear Wheel Speed Sensor B Circuit/Open","The second speed channel at the right rear wheel is open: a wire, terminal or the sensor itself no longer conducts. C0666 is not documented by any carmaker. Where the repair ends depends on the hub design. Schaeffler's wheel bearing brochure notes that some third-generation bearings carry all speed sensors inside the bearing unit, so an internal open there can mean replacing the whole hub assembly.",["Harness or connector open at the right rear wheel","Sensor inside the hub bearing unit failed open","Input stage for channel B in the brake module defective"],["Warning for brake or stability system on every start","Electric parking brake may only apply gradually while the switch is held"],2,2,["C0667","C0668","C0669","C066A","C0512","C065F"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי ימני‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],C0667:["Right Rear Wheel Speed Sensor B Range/Performance","C0667 reports that the second right rear speed signal arrives but is not plausible, while the circuit itself is fine. No maker documents the code. At the rear axle the air gap can change while driving.",["Worn or wrongly adjusted wheel bearing letting the gap vary","Axle shaft deflection under load or a bent shaft","Sensor not fully seated in its bore"],["Warning mainly with load, towing or in fast bends","Stability control functions temporarily withdrawn"],2,2,["C0666","C066A","C066B","C0513","C0660"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי ימני‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0668:["Right Rear Wheel Speed Sensor B Circuit Low","C0668 points to a channel reading that is too low for the second right rear sensor. No carmaker documents the code, so the limit is not public. With a current-output sensor the floor is easy to define: in NXP's KMI25 a constant source of about 7 mA runs the whole chip and is always present, even when no pulse is sent.",["Crushed or chafed lead leaking current to ground","High contact resistance lowering the sensor voltage","Sensor B internal current source defective"],["Warning lamp for ABS or stability control","Redundant speed information at the right rear missing"],2,2,["C0666","C0669","C0514","C0661"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי ימני‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],C0669:["Right Rear Wheel Speed Sensor B Circuit High","With C0669 the second right rear speed channel shows a level above the valid range, which usually means it is connected to a voltage source it should not see. No carmaker publishes this code. Sensor chips are built to survive such faults for a while: NXP builds the input die of the KMI25 with a process rated for high voltage, precisely to shield the measuring parts from the harsh conditions on the supply line.",["Signal lead shorted to battery voltage","Repaired or replacement harness wired to the wrong pins","Sensor B shorted internally"],["Warning lamp right after switching on","Channel B switched off, assistance functions reduced"],2,2,["C0666","C0668","C0515","C0662"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי ימני‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],C066A:["Right Rear Wheel Speed Sensor B Intermittent/Erratic","C066A describes a second right rear speed signal that keeps dropping out or jumping. No carmaker documents it. Apart from loose contacts, the encoder deserves a close look. Schaeffler explains that many wheel bearings carry a multipole encoder just inside the seal: a ring magnetised in alternating poles that the sensor reads.",["Encoder ring with metal swarf, cracks or weakened poles","Intermittent contact in plug or harness","Worn wheel bearing letting the encoder wobble"],["Warning appears and clears again during a drive","Speed of the right rear wheel jumps in live data"],2,2,["C0666","C0667","C0516","C0663"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי ימני‏ B — אות לא יציב"],C066B:["Right Rear Wheel Speed Sensor B Correlation","The second right rear speed value is electrically fine but disagrees with its references. No carmaker documents C066B or its limits. A Ford patent shows a check that suits a driven rear axle: the right rear speed is calculated as twice the output shaft speed divided by the axle ratio, minus the measured left rear speed.",["Mismatched tyre size or tread depth at the right rear","Encoder with missing or extra pulses","Axle ratio or tyre data in the module not matching the vehicle"],["Warning after a fast or long drive","Traction or stability functions temporarily reduced"],2,2,["C0667","C066A","C066C","C0517","C0664"],"חיישן מהירות גלגל אחורי ימני‏ B — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],C066C:["Right Rear Wheel Speed Sensor B Incorrect Component Installed","C066C indicates that the part on the second right rear speed channel differs from the one the module is set up for. No carmaker documents the code or its detection logic. Parts for the rear hub come in several versions: Schaeffler lists wheel bearings both with a multipole encoder and without one, plus third-generation units with the sensors built in, so a hub from the wrong range may lack the encoder or the second…",["Hub or bearing from a variant without encoder or second sensor","Bearing fitted with the encoder side facing away from the sensor","Sensor of another type or vehicle fitted"],["Warning appears right after work on the right rear hub","Redundant or automated brake functions not available"],2,2,["C0666","C066B","C0558","C0665"],""],C066D:["Service/Park Brake Chamber Pressure Sensor","C066D covers a fault in the transducer reporting the air pressure inside the service/spring brake chambers of an air-braked vehicle. No maker documents the code, but the diagnosis of real systems is published. Bendix's Intellipark electronic parking brake measures the delivery pressure of every channel with its own transducer and logs J1939 faults for signals shorted high or to ground;",["Sensor signal or 5 V supply shorted to ground or voltage","Pressure transducer in the valve module defective","Sensor outputs shorted together or connectors swapped"],["Parking brake indicator flashes, park status unknown","Automatic park functions such as rollaway protection unavailable"],3,2,["C066E","C066F"],""],C066E:["Service/Park Brake Chamber Pressure Too High","C066E means the measured chamber pressure is higher than the module allows in the present state. No maker documents the code, so its limit is not public. Too much pressure in the service section raises the push on the brake directly: Bendix calculates about 1,800 lbf on the pushrod when 60 psi reaches a type 30 chamber, and its chamber tests are not to exceed 120 psig. A specific risk is compounding.",["Governor or pressure regulator letting system pressure rise too far","Anti-compound function not working, both forces add up","Pressure sensor reading too high"],["Brake warning or fault message on the dash or trailer lamp","Harsh braking or overheated wheel ends after parking manoeuvres"],3,0,["C066D","C066F"],""],C066F:["Service/Park Brake Chamber Pressure Too Low","C066F reports chamber pressure below what the brake system needs. No maker documents this code. For the spring section the consequences are clear: inside Bendix's piggyback unit the main spring starts to apply the brake once its chamber pressure falls under 78 psi, so a leak or weak supply makes the brakes drag.",["Leaking diaphragm, chamber seal or supply line","Insufficient reservoir pressure from compressor or dryer","Park valve or relay valve not delivering full pressure"],["Red brake or low-air warning, parking brake indicator flashing","Brakes dragging or spring brakes applying on their own"],3,2,["C066D","C066E"],""],C0670:["Left Front Acceleration or Position Sensor Circuit","C0670 is absent from the publicly available J2012 lists, but GM assigns it in its electronic damping control. In Saab's 2011 workshop data for the 9-5 and 9-4X it covers the vertical acceleration sensor at the left front wheel, which the suspension module supplies with 5 V and which answers with 0.5 to 4.5 V.",["Wheel acceleration sensor, its 5 V supply or signal wire faulty","Replacement sensor not compatible with early suspension module (GM PI0954)","Corroded or loose connector at the wheel housing"],["Service suspension message in the instrument cluster","Adaptive damping inactive, firmer or less controlled ride"],2,2,["C0065","C006A"],""],C0671:["Electric Park Brake Actuator Right Circuit","C0671 cannot be traced publicly: no publicly available J2012 list, no NHTSA bulletin, no GM keyword list and no Saab index contains it. GM even uses the neighbouring C0670 for a damping sensor and logs the electric park brake motor of the 2011 Saab 9-5 under C028A, with subcodes for shorts to plus or to ground, an open circuit and wrong frequency. The title points to the right rear caliper actuator.",["Moisture or corrosion at the actuator plug in the wheel housing","Actuator motor or gearbox defective","Chafed or broken wire between module and actuator"],["Park brake warning light or message","Right rear brake does not apply or does not release"],2,0,["C0610","C0611","C0612","C0613","C0680"],"ימני מפעיל בלם חניה חשמלית — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0680:["Electric Park Brake Module Internal Fault","Public evidence for C0680 is lacking: it is in none of the public J2012 tables, bulletins or maker indexes. The title describes a park brake controller that fails its own checks. How GM handles that is documented for the 2011 Saab 9-5, just under other numbers: C056E flags software that is missing, an absent calibration or implausible software, and C0558 a calibration or mechanical fault;",["Calibration after brake service skipped or programming interrupted","Electronics inside the park brake or ABS/ESC module failed","Low battery voltage during self-test or programming"],["Park brake warning, function disabled or degraded","Brake cannot be applied, or only one more release is allowed"],3,0,["C0615","C0616","U0128","C0671"],""],C0700:["Active Steering Module Communication","No public record shows a carmaker using C0700; public J2012 lists, NHTSA bulletins and maker indexes are silent. The title concerns superimposed steering such as the system from the Bosch-ZF venture that BMW introduced on the 2004 5 Series.",["Damaged bus wiring or connector to the active steering controller","Steering angle or wheel speed message missing from another module","Active steering controller without power or defective"],["Steering warning in the instrument cluster","Steering ratio stays fixed, more wheel turns when parking"],3,2,["U0126","U0130","C0460"],"תקשורת מודול היגוי פעיל"],C0710:["Steering Position Signal Malfunction","C0710 does not appear in the publicly available J2012 lists, yet GM uses it widely in the brake control module for the steering angle it feeds to stability control. Saab 9-5 2011 wording matches the title for subcode 00 and adds 42 (centering not stored) and 5A (signal missing, offset out of range or at odds with yaw rate); the 9-4X adds 71 for invalid data. The sensor should sweep from -550 to +550 degrees.",["Steering angle sensor not centred after alignment or repair","Steering wheel mis-splined, or suspension, wheelbase or tyres changed","Faulty steering angle sensor, connector or worn column bearing","Brake module programmed for the wrong sensor design"],["Service StabiliTrak or stability message, ESC indicator on","Unwanted stability intervention while cornering"],2,2,["C0455","C0460","C0440","C0445","C0805"],"אות מצב היגוי — תקלה"],C0712:["Power Steering Position Sensor Range/Performance","No carmaker is known to document C0712; it is not in the J2012 tables, bulletins or maker indexes searched. The title points to a position input of the power steering whose value is outside the expected band or does not track the other signals. An electric power steering relies on three position measurements: driver torque, the angle of the assist motor and the absolute steering wheel angle;",["Steering angle or position learn skipped or done wrongly","Position sensor in the steering gear or column defective","Intermittent connection in the sensor wiring"],["Power steering warning, assist reduced or lost","Steering wheel off centre or vehicle drifts to one side"],2,2,["C0460","C0526","C0528","C0805","C0830"],"חיישן מצב הגה כוח — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0715:["Power Steering Pressure Sensor Range/Performance","C0715 is not traceable in public material; the publicly available J2012 tables, the NHTSA bulletin index and maker code lists all lack it. The function it names is well known from engine diagnostics, where the same check runs as P0551. On hydraulic steering the pump pressure rises with steering effort and a switch or sensor tells the engine controller to raise idle.",["Pressure sensor or switch stuck or drifting","Fluid seeping into the sensor connector","Pump pressure abnormal due to low fluid or worn pump"],["Idle dips or engine stalls at full steering lock","Idle stays raised while driving straight"],1,0,["P0551","P0550","P0552","P0553","C0250"],"חיישן לחץ הגה כוח — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0720:["Electric Power Steering Torque Sensor Circuit","No publicly available J2012 list contains C0720, and the only maker that uses it means something else: GM files C0720 71 on the 2011 Saab 9-5 and 9-4X as invalid engine torque data received by the suspension module over CAN; the damping control stays off for that ignition cycle and a history entry clears after 41 fault-free cycles.",["Steering torque sensor defective","Loose or corroded connector between sensor and EPS module","Sensor zero point not learned after replacement"],["Sudden loss of steering assist with warning message and chime","Heavy steering at low speed"],3,2,["C0825","C0827","C0725"],"חיישן מומנט הגה כוח חשמלי — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0725:["Electric Power Steering Motor Circuit","C0725 has no public documentation; the publicly available J2012 tables, NHTSA bulletins and maker indexes leave it out. Carmakers file assist motor faults elsewhere: GM uses C0475, including symptom 64 for a detected slip in the motor circuit (bulletin PIT5213B), and Stellantis C1592, which the 2019 Jeep Cherokee could log as a general electrical failure and which a software flash addressed under bulletin 08-034-20,…",["Motor winding or power stage in the EPS unit defective","Module software misdiagnoses the motor circuit (update available)","Poor connection between module and motor"],["Steering warning, assist reduced or lost","Steering feels notchy or jerks while turning"],3,2,["C0730","C0735","C0720"],"מנוע הגה כוח חשמלי — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0727:["Trailer Connector Circuit Malfunction","C0727 has no public trace in the public J2012 tables, NHTSA bulletins or maker indexes, and trailer faults usually sit in B or U codes. The circuits behind the title are documented. GM trucks with the trailering app have a trailer lighting module that powers the socket with pulse-width signals;",["Moisture or corrosion in the vehicle trailer socket","Short, LED load too low or own lighting module on the trailer","Damaged vehicle harness or trailer lighting module"],["Trailer lamps inoperative or flickering","Trailer connected/disconnected message without reason"],1,0,["C0784","C0860","U0137"],"מחבר גרור — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0730:["Electric Power Steering Motor Position Sensor Circuit","Neither the publicly available J2012 lists nor NHTSA bulletins or maker indexes show C0730, so its use is not publicly verifiable. The sensor it names reports the rotor angle of the brushless assist motor, without which the module cannot commutate the phases or run field-oriented current control.",["Rotor position sensor in the EPS motor defective","Poor connection between sensor and control board","Sensor magnet loose or misaligned after repair"],["Steering assist drops out suddenly, warning lamp on","Steering jerky or uneven while turning"],4,2,["C0725","C0735"],"חיישן מצב מנוע הגה כוח חשמלי — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0735:["Electric Power Steering Module Internal Fault","No known public source uses C0735; it is absent from the published J2012 lists, from NHTSA bulletins and from maker indexes. Carmakers report an internal EPS controller fault under other codes. GM uses C056D as a general hardware fault and asks technicians to reprogram the module first when symptom 39 is set (PIT5213B, 2014-15 trucks and SUVs). Stellantis uses C2217-00;",["Module software fault, cleared by reprogramming","Internal hardware failure of the EPS controller","Wrong steering gear or module installed, setup not completed"],["Service power steering message, steering lamp on","Assist reduced or absent from start-up"],4,2,["C05D6","U0131","C0740"],""],C0740:["Electric Power Steering Voltage Supply","C0740 is not publicly documented by any carmaker; publicly available J2012 lists, NHTSA bulletins and maker indexes do not contain it. The title concerns the heavy supply feed of an electric steering, which draws high currents when the wheel is turned at standstill.",["Loose or corroded main power or ground connection at the rack","Discharged or failing battery, high-resistance battery cables","Battery cable shorting elsewhere or poor body ground"],["Assist weakens or cuts out at low speed and full lock","Steering wheel jerks, other displays flicker"],2,2,["C0800","C0735","C0745"],"אספקת מתח הגה כוח חשמלי"],C0745:["Electric Power Steering Overtemperature Protection","Public documentation of C0745 is missing; it is not in the publicly available J2012 tables, in NHTSA bulletins or in maker indexes. GM reports an overheated EPS controller as C0176 (PIT5213B).",["Long parking manoeuvres or holding the wheel at full lock","Stiff steering gear, joints or tyres raising motor load","Temperature estimate or sensor in the module faulty"],["Steering gradually heavier after repeated manoeuvring","Power steering warning message"],2,2,["C062A","C0725","C0735"],""],C0750:["Left Front Tire Pressure Sensor","None of the public code lists carries C0750. GM, however, uses it in its tire pressure monitoring for the left front wheel transmitter, and the Saab 9-5 (2010-2011) and 9-4X service pages define the subcodes: 03 for a weak sensor battery, 29 for a sensor that sends too few telegrams, 39 for an internal sensor defect. The check runs above 40 km/h, when the roll switch in each wheel unit should wake the transmitter;",["Built-in battery of the wheel sensor exhausted (subcode 03)","Sensor damaged during tire service, after a flat or replaced by a valve without sensor","Radio interference from aftermarket devices or metallised window tint (GM PIC5650M)","Remote receiver or its antenna unplugged or faulty"],["TPMS lamp flashes about one minute after start, then stays on","Dashes instead of a pressure value for the left front tire","Service tire monitor message in the driver display"],2,0,["C0950","C0083","C0077"],"חיישן לחץ אוויר בצמיגים קדמי שמאלי"],C0784:["Trailer Brake Force Sensor Circuit Malfunction","Searches for C0784 came up empty: the public code lists, the NHTSA bulletin index, GM's keyword table and the Saab and Mitsubishi indexes all miss it. The title points to the signal an integrated trailer brake controller uses to gauge how hard the driver is braking.",["Open, shorted or corroded wiring or connector of the brake force or pressure signal","Brake pressure transducer or deceleration sensor defective","Trailer brake controller module faulty or wrongly configured"],["Trailer brakes weak, delayed or not applied when the vehicle brakes","Trailer brake warning message in the instrument cluster"],2,0,["C0727","C0860"],"חיישן כוח בלם גרור — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0800:["Device Power 1 Circuit","Generic code lists omit C0800, but GM uses it widely for the supply voltage that a chassis module sees, often the brake control module. Saab workshop pages for the 2011 models list the subcodes are 03 below threshold, 07 above, 0D high resistance and 11 high input; the module flags a supply under roughly 9 V or over 18 V lasting about 5 s and may switch itself off.",["Loose or corroded battery cable or ground connection (GM PI1398A)","Weak battery or charging system fault, also after jump start or charger use","High resistance in the module's supply or ground circuit"],["ABS, traction and stability warnings light up, sometimes only briefly","Radio or displays switch off and on, lights flicker","Heavier steering at low speed on vehicles with electric power steering"],2,2,["C0564","C0565","C0740","P0560","P0562","P0563"],"כוח התקן‏ 1 — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0805:["Steering Angle Sensor Calibration","Public evidence for C0805 is lacking: it appears neither in code lists nor in the NHTSA index, GM's keyword table or the Saab and Mitsubishi indexes. The title describes a steering angle sensor whose zero point has not been learned.",["Zero point not learned after battery disconnect or steering gear replacement","Steering wheel or sensor mounted off centre, so the learned offset is out of range","Steering angle sensor defective and unable to store the calibration"],["Stability or traction control lamp stays on","ESC and hill start assist unavailable"],1,2,["C0529","C0710","C0830","C0526"],"כיול חיישן זווית הגה"],C0810:["Air Suspension Compressor Circuit","C0810 cannot be located anywhere public, whether in code lists, the NHTSA index or the GM, Saab and Mitsubishi material. The title concerns the electrical drive of the air suspension compressor, an electric motor that Continental describes with carbon brushes stressed by inrush current.",["Water ingress and corrosion seizing or loading the compressor motor","Compressor relay or fuse failed","Open, shorted or corroded wiring or connector at the compressor"],["Air suspension warning message in the cluster","Vehicle sits low or does not change ride height"],2,2,["C0815","C0301","C0317","C0840"],"מדחס מתלי אוויר — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0815:["Air Suspension Compressor Overtemperature","C0815 has no public owner: code lists and maker indexes skip it, and the NHTSA index only matches it inside unrelated BMW bulletin IDs. The title names thermal protection of the air suspension compressor. Most systems have no temperature sensor and estimate the heat from running time instead.",["Leak in an air spring, line or valve block keeps the compressor running","Repeated manual level changes at standstill or heavy load changes","Worn or moisture-damaged compressor delivering too little air"],["Ride height change stops or is refused for several minutes","Air suspension warning, vehicle sits low after long standing"],2,2,["C0810","C0301","C0840"],"מדחס מתלי אוויר — חום יתר"],C0820:["Air Suspension Height Sensor Front Left","Nobody documents C0820 in the open; apart from Honda bulletin IDs that happen to contain the string, searches of lists and indexes found nothing. The title concerns the ride height sensor at the left front corner, a lever on the control arm turning an angle sensor that reports body height to the air suspension module.",["Bent, detached or seized sensor lever or link at the front left control arm","Water, corrosion or chafing at the sensor plug or harness in the wheel arch","Air suspension module software reporting a false stuck sensor (Stellantis 08-150-24)"],["Service air suspension message","Front left corner sits too high or too low, height changes refused"],2,2,["C0821","C0822","C0823","C0840"],"שמאלי קדמי חיישן גובה מתלי אוויר"],C0821:["Air Suspension Height Sensor Front Right","C0821 leaves no public trace in public lists, bulletins or maker indexes; going by its name it means the front right level sensor. HELLA builds such sensors as a housing on the body with a lever and ball joint to the axle, using potentiometer, Hall or contactless inductive elements, fed with 4 to 11 V and sending analogue, PWM, SENT or PSI5 signals.",["Signal wire shorted to ground by chafing, water or corrosion","Code stored after the car was jacked or lifted, sensor at end of travel","Front right height sensor or its lever defective"],["Service air suspension message","Vehicle leans to the front right or levelling is switched off"],2,2,["C0820","C0822","C0823"],"ימני קדמי חיישן גובה מתלי אוויר"],C0822:["Air Suspension Height Sensor Rear Left","For C0822 the search of code lists, NHTSA and the GM, Saab and Mitsubishi sources returned nothing. Per its title it covers the rear left level sensor of an air suspension. At the rear axle the harness runs close to the subframe and fuel tank, which is where Stellantis found the cause of its own code C1526 subcode 11, short to ground, on a 2019 Grand Cherokee: the wiring rubbed on bracket edges and had to be…",["Harness rubbing on subframe or bracket edges near the fuel tank","Rear left height sensor or its link rod damaged","Module software misjudging the sensor as stuck"],["Service air suspension message","Rear left sags or rear ride height not adjusted"],2,2,["C0820","C0821","C0823"],"שמאלי אחורי חיישן גובה מתלי אוויר"],C0823:["Air Suspension Height Sensor Rear Right","C0823 is unknown to every public source, from code lists to the NHTSA index and maker documentation. The title refers to the rear right level sensor. Its reading matters most when loading, since the module uses the rear heights to keep ground clearance and headlamp aim constant.",["Rear right height sensor, lever or ball joint worn or broken","Corroded or loose sensor connector, damaged harness","Air suspension module software needing an update (Stellantis 08-127-23)"],["Service air suspension message","Rear right sits low or high, load levelling inactive"],2,2,["C0820","C0821","C0822","C0312"],"ימני אחורי חיישן גובה מתלי אוויר"],C0825:["Steering Effort Sensor Range/Performance","No public code list, bulletin or service manual assigns C0825, so its use by any carmaker cannot be shown. The title points at the torque sensor of electric power steering: a torsion bar in the column or pinion twists under the driver's hand force, and Hall elements read that twist as a torque value.",["Torque sensor channel drifting or reading implausibly against the second channel","Unstable sensor supply or internal short in the sensor (as in Honda bulletin 22-011)","Poor contact at the sensor or steering module connector"],["Power steering warning lamp or message","Steering assist reduced or switched off, wheel feels heavy","Uneven assistance between left and right turns"],3,2,["C0827","C0720","C0735","C0740"],"חיישן מאמץ היגוי — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0827:["Steering Effort Sensor Stuck","C0827 appears in no accessible code list, bulletin or manufacturer table, so no carmaker can be named for it. The title describes a steering torque signal that freezes: the value no longer follows the driver, either because a short pins the output at a supply rail or because the sensor delivers a constant value while the wheel is clearly being turned.",["Sensor output shorted to supply or ground, holding the signal at a rail","Hall element or sensor electronics frozen, usually requiring a new steering gear or column","Chafed or pinched harness between sensor and steering module"],["Power steering warning lamp on","Assistance fades out and steering becomes heavy"],3,2,["C0825","C0720","C0735"],"חיישן מאמץ היגוי — תקוע"],C0830:["Steering Wheel Angle Sensor Center Position Not Learned","No public list or bulletin uses C0830; its content overlaps with C0529 (missing calibration) and C0805. The stability control needs to know which sensor reading means wheels straight ahead; until that zero point is stored, it cannot compare steering input with yaw.",["Zero point not relearned after battery disconnect, alignment, sensor or steering gear replacement","Steering wheel not centred or alignment off during calibration","Incorrect calibration from the factory (Kia service action SA641)"],["Stability and traction control lamp on, ESC switched off","Hill start assist or lane functions unavailable","Steering wheel slightly off centre when driving straight"],1,2,["C0529","C0805","C0710","C0460","C0605"],"מצב מרכזי חיישן זווית גלגל הגה — לא בוצע לימוד"],C0840:["Air Suspension Solenoid Valve Circuit","C0840 is not documented anywhere in public; no list, bulletin or manual of any carmaker uses it. The title concerns the electrical side of the valves that route air in a self-levelling suspension. Some systems carry one switching valve per air spring in a central block next to the compressor, as in a Continental patent that also places fast lowering valves there;",["Water or corrosion in the valve connector (Bentley 2064579/1 checks the plug first)","Open or shorted valve coil, often after moisture got into the system","Chafed harness at the valve block or air spring"],["Air suspension warning or service message","One corner sags or ride height cannot be changed"],2,2,["C0810","C0815","C0820","C0821","C0822","C0823"],"שסתום סולנואיד מתלי אוויר — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0850:["Active Damping Control Front Left","No manufacturer publishes C0850, and no code list carries it, so its use cannot be shown. The title refers to the electrically adjusted shock absorber at the left front. Its control unit sends a pulse width modulated current through a valve coil in the damper and measures the current that really flows; when the two differ, it stores a fault.",["Damaged or loose cable and plug at the front left strut","Valve coil inside the damper open or shorted, damper must be replaced","Faulty driver stage in the suspension control module"],["Service suspension message","Damping no longer adapts, ride feels harsher or floatier"],3,2,["C0851","C0852","C0853","C0920"],"שמאלי קדמי בקרת שיכוך פעיל"],C0851:["Active Damping Control Front Right","C0851 has no public owner: neither code lists nor bulletins name it. Its subject is the adjustable damper at the right front corner. GM's electronic suspension on the 2011 Saab 9-5 files this corner as C0580 with three failure types: 02 when the high side is shorted to ground or to voltage, 04 for an open control line, 0F for an erratic coil current. The system works only between 9 and 16 V;",["Corroded or loose plug at the right front damper","Proportional valve in the damper failed","Supply outside 9-16 V causing erratic current readings"],["Suspension warning in the instrument cluster","Body movements less controlled over bumps"],3,2,["C0850","C0852","C0853","C0920"],"ימני קדמי בקרת שיכוך פעיל"],C0852:["Active Damping Control Rear Left","Nothing public ties C0852 to a manufacturer; it is absent from every public list and index. The title covers the adjustable rear left damper. Some modern units use two valves per damper, one for compression and one for rebound. Stellantis does so on the 2024-26 Ram 1500 and Dodge Charger and logs the rear left pair as C15C6 and C15C7;",["Loose pin fit or intermittent contact in the rear left damper connector","Harness damaged by road spray, stones or corrosion near the rear axle","Compression or rebound valve in the damper failed"],["Service suspension warning","Rear feels bouncy or harsh, drive modes no longer change damping"],3,2,["C0850","C0851","C0853","C0920"],"שמאלי אחורי בקרת שיכוך פעיל"],C0853:["Active Damping Control Rear Right","C0853 is undocumented in public sources; no carmaker's list, bulletin or manual mentions it. The title is about the adjustable damper at the right rear. Such dampers only work as well as the inputs behind them: the control unit takes in body and wheel motion from accelerometers and sets each valve accordingly.",["Open or shorted circuit to the right rear damper valve","Implausible wheel acceleration sensor input causing shutdown (BMW SI B37 01 14)","Damper control unit software needing an update"],["Suspension fault message","Car stays on a fixed damper setting regardless of mode"],3,2,["C0850","C0851","C0852","C0920"],"ימני אחורי בקרת שיכוך פעיל"],C0860:["Trailer Stability Assist Performance","No carmaker documents C0860 openly, and it does not appear in any accessible list. The title names trailer sway control, an extra function of the stability control that uses the existing ESC sensors to spot a swinging trailer and then brakes single wheels and trims engine torque until the combination calms down.",["Fault in an ESC input such as brake pedal switch, yaw or wheel speed signal","Trailer not recognised because of trailer socket or wiring faults","Stability control software or configuration needing an update"],["Trailer stability or ESC warning lamp on","No automatic braking when the trailer sways"],2,0,["C0727","C0784","C0196"],"סיוע יציבות גרור — ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0870:["Control Module Voltage Reference Output Circuit","C0870 is missing from the accessible J2012 code lists; it is documented at GM, where it covers the 5 V reference that a module feeds to its sensors. Saab workshop pages for the 2011 9-5 and 9-4X use it in the suspension control module, which feeds five acceleration sensors on the body and at the wheels: subcode 03 means that line is shorted to ground and 07 that it touches battery voltage, each for 1.5 s, checked…",["One acceleration sensor shorting the shared 5 V reference","Reference line chafed to ground or to battery voltage","Module reference supply faulty, module replacement after wiring checks (Saab WIS)"],["SERVICE SUSPENSION SYSTEM message","Adaptive damping inactive for the rest of the trip","Several acceleration sensor codes stored at once"],2,2,["C0670","C0800","C0920"],"יציאת ייחוס מתח מודול בקרה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0900:["TPMS Sensor 1 Battery","C0900 does not appear in the publicly available J2012 code lists, and no carmaker publishes it for tire pressure monitoring. The one official mention points elsewhere: GM upfitter bulletin 80C for the 2008-2014 Silverado and Sierra HD chassis cab lists C0900 subcode 07 as Device Voltage High, a supply fault logged by the PTO module. The title instead means the battery inside the first wheel transmitter.",["Built-in lithium cell of the wheel transmitter at end of life","Aged cell whose voltage sags in cold weather","On GM vehicles the code may instead stem from excessive module supply voltage (Device Voltage High)"],["TPMS warning lamp flashes after start, then stays lit","Pressure reading for one wheel drops out intermittently, more often in cold weather"],2,0,["C0902","C0905","C0907","C0750"],"סוללת חיישן TPMS‏ 1"],C0901:["TPMS Sensor 1 Position Performance","Nothing public ties C0901 to a carmaker: no public code list, NHTSA bulletin or service index contains it. Its title concerns the automatic assignment of wheel transmitter 1 to a corner of the car. Without that link the system knows a pressure value but not which tire it belongs to.",["Learning drive too short or too slow after wheel change or sensor replacement","Wheel speed data from the ABS module missing or implausible, so phase comparison fails","Transmitters of a spare wheel or a nearby vehicle disturbing the assignment"],["TPMS warning lamp lit or flashing although tire pressures are correct","Pressures shown at the wrong wheel position or no position display at all"],1,0,["C0903","C0900","C0912"],"מצב חיישן TPMS‏ 1 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0902:["TPMS Sensor 2 Battery","C0902 cannot be traced in public sources; the NHTSA index only matches it inside an unrelated vehicle number. The title covers the cell feeding wheel transmitter 2. Which corner counts as number 2 is up to each maker; Mitsubishi numbers tires 1 to 4 and uses C1920 for a weak transmitter battery on tire 2.",["Transmitter cell discharged after years of service","Sensor electronics drawing excess current, draining the cell early","After rotating wheels the battery warning is attributed to the wrong position"],["TPMS lamp or a service tire monitor message","Readings from one wheel update less often or vanish"],2,0,["C0900","C0905","C0907"],"סוללת חיישן TPMS‏ 2"],C0903:["TPMS Sensor 2 Position Performance","Searches found C0903 neither in code lists nor in maker documents; a single NHTSA hit is a truck maker's campaign number. The title addresses locating transmitter 2 on the vehicle. Two methods are documented.",["Location learning interrupted, e.g. short trips at low speed after tire service","Sensor does not answer the wheel well initiator (weak LF field, misaligned initiator)","Acceleration or rotation detection inside the sensor faulty"],["TPMS lamp on with all tires correctly inflated","Display shows pressures without assigning them to wheel positions"],2,0,["C0901","C0902","C0912"],"מצב חיישן TPMS‏ 2 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],C0905:["TPMS Sensor 3 Battery Low","No manufacturer is known to use C0905; none of the code lists, service indexes or NHTSA bulletins searched contains it. The title names a weak battery in the third wheel transmitter. GM and Saab file this condition by wheel rather than by number, as subcode 03 Low Voltage under C0750 to C0765;",["Sensor cell near end of life (typically after many years)","Sensor stuck in a fast transmit mode, drawing the cell down early"],["TPMS lamp flashes about a minute after start, then stays on","Pressure values still shown, warning returns after every restart"],2,0,["C0907","C0900","C0902","C0952"],"סוללת חיישן TPMS‏ 3 — ערך נמוך"],C0907:["TPMS Sensor 4 Battery Low","C0907 has no public owner: code lists, the NHTSA index and the GM, Saab and Mitsubishi service indexes all lack it. Per its title it flags a fading battery in transmitter 4. How that state is noticed: the sensor measures its cell through a voltage divider and sends a battery byte with each pressure message, as a CM Automotive patent shows. Mitsubishi stores C1940 for tire 4 in this case;",["Transmitter cell weak from age","Cold weather pushing an ageing cell below the warning level","Fault in the sensor's voltage measurement"],["TPMS warning lamp with a sensor fault message","Later, dashes instead of a value for the affected wheel"],2,0,["C0905","C0900","C0902","C0953"],"סוללת חיישן TPMS‏ 4 — ערך נמוך"],C0910:["TPMS Receiver Circuit Malfunction","There is no public evidence that any carmaker assigns C0910. It describes a fault in the circuit of the radio receiver that collects the wheel sensor telegrams. Designs differ: GM and Saab route the sensors through the remote door lock receiver, which passes the decoded telegrams on to the BCM; Nissan-built cars lacking keyless entry use a stand-alone TPMS receiver that reports to the BCM as well.",["Lost supply voltage or ground at the receiver, e.g. corroded connector","Open or shorted data line between receiver and body control module","Radio interference from aftermarket devices (GM PIC5650M)","Receiver module or its antenna defective"],["TPMS malfunction indication with no pressure shown for any wheel","Poor remote key range where the receiver is shared with the door locks"],2,0,["C0960","C0950","C0083"],"מקלט TPMS — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],C0912:["TPMS Initiator Front Circuit Malfunction","C0912 could not be found in any code list, bulletin or service index, so its use remains unproven. The title refers to the front initiator: a coil near the wheel that wakes the tire sensor with a low frequency field so the system can tell which corner answered.",["Initiator wiring in the wheel arch chafed, corroded or unplugged","Initiator coil open or shorted internally","Initiator knocked out of its mount by wheel arch liner damage","Output stage in the TPMS module defective"],["TPMS malfunction lamp on","Front tire pressures shown without wheel position or not at all after a tire change"],2,0,["C0901","C0903","C0910"],""],C0915:["Active Roll Stabilisation Front Actuator Circuit","No list, bulletin or manual shows C0915 in use; the NHTSA index only matches unrelated BMW document numbers. The title names the front actuator of active roll control, which splits the anti-roll bar and twists its halves against each other to hold the body level in bends and to decouple them on rough roads.",["Damaged plug or harness at the front stabiliser actuator","Actuator motor or internal sensor failed","Fault in the 48 V supply feeding the actuator"],["Suspension or roll stabilisation warning","Noticeably more body lean in corners"],4,2,["C0916","C0920"],""],C0916:["Active Roll Stabilisation Rear Actuator Circuit","C0916 has no documented user; it is absent from every accessible list, bulletin and index. It names the rear axle actuator of active roll control. Systems with actuators on both axles split the stabilising torque between front and rear, which also lets them tune self-steering; ZF describes this for its electromechanical roll control. Faults at the rear unit therefore change balance as well as body lean.",["Damaged harness or plug at the rear stabiliser actuator, exposed to road spray","Roll control software needing an update (Mercedes 2021060016, Land Rover N733)","Rear actuator motor or gearbox failed"],["Amber suspension warning lamp","Speed limit advice in the cluster, more body roll and changed handling balance"],4,2,["C0915","C0920"],""],C0920:["Suspension Control Module Internal Fault","C0920 is not found in any accessible list or bulletin. The title describes a suspension control unit that fails its own checks. GM names such a fault C0550 Electronic Control Unit, as the 2011 Saab 9-5 pages show: the self-test runs at power-up and needs only supply and ground, the module ignores further inputs, and it should only be replaced if the code is present as current and history entry;",["Internal hardware or memory fault confirmed as current and history code","Poor supply or ground at the module triggering self-test failures","Software or parts incompatibility (GM PI0954, Audi 2067804/3)"],["Suspension service message, adaptive damping or levelling off","Other suspension codes may be stored alongside"],3,2,["C0850","C0851","C0852","C0853","C0870","C0915"],""],C0950:["Tire Pressure Monitoring Sensor Front Left","No public source links C0950 to a carmaker. The same content, the left front tire sensor, is documented under other numbers: GM and Saab use C0750, whose 2011 Saab 9-5 subcodes split a weak cell (03), too few telegrams (29) and an internal defect (39); Mitsubishi's 2022 index carries C1731 for the front left sensor and C1741 when its data stay away.",["Cell of the left front sensor exhausted","Sensor broken during tire fitting or wheel swapped for one without sensor","New sensor ID not registered for the front left position","Radio interference from aftermarket devices (GM PIC5650M)"],["TPMS lamp flashes, then stays on","No pressure value for the left front tire"],2,0,["C0951","C0952","C0953","C0750"],"שמאלי קדמי חיישן ניטור לחץ אוויר בצמיגים"],C0951:["Tire Pressure Monitoring Sensor Front Right","C0951 is not documented by any known maker. For the front right sensor GM and Saab rely on C0755 instead, on the 2011 9-4X with the subcodes 03, 29 and 39. Mitsubishi's 2022 data spell out the no-data case in detail as C1742-21: the BCM watches for the right front signal once the car has covered 10 minutes in total at 40 km/h or more, and it stores the code if nothing arrives.",["ID registration of the front right sensor incomplete","Sensor cell exhausted","Radio interference along the route or from devices in the car","Receiving control module defective"],["Dashes instead of a value for the right front tire","TPMS lamp lit after about ten minutes of driving"],2,0,["C0950","C0952","C0953"],"ימני קדמי חיישן ניטור לחץ אוויר בצמיגים"],C0952:["Tire Pressure Monitoring Sensor Rear Left","A manufacturer using C0952 is not on record; the number is absent from all lists and bulletins searched. What it names, the left rear tire sensor, carries other codes elsewhere: C0760 at GM and Saab, C1734 and C1744 in Mitsubishi's 2022 index, and on a 2008 Honda Accord the codes 37 for a low sensor battery and 38 for a sensor that stopped transmitting at the left rear.",["Wheels rotated without relearning sensor positions","Cell of the left rear sensor exhausted","Sensor damaged or missing after tire work"],["No reading for the left rear tire","TPMS warning after a tire rotation"],2,0,["C0950","C0951","C0953"],"שמאלי אחורי חיישן ניטור לחץ אוויר בצמיגים"],C0953:["Tire Pressure Monitoring Sensor Rear Right","C0953 stays without a documented user; neither J2012 lists nor bulletins name it. The right rear sensor appears at GM and Saab as C0765, where subcode 39 marks an internal malfunction. Mitsubishi's 2022 page for C1733-68 shows how implausible data from that corner are caught: above 40 km/h the BCM checks pressure, temperature and G sensor values in each telegram from the right rear unit and flags a fault within one…",["Pressure, temperature or acceleration element inside the right rear sensor defective","Sensor damaged by tire fitting, sealant or impact","Weak cell causing corrupted telegrams"],["TPMS lamp on with no valid value for the right rear tire","Implausible or jumping pressure reading at the right rear"],2,0,["C0950","C0951","C0952"],"ימני אחורי חיישן ניטור לחץ אוויר בצמיגים"],C0960:["Tire Pressure Monitoring Module Internal Fault","Public material does not show C0960 in use by any maker; it is missing from the public lists, indexes and bulletins. The title points to a self-test failure in the control unit that evaluates the tire sensors.",["Memory or processor fault inside the TPMS control unit","Corrupted or incomplete software after programming","Low supply voltage or poor ground disturbing the self-test"],["TPMS malfunction lamp lit permanently","No tire pressures shown at all"],4,0,["C0910","C0083"],""]};export{e as default};
